omium/src/+/fb0b324870..df36763e68\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/9fac5364ca..5ddcb4843f\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/f853eb533f..e9cf7ef159\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/74ec8c2ee5..c2c5a0381b\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/36a8df4ad0..48e2effc16\n    * src/third_party/fontconfig/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/fontconfig.git/+log/d17ee184e4..478e7774a5\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/b8f09d9168..3a170080b3\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/bbae40a551..5bd2baa069\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/fb0b324870..df36763e68/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Id19ead798ce55cda39741af422f10e212c5d28c0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503280\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48594}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "6dd481fa17fc7230c3b0b5a5b4a41e2d4207a6a4", "git_parents": ["99340d255515623decc8a1aa972156bb2d18d561"], "node": "671cb5f9a5635c86ed0dd2bdd35245c31d49a931", "parents": ["81429e0862240e2a50a36a2e0eeb9549fa12f919"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from bbd82081bd\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored c4f21b1f91.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bbd82081bd7ec1477b6db52319ec5a4ab8ffcbaa\n    [Wayland] Fix crash in ProcessDMABuffer and clean up renegotiate event\n\n    When DMA-BUF modifier import fails, ProcessDMABuffer attempts to\n    renegotiate stream parameters via pw_loop_signal_event() using\n    pw_-\u003erenegotiate. However, if pw_-\u003erenegotiate is null (e.g., if\n    pw_loop_add_event failed due to eventfd/file descriptor exhaustion),\n    pw_loop_signal_event() invokes loop_signal_event() with a null\n    source, resulting in a SIGSEGV at address 0x0.\n\n    This CL adds null checks for pw_ and pw_-\u003erenegotiate in\n    ProcessDMABuffer, consistent with UpdateScreenCastStreamResolution and\n    UpdateScreenCastStreamFrameRate. Additionally, PipeWireThreadLoop's\n    destructor now destroys the renegotiate event source using\n    pw_loop_destroy_source() to avoid leaking an eventfd on stream teardown.\n\n    TAG=agy\n    CONV=8d6dd432-bbd6-43de-b1dd-6d1a0d68bffa\n\n    Bug: chromium:559350359\n    Change-Id: Id2463382532dac5a8b9efe58f15dc1d3e003e4fc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502020\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jordan Bayles \u003cjophba@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48595}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/bbd82081bd.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "1a5ef702aa8ed0649d47a0a087f2a6a016dd7ab1", "git_parents": ["6dd481fa17fc7230c3b0b5a5b4a41e2d4207a6a4"], "node": "0ec269b16748066cf9896a53e206e4c74d3f7216", "parents": ["671cb5f9a5635c86ed0dd2bdd35245c31d49a931"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b7ddef1f9e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b7ddef1f9edb130528e935e8972a61b205c87d60\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-15T04:05:07).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie207688830c77b9f6b7b89ad47e5be5f8fb548f2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503400\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48596}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "f116da348522020fc817080598f3e0c22b16cb91", "git_parents": ["1a5ef702aa8ed0649d47a0a087f2a6a016dd7ab1"], "node": "4a37d25caed525407ec28e097e6cb542d1843cfc", "parents": ["0ec269b16748066cf9896a53e206e4c74d3f7216"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from a2a404325f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a2a404325f44993cc82bff9d3b7a5ca6aad6f7f2\n    opus: fix GeneratePlc for stereo and requested length\n\n    WebRtcOpus_Decode returns samples per channel, so a stereo decoder\n    saw only half the samples.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42223518\n    Change-Id: I81e4bca0941ccb970a2bc081d89d417a77712339\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503180\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48597}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8f8446c017b21eec8c58a73445baa3721682f5d1", "git_parents": ["f116da348522020fc817080598f3e0c22b16cb91"], "node": "a423e87a24253120abfedbde7ae8d2e2920727bf", "parents": ["4a37d25caed525407ec28e097e6cb542d1843cfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b629980ef3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b629980ef36d4cc0b60b8998d429c0d5dd2058db\n    Fix test failures triggered by vector/string allocation changes.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I60d25bbe24dbe5db26f15cc8749f8e84272d5bfd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501880\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48598}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/adaptive_fir_filter_avx2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/histogram.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/histogram.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch"], "git_node": "17b6227178b99be275c1550ee0d5685d3b836735", "git_parents": ["8f8446c017b21eec8c58a73445baa3721682f5d1"], "node": "688f20d162f5a796d1a0d4209fbed7ebe7c67bba", "parents": ["a423e87a24253120abfedbde7ae8d2e2920727bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 02bd855a5a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/02bd855a5a2a646215b28653bb9568f1c199882b\n    Log bitrate values in GoogCcNetworkController\n\n    When bitrate constraints violate invariants (max or start bitrate\n    smaller than min bitrate), GoogCcNetworkController logs warnings.\n    Include the actual bitrate values in the warning logs to improve\n    diagnosability of constraint issues.\n\n    Configure the start bitrate in RenegotiateManyAudioTransceivers to\n    avoid warnings when renegotiating many audio tracks.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I20e14c8a5d0320cef49ff6f0330a53b76422564c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503260\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48599}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/goog_cc_network_control.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "57592ff5dc1e3e33fe2bbc2c3ed00500f438514e", "git_parents": ["17b6227178b99be275c1550ee0d5685d3b836735"], "node": "0b93714287c8d14c6d0b22ef2316681d9dc65142", "parents": ["688f20d162f5a796d1a0d4209fbed7ebe7c67bba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from dcab586793\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dcab586793c8e0f798329de0bcba2c026eeb2785\n    Fix VP9 test flake caused by pacer key frame flush\n\n    The pacer intentionally discards packets that are still queued for a\n    stream when the first packet of a key frame is enqueued. That can\n    truncate the picture that is currently being sent, or remove it\n    altogether. Sequence numbers are assigned when packets are dequeued,\n    so the discarded packets leave no gap on the wire.\n\n    Vp9HeaderObserver assumed that every picture is observed in full and\n    that every picture ends with a packet carrying the marker bit. It\n    counted pictures by marker bits, so a truncated picture was never\n    counted. The picture count then no longer matched what the encoder\n    produced, which made every subsequent key frame prediction wrong and\n    resulted in a long cascade of failures.\n\n    - Count pictures on RTP timestamp transitions instead of marker bits,\n      and advance the count by the picture id delta ahead of a key\n      picture, which accounts for pictures that were discarded in full.\n    - Skip the end of picture, marker bit, picture id continuity and top\n      spatial layer checks when the new picture is a key picture.\n    - Associate the observer state with a SequenceChecker to document and\n      enforce that it is only touched on the send sequence, and add a\n      state dump to the assertions so failures can be diagnosed from a\n      log.\n    - Report in PacingController how many packets a key frame flush\n      discarded, since this can truncate a partially sent picture.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I54dffce60039aeebbcac94fcd8c6d2c822d4c29f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502540\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48600}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/pacing_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_tests.cc"], "git_node": "fec0ccc6f24d54ec3bbb7bc72fbfd49645717a58", "git_parents": ["57592ff5dc1e3e33fe2bbc2c3ed00500f438514e"], "node": "5d861f36675304d5d58501d8429292532bdfe667", "parents": ["0b93714287c8d14c6d0b22ef2316681d9dc65142"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 74a0ae52f2\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/74a0ae52f2342c98f3310378709de228780e1e02\n    Fix payload type collision when creating a re-offer\n\n    CodecVendor::GetNegotiatedCodecsForOffer assembled a re-offer from two\n    different payload type mappings: the codecs carried over verbatim from\n    the previous local description, and the codecs of the freshly merged\n    codec list. The payload type suggester may map a codec to a new payload\n    type, in which case the payload type the codec had in the previous\n    description can already belong to a different codec in the merged list.\n    The offer then used one payload type for two codecs, which tripped a\n    DCHECK in CodecList::PushIfNotPresent and dropped a codec from the\n    session description in release builds.\n\n    - Carry codecs over from the merged codec list so that the offer uses a\n      single payload type mapping.\n    - Return CodecList::PushResult from PushIfNotPresent in order to tell an\n      identical codec apart from a payload type that is taken by a different\n      codec.\n    - Report a payload type conflict as an error from codec merging and\n      offer assembly rather than asserting or quietly omitting the codec,\n      since the payload types involved are influenced by the remote\n      description.\n    - Stop discarding the results of the merge steps in the offer path.\n\n    Bug: chromium:558756689, webrtc:455503439\n    Change-Id: I493109ca3481b8f4eec60d7ec0dfb97ed764769a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503380\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48601}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "10d344de5886ecd9aa3b5676f08e88b8e8acff7d", "git_parents": ["fec0ccc6f24d54ec3bbb7bc72fbfd49645717a58"], "node": "c0adbed1d11c2d02f0446381900938f751451792", "parents": ["5d861f36675304d5d58501d8429292532bdfe667"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from ae00e08dea\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ae00e08dea0ff4998eb3d47ce433338cbc94c884\n    dav1d: Remove dead code from Dav1dDecoder\n\n    dav1d_close() ends in dav1d_freep_aligned(c_out), which always\n    resets the context pointer to null.\n    Also remove HasOneRef which is unused.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I482ae83e7c92e7fe830b6435fe914396322fc48f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503440\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48602}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/dav1d_decoder.cc"], "git_node": "126f14704f5851a506b5a30dde3f445fb9e9a700", "git_parents": ["10d344de5886ecd9aa3b5676f08e88b8e8acff7d"], "node": "408c70cd06e7141e8f555a7d35eecd454eb1e748", "parents": ["c0adbed1d11c2d02f0446381900938f751451792"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d8c5a46d99\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d8c5a46d991d752f24d7e985f0a0c0cb1cc2c48f\n    Remove support of sending RTCP TargetBitrate from the RTP layer\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222127\n    Change-Id: I13a0c12d52d47ff00c4c0bd441be74fd05849fcb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503480\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48603}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_video_sender_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/mocks/mock_rtp_rtcp.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_sender_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_rtcp_impl2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_rtcp_impl2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_rtcp_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0004.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0035.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0041.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0079.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0100.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0125.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d57c259a5e435beb4954fde329773e2f1e7274d3", "git_parents": ["126f14704f5851a506b5a30dde3f445fb9e9a700"], "node": "8df9ba194148f04aa9be8d4150ea323b05fbaa7a", "parents": ["408c70cd06e7141e8f555a7d35eecd454eb1e748"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from e8038893ea\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e8038893eaf0e46fc0232359436acb823128c080\n    Introduce NativeLifecycleLock and protect PeerConnectionFactory against UAF.\n\n    Add a reusable NativeLifecycleLock helper based on ReentrantReadWriteLock\n    to prevent use-after-free race conditions between JNI method invocations\n    and dispose() in Android SDK wrapper classes.\n\n    Concurrent calls to JNI methods on PeerConnectionFactory while dispose()\n    is executing can lead to native memory corruption when freeFactory() is\n    called while another thread is actively invoking native C++ methods.\n\n    Changes:\n    * Introduce NativeLifecycleLock in base_java to provide thread-safe\n      read-locked execution (call/run) and write-locked disposal.\n    * Refactor PeerConnectionFactory to guard all native calls with\n      NativeLifecycleLock, and free native pointers under write-lock before\n      nulling thread references.\n    * Refactor PeerConnection to adopt NativeLifecycleLock, eliminating\n      duplicate lock and functional interface boilerplate.\n    * Add NativeLifecycleLockTest to android_sdk_junit_tests covering\n      callback execution, post-disposal exceptions, idempotency, and\n      read/write lock concurrency.\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: Icbee403b2815a688fd8087708a079a34fcdb01ec\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501480\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48604}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "71b71029f73f2817369649627939bb7c97bb7c69", "git_parents": ["d57c259a5e435beb4954fde329773e2f1e7274d3"], "node": "cb2581ebee0c7392295e6eba3c4037ed602574d7", "parents": ["8df9ba194148f04aa9be8d4150ea323b05fbaa7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 26b31d40fe\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/26b31d40fe8f13d76d70076223b11437ce0471a8\n    Add Sframe decrypt error types and reporter\n\n    Adds `SframeDecryptErrorReporter`, which wraps an application-supplied\n    `SframeDecryptErrorCallback` and deduplicates consecutive failures of\n    the same type \u2014 a sustained failure (e.g. a missing key) fires the\n    callback once rather than once per frame or packet.\n\n    The reporter is aligned with\n    [SFrameTransformErrorEvent](https://w3c.github.io/webrtc-encoded-transform/#sframetransformerrorevent):\n    on failure the callback receives the error type (`kAuthentication`,\n    `kKeyId`, or `kSyntax`), an optional key identifier, and the frame that\n    failed decryption.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: Iada96ab5cbb8aa6c9e82629e2f86be917afd2032\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483920\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48605}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/sframe/sframe_decryptor_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_decrypt_error_reporter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_decrypt_error_reporter.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_decrypt_error_reporter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "5c402eaebd1331f57f5411d1cf379940c62525ba", "git_parents": ["71b71029f73f2817369649627939bb7c97bb7c69"], "node": "0279ff6945780ad7e32a7639bd6e412bc9c22cde", "parents": ["cb2581ebee0c7392295e6eba3c4037ed602574d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from a089f8428f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a089f8428f757c3f4a6f0715c628bb27d5980f4d\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-16T04:06:56).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie8fe2eb8f1d57facf3b14dd69400e3b0a87eefe6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503600\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48606}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "faa53c25c93fee3d7d2b59e75f7b64e42c96bcab", "git_parents": ["5c402eaebd1331f57f5411d1cf379940c62525ba"], "node": "484661698ed8a34779045b6d2092330ff43a2923", "parents": ["0279ff6945780ad7e32a7639bd6e412bc9c22cde"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3c1c05254c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3c1c05254c994efcf68a2b1ac213ace1e6e6b432\n    Relax quality thresholds in VideoCodecTestAv1.VeryLowBitrate\n\n    Lower min_min_psnr from 24.8 to 24.5 and min_min_ssim from 0.55 to 0.54\n    to fix test flakiness observed on Android x86.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I4288b957df0634e5e477baa98ae9916b46356cb3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503481\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48607}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/test/videocodec_test_av1.cc"], "git_node": "ebf442067ba5773003299e378b721c4ae92fbef6", "git_parents": ["faa53c25c93fee3d7d2b59e75f7b64e42c96bcab"], "node": "eb3a423a948f1d5fa3ba167901f450e592f087bf", "parents": ["484661698ed8a34779045b6d2092330ff43a2923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from aee44dca69\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/aee44dca69641529c7a313ddf0e5d20c42933f9c\n    VideoFrameBuffer: introduce ToI420ForInspection\n\n    Under pure-hardware-encoding conditions, corruption detection\n    will receive kUnknown video frame buffers which it inspects using\n    ToI420. This triggers a readback signal in Chromium which forces\n    the vide pipeline to read back frame information. This leads to\n    reconfigurations of hardware encoders in chromium.\n\n    Fix this by introducing ToI420ForInspection that will not trigger\n    readbacks.\n\n    Bug: chromium:555719593\n    Change-Id: Ic14e32ebd98578e9e5034b2a0a927e423164b5e6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503522\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48608}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/video_frame_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/video_frame_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/video_frame_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0147.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/halton_frame_sampler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/video_frame_sampler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/video_frame_sampler_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "17bd358b43968f90d6c783042db4416a8e5a4901", "git_parents": ["ebf442067ba5773003299e378b721c4ae92fbef6"], "node": "0bf1a4755655db1d74c9f643750ad1457e03224f", "parents": ["eb3a423a948f1d5fa3ba167901f450e592f087bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from ad898d45fa\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ad898d45fa2f4df2c30dd4312c59fa8c32a2c372\n    ssl: use SSL_AD_INTERNAL_ERROR on timeout instead of -1\n\n    Bug: webrtc:562024415\n    Change-Id: Ifa328f60ffc0a3d55d703c2d3aa8b1a27bd41f43\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503660\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48609}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc"], "git_node": "2411b52585f527666c5fa60a8677cd6e338cb850", "git_parents": ["17bd358b43968f90d6c783042db4416a8e5a4901"], "node": "6b6984828605552779c57ad4190a2160cd479f65", "parents": ["0bf1a4755655db1d74c9f643750ad1457e03224f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from fbfb49af6a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fbfb49af6adb4d4e3efd3ba4d3c9b46604c5af85\n    stats: only show media-playout when receiving audio\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I667502b52797b838c0056a3d9597ee2388b2e583\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501420\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48610}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "2628855d9fa27d1ac58ccfd5a7b705d82da2c056", "git_parents": ["2411b52585f527666c5fa60a8677cd6e338cb850"], "node": "78385afb7e1b9d00cad516a8877199e14ec13d34", "parents": ["6b6984828605552779c57ad4190a2160cd479f65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from f731aabbc0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f731aabbc0280bbf5768feaf73530b7a4a61ca48\n    vp9: memset buffers to zero when enlarging them\n\n    as required by libvpx:\n      https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/libvpx/source/libvpx/vpx/vpx_frame_buffer.h;l=47;drc=6d3729ca1a8ea1b1dc4176e2e9812d79b762eeaf\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I11b74e64d23cf53f4f822d637534d3c1fa49b3b6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503563\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48611}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/vp9_frame_buffer_pool.cc"], "git_node": "a32b6b5fe015a621ddd6b4b36fb2b1efc6253fb0", "git_parents": ["2628855d9fa27d1ac58ccfd5a7b705d82da2c056"], "node": "0088a1d2ea669e4facf3d7e1b53f19761f515164", "parents": ["78385afb7e1b9d00cad516a8877199e14ec13d34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7314d79803\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7314d7980362fd1f22635d309636adc8c45d8714\n    Defer codec list consistency check to complete lists\n\n    An application can swap the payload types of two codecs in an offer and\n    apply it with setLocalDescription, since all RTX codecs still refer to a\n    payload type that exists. Creating a re-offer from such a description\n    adds the codecs in the order of the previous description, which now\n    lists an RTX codec before the codec that it refers to. Verifying that\n    every RTX codec refers to a codec in the list after every insertion made\n    that intermediate state fatal, although the assembled codec list was\n    consistent.\n\n    Split the codec list invariants by when they hold: payload types have to\n    be unique at all times, which is what push_back() verifies, while the\n    codecs referred to by RTX codecs only have to be present once the list\n    is complete, which is left to CheckConsistency(). Lists created from\n    untrusted data are verified as before. CodecVendor now checks the\n    consistency of the offered codec list once it is fully assembled.\n\n    Bug: chromium:558756689\n    Change-Id: I0b8084d26812aa474566945ec8e412d547a34d37\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503620\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48612}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/codec_list_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "0649b9324988a1dc8547e06b1438a804109c3b14", "git_parents": ["a32b6b5fe015a621ddd6b4b36fb2b1efc6253fb0"], "node": "7678b198f3a3b7d0adf0c36cb861f84074f36884", "parents": ["0088a1d2ea669e4facf3d7e1b53f19761f515164"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6c3c1fe605\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6c3c1fe605015581560866db99056e46f210bcaa\n    cryptex consistency fixes\n\n    * ValidateCryptex: identify RTP m= sections by protocol instead of media\n      type so an unsupported m= section can not become the reference.\n    * JsepTransportController: take cryptex from the first RTP-based m=\n      section of the bundle group. The BUNDLE-tagged one may be the data\n      channel which does not have a cryptex attribute.\n    * CreateMediaContentAnswer: declare cryptex at media level when the\n      answer is not declaring it at session level.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:455813732\n    Change-Id: Ifd8fc72560cbcb4567c199e35d11114522a3b9a1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502140\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48613}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/media_session.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "93918e614868632ae76f020862aa70c86821733d", "git_parents": ["0649b9324988a1dc8547e06b1438a804109c3b14"], "node": "2749477a958a6a88538c9f2eb39e25bc3bc265fe", "parents": ["7678b198f3a3b7d0adf0c36cb861f84074f36884"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from dcfe2ae612\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dcfe2ae6125519c57fd0012cd84ec741162ea20d\n    [vpython] Migrate legacy .vpython3 to modern vpython.toml (UV)\n\n    Migrate WebRTC's root .vpython3 spec to a modern vpython.toml plus its\n    generated vpython.toml.uv.lock lockfile, and delete .vpython3.\n\n    Roll src/build to a56d226360eb0b3eaf423bfbf3cfe35a19e4951a (which adds\n    the overridable vpython_spec_files list) and configure\n    build_overrides/build.gni with:\n\n      vpython_spec_files = [\n        \"//vpython.toml\",\n        \"//vpython.toml.uv.lock\",\n      ]\n\n    Also update mb.py, mb_unittest.py, OWNERS_INFRA, and\n    infra/specs/trybot_analyze_config.json to reference vpython.toml and\n    vpython.toml.uv.lock instead of .vpython3, and add *.toml and *.lock to\n    .gitattributes.\n\n    TAG=agy\n    CONV=d815e88c-b2bf-4eff-aa46-4de7d9ef4406\n\n    LSC: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1D65SXziXtVmFRtZ7C2_zJp-NZc5Vjm0ZShTF29lwvjo/edit\n    Bug: chromium:491263752\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: I4b0bc8b55cc852d6c99d9e47098189ffcca6d69e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503420\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Alex Ovsienko \u003covsienko@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48614}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/.vpython3", "third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/OWNERS_INFRA", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/trybot_analyze_config.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/mb/mb.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/mb/mb_unittest.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/vpython.toml", "third_party/libwebrtc/vpython.toml.uv.lock"], "git_node": "e3de130d32d09004c31a9b2366aec7e3e8d15e28", "git_parents": ["93918e614868632ae76f020862aa70c86821733d"], "node": "325309b7343f078989bb087c7de43a95a77772ac", "parents": ["2749477a958a6a88538c9f2eb39e25bc3bc265fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7a24158da5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7a24158da5bbbc72330f8c71a0104a3536cd970f\n    Don't crash when SDP describes fewer send layers\n\n    RtpSenderBase::SetSsrcTask() applies the encodings the application\n    configured via addTransceiver() to the media channel once a local\n    description has been applied. The media channel derives its encodings\n    from the negotiated StreamParams, so the number of layers it knows\n    about is whatever the local description describes.\n\n    When the description describes fewer layers than the application asked\n    for, for instance because simulcast was removed by SDP munging, or\n    because the sender is attached to an ssrc the media channel has no send\n    stream for, the two views disagree and the RTC_CHECK_GE in the worker\n    thread lambda terminates the process. The mismatch is a negotiation\n    outcome, not memory corruption, so crashing is too strong a response\n    and the SDP remains authoritative either way.\n\n    Apply the layers that the media channel knows about, log a warning for\n    the ones that are dropped, and leave the channel untouched when it has\n    no send stream for the ssrc, which is the same treatment ssrc 0 gets.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558756689, webrtc:562462476\n    Change-Id: I1775221261eae116f55d5fc45e3e5a7417db88b0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503820\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48615}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "7a9be4574c75a053df2d3a0ca82d1c9eabc9318d", "git_parents": ["e3de130d32d09004c31a9b2366aec7e3e8d15e28"], "node": "08a199f51b9d55164401e95db5dc3bf65b6caef3", "parents": ["325309b7343f078989bb087c7de43a95a77772ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b32e4b35e6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b32e4b35e6025f044e88f4cc3169523b3021e3a9\n    Reimplement in Rust CorruptionDetection RTP header extension parsing\n\n    With intention to replace c++ parser and use this code to verify\n    infrastructures are ready to support Rust in WebRTC production code\n\n    Bug: webrtc:416446214\n    Change-Id: I7f8e13d56cf1b8bce9597047561fee07f6506025\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497560\n    Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48616}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/corruption_detection_extension.rs", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/corruption_detection_extension_cxx.rs", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/corruption_detection_extension_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch"], "git_node": "fe625463895576f74b2d5efb5f030cff37497ee6", "git_parents": ["7a9be4574c75a053df2d3a0ca82d1c9eabc9318d"], "node": "30277e5eab68b148afef9d8775b615554ebb0d8d", "parents": ["08a199f51b9d55164401e95db5dc3bf65b6caef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2960bf4a60\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2960bf4a6004806fb7caf5eb61bb00858eef0dc0\n    Disable windows chromium bots.\n\n    This is to unblock CQ and LKGR.\n\n    Change-Id: Iaac305aeb7cb8a8cc997f3358ffa22bcd518ffcc\n    Bug: b/562984134\n    No-Try: True\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504180\n    Reviewed-by: Christoffer Dewerin \u003cjansson@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48617}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/builders.star", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/commit-queue.cfg", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/cr-buildbucket.cfg", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/project.cfg"], "git_node": "d436003d315cb0cf040ac186486ca44c6a01e17e", "git_parents": ["fe625463895576f74b2d5efb5f030cff37497ee6"], "node": "6e49163d319517a40f6f780c6d3210df23273524", "parents": ["30277e5eab68b148afef9d8775b615554ebb0d8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from cfb487e0a5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/cfb487e0a5d5dba350ff1cfe09e28d5d5b74ff24\n    Use FakeRenderer when fuzzing\n\n    Real test Renderer can't create a window on a headless fuzzing bot\n\n    This is reland of https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/156620\n    It was reverted speculatively, later comments mention revert didn't\n    resolve OOM it tried to resolve, yet it wasn't relanded back then.\n\n    Bug: chromium:560246191\n    Change-Id: I1648e1c525b305af5b73d4face33d1c40bcb2eca\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503940\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48618}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/utils/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/utils/rtp_replayer.cc"], "git_node": "0b309da0fb84a03390912dd1cbc931c346db701d", "git_parents": ["d436003d315cb0cf040ac186486ca44c6a01e17e"], "node": "8ced4617a3c3b75de365f8d836fac22a34d26083", "parents": ["6e49163d319517a40f6f780c6d3210df23273524"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 72107b0541\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/72107b0541f4ae303cb4c66ccaeae129268b3ad0\n    [agc2] Make background speaker offset configurable via field trial\n\n    Make the background speaker detection threshold offset configurable via\n    the WebRTC-Agc2SpeechLevelEstimatorExperimental field trial using the\n    'offset' parameter (e.g. WebRTC-Agc2SpeechLevelEstimatorExperimental/Enabled,offset:15.0/).\n\n    - Parse the 'offset' parameter in SpeechLevelEstimator::Create and pass\n      the configured value to SpeechLevelEstimatorExperimentalImpl at\n      construction time.\n    - Fall back to the default 10.0 dBFS threshold if the parameter is\n      omitted or invalid.\n    - Add unit tests verifying field trial parsing and fallback behavior.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42232605\n    Change-Id: I184cfe5a87aa1e4adf98bf948afc988d5af30161\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504160\n    Commit-Queue: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48619}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/speech_level_estimator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/speech_level_estimator_experimental_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/speech_level_estimator_experimental_impl.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/speech_level_estimator_experimental_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "77474c12260291ed0800f152e1261182943e5be8", "git_parents": ["0b309da0fb84a03390912dd1cbc931c346db701d"], "node": "9d7470114e858506c486daf285373806386215a0", "parents": ["8ced4617a3c3b75de365f8d836fac22a34d26083"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b2a7366594\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b2a7366594f7241e4c7e22e91c7e1ee59781e1d9\n    Add RtpPacketizerSframe (SFrame RTP packetizer)\n\n    Adds the send-side Sframe RTP packetizer,\n    PacketizeSframeRtpPacketOrError(), which prepends the 1-byte Sframe\n    payload descriptor (S/E/T) to outgoing RTP media packets. For video, S\n    and E reflect whether the packet is the first or last fragment of a\n    frame; for audio, both are always set. The T bit indicates per-frame vs\n    per-packet encryption granularity. This CL is limited to the wire-format\n    step \u2014 wiring into the video and audio send paths, and adjusting payload\n    limits for Sframe overhead, will follow in separate changes.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: Ic7a5f657160db866128e0ec8d36191cf027955e4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/487380\n    Commit-Queue: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48620}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_depacketizer_sframe.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_depacketizer_sframe_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packet_to_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/sframe_descriptor.h"], "git_node": "afb1883aab8c4f619d8ec0b79f156c7a23cecf1d", "git_parents": ["77474c12260291ed0800f152e1261182943e5be8"], "node": "7e59097d8a439556346f0855097ffdc6dd027fab", "parents": ["9d7470114e858506c486daf285373806386215a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b2a7366594 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/rtp_rtcp_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "52a94ac9ae7497538f841ac130eb2ffbda7e0b9a", "git_parents": ["afb1883aab8c4f619d8ec0b79f156c7a23cecf1d"], "node": "8e72342a43ad8b8f718d62b78ac1250dc54a0e30", "parents": ["7e59097d8a439556346f0855097ffdc6dd027fab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from fb27a1c57d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fb27a1c57d7f133dd0acf9a888d88f823b425089\n    dtls-in-stun: add ice-option for embedding to the SDP\n\n    This change introduces the `sped` ice-option for embedding dtls in stun.\n    This allows the remote side to not negotiate it upfront. The existing\n    in-band discovery is still done which remains important since STUN\n    packets may arrive before the answer.\n\n    This considers embedding an ICE option as defined in\n      https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8445#section-13\n\n    SDP munging of this new feature is disallowed.\n\n    Re-upload of\n      https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/386820\n\n    Bug: webrtc:367395350\n    Change-Id: I65f18d22a4569f75462e325d5cee1c9a5d51a897\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/428980\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48621}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/uma_metrics.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description_factory_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_internal.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_peer_connection_base.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_peer_connection_internal.h"], "git_node": "536f6afd743b159e03a3f2a9b40eab33c999c48d", "git_parents": ["52a94ac9ae7497538f841ac130eb2ffbda7e0b9a"], "node": "31ab0d0a94b9c699c599fedb2866e365a3204fdd", "parents": ["8e72342a43ad8b8f718d62b78ac1250dc54a0e30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4f41278635\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4f41278635980c7033ff300f1ae58dc2d9027ccc\n    Remove the GoogCC/Scream wrapper controller\n\n    GoogCcScreamNetworkController was the only implementation behind the\n    WebRTC-Bwe-ScreamV2 values mode:only_after_ce and\n    mode:goog_cc_with_ect1. Neither is needed any more. The remaining modes\n    still cover Scream with RFC 8888 and mode:always.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225697\n    Change-Id: Iea82fd8cf8f3493fc074d07a3f2d7bccf8c56547\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504080\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48622}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/goog_cc_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "b0c6b478817a0266168efba16f6ea23e3645b70a", "git_parents": ["536f6afd743b159e03a3f2a9b40eab33c999c48d"], "node": "75ede296749f2895dc79644a50e780c147c2292f", "parents": ["31ab0d0a94b9c699c599fedb2866e365a3204fdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4f41278635 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz.build"], "git_node": "0f22288282fbcff072d5b993a12976e41ce59565", "git_parents": ["b0c6b478817a0266168efba16f6ea23e3645b70a"], "node": "e5ab68ce9bbc9192744502c0dc5274839b28b253", "parents": ["75ede296749f2895dc79644a50e780c147c2292f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2d9b4fccc7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2d9b4fccc762d0ad4dfe28eec1d7306e45adc83a\n    Make the CBR intra frame budget an explicit encoder setting\n\n    The libaom AV1 encoder wrapper hard coded an allowance of three times\n    the per frame bit budget for intra frames. That is a sane default, but\n    it is an implementation detail that callers can neither see nor tune,\n    and any caller reasoning about the bitrate of a stream containing a\n    keyframe has to guess it.\n\n    Add `max_intra_bitrate_factor` to StaticEncoderSettings::Cbr, pass it on\n    to libaom, and document the CBR settings in terms of the leaky bucket\n    buffer they describe. That also resolves the open question about the\n    initial buffer level: the buffer starts out at the target level, which\n    is what the libaom wrapper has been doing all along.\n\n    Since an encoder that silently ignores a setting is a problem of its\n    own, Capabilities::BitrateControl gains `supported_cbr_settings`, in\n    which an encoder lists the CBR settings it honors.\n\n    Plus some minor other API cleanups to make the surface more consistent.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: Ib11bde0b0c524f8e03bcd732b9140fe72cafaca5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503980\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48623}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/g3doc/video_encoder_api_v2.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/libaom_av1_encoder_factory_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_codec_test_utils.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_functional_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_builders.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_builders.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_factory_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.cc"], "git_node": "0c1ef1d6669df38ffc5c946173efefb485c239a9", "git_parents": ["0f22288282fbcff072d5b993a12976e41ce59565"], "node": "a42336387a7949d4ad5e7cb9833289c405f51ef1", "parents": ["e5ab68ce9bbc9192744502c0dc5274839b28b253"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from e47a101e95\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e47a101e95a762cbbd37390640e77b35426a3074\n    p2p: listen to socket close events\n\n    which were emitted e.g. when trying to use port 53 which is not\n    allowed anymore as of\n      https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8032493\n\n    While that is not done anymore, the UDP socket closing should still cancel pending requests and be logged.\n\n    Bug: chromium:511794959, chromium:559795244\n    Change-Id: Ifef3b6dc8477eb7e599886bb223b0b2cb29878b8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501500\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48624}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "59ef38e704569b3e907e3aa378ee1f936262462d", "git_parents": ["0c1ef1d6669df38ffc5c946173efefb485c239a9"], "node": "7c5e8a2ab148292846843ee5dc4bd01ac44c3a07", "parents": ["a42336387a7949d4ad5e7cb9833289c405f51ef1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from e7c0982141\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e7c0982141b286e595807aa9d2c0bc2d1702c53b\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-19T04:07:48).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Idcfcfccfe43f894e68910975f40ccdc7268336c2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504260\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48625}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "9bf51fe5a8e457e5c39516ffdc864a1aeb14340a", "git_parents": ["59ef38e704569b3e907e3aa378ee1f936262462d"], "node": "2a0e670bd17c24c3e4050cb03a2a9a44b125b4d5", "parents": ["7c5e8a2ab148292846843ee5dc4bd01ac44c3a07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from c250ac7568\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c250ac7568212f05892447d8e8673f8e55d716d9\n    Reconcile send layer count on the signaling thread\n\n    RtpSenderBase::SetSsrcTask() applies the encodings the application\n    configured to the media channel from a worker thread task. When the\n    applied local description describes fewer layers than the application\n    asked for, the sender discovers this on the worker thread, where the\n    negotiation context needed to reason about the mismatch is no longer\n    available.\n\n    The signaling thread already knows the answer. The media channel derives\n    its encodings from the StreamParams of the applied local description\n    through CreateRtpParametersWithEncodings(), which uses one encoding per\n    primary SSRC, and UpdateSenderSsrcsFromLocalDescription() holds those\n    same StreamParams. The layer count can therefore be computed without\n    asking the media channel, and without a blocking call.\n\n    - Pass the negotiated layer count to RtpSenderInternal::SetSsrcTask().\n    - Drop surplus encodings in the SetSsrcTask() prologue, which runs on\n      the signaling thread before the worker task is queued.\n    - Keep the clamp in the worker task for the cases the layer count cannot\n      describe: voice channels always report a single encoding, and the\n      channel may have no send stream for the ssrc at all.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558756689\n    Change-Id: I174f62b9f6a05f4691a8e4cfccaa145dd9d33f37\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503840\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48626}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_rtp_sender_internal.h"], "git_node": "c38e9f584c198f3a61c5775ae70104c52817e282", "git_parents": ["9bf51fe5a8e457e5c39516ffdc864a1aeb14340a"], "node": "7a4918f2ef2463a6a465c58e2c72adce55e9a05b", "parents": ["2a0e670bd17c24c3e4050cb03a2a9a44b125b4d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3f798e3502\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3f798e3502bfa27639d7b791c83548782fa99677\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-20T04:06:59).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I2c6665386c3d95a881bae4dcd553e592cf59219e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504300\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48627}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "5f8e197a7a87ce1f96233d076b7a40f1e826e149", "git_parents": ["c38e9f584c198f3a61c5775ae70104c52817e282"], "node": "0d351fd0dadc57ad112b4528c8425738cf370840", "parents": ["7a4918f2ef2463a6a465c58e2c72adce55e9a05b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 80a2d4352d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/80a2d4352dbab7c7af774a49ff95ab4b0c3609d3\n    Add unit tests for ChannelReceiveFrameTransformerDelegate\n\n    Verify cross-thread StartShortCircuiting and receive-thread Reset\n    in ChannelReceiveFrameTransformerDelegate, and guard callback invocation\n    when short-circuiting in Transform().\n\n    Bug: webrtc:11993\n    Change-Id: Ib79c07cced700353d5c2dcb1ecc9e46d15bc53a5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/495020\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48628}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_receive_frame_transformer_delegate.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_receive_frame_transformer_delegate_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d2d926a3215a39b46035bc3372e3d6b91926ad91", "git_parents": ["5f8e197a7a87ce1f96233d076b7a40f1e826e149"], "node": "308d6e3eef0c8a676f32bec7f8686f52ba5746a8", "parents": ["0d351fd0dadc57ad112b4528c8425738cf370840"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 438e0746c4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/438e0746c4e0c62dfec936de2f76cbd55f390710\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-21T04:05:20).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ib95c7f8714cee0ce8dbae6b40b92db769522f4ab\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504320\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48629}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "fff9ffce25aee4af2f9230f3ddef147970a3f837", "git_parents": ["d2d926a3215a39b46035bc3372e3d6b91926ad91"], "node": "9e93f0a222bcb9a53bdf8d08e35922f635abd39e", "parents": ["308d6e3eef0c8a676f32bec7f8686f52ba5746a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from fb8ad81325\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fb8ad81325fb9a85497a4ecfb31e163d1be7239b\n    Remove 'WebRTC Chromium FYI Win Builder (dbg)' from LKGR\n\n    Change-Id: I31ccfda1ed30cf445bf34881ec1bbaeb7df1d3ad\n    Bug: b/562984134\n    No-Try: True\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504340\n    Reviewed-by: Christoffer Dewerin \u003cjansson@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48630}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/builders.star", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/cr-buildbucket.cfg"], "git_node": "be5053a5dc676eb8cc2839bec903bb6d7bc30455", "git_parents": ["fff9ffce25aee4af2f9230f3ddef147970a3f837"], "node": "55649b691196e775177ce0030a4f6ba1768500fa", "parents": ["9e93f0a222bcb9a53bdf8d08e35922f635abd39e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 176602de15\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/176602de153df474512c03b77869bbd2a74e9a17\n    Keep operations pending through result delivery\n\n    libwebrtc invokes observers on the signaling sequence, but embedders may deliver their results asynchronously on another sequence. Advancing the chain when the observer returns can therefore start the next operation before the API promise settles.\n\n    Let embedders defer operation completion until createOffer(), createAnswer(), setLocalDescription(), and addIceCandidate() results reach their API consumers. Add tests that hold result delivery and verify the next operation remains blocked.\n\n    Bug: chromium:488071544\n    Change-Id: I38c98d0a2d6028aea33d30fa907980c9224f3e34\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499640\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48631}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/set_local_description_observer_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_ice_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_proxy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_signaling_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.h"], "git_node": "1a653687d918aaa3c1f8ece070e11b7d357b5af0", "git_parents": ["be5053a5dc676eb8cc2839bec903bb6d7bc30455"], "node": "1eed15bd977664d99263628ccdaf00fe161d34e8", "parents": ["55649b691196e775177ce0030a4f6ba1768500fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from edbe4116a5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/edbe4116a542888dd4d0dde80145785bf417c29e\n    Derive ECT(1) bleaching from PacketResult\n\n    `TransportPacketsFeedback::transport_supports_ecn` is cleared for any\n    received Not-ECT packet, without checking whether that packet had been\n    sent with ECT(1). A packet deliberately sent as Not-ECT and correctly\n    received as Not-ECT therefore counts as evidence that the path bleaches\n    the ECT(1) marking. This becomes reachable once ECT(1) is re-enabled\n    without a route change, when both markings are in flight at the same\n    time.\n\n    PacketResult already carries everything needed to answer the question, so\n    add `HasPacketWithBleachedEct1()` and deprecate the flag. Note that only\n    received packets are considered: packets reported lost carry a defaulted\n    Not-ECT marking and are otherwise indistinguishable from bleached ones.\n\n    The deprecated flag is left populated exactly as before.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225697\n    Change-Id: I07538733e5667c37091115c64319b7ccfa69c707\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503781\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48632}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_types.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_types.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/transport_feedback_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/rtp/transport_feedback_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0122.patch"], "git_node": "642018dd268698827ef82e8d7e2eebca09b27784", "git_parents": ["1a653687d918aaa3c1f8ece070e11b7d357b5af0"], "node": "95e198757bb8b1ba21b99c847f2e0073fc058f92", "parents": ["1eed15bd977664d99263628ccdaf00fe161d34e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from f98760a625\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f98760a625b3fc82ead05e4a641ce3eaa7b4e46f\n    Split ConfigureForRtcpFeedback into two setters\n\n    PacketRouter::ConfigureForRtcpFeedback set two unrelated things at\n    once: whether transport sequence numbers are generated for all\n    packets, and whether packets are marked ECT(1). They have different\n    triggers. The first only changes when the feedback format is\n    negotiated, the second whenever an input to the ECT(1) decision\n    changes.\n\n    Combining them means the ECT(1) decision can not be pushed on its own.\n    A caller that wants to avoid redundant work has to gate both settings\n    on whether the ECT(1) decision changed, which silently drops transport\n    sequence number updates. That matters for the upcoming blackhole\n    detection, which re-evaluates the decision on every sent packet.\n\n    No behavior change. SetGenerateTransportSequenceNumbers is now only\n    called when the feedback format is negotiated, which is the only place\n    where its input can change.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225697\n    Change-Id: I1cb75ee2f2a0d7164652dde6952822c5c6f32244\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504020\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48633}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/packet_router.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/packet_router.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/packet_router_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0122.patch"], "git_node": "bd11aa8e8118564e525060d42e857da51e8fa87e", "git_parents": ["642018dd268698827ef82e8d7e2eebca09b27784"], "node": "3422e07bb4e147ed585d7c5b4b76062421aa5732", "parents": ["95e198757bb8b1ba21b99c847f2e0073fc058f92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d6d8d973b7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d6d8d973b7da280c669665598c4f441219927a69\n    Link Rust code into prod library.\n\n    This change integrates a Rust implementation of the\n    CorruptionDetectionMessage into the existing C++\n    CorruptionDetectionExtension using a cxx bridge.\n\n    This change verifies readiness of various toolchains to accept Rust code\n    in WebRTC\n\n    Bug: webrtc:416446214\n    Change-Id: I288e130e20bcfaf7c9761fe5b2b9326fbfd2feeb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497460\n    Reviewed-by: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48634}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/g3doc/rust-in-webrtc.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/corruption_detection_extension.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/libs/generate_licenses.py"], "git_node": "462dc57731a3425ad02112c86961ee9691434e04", "git_parents": ["bd11aa8e8118564e525060d42e857da51e8fa87e"], "node": "b795071e5bbc5afd809cc666f69b9bcf3fdf66c4", "parents": ["3422e07bb4e147ed585d7c5b4b76062421aa5732"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3a56730266\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3a56730266ef1517608ec82bb0ce2d90f08cb88d\n    Move the ECT(1) marking decision into Ect1Policy\n\n    Whether packets are marked ECT(1) was decided in three places in\n    RtpTransportControllerSend. Collect it in a new Ect1Policy, placed in\n    modules/congestion_controller since modules can not depend on call.\n\n    Deriving the decision from its inputs instead of keeping it as mutable\n    state fixes two things: ECT(1) is no longer enabled when the congestion\n    controller does not adapt to ECN, and renegotiation no longer\n    re-enables it on a route already found to bleach the marking.\n\n    SupportsEcnAdaptation() is now read once, when the congestion\n    controller is created. No controller changes it during a call since\n    the GoogCC/Scream wrapper was removed.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225697\n    Change-Id: If8e88bb2f82ec3e059433a5e206c4438a78ce3f4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504000\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48635}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0122.patch"], "git_node": "9c970491c9bb896dc26fc76d4046b10e3585ebc4", "git_parents": ["462dc57731a3425ad02112c86961ee9691434e04"], "node": "2af79a43e79a0cc48f51aefa1fc1bb36a6203ecb", "parents": ["b795071e5bbc5afd809cc666f69b9bcf3fdf66c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3a56730266 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz.build"], "git_node": "1f855b5bb211ed669ba3a712aa58c7714226e173", "git_parents": ["9c970491c9bb896dc26fc76d4046b10e3585ebc4"], "node": "d57df73074e608521b482e636ecd239e02276010", "parents": ["2af79a43e79a0cc48f51aefa1fc1bb36a6203ecb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 27657fd378\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/27657fd3787f9f904b77f84f266a41edf4143ba0\n    Skip BasicOfferAnswerPayloadTypesStable if rtc_use_h264=false.\n\n    Since it is good to keep H264 in the test expectations, let's just\n    disable it in case the build turns off H264 explicitly.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ia58e5df5f2a2577833ecd7c93d13e1b205190d75\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504140\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48636}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_stability_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "7a88a3d29d502f5c1f6a9b46483d545206424b09", "git_parents": ["1f855b5bb211ed669ba3a712aa58c7714226e173"], "node": "c690982416cebdbe5e8e5bcb85f971d3a32494e4", "parents": ["d57df73074e608521b482e636ecd239e02276010"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d40ac5b8b9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d40ac5b8b944749d748e6e7bf44e01063ba23a23\n    dav1d: Handle dav1d_data_wrap failures\n\n    When dav1d_data_wrap() fails it does not install the free callback\n    so the EncodedImageBufferInterface reference taken was leaked and\n    the decode continued with empty data.\n\n    Also release previous context in Dav1dDecoder::Configure().\n\n    Bug: webrtc:561877904\n    Change-Id: I47d53d29c7f7bdf27f4865836ef4cf973fb4c622\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503580\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48637}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/dav1d_decoder.cc"], "git_node": "a56eb1345686585b6a2ee4215fbb3330336ec21f", "git_parents": ["7a88a3d29d502f5c1f6a9b46483d545206424b09"], "node": "b02cee897722288285f9461bd8c0b212ca3a1d8e", "parents": ["c690982416cebdbe5e8e5bcb85f971d3a32494e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 65837624d7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/65837624d7e3a419b5f1b92ea29ed86219d87570\n    pc: make always_negotiate_datachannels immutable\n\n    which is less surprising. Spec change:\n      https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-extensions/pull/254\n\n    Bug: chromium:433898678\n    Change-Id: I6bb451b29183a2a726becae5998ecb034731caf4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490381\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48638}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f2a3da8a91f7659cb0c2a7653de7a8b8ac920d6f", "git_parents": ["a56eb1345686585b6a2ee4215fbb3330336ec21f"], "node": "7f5e9c8634537ff2a54c3e05512b7d259170d8a3", "parents": ["b02cee897722288285f9461bd8c0b212ca3a1d8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5516497a48\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5516497a486929823bfce81f4a0527f2339806ec\n    Cleanup p2p unit test + SDP munging detector\n\n    Follow-up from\n      https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/428980\n\n    Bug: webrtc:367395350\n    Change-Id: Ie78e7f716d61ea82dd5630d96da571b1e831809f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/498000\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48639}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description_factory_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a19b98818ca0510ee67fc7649211d8705df9f21f", "git_parents": ["f2a3da8a91f7659cb0c2a7653de7a8b8ac920d6f"], "node": "65603108244a1c6f567dbda689a5acbad034dc76", "parents": ["7f5e9c8634537ff2a54c3e05512b7d259170d8a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 49fe6a3388\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/49fe6a33889f0786ce0251e54b24ee6a89422d1e\n    Add test for munged local offer with fewer layers\n\n    The local description is authoritative for the number of send layers\n    configured on a sender. However, no end-to-end test verified the\n    behavior when an application reduces the simulcast layer count by\n    munging the offer before applying it.\n\n    Add a test ensuring the sender strictly adheres to the layer count\n    present in the applied local description rather than the initial\n    encodings requested via addTransceiver().\n\n    A rollback variant of this scenario fails earlier in the flow due to an\n    existing SSRC without an associated channel after rollback. That\n    behavior is tracked separately in chromium:562462476.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558756689\n    Change-Id: Idcae41db1238d130e5f1430c1d1ae3468a991a51\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503841\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48640}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_simulcast_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f5d62e3f3560b677d2529019bb1d63255067f6d0", "git_parents": ["a19b98818ca0510ee67fc7649211d8705df9f21f"], "node": "5f56b3ceed6243eb37fe51dfaf1db863d5b5277b", "parents": ["65603108244a1c6f567dbda689a5acbad034dc76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from c0dd1f8ffe\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c0dd1f8ffe945e9fd5ffab70afb73a5c2bcb35ad\n    Split FakeVideoRenderer into own helper target\n\n    In particular build it even when !rtc_include_tests because it is also\n    used by fuzzers now.\n\n    Follow up of the https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503940\n\n    Bug: chromium:560246191\n    Change-Id: I7108818de558991577441d39dd0130ab4d6f0ec0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504360\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48641}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/utils/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "6dee4bde8f826fce4732fdc54eb2e3c3d2d02a06", "git_parents": ["f5d62e3f3560b677d2529019bb1d63255067f6d0"], "node": "bcc41bf9a456f826e1d35af7d2ecad62e6f89b69", "parents": ["5f56b3ceed6243eb37fe51dfaf1db863d5b5277b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 98de979765\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/98de979765ecc205542e978456827d27edf8a604\n    Let encoders publish a max frame size and clamp the source to it\n\n    Add EncoderInfo::max_pixels_per_frame. VideoStreamEncoder feeds it to\n    VideoSourceSinkController::SetPixelsPerFrameUpperLimit, which already\n    exists but had no caller, so sink wants never ask the source for more\n    pixels than the active encoder can encode. Without this, an encoder\n    that rejects InitEncode for an oversized resolution stalls the stream\n    when no encoder switch callback, selector or software fallback exists.\n\n    SimulcastEncoderAdapter reports the minimum across its encoders. The\n    software fallback wrapper reports its fallback encoder's limit, which\n    is the one that always holds since frames the default encoder rejects\n    fall back to it.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:562778572\n    Change-Id: I9aac9435871bd0e98392cb1cb4b202b46a6a6964\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504040\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48642}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_software_fallback_wrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_software_fallback_wrapper.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0045.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "3569cb5585e1b6876c53a7d7135ffbe9bc683fff", "git_parents": ["6dee4bde8f826fce4732fdc54eb2e3c3d2d02a06"], "node": "3b25f9862fd3e95a2ac7b146831942070b81c4bb", "parents": ["bcc41bf9a456f826e1d35af7d2ecad62e6f89b69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d55353311e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d55353311ea8aaa224550823568264cdd41d0159\n    Keep send parameters that were not applied\n\n    When a sender is attached to an SSRC, the encodings and degradation\n    preference the application configured before negotiation are applied to\n    the media channel and then cleared. They were also cleared when they\n    were never applied, which silently discarded what the application asked\n    for, with no way to recover.\n\n    Keep the encodings when the media channel rejects them, and log a\n    warning. Keep the degradation preference until it has been applied: it\n    is not tied to a specific send stream, so a preference configured before\n    negotiation should still take effect if the sender is attached to a send\n    stream later.\n\n    The encodings are still cleared once they have been applied, and when\n    there is no send stream to apply them to, which is what the clear was\n    introduced for.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558756689\n    Change-Id: I125475aa81f606220c3d9988f20b0a6877b1213e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503860\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48643}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "debf9f766a24a2ab96cb5992f786c7a5499534df", "git_parents": ["3569cb5585e1b6876c53a7d7135ffbe9bc683fff"], "node": "acafab6cf2ec12a8635718f400129185e53a05ec", "parents": ["3b25f9862fd3e95a2ac7b146831942070b81c4bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 (MOZ) - Vendor NativeLifecycleLock.java\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/third_party_build/vendor-libwebrtc.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/src/java/org/webrtc/NativeLifecycleLock.java"], "git_node": "a0efe797e836937a964092ed6e06ab898e90488a", "git_parents": ["debf9f766a24a2ab96cb5992f786c7a5499534df"], "node": "938a087ca06a8701fd5fe48a31fc12a65e25b119", "parents": ["acafab6cf2ec12a8635718f400129185e53a05ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0f3da5545c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0f3da5545cdab1773188e2f1ba2b4783c4fdc1d5\n    Adopt NativeLifecycleLock in DataChannel.java\n\n    Prevents use-after-free race conditions between JNI method invocations\n    and dispose().\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: Ice667be0319cf22a17a3175efa187dce1578c084\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503680\n    Commit-Queue: Linus Nilsson \u003clnilsson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48644}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/DataChannel.java"], "git_node": "c07e0e728e6e4c902abd912fc5baedbbb74cbee9", "git_parents": ["a0efe797e836937a964092ed6e06ab898e90488a"], "node": "232398af6e503eee3e4bf84abb3320170994c68b", "parents": ["938a087ca06a8701fd5fe48a31fc12a65e25b119"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7b28688748\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7b286887483d99ecb25e1181e342089d606f1a82\n    Protect RtpSender, RtpReceiver, and RtpTransceiver against UAF.\n\n    Adopt NativeLifecycleLock in RtpSender, RtpReceiver, and RtpTransceiver to\n    prevent use-after-free race conditions between concurrent JNI method calls\n    and dispose().\n    Concurrent invocations of JNI methods while dispose() is executing can\n    result in native memory corruption if JniCommon.nativeReleaseRef() frees\n    the underlying C++ object while another thread is actively using it.\n\n    Changes:\n    * Replace raw native pointers with NativeLifecycleLock in RtpSender,\n      RtpReceiver, and RtpTransceiver.\n    * Guard all JNI method invocations with read-locked call() and run()\n      blocks.\n    * Execute child disposals (dtmfSender, cachedTrack, cachedSender,\n      cachedReceiver), observer unregistration, and nativeReleaseRef()\n      inside write-locked dispose() blocks, making disposal thread-safe and\n      idempotent.\n    * Delegate getNativeRtpSender() and getNativeRtpReceiver() to\n      lifecycleLock.getNativePointer().\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: Idb7bacce6ebd6894ffd9f1e765de1a131ff813c3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503700\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Linus Nilsson \u003clnilsson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48645}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "f259ee70c4179551bbaa8d2cdb3ae5e58651b17d", "git_parents": ["c07e0e728e6e4c902abd912fc5baedbbb74cbee9"], "node": "5c14e8e17dbface845769d1bcbb989bb7916b0d3", "parents": ["232398af6e503eee3e4bf84abb3320170994c68b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from f4348b8541\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f4348b85417b4cfd9e026aa378a81b54407b47a4\n    Protect Android MediaStream, MediaStreamTrack, and MediaSource against UAF.\n\n    Adopt NativeLifecycleLock across MediaStreamTrack (and subclasses AudioTrack\n    and VideoTrack), MediaStream, MediaSource, and VideoSource to prevent\n    Use-After-Free and double-free race conditions when JNI methods or capturer\n    callbacks execute concurrently with dispose().\n\n    In VideoTrack, synchronize access to the sinks map under the lifecycle lock to\n    prevent concurrent modification and native sink leaks during teardown. In\n    VideoSource, route CapturerObserver callbacks through runWithReference() so\n    in-flight camera events hold a valid native reference.\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: I826ff486a619c50d6f80fda39e9f6994b8f94c08\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504400\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Linus Nilsson \u003clnilsson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48646}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/AudioTrack.java", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/MediaSource.java", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/MediaStreamTrack.java", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/VideoSource.java", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/VideoTrack.java"], "git_node": "05b15a142d90b352719f4f4901055e10c25183f8", "git_parents": ["f259ee70c4179551bbaa8d2cdb3ae5e58651b17d"], "node": "64537ef0a337e64dada405a08c7c5f4c403e7557", "parents": ["5c14e8e17dbface845769d1bcbb989bb7916b0d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d943abd375\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d943abd3750afb3fb6c956a4bafc4ef294b55198\n    Removing bitexactness verification functionality in audioproc_f\n\n    This CL removes the non-working and unused  bitexactness verification functionality\n    in audioproc_f.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42230301\n    Change-Id: I4c53fea1f3d924a957d4d821dd2353dc86eb1692\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/487120\n    Reviewed-by: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48647}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/aec_dump_based_simulator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/aec_dump_based_simulator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audio_processing_simulator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audioproc_float_impl.cc"], "git_node": "a045c6ed68c39c02e9a7ce4bc149d8746c051d80", "git_parents": ["05b15a142d90b352719f4f4901055e10c25183f8"], "node": "f60423ba4bf7c7126a66b3f86737687ced9ff371", "parents": ["64537ef0a337e64dada405a08c7c5f4c403e7557"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 09297de989\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/09297de98949ca64ff22135189a65ee57b6caf80\n    The ComplexFft functionality beneath common_audio is no longer used.\n    This CL removes the code for that.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:505072868\n    Change-Id: Ic6caaf37e53f80685ed8fa1110aa03826da2be35\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/465800\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48648}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse_arm.S", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse_mips.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft_mips.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft_tables.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/include/signal_processing_library.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/signal_processing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "017d5b32e8980fc9bc2b1223b3a302584a8a420d", "git_parents": ["a045c6ed68c39c02e9a7ce4bc149d8746c051d80"], "node": "581783c3a33ed3625fa1dd89572fb13d7d97198b", "parents": ["f60423ba4bf7c7126a66b3f86737687ced9ff371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 09297de989 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/common_audio_c_arm_asm_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/common_audio_c_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "0fffbe77abac193fa9cfe3f072683084e1a43505", "git_parents": ["017d5b32e8980fc9bc2b1223b3a302584a8a420d"], "node": "6b990cd1f39eb3accd274ca17c5b472a5a039149", "parents": ["581783c3a33ed3625fa1dd89572fb13d7d97198b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 23df7ef65b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/23df7ef65bc831dfe10c5150146bf9e6bebe7194\n    Removed the unused WebRtcSpl_SqrtOfOneMinusXSquared functionality\n\n    Bug: webrtc:505072868\n    Change-Id: Ie9653b06e57c5d64f5360174c02683be58337990\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/465801\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48649}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/include/signal_processing_library.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/signal_processing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/sqrt_of_one_minus_x_squared.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "2a6b5fca35e5c3fe061b2fec711fcdf54dd9bb62", "git_parents": ["0fffbe77abac193fa9cfe3f072683084e1a43505"], "node": "b90f7cf5405c40ab7d62a8eaf09c78499fc0b6af", "parents": ["6b990cd1f39eb3accd274ca17c5b472a5a039149"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 23df7ef65b - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/common_audio_c_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "47fd2e929600beac753c23d311d158c3dc1e2da7", "git_parents": ["2a6b5fca35e5c3fe061b2fec711fcdf54dd9bb62"], "node": "b7404a70177d9fbd39ca0f7dd82a341056c6ab55", "parents": ["b90f7cf5405c40ab7d62a8eaf09c78499fc0b6af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from a9c6ddcd2d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a9c6ddcd2d110639bc5443e4de7172b662efe448\n    Preserve builder APM and AEC configurations in AudioprocFloat\n\n    Currently, AudioprocFloat resets any APM and AEC configurations provided\n    via BuiltinAudioProcessingBuilder:\n    - SetDependencies() unconditionally overwrote the builder's\n      EchoCanceller3Config with a default instance unless --aec_settings was\n      specified.\n    - AudioProcessingSimulator::ConfigureAudioProcessor() constructed a blank\n      AudioProcessing::Config from scratch rather than reading from the\n      initialized processor.\n    This change updates AudioprocFloat to: 1. Retain the builder's\n    EchoCanceller3Config unless explicitly overridden\n       via CLI flags (--aec_settings, --linear_aec_output).\n    2. Initialize apm_config using ap_-\u003eGetConfig() in\n       AudioProcessingSimulator (matching AecDumpBasedSimulator behavior) so\n       pre-configured settings are preserved unless overridden by CLI flags.\n\n    Bug: b/502437863\n    Change-Id: I6676aae9e4e3d86a54d72d22435602f8f0bdfb29\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504420\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48650}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio/builtin_audio_processing_builder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audio_processing_simulator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audioproc_float_impl.cc"], "git_node": "1a0c5c0985b2ef64d0083258dc2047c845f025b1", "git_parents": ["47fd2e929600beac753c23d311d158c3dc1e2da7"], "node": "23f0c65fe1201defc39968942be1ffb61824e0e1", "parents": ["b7404a70177d9fbd39ca0f7dd82a341056c6ab55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7e4a6a20b4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7e4a6a20b4735eb19f64e36f66ead8a3033465e6\n    Remove restrictions listener test hooks from VideoStreamEncoder\n\n    AddRestrictionsListenerForTesting and RemoveRestrictionsListenerForTesting\n    blocked the worker thread on a task posted to the encoder queue.\n    They existed only so that VideoStreamEncoderTest could tell when\n    SetSource had been processed. The tests run on simulated time, where\n    advancing the clock by zero drains the encoder queue\n    deterministically, so the listener and its event are not needed.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I8523fcbdb761fef741552a4de509b73ce03fad42\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504381\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Markus Handell \u003chandellm@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48651}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "142ee6bda305495e950fb4233df3ed8c2ebafbf8", "git_parents": ["1a0c5c0985b2ef64d0083258dc2047c845f025b1"], "node": "5241bc9c238681de0a11f4bb2f378011d2af5f4b", "parents": ["23f0c65fe1201defc39968942be1ffb61824e0e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7994089bab\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7994089babd4ae8b62cd696ae1238026238a02b5\n    Remove event waits from VideoStreamEncoder tests\n\n    These tests run on simulated time, but Event::Wait() yields only once\n    to run the tasks that are ready at the current timestamp before\n    blocking on the wall clock. Anything that needs time to advance is\n    never run, and the wait becomes a five second stall.\n    SetSourceAndWaitForFramerateUpdated() ignored the return value, so\n    such a stall passed unnoticed.\n\n    Drain the encoder queue with AdvanceTime(TimeDelta::Zero()) instead.\n    The Trigger* helpers already did so right after their wait, making\n    the event pure duplication. CpuOveruseDetectorProxy used its event\n    only to report whether OnTargetFramerateUpdated() had been called,\n    which is now a flag. This removes the last blocking waits on the\n    encoder queue, a prerequisite for merging it into the worker queue.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: Iadfffdd82c3b02b1e82f1d066c45ad762812266a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504440\n    Commit-Queue: Markus Handell \u003chandellm@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48652}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "12a4e156c27aa8872738ffb1f035ce28b699124b", "git_parents": ["142ee6bda305495e950fb4233df3ed8c2ebafbf8"], "node": "de2822dd668273ad38e9b2a419a00ac577b6e638", "parents": ["5241bc9c238681de0a11f4bb2f378011d2af5f4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 48de43219d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/48de43219ddc3a47188814d512875eaeb0bcf0d0\n    Remove VideoStreamEncoder::encoder_queue()\n\n    The accessor existed only so that VideoStreamEncoderTest could post\n    tasks to the encoder queue. The fixture creates that queue and\n    already holds a pointer to it, so pass the pointer to the test\n    encoder instead. VideoStreamEncoderFrameCadenceRestrictionTest\n    already works this way.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I006224a619ce488918f06fa9aad28a6a189d80b2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504382\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Markus Handell \u003chandellm@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48653}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "1cc968202f98fb03ee0984e1feb82d9aefbc44bd", "git_parents": ["12a4e156c27aa8872738ffb1f035ce28b699124b"], "node": "585f5e24bda4e2a171af50c1945dc6619aa218af", "parents": ["de2822dd668273ad38e9b2a419a00ac577b6e638"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from fe36fc7ca1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fe36fc7ca1e7453a0b3b846c9f1c48fe3585173f\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-09-22T04:09:49).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I136314f9596a025ca49ee135bba73f0b6b79130a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504600\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48654}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "89bdfe0de1bde9ee6b704e50ef9c72aec60a125c", "git_parents": ["1cc968202f98fb03ee0984e1feb82d9aefbc44bd"], "node": "5943584817bbcf9894ed7568eff2f050971b0f56", "parents": ["585f5e24bda4e2a171af50c1945dc6619aa218af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from acf66074c5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/acf66074c577664403f2f6b98ab38826cf18af52\n    Stop sending ECT(1) if the path drops the marking\n\n    A path can drop ECT(1) marked packets outright rather than bleach the\n    marking. Nothing recovers from that today: the receiver generates RFC\n    8888 feedback only for packets it receives, so no feedback arrives to\n    report the problem, ICE stays writable because STUN is Not-ECT, and no\n    route change is triggered. Media stops flowing for as long as the route\n    lasts.\n\n    Detect it in Ect1Policy by accumulating the time spent sending packets\n    with the marking while no feedback arrives, and fall back to Not-ECT\n    once that exceeds a timeout. Time when nothing was sent does not count,\n    and each gap between two sent packets contributes at most a fixed\n    amount, so that a pause cannot by itself trigger detection.\n\n    The timeout is short until an ECT(1) packet has been acknowledged on\n    the route, so that a path which drops them from the start is found\n    quickly. Afterwards it matches the ICE unwritable timeout, so that an\n    outage affecting all packets has made ICE look for another route before\n    the marking is blamed for it.\n\n    Unlike bleaching, which feedback reports directly, this is inferred\n    from the absence of feedback and can be wrong, for instance if the\n    round trip time exceeds the timeout used before the first\n    acknowledgement. Sending ECT(1) is therefore retried once per route,\n    10s after the path was judged to drop the marking.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225697\n    Change-Id: I8f8cedb88b832289cb894a24305fc6964e7154f8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504060\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48655}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_types.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_types.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/rtp_transport_controller_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/ect1_policy_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0122.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/l4s_test.cc"], "git_node": "801142d6a4b77cf6bad12537dfbf64122a5c98cb", "git_parents": ["89bdfe0de1bde9ee6b704e50ef9c72aec60a125c"], "node": "83d8ea1d77f6af9709cd670d77760db51d407284", "parents": ["5943584817bbcf9894ed7568eff2f050971b0f56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from a3553f1c82\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a3553f1c82a5580c91ad1f82baab4b11ed4b34b6\n    [dcsctp] Immediately send outstanding data after handover\n\n    During handover, in-flight chunks are correctly marked as\n    is_to_be_retransmitted = true so they don't stall waiting\n    for ACKs on the old connection. However, SendBufferedPackets\n    was missing on resumption, causing the socket to idle until the\n    T3-RTX timer naturally expired (1000ms by default) to flush\n    the queue.\n\n    This adds the missing explicitly flush and verifies it with a\n    regression test against the stall.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:477364365\n    Change-Id: I47bd79e929c96d624e17be42db65ea920309fb09\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504100\n    Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Priya Rajarathinam \u003crajarathinam@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48656}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_test.cc"], "git_node": "40964cadbb5988ed7a32dafe75ffadb215b86ed1", "git_parents": ["801142d6a4b77cf6bad12537dfbf64122a5c98cb"], "node": "215a35fea783c25a1420d413349effa148d9901a", "parents": ["83d8ea1d77f6af9709cd670d77760db51d407284"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 767dd4d831\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/767dd4d83168d99f65a323b4602e343d7db35935\n    dtls-in-stun: skip sped/pqc tests when not built with BoringSSL\n\n    DTLS-in-STUN and PQC are only available with BoringSSL, but a number of\n    tests assert that piggybacking happens whenever the configuration asks\n    for it, or that a HelloRetryRequest produces a second ClientHello. Those\n    fail in OpenSSL builds. Skip the affected parameter combinations,\n    leaving the ones that assert the absence of piggybacking running.\n\n    Base::TearDown() dereferenced a null TimeController for a test that\n    skipped before reaching Prepare(), which crashed the test binary and\n    hid every test after it.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:367395350\n    Change-Id: I317de25a4f32507c58293ba58c095194930787e5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/496780\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48657}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/transport_description_factory_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_ice_integration_fixture.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_ice_integration_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "64bb53a317af9aa101ed8e544c23596bd142aa56", "git_parents": ["40964cadbb5988ed7a32dafe75ffadb215b86ed1"], "node": "1eb951799d154e2ea94224eda6e94eeb1e2ded9f", "parents": ["215a35fea783c25a1420d413349effa148d9901a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from f24ae71bc7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f24ae71bc72894d16ef4b85900f872240c76aa0d\n    Add model load latency metric for ML residual echo estimation\n\n    This metric is only reported if the model finishes loading. A different metric will track init results / failures.\n\n    Metric XML declaration: http://crrev.com/c/8367289\n\n    Tested: logs as expected in Chrome with/without --enable-features=WebRtcNeuralResidualEchoEstimationAsyncInit\n    No-Iwyu: Manually vetted the tflite includes. IWYU has problems with them.\n    Bug: chromium:553120507\n    Change-Id: I03b4ce5dd425a60814050cd265e573e42cbb6b23\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/501160\n    Commit-Queue: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48658}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio/neural_residual_echo_estimator_creator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d896c05179ddca9008c821871ebeb777f2ee4bda", "git_parents": ["64bb53a317af9aa101ed8e544c23596bd142aa56"], "node": "99b93688cb1ebe8724d1efa27fa8a1a2fc8230fe", "parents": ["1eb951799d154e2ea94224eda6e94eeb1e2ded9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from aa0877a5b5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/aa0877a5b5bbf9db42892ab22c1df0fdf6a540ed\n    Per temporal layer rate control in the V2 libaom AV1 encoder.\n\n    The encoder reported every frame as belonging to temporal layer 0, so\n    libaom ran a single rate control context for the whole stream and sized\n    every frame against the same budget regardless of how the bitrate was\n    distributed across the layers. The per frame budget was communicated by\n    scaling the frame duration, which left the duration meaning something\n    other than the interval between frames.\n\n    Signal the real temporal id instead, declare the layer configuration to\n    libaom, and derive the cumulative layer bitrates and frame rate factors\n    it expects via the new TemporalLayerRateTracker. Cbr::duration is now\n    passed through verbatim, and the meaning of both Cbr fields is spelled\n    out in video_encoder_interface.h.\n\n    The existing rate control tests are adjusted to allow the total to\n    overshoot by what the keyframes were actually allowed, which the\n    microsecond precision duration no longer leaves room for.\n\n    This is a precursor to\n    https://webrtc-review.git.corp.google.com/c/src/+/503780\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: Ic9183a9757d624293148ec28af0b6adfcd0f2e1c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504280\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48659}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch"], "git_node": "402962aa1507cd06fa55a6ebcaa573d3ef0cf9e2", "git_parents": ["d896c05179ddca9008c821871ebeb777f2ee4bda"], "node": "0a3e25fd7d6b0508d672738eea57dfb704da48cd", "parents": ["99b93688cb1ebe8724d1efa27fa8a1a2fc8230fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from aa0877a5b5 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_coding_utility_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "babd367b115f515c11050ed02fb476edb1bc0226", "git_parents": ["402962aa1507cd06fa55a6ebcaa573d3ef0cf9e2"], "node": "dab2e681af7a3675099083a8a61efefcb05ba7da", "parents": ["0a3e25fd7d6b0508d672738eea57dfb704da48cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 95fceffacb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/95fceffacbb80bf0d781177d40892bbbc6f5425f\n    Detach senders from their send stream on rollback\n\n    Rolling back a local description deletes the channels that the rolled\n    back description created, but the senders kept the ssrc that the\n    description gave them. A sender left in that state refers to a send\n    stream that no longer exists: applying a later description that disables\n    a simulcast layer goes through the media channel instead of the sender's\n    pre-negotiation state, fails with an empty error, and\n    SetLocalDescription() reports \"Failed updating status for simulcast\n    layers.\"\n\n    Detach the senders as part of the rollback, before the channels are\n    deleted, so that they return to the un-negotiated state. The encodings\n    the application configured are restored after the batched teardown tasks\n    have run, since detaching a sender clears them.\n\n    Fixed: chromium:562462476\n    Change-Id: I548c5444255f5fcb6e7d2a3519979f6b8510b822\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503880\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48660}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_simulcast_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "b70ba60e6ea80b218be396b54ed16b8a34fe894c", "git_parents": ["babd367b115f515c11050ed02fb476edb1bc0226"], "node": "a58f81489672ef78cc060309ee2485a5d88bb242", "parents": ["dab2e681af7a3675099083a8a61efefcb05ba7da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 63f7a75c2b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/63f7a75c2b8d08cddefb9ecc1d6c8f40fd002fa8\n    Set export_linear_aec_output on multichannel AEC config\n\n    When linear AEC output export is enabled via the `--linear_aec_output` flag,\n    `export_linear_aec_output` was previously only enabled on the mono\n    `EchoCanceller3Config`, leaving the builder's multichannel config unset.\n    This caused config compatibility validation in `ConfigSelector` to fail.\n    This CL ensures `export_linear_aec_output` is also enabled on\n    `echo_canceller_multichannel_config` when present.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42230301\n    Change-Id: I7e4f42089e2862b56e7ca070e94c96dd786d8b78\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504741\n    Reviewed-by: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48661}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audioproc_float_impl.cc"], "git_node": "4efc710db37e742f19a6ad7ff052b613dbd15a97", "git_parents": ["b70ba60e6ea80b218be396b54ed16b8a34fe894c"], "node": "19554b9782aa0e1b072c836bfda3311c0d94bcfb", "parents": ["a58f81489672ef78cc060309ee2485a5d88bb242"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from bbc2085d45\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bbc2085d45083ee75786b50bf23d86df20a80050\n    Inject test adaptation resources at construction\n\n    InjectAdaptationConstraint() blocked the worker thread on a task\n    posted to the encoder queue, and had an early return that never set\n    the event it was waited on, so a stopped encoder would have hung the\n    caller forever. Both it and InjectAdaptationResource() existed only\n    for VideoStreamEncoderTest, which calls them from its constructor.\n\n    Pass the resources and constraints to the constructor instead and\n    register them in the init task it already posts. Nothing blocks, and\n    the ordering is stronger than before: the injections used to race\n    that task and worked only because both landed on the same queue in\n    order.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I112df0d254dff6328409b9be71bc92e12a8fa7bf\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504421\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48662}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "cda470f1f94360935b2e8ab1a1cea05f3f1edb54", "git_parents": ["4efc710db37e742f19a6ad7ff052b613dbd15a97"], "node": "73f8438906354c70cb6cea0e198c1527e9c84b0a", "parents": ["19554b9782aa0e1b072c836bfda3311c0d94bcfb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8e46acc347\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8e46acc347de8ea6c23bc6b1da6ca9ab782e41c4\n    Add initialization outcome metric for ML residual echo estimation\n\n    See XML declaration for definition: http://crrev.com/c/8367289\n\n    Tested: logs as expected in Chrome with/without --enable-features=WebRtcNeuralResidualEchoEstimationAsyncInit\n    No-Iwyu: Manually vetted the tflite includes. IWYU has problems with them.\n    Bug: chromium:553120507\n    Change-Id: Id9322558e91318035a884235aa08b5141ec46f42\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503220\n    Reviewed-by: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48663}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/neural_residual_echo_estimator/neural_residual_echo_estimator_impl_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "5ee8335e499a6414b23933b14b17ca7459818cff", "git_parents": ["cda470f1f94360935b2e8ab1a1cea05f3f1edb54"], "node": "c174f4d9d1cc663f79fd1d01465cbe5fcc36e17e", "parents": ["73f8438906354c70cb6cea0e198c1527e9c84b0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from a98a2e872a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a98a2e872a26bc365ed9bb0e5f67b48ddd469c3e\n    Align AEC flag handling with other APM config flags\n\n    Align the AEC flag handling pattern in AudioProcessingSimulator with the rest of the config flags. This allows `--aec=0` to properly override and disable AEC in configs where it was previously enabled.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42230301\n    Change-Id: Ia8525044b0ec24e6ef215334cd1830c9cdbfe50b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504740\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48664}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/test/audio_processing_simulator.cc"], "git_node": "ddacb521d3d5ec768a05784c20a9db197ec8b471", "git_parents": ["5ee8335e499a6414b23933b14b17ca7459818cff"], "node": "32c7e76c354716f4e0a4ae5ec75823806d2116bc", "parents": ["c174f4d9d1cc663f79fd1d01465cbe5fcc36e17e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 57b98b1c1e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/57b98b1c1e405f017aada77b1b0ca61c9b3f31e2\n    sdk: Stop using a distinct worker thread\n\n    The Android and Objective-C SDKs each created a dedicated worker thread\n    and supplied it through\n    PeerConnectionFactoryDependencies::worker_thread. Support for a worker\n    thread that is separate from the network thread is being removed from\n    WebRTC, so the network thread now serves both roles.\n\n    - The Android and Objective-C peer connection factories no longer create\n      a worker thread.\n    - OwnedFactoryAndThreads::worker_thread() falls back to the network\n      thread when no separate worker thread is owned, so that the existing\n      JNI entry points keep working for embedders that still supply one.\n    - RTCPeerConnectionFactory's workerThread property returns the network\n      thread.\n    - The native API sample applications and the Android native unit test\n      stop supplying a worker thread as well.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558821261\n    Change-Id: Ibbf08b80e6e40d7602e84bc006303910222d5131\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/502860\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48665}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/androidnativeapi/jni/android_call_client.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/androidnativeapi/jni/android_call_client.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/objcnativeapi/objc/objc_call_client.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/objcnativeapi/objc/objc_call_client.mm", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCPeerConnectionFactory.mm"], "git_node": "15c83fa0b4143331d8e0935e816dd05d5844ac08", "git_parents": ["ddacb521d3d5ec768a05784c20a9db197ec8b471"], "node": "336b17d920ccc34e3ff6b62bf36ea3118630dc5d", "parents": ["32c7e76c354716f4e0a4ae5ec75823806d2116bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8bea72f030\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8bea72f030f26e2633c15b343f79a163fbb21fe4\n    Add init readiness metric for ML residual echo estimation\n\n    This metric measures the actual impact of delayed initialization of ML-REE, since estimator initialization delay only affects processing if the model is needed (i.e., if AEC3 has left nonlinear mode).\n\n    See XML declaration for definition: http://crrev.com/c/8367289\n\n    Tested: logs as expected in Chrome with/without --enable-features=WebRtcNeuralResidualEchoEstimationAsyncInit\n    No-Iwyu: Manually vetted the tflite includes. IWYU has problems with them.\n    Bug: chromium:553120507\n    Change-Id: Ib0350aa58fa47ccf06eed6dcf174ee94f0aefeb3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/503240\n    Reviewed-by: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sam Zackrisson \u003csaza@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48666}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/residual_echo_estimator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/residual_echo_estimator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/residual_echo_estimator_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "3722b5037dc93bea7dc4c11d26c0c3fedc9280e4", "git_parents": ["15c83fa0b4143331d8e0935e816dd05d5844ac08"], "node": "36a0c68b85eb390608cff99a01078368a2dd7e6a", "parents": ["336b17d920ccc34e3ff6b62bf36ea3118630dc5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1e70146f6e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1e70146f6e75b3867a4fb2f1aac74941eff8c2c7\n    Protect Android DtmfSender and TimestampAligner against UAF.\n\n    Adopt NativeLifecycleLock in DtmfSender and TimestampAligner to prevent\n    Use-After-Free and double-free race conditions when JNI methods\n    (canInsertDtmf, insertDtmf, tones, duration, interToneGap,\n    translateTimestamp) execute concurrently with dispose().\n\n    Bug: b/533453798\n    Change-Id: I0f4530810e16cecebcd1c914a833d5d5116a4a0f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504700\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48667}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/DtmfSender.java", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/TimestampAligner.java"], "git_node": "968625276c76f24511cdaf29734de0fe8240c44a", "git_parents": ["3722b5037dc93bea7dc4c11d26c0c3fedc9280e4"], "node": "587d02b63096f7bc094698b12e0974b3b6c0030a", "parents": ["36a0c68b85eb390608cff99a01078368a2dd7e6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7a951d8562\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7a951d8562a80b15039b874411f10c3f05b33995\n    Allocate RejectsHugeSize payload on the heap.\n\n    A 40 MB automatic array overflows the stack on platforms with a small stack limit, e.g. 32-bit Android.\n\n    Change-Id: Iff47dbf5e67dd77bc739f3200dfc7361edf8608b\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504760\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48668}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_format_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "6dba42c9fe5beb3a37cf4e6017a004ae96fe26dd", "git_parents": ["968625276c76f24511cdaf29734de0fe8240c44a"], "node": "df10858b80218a40686f3299a82e4c94e47560f1", "parents": ["587d02b63096f7bc094698b12e0974b3b6c0030a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from dfb97f00e3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dfb97f00e38c0bbb5f1abb9aead36e19e533b7f0\n    Avoid port collisions in AppRTC Robolectric JUnit tests\n\n    Robolectric test shards for different simulated Android SDK versions\n    (e.g. SDK 29 and SDK 36) run concurrently on the same host and\n    previously collided on hardcoded port 8888 between DirectRTCClientTest\n    and TCPChannelClientTest.\n\n    Offset the test ports by Build.VERSION.SDK_INT using distinct base\n    ports (8888 + SDK_INT and 9000 + SDK_INT) so concurrent shards never\n    bind the same TCP port.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I5fa6dac067e7d3271d90037e2942ab6b28f67917\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504680\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48669}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/exa