   * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/783a0d437a..7248d54374\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/6f55acdade..9f68173f2d\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/e7b072867d..b2bd7f8240\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/7ccadeaefc..55a39e603b\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/8c6b5162b5..ab4f7316dc\n    * src/third_party/fuzztest/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/fuzztest.git/+log/853cda93a7..a8861f3aa7\n    * src/third_party/google-truth/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/truth.git/+log/a5594857f5..838b9b3ed5\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/d2dc893f59..0d1b416b09\n    * src/third_party/libyuv: https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv.git/+log/749f9742bb..7c85a3a082\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/a11b920092..a169eadb01\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/aac4c25edf..388d17a921\n    * src/third_party/turbine/cipd: 962n3CvRk8aEByuyx7pFpfeVdQlbk9Y2IsmKDNTddasC..rqbGMhci4trzUCXgMBzoRMpTKADs_F5sWUKJXxsu6BYC\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/c60db23beb..c70ca011dd\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/971f8da90a..daa394365f/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I8e4ca20578a7475dab1cb16f67f79f7f5d3ab68f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504960\n    Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48681}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "c1091d2975425f53d604e2fdf07544536a5ce96f", "git_parents": ["7205004c64d2ecfb6ccb2a807fbda0a4d3d01a8e"], "node": "002b186b7a9e82ffeab1b69a0871dcac3a6870d8", "parents": ["07e14a4b7768fcea15c883a4bf827fb892256387"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from fe73be2bbf\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fe73be2bbfc491176d546b377045c9b7cf12971d\n    Remove the usage of OPUS_FIXED_POINT macro.\n\n    As mentioned in third_party/opus/src/include/opus_defines.h:\n\n    * Applications may look for the substring \"-fixed\" in the version string to determine whether they have a fixed-point or floating-point\n\n    Change-Id: Ie5dfbd4a4915f4e8aac1e039c813596a7199aaf7\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504940\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48682}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/codecs/opus/opus_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "7635920cfffa87345cad6dbc1dc21d838bc25eba", "git_parents": ["c1091d2975425f53d604e2fdf07544536a5ce96f"], "node": "5c967e5c9f60cd70662f78921352de6bb6a2c375", "parents": ["002b186b7a9e82ffeab1b69a0871dcac3a6870d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from f07112862d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f07112862d1461c1a0f7d9f3ae5f5bbcb13d03a3\n    Clear local address in TURN candidate error for non-UDP servers\n\n    TurnPort::OnAllocateError clears the local address and port from the\n    candidate error event when the TURN server is at a private IP, but only\n    when the transport is PROTO_TCP. Non-UDP transports such as PROTO_TLS\n    and PROTO_DTLS share the same connection error handling path but were\n    omitted from the check.\n\n    Match the != PROTO_UDP pattern used by TurnPort::Close() so all non-UDP\n    transports are handled uniformly. Add unit and integration tests for\n    candidate error events with TCP and TLS transports against private and\n    public server addresses.\n\n    Fixed: webrtc:513452928\n    Change-Id: Ic6b92f309de87ed3fd7f09a5b34383fbb12419bb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505000\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48683}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "05d853e21a9b77130c121fbf385a2ea77be0c314", "git_parents": ["7635920cfffa87345cad6dbc1dc21d838bc25eba"], "node": "fcb7efb85a6e6d63935ef3d05b68d33ccbfa295a", "parents": ["5c967e5c9f60cd70662f78921352de6bb6a2c375"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from c070462526\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c0704625261d9de9e73928c9c223b73ff0739476\n    Support releasing unused payload types in PayloadTypePicker\n\n    PayloadTypePicker reserves a payload type the moment it suggests one and\n    never releases it again. Payload types are suggested for every codec the\n    media engine supports, well before codec preferences and the codecs that\n    an application actually offers have been taken into account, so the\n    reserved set grows far beyond what any session description contains. A\n    peer that renegotiates often, or that supports many codecs, runs out of\n    the 61 dynamic payload types and createOffer() starts failing with\n    RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED.\n\n    Introduce core support in call/ for tracking active recorders and\n    reclaiming unused payload types:\n\n    - Let PayloadTypePicker keep track of the recorders that are alive, and\n      add ReleaseUnusedPayloadTypes() to rebuild the reserved set from the\n      payload types those recorders map, plus the well known assignments\n      that the constructor seeds.\n    - Add PayloadTypeRecorder::RetainOnly() to drop the mappings that a\n      newly applied description does not use, and make the recorder\n      non-copyable now that it registers itself with the picker.\n    - Remove redundant `excluder` parameter from SuggestMapping() since all\n      registered recorders are now checked directly by PayloadTypePicker.\n    - Make PayloadTypeRecorder::AddMapping() report accepted redefinitions\n      to the picker, and make PayloadTypePicker::AddMapping() reserve the\n      payload type even when the mapping is already known.\n    - Keep the mapping history in PayloadTypePicker::entries_ untouched, so\n      that a codec still gets the payload type it had the last time around.\n\n    Bug: b/564522509, webrtc:360058654\n    Change-Id: Ib2ee6504b3a398c7d5a927b30557efc0f9127e7c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504620\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48684}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/fake_payload_type_suggester.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0135.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester.cc"], "git_node": "183c60cf336b2ba0e08c531e969b35f16248ad98", "git_parents": ["05d853e21a9b77130c121fbf385a2ea77be0c314"], "node": "76929d4011d035ba05f2ecd263bdb550e517fe37", "parents": ["fcb7efb85a6e6d63935ef3d05b68d33ccbfa295a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from e406e16546\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e406e165463dbbac5ebfacdf70067ba561ab3108\n    Reclaim payload types in SdpPayloadTypeSuggester\n\n    PayloadTypePicker now tracks live recorders and allows reclaiming unused\n    payload types via ReleaseUnusedPayloadTypes(). This CL integrates that\n    mechanism into SdpPayloadTypeSuggester during description updates:\n\n    - Scope DisallowRedefinition() across the entire session description\n      rather than per media section, ensuring codec redefinitions are\n      properly detected and rejected across bundled media sections.\n    - Retain only active payload types on each recorder based on the\n      description being applied, dropping unused or unnegotiated mappings.\n    - Prune stale recorders for media sections no longer in the description\n      or that have been rejected.\n    - Call ReleaseUnusedPayloadTypes() after updating recorders to make\n      unnegotiated dynamic payload types available for reassignment.\n    - Add unit and integration tests covering redefinition rejection across\n      bundled sections, dynamic payload type reclamation across repeated\n      renegotiations, and rollback behavior.\n\n    Bug: b/564522509, webrtc:360058654\n    Change-Id: I5914be2dd9d449e48a4b125ffaffbb8d8fa5cfce\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504780\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48685}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_media_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ed7c5581819bbba14657e129d26c6b11df0cdc06", "git_parents": ["183c60cf336b2ba0e08c531e969b35f16248ad98"], "node": "034ea2a561ce54d2ddec0fcd87d1725d6585e88c", "parents": ["76929d4011d035ba05f2ecd263bdb550e517fe37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6db7708ce3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6db7708ce3b7b7adb5c552a9d6d396ac2cc6a741\n    Roll chromium_revision daa394365f..a8c1f6d63d (1702789:1703232)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/daa394365f..a8c1f6d63d\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/daa394365f..a8c1f6d63d\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * fuchsia_version: version:33.20260915.5.1..version:33.20260922.5.1\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/5df2171a1f..85497c09eb\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/7248d54374..b43a6b1ad7\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/9f68173f2d..3a69c1ea9c\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/b2bd7f8240..4b4b0b498e\n    * src/third_party/androidx/cipd: 8Yjj73bTq_VrrX2nPOPLnOsY_HetcOeEJ5C6-yhIyx8C..2dsEI33MPTAv4FzDyj8iDpa9PQ_Us0xrMiuFFMyJAT0C\n    * src/third_party/boringssl/src: https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl.git/+log/81913f592d..62fb8ab5bd\n    * src/third_party/compiler-rt/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/compiler-rt.git/+log/bd6a08e0a4..7dc7227733\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/55a39e603b..db1dc923aa\n    * src/third_party/eigen3/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen.git/+log/ab4f7316dc..ec8593a7db\n    * src/third_party/fuzztest/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/fuzztest.git/+log/a8861f3aa7..487de66b54\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/0d1b416b09..eef57557d7\n    * src/third_party/libc++abi/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libcxxabi.git/+log/92767730c5..08130b4e4f\n    * src/third_party/libunwind/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libunwind.git/+log/24a407d535..0f1248103c\n    * src/third_party/libyuv: https://chromium.googlesource.com/libyuv/libyuv.git/+log/7c85a3a082..a09d909f63\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/388d17a921..99234d73fe\n    * src/third_party/tflite/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow.git/+log/a757345c62..cbec5fc4f1\n    * src/third_party/xnnpack/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/XNNPACK.git/+log/0c9f46a16e..ced54bb986\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/c70ca011dd..2854c9599b\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/daa394365f..a8c1f6d63d/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Ie7ab0c5efc4f8b5447e5ee719f6399ef4901b48a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505100\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48686}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "eb54a972bf9dc505754bc5533d11867c356b13f6", "git_parents": ["ed7c5581819bbba14657e129d26c6b11df0cdc06"], "node": "5bf90eae5e61e44c562286340ee303d1eecd32a6", "parents": ["034ea2a561ce54d2ddec0fcd87d1725d6585e88c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 63b4356a0e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/63b4356a0ed7385943f153dd01025208b0fce03b\n    Only assign payload types to codecs that can be offered\n\n    When creating an offer, CodecVendor assigns a payload type to every\n    codec in both the send and the receive list of the media engine, and\n    only afterwards narrows the list down to the codecs that the direction\n    of the media section allows. The codecs that are dropped keep their\n    payload type for the rest of the session, which on an endpoint with a\n    large codec matrix uses up a good part of the 61 dynamic payload types\n    for codecs that are never put on the wire.\n\n    Compute the list of codecs that the media section can offer before\n    assigning payload types, and skip the codecs that are not on it. The\n    send and receive lists are still walked in the same order, so the\n    payload types that the remaining codecs are given do not change.\n\n    Bug: b/564522509, webrtc:360058654\n    Change-Id: Ia70f79f6ec5bc63b916cabaea387c2522b13ed50\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504640\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48687}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "14b5cbc1832b4dd93064cb63e60a99296d9df3fa", "git_parents": ["eb54a972bf9dc505754bc5533d11867c356b13f6"], "node": "06c13b8bf7f2c5448cefbb635ae2ba2c1d66594c", "parents": ["5bf90eae5e61e44c562286340ee303d1eecd32a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from d2c54326b9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d2c54326b9746e4d48036c374f76f977020b896c\n    Replace ABSL_DEPRECATED with [[deprecated]]\n\n    ABSL_DEPRECATED is deprecated, see\n    https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/commit/f573cfba0bd0de72949cf32f31be544adf09e683\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I373c51b1b2d69ef694f9a0bb191882cbe2561a4a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504883\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48688}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/audio_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/dtls_transport_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/rtp_transceiver_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/network_types.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/logging/rtc_event_log/events/rtc_event_log_parse_status.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/include/aec_dump.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/pacing_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/public/dcsctp_socket.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.h"], "git_node": "a6545d0915764f41f52fe3e7dc0f8a88353a258f", "git_parents": ["14b5cbc1832b4dd93064cb63e60a99296d9df3fa"], "node": "7d6f9c8341fb79ba202419e39e749dfdf791ed83", "parents": ["06c13b8bf7f2c5448cefbb635ae2ba2c1d66594c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5f44d6e048\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5f44d6e0484f47ffc38178ece08348ca6c2caeb0\n    Remove unused payload type recorder transaction support\n\n    PayloadTypeRecorder and RtpHeaderExtensionRecorder both keep a\n    checkpoint copy of their mapping table so that a negotiation can be\n    rolled back, but nothing outside of the unit tests ever uses it. SDP\n    rollback goes through BundleManager, and the recorders are rebuilt from\n    the session description that was applied, so the checkpoints only cost\n    one duplicate map per recorder, of which there are two per bundle group.\n\n    - Drop PayloadTypeRecorder::Commit(), Rollback() and the checkpoint map,\n      together with the test that covered them.\n    - Drop RtpHeaderExtensionRecorder::Commit(), Rollback() and its\n      checkpoint map. Commit() had a caller, but no one ever read back what\n      it stored, so SdpPayloadTypeSuggester::RecordRtpHeaderExtensions() no\n      longer needs to know the SDP type.\n    - Drop PayloadTypeRecorder::GetMappings(), which has no callers.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:360058654\n    Change-Id: Ie6985a145287f5050370c38462c650fe22c95dae\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504660\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48689}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0135.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_payload_type_suggester.h"], "git_node": "31007baf1d00e605016757a23b5bf11f52cf0d86", "git_parents": ["a6545d0915764f41f52fe3e7dc0f8a88353a258f"], "node": "56950b19b294896ba3f556febcaa1bbe9cd2873f", "parents": ["7d6f9c8341fb79ba202419e39e749dfdf791ed83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from b8f901d4ff\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b8f901d4ff76a9f3dda09c8cee87be032b1b301f\n    Remove modules_tests.\n\n    Distinction between modules_unittests and modules_tests does not make sense anymore.\n\n    The tests are migrated to other rtc_test_suites.\n\n    Change-Id: I0fda6c6b50fc080bc0207ea85a4be952cca593ec\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504882\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48690}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/client.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/gn_isolate_map.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/test_suites.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/tryserver.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/resources/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "3df266e9c2cd9d42d357c4a8c232a2044dc984aa", "git_parents": ["31007baf1d00e605016757a23b5bf11f52cf0d86"], "node": "cff72b03903ea2d433437f033b8513a30a06fe3e", "parents": ["56950b19b294896ba3f556febcaa1bbe9cd2873f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5bb14da06e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5bb14da06e6e59db739f7790f4c74cf601598c83\n    Remove fallback code for when thread_local is not available\n\n    thread_local should be available for all platforms WebRTC supports\n\n    ABSL_HAVE_THREAD_LOCAL macro doesn't enable thread_local only for xtensa cpus that WebRTC doesn't support.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I089601fd823fdf2be7cc3d650bb12a666d96b09f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/487820\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48691}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/task_queue/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/task_queue/task_queue_base.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/allocation_counter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/synchronization/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/synchronization/yield_policy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/objc/components/audio/RTCAudioSession.mm"], "git_node": "c7cac7fb25260e26abea2039281bd017a8751131", "git_parents": ["3df266e9c2cd9d42d357c4a8c232a2044dc984aa"], "node": "3f77c6d172d140a17c391844b929f8c69c729caf", "parents": ["cff72b03903ea2d433437f033b8513a30a06fe3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 86ef7fa42d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/86ef7fa42dc3429bb4813aa98699c70ad570cac9\n    aec: fix wrong sentinel usage in echo metrics\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42233709\n    Change-Id: I7d8ad5a6ce72a1d4b259681445be4890e190820a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/498400\n    Reviewed-by: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Gustaf Ullberg \u003cgustaf@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48692}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/echo_remover_metrics.cc"], "git_node": "a405b906523e3416ca718084c34cf48fb5e9ed8e", "git_parents": ["c7cac7fb25260e26abea2039281bd017a8751131"], "node": "b1d66241cf40c2b057a50048a7d3aa3b9d961cca", "parents": ["3f77c6d172d140a17c391844b929f8c69c729caf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0bf80eadef\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0bf80eadef4a63664c8b292cdaae18cfc0d666c7\n    Cleanup usage of absl attributes\n\n    Most of these attributes are replaces with C++ keywords and C++ attributes.\n    Thus direct dependency on absl core_headers target can be reduced.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ib725c71cf2d3b2bb607e84cd9f17b1c2bd4bf9ac\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505140\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48693}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/voip/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/utility/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/logging/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_device/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/mac/sck_picker_handle.mm", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/pacing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0073.patch", "thir