-init-7747-g62397f8b-31.tar.xz,Win/clang-win-runtime-library-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-31.tar.xz,Win/clangd-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-31.tar.xz,Win/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-31.tar.xz,Win/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-31.tar.xz\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/12115cb265..e9603ed549\n    * src/third_party/r8/cipd: IftCs1-T5uV7FcoEpDBQyEzPJr0DguIcmwK2BrNjsMYC..w54n0EzIuf2nxIQEJKv3LqGFqg_hJ-HDBOAxQWcu46IC\n    * src/third_party/tflite/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow.git/+log/cbec5fc4f1..9edd58f895\n    * src/third_party/xnnpack/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/XNNPACK.git/+log/ced54bb986..b6d54fe945\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/155c581e13..54ea956b29\n    Removed dependencies\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/com_android_tools_common\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/com_android_tools_layoutlib_layoutlib_api\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/com_android_tools_sdk_common\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/com_squareup_javapoet\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/org_jetbrains_kotlin_kotlin_android_extensions_runtime\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/cipd/libs/org_jetbrains_kotlin_kotlin_parcelize_runtime\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/b8d3e2cdc8..80137986d5/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Id0412816000ee4ea5987e2d264d89f68e7d3c35b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505360\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48705}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "fa9e5df086f46f5572106c11924f05fae79801be", "git_parents": ["6db73f13ff6f088babe0ee0538458302089275e0"], "node": "8dfb095e66b5969494ef896ae9d3574760a93569", "parents": ["38c1fa2bcf25374e3cbcbd137c3b622f3f955e44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 05d6bc269c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/05d6bc269c816c7619be9d54e697c8c0b94599d5\n    Remove field-trial WebRTC-Aec3HighPassFilterEchoReference\n\n    Bug: webrtc:5298\n    Change-Id: I3e996cb42e465b9e2da768aa7088378cd8a78762\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505261\n    Reviewed-by: Jesus de Vicente Pena \u003cdevicentepena@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per \u00c5hgren \u003cpeah@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48706}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec3/echo_canceller3.cc"], "git_node": "7d94fa27a35c2163f9ce12307612f1506b8ac1b9", "git_parents": ["fa9e5df086f46f5572106c11924f05fae79801be"], "node": "b10c3a5f38710faad4b32da8fbe3012157b3152d", "parents": ["8dfb095e66b5969494ef896ae9d3574760a93569"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 65e9395a00\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/65e9395a000fac568737925a0d82096409d6b11d\n    Add temporal layer rate allocation tests for V2 VideoEncoderInterface.\n\n    Drives the encoders through L1T2, L1T3 and L1T4 patterns with\n    both a geometric and a linear bitrate distribution, and checks that each\n    temporal layer gets the share of the bitrate it was allocated, and that\n    the layers stay in the order their allocation implies.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: I3966f41de03fc18cc6b0b7068264b8be3681ce01\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/504781\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48707}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/temporal_layer_pattern_for_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/temporal_layer_pattern_for_test.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/temporal_layer_pattern_for_test_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "3564d762ffc8fdd5e3853290272139ee76353193", "git_parents": ["7d94fa27a35c2163f9ce12307612f1506b8ac1b9"], "node": "d9141a5528c5bc65c30d1e015e8f15a3b11b726b", "parents": ["b10c3a5f38710faad4b32da8fbe3012157b3152d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3f38d05039\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3f38d05039f1386ce129b45cafc244ce819005a8\n    Only assign payload types to answerable codecs\n\n    When creating an answer, CodecVendor assigns a payload type to every\n    codec in both the send and the receive list of the media engine, even\n    though the answer can only contain codecs that the offer, the direction\n    of the media section and the codec preferences allow. As on the offer\n    side, the codecs that are dropped keep their payload type for the rest\n    of the session, which uses up the dynamic payload type space for codecs\n    that are never put on the wire.\n\n    - Compute the codecs that the media section can answer with before\n      assigning payload types, and skip the codecs that are not on that\n      list. The list is built the same way as the list of offerable codecs:\n      the supported codecs for the direction, narrowed down by the codec\n      preferences, without comfort noise if the session has VAD disabled\n      and without RED codecs whose primary codecs are absent.\n    - Strip comfort noise codecs from the codecs that are given a payload\n      type when creating an offer as well, when the session has VAD\n      disabled.\n    - Pass the codec preferences and the VAD setting on to the payload type\n      assignment that works on codec configurations, so that the codecs\n      that the media section cannot use, and the RTX, RED, ULPFEC and\n      FlexFEC entries that the codec preferences do not ask for, are\n      skipped there as well.\n\n    The codecs that end up in the offer and the answer do not change, with\n    one exception: a RED codec whose primary codecs are not supported for\n    the direction of the media section is no longer offered or answered.\n\n    While here, reduce duplication between the offer and the answer path by\n    extracting helpers for looking up the codecs of a previously negotiated\n    media section, for intersecting the send and receive codec\n    configurations and for filtering codec configurations.\n\n    Bug: b/564522509, webrtc:360058654\n    Change-Id: Ic43a1ba512fee80960066a4fe36c4b10145c7f00\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505120\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Taylor Brandstetter \u003cdeadbeef@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48708}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/codec_vendor_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_media_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/full_codec_matrix.h"], "git_node": "24777a2878c1b5506cb18377d719e830ea65db70", "git_parents": ["3564d762ffc8fdd5e3853290272139ee76353193"], "node": "446d5bfb17b737565b6204a9fe0e9a7ac71f4997", "parents": ["d9141a5528c5bc65c30d1e015e8f15a3b11b726b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 77e812c8ad\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/77e812c8ade9433ccba3d0982a940f1c54941ac4\n    Propagate Sframe enablement from negotiation down to media channels\n\n    Wires the negotiated Sframe state from the transceiver through the pc/\n    layer into the media engines, so that once Sframe is agreed in SDP (the\n    a=sframe attribute), every send and receive media channel records that\n    Sframe encryption is required.\n\n    Flow:\n    - RtpTransceiver::ApplySframeEnabled() now calls channel-\u003eEnableSframe()\n      on the worker thread (previously a TODO placeholder) when Sframe was\n      negotiated.\n    - BaseChannel::EnableSframe() fans the call out to both the send and\n      receive media channels.\n    - Each media channel (voice/video, send/receive) stores\n      sframe_options_.required.\n\n    This CL deliberately stops at the media channel level. Carrying the\n    options onto the streams the channel creates, and hooking the actual\n    Sframe encryptor/decryptor into the RTP send/receive pipeline, are\n    follow-ups.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I400a0d9c652f0ddb78f10e6dbf322f0813b34c0e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/486880\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48709}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/sframe_options.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/media_channel.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/channel.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/channel.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/channel_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_channel_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_voice_media_receive_channel_interface.h"], "git_node": "1e7d1a6391616c8c73231c2ab92360a6fd2c53f1", "git_parents": ["24777a2878c1b5506cb18377d719e830ea65db70"], "node": "a063321093979c13400a06dd064a2d6463f30b19", "parents": ["446d5bfb17b737565b6204a9fe0e9a7ac71f4997"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 77e812c8ad - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/sframe_options_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz.build"], "git_node": "d6332c1916c8178a90130283eae0f140ef820ef9", "git_parents": ["1e7d1a6391616c8c73231c2ab92360a6fd2c53f1"], "node": "d64401dcb68e95bbf6964a7945da269d1e3ba577", "parents": ["a063321093979c13400a06dd064a2d6463f30b19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 730026375d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/730026375d12847826f86bfe7a31c556b79f4f6d\n    Add allow_sending flag to RtpPacketToSend.\n\n    This flag indicates whether a packet is allowed to be sent to the\n    network. Defaults to true. When set to false, the intent is that sending\n    of this packet to the network will be skipped. That logic will be added\n    in follow-up CLs.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:564720400\n    Change-Id: I966fe311beef55cf5d71bc59182759723fa10823\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505440\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48710}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packet_to_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packet_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch"], "git_node": "08f5895f4d6c7d5aede75e28d4cdd9612dff31e9", "git_parents": ["d6332c1916c8178a90130283eae0f140ef820ef9"], "node": "922f537c545ecbe1fd9a3e4347154214dd7b1543", "parents": ["d64401dcb68e95bbf6964a7945da269d1e3ba577"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077266 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4b8ea1350c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4b8ea1350cae15605b5aedf3086b491c3b8f1adc\n    Roll chromium_revision 80137986d5..c67a753d3c (1704109:1704261)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/80137986d5..c67a753d3c\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/80137986d5..c67a753d3c\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/968af5e6c5..2d1798e676\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/d7c3980a9f..b41450aa61\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+log/c542c3898c..af9cdcb167\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/5079f996a8..b71bc411fe\n    * src/third_party/android_build_tools/error_prone/cipd: HLl1c2Gry_NXi-iC0l0MVfQ7C-vumHJOs1-Qd35ghAEC..RGU_pYZ7wIDYsomPZurJEevS4IVfXFNvxf_2KIpV_40C\n    * src/third_party/android_deps/autorolled/cipd: cAIV9KhFHhVi86frHZTKiaGYkbGSn1bRoxYkD1NWyI4C..gDS_f-3foKUmcuifytnd9_t-5Jp8XmWll0MIbRY0CP4C\n    * src/third_party/androidx/cipd: 1k7M-khGB8Hv020Vpfh8eyIVwYjKN0wSzkHEkyLzRPgC..Xeu8AlvK0qfOypyiuDxFDtrPzC23MBIV78p1Qj72NFIC\n    * src/third_party/depot_tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git/+log/a5b1df38b3..91b9ca4db8\n    * src/third_party/grpc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/grpc/grpc.git/+log/e55859adca..d3d14cf725\n    * src/third_party/icu: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/deps/icu.git/+log/6ebb40c594..5aa5262071\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/cd4309f8c5..ffb2c561c3\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/e9603ed549..084ed71c4e\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/54ea956b29..696ac5c235\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/80137986d5..c67a753d3c/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Idf011b646abd395d7b621e56d21a10b4a9da6485\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/505480\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48711}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mo