": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058653 - Don't mark through ephemeron edges until their target's zone is in the required state r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330132\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Marking.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2058653.js"], "git_node": "a52b040d2697ccdc47f3c2abb53c72cc23da35bb", "git_parents": ["d97c7730c880a3d89a077baf98b8c94ffebd4eee"], "node": "28411b3f513a5ddc2bde321dbd9008cef350cf5b", "parents": ["c6eada363031417072e54e6a4223d029807fbccd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033204 - Update metadata for html/dom/render-blocking/remove-attr-style-keeps-blocking.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331589\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/render-blocking/remove-attr-style-keeps-blocking.html.ini"], "git_node": "b93c1464e79c569a4567d6be6b85764443154d84", "git_parents": ["a52b040d2697ccdc47f3c2abb53c72cc23da35bb"], "node": "a00f9413c5ffb90e7745e5e1aa16ef516c494890", "parents": ["28411b3f513a5ddc2bde321dbd9008cef350cf5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079246 - Ignore private members in jsdoc. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,search-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,jteow,reemhamz,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331587\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/MerinoClient.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TemporaryMerinoClientShim.sys.mjs", "docs/jsdoc-plugins/skip-private-members.mjs", "docs/jsdoc-plugins/skip-unnamed-members.mjs", "docs/jsdoc.json", "toolkit/components/search/SearchSuggestions.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "6afa3410d220f6c8d0079667bb79e08293a0f39a", "git_parents": ["b93c1464e79c569a4567d6be6b85764443154d84"], "node": "470c36e6df4f9686882c87392e87401f44b2072f", "parents": ["a00f9413c5ffb90e7745e5e1aa16ef516c494890"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073685 - Wrap value in TransformerAlgorithmsWrapper::TransformCallback r=mgaudet\n\nThis also saves per-implementation init of JSAPI.\n\nThis also changes CompressionStream, but it's not affected as it uses bindgen function that knows better how to deal with JS values.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328883\n", "files": ["dom/compression/BaseAlgorithms.cpp", "dom/compression/BaseAlgorithms.h", "dom/encoding/TextDecoderStream.cpp", "dom/encoding/TextEncoderStream.cpp", "dom/streams/TransformerCallbackHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/TransformerCallbackHelpers.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/encoding/streams/crashtests/from-cross-realm.html"], "git_node": "671c6f648c03a658fda1b089189f4e0d9122ef0c", "git_parents": ["6afa3410d220f6c8d0079667bb79e08293a0f39a"], "node": "22018e93ef47f0f4409a068b69f5ecefb9f6e425", "parents": ["470c36e6df4f9686882c87392e87401f44b2072f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074772 - Gate MOZ_SYSTEM_CONFIG_DIR on automation. r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330847\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/SpecialSystemDirectory.cpp"], "git_node": "645222b596c0b1d8ed6d907a37a782c56e492728", "git_parents": ["671c6f648c03a658fda1b089189f4e0d9122ef0c"], "node": "b7af110095afd37370c3299cc7e9c95e2189aa9d", "parents": ["22018e93ef47f0f4409a068b69f5ecefb9f6e425"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikolas Wipper \u003cnwipper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048600 - Link primary password to lockstore. r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson,simonf,akulyk,keeler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308276\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "security/lockstore/ProfileKek.cpp", "security/lockstore/ProfileKek.h", "security/lockstore/moz.build", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/changepassword.js", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/resetpassword.js", "toolkit/modules/ProfileKekPassword.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_ProfileKekPassword.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/preferences/changemp.js", "toolkit/mozapps/preferences/removemp.js", "toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp"], "git_node": "ad9a51e7878a65d976fab20f3f05356fb6df2b35", "git_parents": ["645222b596c0b1d8ed6d907a37a782c56e492728"], "node": "8f168bcc5e1d46fd96f2b8fef198e73ce1ce5f17", "parents": ["b7af110095afd37370c3299cc7e9c95e2189aa9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikolas Wipper \u003cnwipper@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048600 - Prompt to unlock the lockstore primary password at startup. r=simonf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308856\n", "files": ["security/lockstore/ProfileKek.cpp", "security/lockstore/ProfileKek.h", "security/lockstore/gtest/TestProfileKek.cpp", "security/lockstore/gtest/moz.build", "security/lockstore/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp"], "git_node": "97bd300c768dca5f478fc2159de925ead7f15e99", "git_parents": ["ad9a51e7878a65d976fab20f3f05356fb6df2b35"], "node": "df3b7e850204cb7c29a36f96c2ce9f9485951f0f", "parents": ["8f168bcc5e1d46fd96f2b8fef198e73ce1ce5f17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076827 - Record urlbar.bounce for engagements that load a page without picking a result. r=urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nThe engine search tells openSERP() it tracks a bounce, which sets initiatedByURLBar for its load; without it, URILoadingHelper triggers the bounce the moment the results page starts loading and discards it with no view time. The direct path no longer tracks an engagement it can't resolve a sap for, matching the message path; otherwise paste & go of a search term, which records the engagement before picking the parent's heuristic result, would have that pick trigger and discard the bounce just tracked.\n\nThe direct path also resolves a bounce's search mode at engagement time, as the message path does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331532\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_bounce.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_bounce_sap.js"], "git_node": "28b6e61d570c314befccd0d37a315abe3a88045f", "git_parents": ["97bd300c768dca5f478fc2159de925ead7f15e99"], "node": "ef2e2db6ec9a98bf00d0a23adc39f8579ee20a0f", "parents": ["df3b7e850204cb7c29a36f96c2ce9f9485951f0f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069403 - Track urlbar.bounce against the browser the result loads in. r=urlbar-reviewers,adw\n\nThe bounce is now stored before an earlier bounce for the same tab resolves, so the load finds it: on the direct path the load follows synchronously, and on the message path its message follows the bounce's. A trigger also takes the bounce out of the store before awaiting the view time, where it used to delete whatever was stored once the await returned, which could be a bounce tracked in the meantime.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331579\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/browser_glean_telemetry_bounce.js"], "git_node": "50a59cd5cedac95e739109b4f11fd89aa58800cc", "git_parents": ["28b6e61d570c314befccd0d37a315abe3a88045f"], "node": "2c57712b0d491b823af82e2576e8bfc28fbd5939", "parents": ["ef2e2db6ec9a98bf00d0a23adc39f8579ee20a0f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1980466 - Avoid skipping remaining media junit tests due to isolated content processes. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThese tests are currently skipped specifically when using isolated\ncontent processes due to historically crashing. Since 1988727 landed\nthey no longer crash, as the Java PDM is disabled when using isolated\ncontent processes. We can therefore remove these assumptions causing\nthem to be skipped.\n\nNote that these tests are also currently skipped for other reasons\n(not just when isolated content processes are enabled) which will\nremain the case. Bug 1988041 tracks them being re-enabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331995\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/MediaSessionTest.kt"], "git_node": "dd95d538519a75b166d0cf05f1f389c78ea3c70f", "git_parents": ["50a59cd5cedac95e739109b4f11fd89aa58800cc"], "node": "c7952592dd0253f40a1af68d36473f7628ce9b21", "parents": ["2c57712b0d491b823af82e2576e8bfc28fbd5939"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078551 - Annotate some nativePrinter orange.\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/monolithic-overflow-019-print.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/monolithic-overflow-032-print.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-page/page-background-002-print.html.ini"], "git_node": "30c8c283cd6972d4a1cf73a4d65fbd6f9f5a8b06", "git_parents": ["dd95d538519a75b166d0cf05f1f389c78ea3c70f"], "node": "59d0690757e88432bea3d8da7f762e599af24aa9", "parents": ["c7952592dd0253f40a1af68d36473f7628ce9b21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/.vpython3", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse_arm.S", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_bit_reverse_mips.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft_mips.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/complex_fft_tables.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/sqrt_of_one_minus_x_squared.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller/goog_cc_scream_network_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "53be171dd89709456e0121507c9857bd32a54dc5", "git_parents": ["30c8c283cd6972d4a1cf73a4d65fbd6f9f5a8b06", "098e537cc4338b343383540dd7e7907fece986b7"], "node": "1b3734315edc8c8861d94a0853db470c1671ca52", "parents": ["59d0690757e88432bea3d8da7f762e599af24aa9", "27184f7c44062f2fc7ed2907356782d20378fb14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1877510 - Add an access key to the bookmark panel's Save button. r=mak,fluent-reviewers,places-reviewers,flod\" for causing bc failures @ browser_bookmark_popup.js\n\nThis reverts commit d97c7730c880a3d89a077baf98b8c94ffebd4eee.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1877510 - Let Enter in the edit bookmark folder tree save the bookmark. r=mak,places-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 679598de6dfc2ce86a0000a7d63d2e0272cafc45.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/places/content/editBookmark.js", "browser/components/places/content/places-tree.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_addBookmarkForFrame.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_bookmark_popup.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl"], "git_node": "99dfbd65f56734abb66907f7f6b6698a094a44a5", "git_parents": ["53be171dd89709456e0121507c9857bd32a54dc5"], "node": "e57a5eb02f675d01f11b2c39e33f3fea60b58824", "parents": ["1b3734315edc8c8861d94a0853db470c1671ca52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1981768 - Log HSTS and HTTPS RR connection upgrades to the web console. r=valentin,necko-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\" for causing devtools failures at browser_source_map-cross-domain.js\n\nThis reverts commit 4aca506e89083cd6bc14345cb60312762ee45909.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_webconsole_filters.js", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/security/security.properties", "dom/security/test/https-only/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/https-only/browser_hsts_host.js", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_mock_https_rr.js"], "git_node": "49ccfc913051e4760236dce73f3b12975960d627", "git_parents": ["99dfbd65f56734abb66907f7f6b6698a094a44a5"], "node": "3ee64f94258deab4aa13067883882b298f024ec2", "parents": ["e57a5eb02f675d01f11b2c39e33f3fea60b58824"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078969 - Clean up some nsContentPermissionHelper.h includes. r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,gtk-reviewers,smaug,emilio,valentin\n\nOriginally, the patch for bug 1960577 had a PromptResult passed as an argument\nto HttpTransactionShell::Init(), which required adding a serializer for it.\nHowever, that was changed before landing and it appears to be unused.\nIncluding nsContentPermissionHelper.h in IPCMessageUtilsSpecializations.h\nmeans that changing the former requires a lot of rebuilding, so let's remove it.\n\nnsHttpTransaction.h also does not actually need the include.\n\nnsContentPermissionHelper.h includes nsIMutableArray.h, but it only needs\na forward declaration. Various places were bootlegging it via\nnsContentPermissionHelper.h that we need to fix.\n\nRemoteType is somehow bootlegging ResultVariant.h in a way that breaks\nin non-unified builds with my changes here.\n\nThe nsIArray includes are because those files are currently bootlegging\nthe header somehow in a way that still works, but I'm adding the includes\nto make it less fragile in the future.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331438\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentPermissionHelper.h", "dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/RemoteType.h", "ipc/glue/IPCMessageUtilsSpecializations.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h", "widget/cocoa/nsClipboard.mm", "widget/gtk/nsClipboard.cpp", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp"], "git_node": "6da3783cf5cd599356fd111bd32e20517e3eec0b", "git_parents": ["49ccfc913051e4760236dce73f3b12975960d627"], "node": "e7b7366ed03c6278a60b696a4d308bd2c7d57d85", "parents": ["3ee64f94258deab4aa13067883882b298f024ec2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Holger Benl \u003chbenl@evandor.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075253 - [webdriver-bidi] Add CapabilityResponseExtension to our vendor extensions CDDL. r=w