3cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080665 - Update PDF.js to e0b4f473cf6bc0aff8a35632c8ecec60776af543 r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332778\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.renderer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.css", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "1b700fd43347df606f217a0a5ad4e356712fd9de", "git_parents": ["9fd8198bec75b87bd8e106888444053ee8c920a0"], "node": "e1a9010d79849a3db9531b9ea6faba758d7b6f75", "parents": ["2f294f32527662974453c93cc7a6c46c71a78c9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080693 - Derive readback_rows_top_down from the surface origin. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe composition recorder reads the default framebuffer directly, so its rows\narrive top first whenever the surface has a top-left origin. Only ANGLE was\ndetected as such, by checking for a GLES context on Windows, so frames\nrecorded with SWGL, e.g. in headless mode, were flipped upside down.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332797\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs"], "git_node": "fc0776ded8ae4a029ef222852fbfceecffcfa3ca", "git_parents": ["1b700fd43347df606f217a0a5ad4e356712fd9de"], "node": "efa06a7aa2b04587908dcf4f3d3805f56eae6d1e", "parents": ["e1a9010d79849a3db9531b9ea6faba758d7b6f75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079674 - Make schema and ftl consistent for some Ent Policies. r=mkaply,fluent-reviewers,bolsson DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332376\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/policies/policies-descriptions.ftl"], "git_node": "90c4c55c4b4f2895e3d5cec75984e2fda314fb46", "git_parents": ["fc0776ded8ae4a029ef222852fbfceecffcfa3ca"], "node": "160f568b21d723b85fd1362127a1e2c5352bb895", "parents": ["efa06a7aa2b04587908dcf4f3d3805f56eae6d1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075175 - [remote] Disable parsing network security certificate for WebDriver BiDi r=webdriver-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,Sasha,bomsy\n\nAdds a flag in the DevTools NetworkObserver to optout from parsing security info.\nWe have an upcoming requirement from Playwright to add security details, we will\neither implement it as a dedicated command or a delayed step before sending the\nresponseCompleted event.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331918\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkObserver.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkResponseListener.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/browser/browser_networkobserver_security_info.js", "remote/shared/listeners/NetworkListener.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7e3eb0ce49a54f7ad9343cd6ef6c7b670288a280", "git_parents": ["90c4c55c4b4f2895e3d5cec75984e2fda314fb46"], "node": "ab942c8b88b313b1c8e3f3e0deb8026abab989c7", "parents": ["160f568b21d723b85fd1362127a1e2c5352bb895"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075175 - [devtools] Reorder and format private fields in NetworkObserver r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332335\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkObserver.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f7d6f1639a0417f6b7891a7e8088ffd62b1d0581", "git_parents": ["7e3eb0ce49a54f7ad9343cd6ef6c7b670288a280"], "node": "b53285461a5fc0c61675450e6853c227ff1d9bf2", "parents": ["ab942c8b88b313b1c8e3f3e0deb8026abab989c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Almeida \u003cjonalmeida942@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080377 - Make the search bar shortcuts fill the width so they are centered r=mcarare,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332649\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/focus/activity/ShortcutsTest.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/focus/activity/robots/HomeScreenRobot.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/focus/activity/robots/SearchRobot.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/searchsuggestions/ui/SearchOverlay.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/topsites/TopSites.kt"], "git_node": "b82066acf301b27fac4e0d9ed4f0a34993ef80e0", "git_parents": ["f7d6f1639a0417f6b7891a7e8088ffd62b1d0581"], "node": "4378053e1b9b4df7ebb12d62e2b24ae9442d04e8", "parents": ["b53285461a5fc0c61675450e6853c227ff1d9bf2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070584 - [customizable-menu] Show the back, forward, share, refresh, open in app, find in page, desktop site, translate page and summarize page buttons navigation items in custom tabs menu. r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331914\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BackMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserToolbarStoreBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/ForwardMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/ShareMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/applinks/OpenInFirefoxMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuConfigurations.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuItemProvidersFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuSectionConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuTarget.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/bookmarks/BookmarkMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BackMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/DesktopSiteMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/ForwardMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/ShareMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/applinks/OpenInFirefoxMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuItemProvidersFactoryTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuTargetTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/summarization/SummarizePageMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/translations/TranslationsMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "a755ab45f9b3df650d2458476425f745e8de4433", "git_parents": ["b82066acf301b27fac4e0d9ed4f0a34993ef80e0"], "node": "88304b53be1778c013961733150c0a8e91dfd3ad", "parents": ["4378053e1b9b4df7ebb12d62e2b24ae9442d04e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Davis Zeller-Pies \u003cDavis.pies1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080307 - [Wayland] Apply toplevel opaque region changes immediately. r=gtk-reviewers,stransky,emilio\n\nOn Wayland, gdk_window_set_opaque_region() is cached by GTK and only sent\nto the wl_surface when the GdkWindow repaints. Gecko draws into its own\nsubsurface, so the toplevel rarely repaints and its opaque region lags the\nsubsurface's, sometimes by seconds. While it is stale the compositor skips\ndrawing what's behind that area, which shows up as stale or black blocks on\ntransparent windows.\n\nSet the region on the toplevel wl_surface directly and commit it with\nForceToplevelCommit(), so it applies without repainting the window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332610\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "2dd0b125686c3aa348b94f3967e17cac6faf7acc", "git_parents": ["a755ab45f9b3df650d2458476425f745e8de4433"], "node": "0b7f3d862d7ea69f2326342dc67f03b66e94868b", "parents": ["88304b53be1778c013961733150c0a8e91dfd3ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076271 - Make sure executor outlives stream parser. r=smaug\n\nAlso stop the document load explicitly when canceling XHR.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331564\n", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestMainThread.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParser.cpp"], "git_node": "cc7a5b83a2d85a767c4f16dd61a23af8bcd080d8", "git_parents": ["2dd0b125686c3aa348b94f3967e17cac6faf7acc"], "node": "e5668f89e74f01935c2fd278bd92152780e78a69", "parents": ["0b7f3d862d7ea69f2326342dc67f03b66e94868b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080131 - Remove the live region from the built-in VPN menu item r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\n`IPProtectionMenuItem` set `liveRegion` on the row, so on every state change, TalkBack reads the whole content of the row, including the nested settings button (`On, VPN, Open VPN settings button, switch`).\n\nThe row already exposes its status through `stateDescription`, which Talkback announces when the row is focused and the status is updated. The live region has been removed so that toggling the row now only announces the new state (`On`, `Off`), like a standard switch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332366\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/IPProtectionMenuItem.kt"], "git_node": "f136161bf69ef2cfa3ffd2c214591014f56cf45f", "git_parents": ["cc7a5b83a2d85a767c4f16dd61a23af8bcd080d8"], "node": "8260d160650e1593d475e597c69c237242491e3d", "parents": ["e5668f89e74f01935c2fd278bd92152780e78a69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079711 - Rename the mach vendor rust license whitelists to allowlists r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332099\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/vendor_rust.py"], "git_node": "dd015892d9dbde3ecce047affb04c7eb3811ceec", "git_parents": ["f136161bf69ef2cfa3ffd2c214591014f56cf45f"], "node": "c51d24bf6d3db49d444b4a0562015b891eb0a380", "parents": ["8260d160650e1593d475e597c69c237242491e3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079711 - Remove the stale mach crate from the mach vendor rust license allowlist r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nOnly mach2 is vendored now, and it is accepted under MIT or Apache-2.0 without being named.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332100\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/vendor_rust.py"], "git_node": "b8b61486a9d1ec8b2ed206b2ce7a9889523c5319", "git_parents": ["dd015892d9dbde3ecce047affb04c7eb3811ceec"], "node": "5f9b2cefbf7469041c0fac0ccb338b57a49828b4", "parents": ["c51d24bf6d3db49d444b4a0562015b891eb0a380"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079710 - Make mach vendor rust require an about:license notice for crates allowed only by name r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nCrates in RUNTIME_LICENSE_PACKAGE_ALLOWLIST are accepted under a license that needs a notice on about:license, but nothing checked one exists. The moz.build files are read from their syntax trees, as mach vendor rust has no configured tree, so every branch counts and non-literal values count as uncovered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332101\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/licenses.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_license_collection.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_licenses.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/vendor_rust.py"], "git_node": "afe8057f76387492b4b5fe0cbf500faef5c3dd4e", "git_parents": ["b8b61486a9d1ec8b2ed206b2ce7a9889523c5319"], "node": "c225c3073e5a83528c08ed3f2edef2d6ec3d6fee", "parents": ["5f9b2cefbf7469041c0fac0ccb338b57a49828b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025386 - Replace per-instance weak memory reporters with a strong singleton. r=nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328759\n", "files": ["dom/file/BlobImpl.h", "dom/file/BlobMemoryReporter.cpp", "dom/file/BlobMemoryReporter.h", "dom/file/StreamBlobImpl.cpp", "dom/file/StreamBlobImpl.h", "dom/file/StringBlobImpl.cpp", "dom/file/StringBlobImpl.h", "dom/file/moz.build"], "git_node": "a4f6917449ad418ee89c9e959ca9284771baac34", "git_parents": ["afe8057f76387492b4b5fe0cbf500faef5c3dd4e"], "node": "79f854b6a094eb1005fb309e7312af0051a216c6", "parents": ["c225c3073e5a83528c08ed3f2edef2d6ec3d6fee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079097: Make the crash helper log under MOZ_APP_DATA. r=crashreporting-reviewers,gsvelto\n\nOn macOS 27, a build that isn't signed by Mozilla shows a \"Data Access Blocked\" notification when the crash helper writes its log into ~/Library/Application Support/Firefox, even with MOZ_APP_DATA pointing elsewhere. On Unix, the crash helper now uses MOZ_APP_DATA the way the main process does. Windows keeps the default location, since nsLocalFile's Windows path rules aren't replicated here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332262\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/logging/env.rs"], "git_node": "d404426a7ae292340da9829305fe00ce470a7d0e", "git_parents": ["a4f6917449ad418ee89c9e959ca9284771baac34"], "node": "ec577969c934360ea95d9996ad42fcc3044d5d3f", "parents": ["79f854b6a094eb1005fb309e7312af0051a216c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079097: Include the update channel in the crash helper log's name. r=crashreporting-reviewers,gsvelto\n\nThe log still starts empty on every launch, but builds from different channels that share a data folder no longer overwrite each other's log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332548\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/src/logging/env.rs"], "git_node": "ea0b0a7c92ffadd60795ce03bd449c58c50070b6", "git_parents": ["d404426a7ae292340da9829305fe00ce470a7d0e"], "node": "add53aee70955554f3f1d58bb16229bcede1e200", "parents": ["ec577969c934360ea95d9996ad42fcc3044d5d3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075296 - Part 10: Add tests from related bugs r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331082\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2068369.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2068384.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2073649.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2074215.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2077750.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2078783.js"], "git_node": "427c9a61347c910ebe2553ce8476c6cbc1413650", "git_parents": ["ea0b0a7c92ffadd60795ce03bd449c58c50070b6"], "node": "52bb88b4b06c53d53d4d766c0bc08a9c16aa2d9c", "parents": ["add53aee70955554f3f1d58bb16229bcede1e200"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079277 - Migrate/create new normal browsing tabs tray related UI regression tests to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=101933  | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=101932  | Try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332124\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TabDrawerSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "21d87a4366586bb51b1e847ad72cd138aef4a688", "git_parents": ["427c9a61347c910ebe2553ce8476c6cbc1413650"], "node": "33aa41822ca4ac57a7f4aeb285a320346e031e76", "parents": ["52bb88b4b06c53d53d4d766c0bc08a9c16aa2d9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079703 - Migrate/create new private browsing tabs tray related UI regression tests to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=102009  | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=102008  | Try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332125\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TabDrawerSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "703c5e68d1a64b7c3f4febf44c8d8533cc3a355a", "git_parents": ["21d87a4366586bb51b1e847ad72cd138aef4a688"], "node": "93bfd59fd12b208a3a4d8d41eaad4e29a779ae66", "parents": ["33aa41822ca4ac57a7f4aeb285a320346e031e76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079723 - Create new tab groups related UI regression tests to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase.  [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=102125  | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332126\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "b9cd50208aea086374ac6e5efc38fe929c21e4d1", "git_parents": ["703c5e68d1a64b7c3f4febf44c8d8533cc3a355a"], "node": "0eec19a355e4bf1597f911077a84876766f8a05b", "parents": ["93bfd59fd12b208a3a4d8d41eaad4e29a779ae66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078635 - Keep failing LeakSanitizer records in TestSummaryFormatter output r=jgraham\n\nLeakSanitizer reports its summary and each leak through the lsan_summary and\nlsan_leak actions, which TestSummaryFormatter dropped. mochitest also logs each\nleaking stack as an ERROR line but not the summary, and wpt (mozleak) logs\nneither, so a wpt job failing on an LSan leak got a summary.jsonl without it.\n\nKeep the records the TBPL formatter prints as failures: an lsan_summary not\nmarked allowed, and an lsan_leak without an allowed_match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331251\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/testsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_testsummary.py"], "git_node": "b1b4b13866046aaf41f1e85d180bc13ff2da1f08", "git_parents": ["b9cd50208aea086374ac6e5efc38fe929c21e4d1"], "node": "fa1f2477be5fa6e85806de1bd3f5317dda3e04d4", "parents": ["0eec19a355e4bf1597f911077a84876766f8a05b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arne Fucks \u003cafucks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067020 - Make DoH URL and DoH mode in about:networking more intuitive r=kershaw,valentin,necko-reviewers\n\nThe DoH URL is now only shown when DoH is enabled and the DoH mode now\ndisplays user readable states instead of numbers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332023\n", "files": ["netwerk/docs/submitting_networking_bugs.md", "toolkit/content/aboutNetworking.js", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_about_networking.js"], "git_node": "12bc542445fbcd3ce1a65598bf46dfa7da02e3c0", "git_parents": ["b1b4b13866046aaf41f1e85d180bc13ff2da1f08"], "node": "84125afce444dc3f676a2daed5984c100bc7717d", "parents": ["fa1f2477be5fa6e85806de1bd3f5317dda3e04d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080242 - Include WidgetUtilsGtk.h for Wayland builds in nsAppShell.cpp. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers,emilio\n\nnsAppShell::IsSessionRestoreSupported() calls IsGnomeDesktopEnvironment()\nunder MOZ_WAYLAND, but WidgetUtilsGtk.h, which declares it, was included\nunder MOZ_ENABLE_DBUS only. Builds with dbus disabled fail to compile.\n\nInclude the header when either is enabled: the dbus code uses\nIsCancelledGError() and the Wayland code uses IsGnomeDesktopEnvironment().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332621\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp"], "git_node": "e5d3224118cacf44e21f1e576507d19f9a6110c0", "git_parents": ["12bc542445fbcd3ce1a65598bf46dfa7da02e3c0"], "node": "b216583930736c8f3bd2edae7f53c79d1c185174", "parents": ["84125afce444dc3f676a2daed5984c100bc7717d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076810 - Exclude clang-plugin alpha tests from clang-format. r=sergesanspaille\n\nBug 2065403 excluded build/clang-plugin/tests/ from clang-format but not\nbuild/clang-plugin/alpha/tests/, so the reformat wrapped the\nexpected-warning {{...}} comments in TestNonStdMove.cpp and\nTestTempRefPtr.cpp across lines and broke their -verify matching. The\nalpha tests only build with --enable-clang-plugin-alpha, which CI does\nnot exercise.\n\nExclude the alpha tests too and restore the two files to their\npre-reformat contents.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329975\n", "files": [".clang-format-ignore", "build/clang-plugin/alpha/tests/TestNonStdMove.cpp", "build/clang-plugin/alpha/tests/TestTempRefPtr.cpp"], "git_node": "51d9c2b5aba7d75db46204a058fe88a001e457e2", "git_parents": ["e5d3224118cacf44e21f1e576507d19f9a6110c0"], "node": "f4a0ff201655f60f3b249dbb70fcca44c1356178", "parents": ["b216583930736c8f3bd2edae7f53c79d1c185174"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080664 - Update metadata for encrypted-media/drm-events.https.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332823\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-events.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9b7c990b84b33e030e2eb0c57475a845004146c2", "git_parents": ["51d9c2b5aba7d75db46204a058fe88a001e457e2"], "node": "3e4f2f69658ad08c6c560dfde6388365f8ed9e9a", "parents": ["f4a0ff201655f60f3b249dbb70fcca44c1356178"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080585 - Avoid UB when converting double to size_t in ScriptOffset. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nConverting a double value outside size_t's range is, strictly speaking,\nUB. For example, on Loong64, Clang seems to take advantage of this and\nsimplifies the conversion-then-compare to a single `d != trunc(d)`:\n\n        vreplvei.d  $vr1, $vr0, 0       # $vr1 \u003c- ($vr0.d[0], $vr0.d[0])\n        vfrintrz.d  $vr1, $vr1          # for all i, $vr1.f64[i] \u003c- (f64)(i64)$vr1.f64[i]\n        fcmp.cune.d $fcc0, $fa0, $fa1   # if ($vr0.f64[0] != $vr1.f64[0])\n\nThis is valid under C++ Std, but fails the check since -1.0 !=\ntrunc(-1.0) is false. So the exception is never thrown thanks to the UB.\n\nOn x86, this works by pure accident, since the converted bit pattern is\nall 1, which equals 2**64 - 1 and thus != -1.0 when converted back.\n\nAvoid this by explicitly spelling out all constraints.\n\nLink:\n https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/implicit_conversion#Floating-point_conversions\n (\"Implicit conversions: Floating-point conversions\")\nLink:\n https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/93a5597d119439a8cc05533fa695db73a63a0cd0/llvm/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp#L20572\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332730\n", "files": ["js/src/debugger/Script.cpp"], "git_node": "a1589617882623302e829091330e0a72ea05965b", "git_parents": ["9b7c990b84b33e030e2eb0c57475a845004146c2"], "node": "06ee67acbfd47865685c0d81141514c420c09133", "parents": ["3e4f2f69658ad08c6c560dfde6388365f8ed9e9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080587 - Update metadata for encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses-multiple-sessions.https.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332824\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses-multiple-sessions.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "2b9063e59e0e19e0f51a77ce272018a4520140b7", "git_parents": ["a1589617882623302e829091330e0a72ea05965b"], "node": "3bba889769aae3ea6c32f576a78abba5ee2a4120", "parents": ["06ee67acbfd47865685c0d81141514c420c09133"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079534 - reduce Gecko Decision Task maximum duration to 1800 seconds. r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,jcristau\n\nReverts the change from bug 1721729.\nThe bulk of runs completed in less than 4 minutes for the last 4 weeks but\nsome buffer in case there is a degradation of services involved (taskcluster,\ntaskcluster-artifacts, bugbug) should be kept.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331848\n", "files": [".taskcluster.yml"], "git_node": "510f03a22fd052e42ff609de1e170c5a117466e2", "git_parents": ["2b9063e59e0e19e0f51a77ce272018a4520140b7"], "node": "695c43236c27c0407925be9937238f8c0634d15c", "parents": ["3bba889769aae3ea6c32f576a78abba5ee2a4120"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080591 - Update metadata for speculation-rules/prefetch/inline-speculation-rules-after-stylesheet.https.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332825\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/inline-speculation-rules-after-stylesheet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "8e6b3cc359863c91361aeb7d09ca16a3f42f70ae", "git_parents": ["510f03a22fd052e42ff609de1e170c5a117466e2"], "node": "55df5570231ded5dd302aa5fdf84612a44eb9d8d", "parents": ["695c43236c27c0407925be9937238f8c0634d15c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1983514 - Update metadata for html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332827\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.ini"], "git_node": "4dca0ab9d06574f9c617ad55538f76e8c273c74c", "git_parents": ["8e6b3cc359863c91361aeb7d09ca16a3f42f70ae"], "node": "3fe99f5674787eeb04abd1f59ee28ad52bd6870c", "parents": ["55df5570231ded5dd302aa5fdf84612a44eb9d8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079057 - Avoid registering a font-set that is being destroyed. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\n(based on clauditor-suggested patch)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332737\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.h"], "git_node": "1e643a857bfb2b1f976b68a37db919d96681f9ed", "git_parents": ["4dca0ab9d06574f9c617ad55538f76e8c273c74c"], "node": "8bdaf87de64b120156f7a9102143ba472a5bd891", "parents": ["3fe99f5674787eeb04abd1f59ee28ad52bd6870c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2025386 - Replace per-instance weak memory reporters with a strong singleton. r=nika\" for causing failures at test_aboutmemory3.xhtml.\n\nThis reverts commit a4f6917449ad418ee89c9e959ca9284771baac34.\n", "files": ["dom/file/BlobImpl.h", "dom/file/BlobMemoryReporter.cpp", "dom/file/BlobMemoryReporter.h", "dom/file/StreamBlobImpl.cpp", "dom/file/StreamBlobImpl.h", "dom/file/StringBlobImpl.cpp", "dom/file/StringBlobImpl.h", "dom/file/moz.build"], "git_node": "2ae605c9b99ce1030cfcf75b00cd28e6b76531bb", "git_parents": ["1e643a857bfb2b1f976b68a37db919d96681f9ed"], "node": "e956143d1c6c012a4f94ced9fd5abda8b36681c1", "parents": ["8bdaf87de64b120156f7a9102143ba472a5bd891"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1940389 - [bidi] Split newline-merged headers value on \\n (e.g. set-cookie) r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328643\n", "files": ["remote/shared/NetworkResponse.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a13f08cdee230b57396c2dacfd9e81ffc710fcca", "git_parents": ["2ae605c9b99ce1030cfcf75b00cd28e6b76531bb"], "node": "d620ae064a587feae42d9217953661a378440895", "parents": ["e956143d1c6c012a4f94ced9fd5abda8b36681c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1940389 - [wdspec] Add bidi tests for newline-merged headers with multiple values r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328644\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/response_completed/response_completed.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/response_started/response_started.py"], "git_node": "60497ff5ba7119361839f174e76e22e5c951b824", "git_parents": ["a13f08cdee230b57396c2dacfd9e81ffc710fcca"], "node": "369590a24497708f45d7ac295850a1c952795a53", "parents": ["d620ae064a587feae42d9217953661a378440895"], "tags": []}, {"author"