]}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077803 - ElementInternals attr-element getters should check shared-root. r=edgar\n\nThis follows https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/8932, which lets\nElementInternals refer to any element that has the same shadow-including root\nas the target element. Chrome does the same, except that it also returns\nelements that are in a different, disconnected tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330610\n", "files": ["dom/html/ElementInternals.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/element-internals-aria-element-reflection-shadow-including-root.tentative.html"], "git_node": "9494b4009376de5b6fa4fa5b54ef80d6cde7c2fb", "git_parents": ["04f74f696e004d56c6527823e3e407c36f89d878"], "node": "e21e616c57688b507dd5be5e8516aac7528ab22d", "parents": ["863f13fef2b0d47e2e678c33fcb691c656e00a66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078564 - Clean up permissions left by tests in browser/modules/test/browser, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,dao.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331139\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_TabUnloader.js"], "git_node": "5d6ec800b6dc8fccf12a4975ce58334afac3ecb6", "git_parents": ["9494b4009376de5b6fa4fa5b54ef80d6cde7c2fb"], "node": "c0073d36a752e826b62310c3841d105cc7ac3e4e", "parents": ["e21e616c57688b507dd5be5e8516aac7528ab22d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078564 - Stop removing default permissions in browser_forgetthissite.js and browser_394759_purge.js, r=places-reviewers,sessionstore-reviewers,nsharpley,Standard8.\n\nBoth tests forget mozilla.org, which removes the built-in default uitour, install and remote-troubleshooting permissions of www.mozilla.org, support.mozilla.org and addons.mozilla.org. Removing a default permission stores an override, so they don't come back for the rest of the session. The tests only need a site to forget, so use example.org, which has no default permissions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331140\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_forgetthissite.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_394759_purge.js"], "git_node": "2b67a904882e8ac2d17fc9fdecec72f7a450c967", "git_parents": ["5d6ec800b6dc8fccf12a4975ce58334afac3ecb6"], "node": "8796b80dc547bb33c1b8f59fc35a6f82b1a6a6f3", "parents": ["c0073d36a752e826b62310c3841d105cc7ac3e4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078564 - Clean up permissions left by tests in dom/credentialmanagement/identity/tests/browser, r=emz.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331131\n", "files": ["dom/credentialmanagement/identity/tests/browser/browser_autoreauthn_doesnt_show_ui.js", "dom/credentialmanagement/identity/tests/browser/browser_passive_requires_connected.js"], "git_node": "2ea4558c818a7b044610fca40bec697f7375c15f", "git_parents": ["2b67a904882e8ac2d17fc9fdecec72f7a450c967"], "node": "2ad69e65543bc68cbabb14c7c0f8356bc42a6e31", "parents": ["8796b80dc547bb33c1b8f59fc35a6f82b1a6a6f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078207 - Remove explicit promise gripping attributes on SpeechRecogntion object for model dowload. r=media-webspeech-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330744\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/recognition/SpeechRecognition.h"], "git_node": "f659bbe3e6c63547b6aac805f2c2e5ce8f55c0f0", "git_parents": ["2ea4558c818a7b044610fca40bec697f7375c15f"], "node": "ba9cdd53ab2f103ea25f3f2938d19a914fd76723", "parents": ["2ad69e65543bc68cbabb14c7c0f8356bc42a6e31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bas Schouten \u003cbschouten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078903: Ensure that native-anonymous content doesn't use a cached container timing root. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331609\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/crashtests/2078903.html", "dom/base/crashtests/crashtests.list", "dom/performance/PerformanceContainerTiming.cpp"], "git_node": "834c1826680eef73c93c4db16b66d1e7a79a127e", "git_parents": ["f659bbe3e6c63547b6aac805f2c2e5ce8f55c0f0"], "node": "cc3bb6cff097753af71b84ba7887d7ecf23bf541", "parents": ["ba9cdd53ab2f103ea25f3f2938d19a914fd76723"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080436 - Avoid accelerated canvas' PBO upload path on macOS with native GL on Intel GPUs. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nUsing the shared PBO upload path can result in broken rendering when\nwith the native macOS GL driver on Intel GPUs. We therefore avoid\nit. Rendering when using ANGLE is unaffected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332840\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.cpp", "dom/canvas/DrawTargetWebgl.h"], "git_node": "83327dc7d4e39600fcaa2038b07170190625e1bf", "git_parents": ["834c1826680eef73c93c4db16b66d1e7a79a127e"], "node": "6caeabd73fc9284c941053a8c6456c295c0bbf2d", "parents": ["cc3bb6cff097753af71b84ba7887d7ecf23bf541"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075336 - Add telemetry to determine the time it takes to share a file r=android-reviewers,kaya\n\nPatch adds metrics for sharing a file on the share sheet:\n* share_file_resource_success:\n    * duration_ms, how long it took to acquire the bytes and show the share sheet\n    * share_type, how the bytes were obtained (direct, internet, local)\n    * content_type, type of content being shared (pdf, other)\n* share_file_resource_fail:\n    * failure_reason, why it failed (timeout, cancelled, error)\n    * share_type, how the bytes were obtained (direct, internet, local)\n    * content_type, type of content being shared (pdf, other)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332123\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/downloads/facts/ShareResourceFacts.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/downloads/temporary/ShareResourceFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/downloads/temporary/ShareResourceFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "4afc370960bde75e655b00593166d219d143afbd", "git_parents": ["83327dc7d4e39600fcaa2038b07170190625e1bf"], "node": "6ccd2c788ec03e53d97b0752c02fdcb0f513cb13", "parents": ["6caeabd73fc9284c941053a8c6456c295c0bbf2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2004379 - Add rule SupportsOptions for InspectorUtils.supports to check support for a given rule type. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin,emilio,devtools-reviewers.\n\nIn some cases, a declaration will be valid for a rule type, and not for another\nrule type. At the moment, InspectorUtils.supports will only watch the validity\nof the passed string for `CssRuleType::Style`.\nThis patch adds a `rule` option to `SupportsOptions`, from which we then\nextract its type and pass it to `Servo_CSSSupports` so we can check the validity\nof a string against a specific rule type.\n\nTest cases are added in layout/inspector/tests/test_supports.html.\n\nThis also adds a CssRuleTypes#allows_declarations method that is called from\nDeclaration#eval and NonCustomPropertyId#allowed_in_rule.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D275192\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/InspectorUtils.webidl", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "layout/inspector/tests/test_supports.html", "layout/style/CSS.cpp", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/supports_rule.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "2ef09bbf347cd5c182552fdafb6d3e3da1864760", "git_parents": ["4afc370960bde75e655b00593166d219d143afbd"], "node": "98fd4e220ec95c0e1747464dbc8bc04226259efb", "parents": ["6ccd2c788ec03e53d97b0752c02fdcb0f513cb13"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791831472, "git_changesets": ["c94ba4f19be18a769c0ca47dfad1905d371b9fe1", "29f53ba184a5fdd76feb3481ed30cf4e92726df9", "9fd8198bec75b87bd8e106888444053ee8c920a0", "1b700fd43347df606f217a0a5ad4e356712fd9de", "fc0776ded8ae4a029ef222852fbfceecffcfa3ca", "90c4c55c4b4f2895e3d5cec75984e2fda314fb46", "7e3eb0ce49a54f7ad9343cd6ef6c7b670288a280", "f7d6f1639a0417f6b7891a7e8088ffd62b1d0581", "b82066acf301b27fac4e0d9ed4f0a34993ef80e0", "a755ab45f9b3df650d2458476425f745e8de4433", "2dd0b125686c3aa348b94f3967e17cac6faf7acc", "cc7a5b83a2d85a767c4f16dd61a23af8bcd080d8", "f136161bf69ef2cfa3ffd2c214591014f56cf45f", "dd015892d9dbde3ecce047affb04c7eb3811ceec", "b8b61486a9d1ec8b2ed206b2ce7a9889523c5319", "afe8057f76387492b4b5fe0cbf500faef5c3dd4e", "a4f6917449ad418ee89c9e959ca9284771baac34", "d404426a7ae292340da9829305fe00ce470a7d0e", "ea0b0a7c92ffadd60795ce03bd449c58c50070b6", "427c9a61347c910ebe2553ce8476c6cbc1413650", "21d87a4366586bb51b1e847ad72cd138aef4a688", "703c5e68d1a64b7c3f4febf44c8d8533cc3a355a", "b9cd50208aea086374ac6e5efc38fe929c21e4d1", "b1b4b13866046aaf41f1e85d180bc13ff2da1f08", "12bc542445fbcd3ce1a65598bf46dfa7da02e3c0", "e5d3224118cacf44e21f1e576507d19f9a6110c0", "51d9c2b5aba7d75db46204a058fe88a001e457e2", "9b7c990b84b33e030e2eb0c57475a845004146c2", "a1589617882623302e829091330e0a72ea05965b", "2b9063e59e0e19e0f51a77ce272018a4520140b7", "510f03a22fd052e42ff609de1e170c5a117466e2", "8e6b3cc359863c91361aeb7d09ca16a3f42f70ae", "4dca0ab9d06574f9c617ad55538f76e8c273c74c", "1e643a857bfb2b1f976b68a37db919d96681f9ed", "2ae605c9b99ce1030cfcf75b00cd28e6b76531bb", "a13f08cdee230b57396c2dacfd9e81ffc710fcca", "60497ff5ba7119361839f174e76e22e5c951b824", "41d0f9c21cce70426d48e0b542c5eb1865093ef8", "4f4cf257050385a9a18ef2e99b0c96d16a93e527", "e808de57b84b12a976df94086e640a5f33230cd2", "bcc02e5952f6021b035760e4a0ea6ed2cc7e2b52", "04f74f696e004d56c6527823e3e407c36f89d878", "9494b4009376de5b6fa4fa5b54ef80d6cde7c2fb", "5d6ec800b6dc8fccf12a4975ce58334afac3ecb6", "2b67a904882e8ac2d17fc9fdecec72f7a450c967", "2ea4558c818a7b044610fca40bec697f7375c15f", "f659bbe3e6c63547b6aac805f2c2e5ce8f55c0f0", "834c1826680eef73c93c4db16b66d1e7a79a127e", "83327dc7d4e39600fcaa2038b07170190625e1bf", "4afc370960bde75e655b00593166d219d143afbd", "2ef09bbf347cd5c182552fdafb6d3e3da1864760"], "user": "abutkovits@mozilla.com"}, "45544": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging c0c03f3f899017ae4b7e56c0713f1ada51173c41 with DEVEDITION_159_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "175d1491ecd125bc92af561abd64382950f71376", "git_parents": ["5be826c462f6496c23cbd9c0f6b74b9cb867d505"], "node": "fe2a99f3bc9e363942935ca68806da4a1daa8bc9", "parents": ["183aea2022483de58e63903b8b36a42d15b8f2a7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791831515, "git_changesets": ["175d1491ecd125bc92af561abd64382950f71376"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45545": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging c0c03f3f899017ae4b7e56c0713f1ada51173c41 with FIREFOX_159_0b1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "b6c8aca3a9e8ca4abb55a6f016e17417d43bd53b", "git_parents": ["175d1491ecd125bc92af561abd64382950f71376"], "node": "f9d3bee3f71c847be0402dbb2b3e6a8ed99856c1", "parents": ["fe2a99f3bc9e363942935ca68806da4a1daa8bc9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791831583, "git_changesets": ["b6c8aca3a9e8ca4abb55a6f016e17417d43bd53b"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45546": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080228 - Fix review_group for DOM and Crash Reporting in mots. r=smaug,crashreporting-reviewers,webidl,emilio,gsvelto DONTBUILD\n\nThe review group for the DOM module is dom-core which is presumably intended\nto be dom-core-reviewers, but I think webidl is better because that is\nprecisely the set of DOM peers, whereas dom-core-reviewers reflects the MoCo\norg structure and does not include all DOM peers. I have added a new alias\nfor the WebIDL reviewer group, dom-reviewers.\n\nFor crash reporting, there's a reviewer group, but it just isn't listed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332441\n", "files": ["mots.yaml"], "git_node": "8b5b50de20e8ad73d13400980a9a7a6bd235968f", "git_parents": ["2ef09bbf347cd5c182552fdafb6d3e3da1864760"], "node": "0ca27fba99fab60a919cae44e3e3bff77da48d5a", "parents": ["98fd4e220ec95c0e1747464dbc8bc04226259efb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080120 - Clear the promise holder before resolving in TestOfflineClockDriver.TimeAdvance. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nMozPromiseHolder::Resolve() clears the holder after resolving, so the main\nthread could see the resolution and destroy the holder while the driver\nthread was still using it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332351\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestOfflineClockDriver.cpp"], "git_node": "1c6527f64d35c6225bf1a703542a30e1ed5b1ffc", "git_parents": ["8b5b50de20e8ad73d13400980a9a7a6bd235968f"], "node": "224a8c46742b1461f1b383b51a8c51eae7566b27", "parents": ["0ca27fba99fab60a919cae44e3e3bff77da48d5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080173 - Don't parse MOZ_LOG in the WMF CDM origins list service. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThis lets its logging be enabled from about:logging. A console created with\nthe EME prefix already logs through the EME log module, so checking the\nMOZ_LOG environment variable for \"EME\" was redundant and ignored the\nlogging.EME pref. The messages now only go to MOZ_LOG, like the rest of the\nEME logging, instead of also reaching the Browser Console.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331975\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/media/WindowsMediaFoundationCDMOriginsListService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d40bd40c6d711f8977e1910150627fdbcdcbeac2", "git_parents": ["1c6527f64d35c6225bf1a703542a30e1ed5b1ffc"], "node": "5cc7abd8f59a69a650a0ebfbd9e1d18bb28a5410", "parents": ["224a8c46742b1461f1b383b51a8c51eae7566b27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071871 - Write summary.jsonl from mozharness's StructuredOutputParser r=ahal\n\nThe harnesses write the task's summary.jsonl themselves, through\n--log-testsummary: each run truncates the file it is given, so mozharness\nhands out one part per run and concatenates them afterwards. That leaves no\nway for mozharness to add records of its own in order, which the next patch\nneeds for the lines of Treeherder's failure summary.\n\nmozharness already receives every raw mozlog record on the harness's stdout.\nApply TestSummaryFormatter to them in StructuredOutputParser and append the\nresult to the task's summary.jsonl, which becomes the file's only writer:\nthe per-run parts and append_test_summary() go away.\n\nSuites opt in with \"test_summary\": True in their definition instead of\npassing --log-testsummary to the harness, and web-platform-tests in the\nscript's default config; mochitest flavors, xpcshell and web-platform-tests\nkeep producing the artifact, with the same records as before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325870\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/android/android_common.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/linux_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/mac_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/win_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/per_test_base.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_emulator_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_hardware_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_per_test_base.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_structured.py"], "git_node": "375459800258cafdc1e31df7afb9145b9c9e0940", "git_parents": ["d40bd40c6d711f8977e1910150627fdbcdcbeac2"], "node": "dce3d532e403da194c6087a532deb6655239eed9", "parents": ["5cc7abd8f59a69a650a0ebfbd9e1d18bb28a5410"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071871 - Keep Treeherder's failure summary lines in summary.jsonl r=ahal\n\nTreeherder builds a job's Failure Summary by running every task log line\nthrough the ErrorParser heuristics of its log parser. A consumer of\nsummary.jsonl that wants the same lines had to fetch and reparse the whole\nlog.\n\nPort those heuristics into mozharness (TreeherderErrorParser, to be kept\nin sync with treeherder/log_parser/parsers.py). While a\nStructuredOutputParser writes a summary.jsonl, it attaches a logging\nhandler of its own to the mozharness logger, from the first line it\nparses, or from evaluate_parser(), until finish(), and appends an\n\"error_line\" record for every line Treeherder would select, judged from\nthe record's level and message, with the mozharness level and message and\nthe time. mozharness/base/log.py is left alone. Every selected line gets a\nrecord, including lines whose structured record is already in the file, so\nthe error_line records alone reproduce the failure summary. A line logged\nwhile a structured record is being parsed is written after that record;\nany other line is written at once, so a FATAL line, which raises\nSystemExit as soon as it is logged, is kept.\n\nThe records carry no position in the task log: that file belongs to the\nworker, which adds lines of its own, so nothing inside the task can number\nits lines reliably. A consumer holding the log finds a record from its\ntext and its time, which run-task stamps on every line.\n\nCall parser.finish() once the run has been evaluated rather than right\nafter the harness exits, so the ERROR lines evaluate_parser logs (\"No\nchecks run.\", ...) are captured too, and from a finally block, so the\nhandler is removed even when the run raises.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325871\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/errors.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_emulator_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_hardware_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py", "testing/mozharness/test/python.toml", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_structured.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_testing_errors.py"], "git_node": "79a9295a1e1296254e55c2633b5bf7d031bd2c3d", "git_parents": ["375459800258cafdc1e31df7afb9145b9c9e0940"], "node": "9e5bf663928f72095c58ad9ce59dcd3a4c0ce38e", "parents": ["dce3d532e403da194c6087a532deb6655239eed9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079984 - Round up nine-patch segment render task size. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe device-space size of a nine-patch segment can be fractional where the\nsegment intersects the antialiased bounds of the primitive, and truncating\nit to an integer can produce an empty render task. Round the size up so\nthat the task is never empty and still covers the area that gets drawn.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332390\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-subpixel-corner.yaml"], "git_node": "8432904d8578a5c7ca28029403bbc3d2faf3f5e1", "git_parents": ["79a9295a1e1296254e55c2633b5bf7d031bd2c3d"], "node": "a56bed1ccfde65233b5ab1fefa4568aa196a1f19", "parents": ["9e5bf663928f72095c58ad9ce59dcd3a4c0ce38e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080074 - Prompt for the primary password when the store's key needs it r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nThe store's key lives in NSS, so with a primary password set it cannot be read\nuntil the user unlocks the token. The authenticator follows passwordmgr's\nRustLoginStorageAuthenticator, since both stores share key4.db: it notifies the\nsame topics and declines while LoginHelper.requestReauth holds the token logged\nout.\n\nThe store decrypts every card it reads and fails the whole read on a number it\ncannot decrypt, so with the token locked even listing the cards needs the key.\nReads the user asked for -- the dropdown, the preferences list, filling, saving\nand editing -- run inside RustAutofillStore.allowingPrompt() and prompt; the\nsaved-field-name scan and the migration never do. A locked token is reported as\nNS_ERROR_ABORT, as crypto-SDR and the JSON store do. A declined prompt shows no\ncards in the dropdown, which then holds off prompting as passwordmgr's\nautocomplete does, and no save doorhanger for a submitted card.\n\nA read that fails with the token unlocked is a number another key wrote. The\nstore's CryptoError is passed on and the stored numbers are left as they are,\nas passwordmgr leaves logins it cannot decrypt.\n\nCreditCardStorageMigrator unlocks the key before copying, as\nLoginStorageMigrator does, so a declined prompt defers the migration instead of\nusing up one of its attempts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325418\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rustCreditCard/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/rustCreditCard/browser_creditCard_primaryPassword.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rustStoreShutdown.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAdapterBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f7763ffe866473baca446479e79b2710215b5d56", "git_parents": ["8432904d8578a5c7ca28029403bbc3d2faf3f5e1"], "node": "ea30057cc197384f3303aaa9d6a70b21c9c9e7f5", "parents": ["a56bed1ccfde65233b5ab1fefa4568aa196a1f19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmed Ashraf ElGendy \u003cahmedashrafelgendy25@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076779 - Add support for grid-lanes and inline-grid-lanes display badges and tests in DevTools. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332684\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/markup/markup.js", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/browser_markup_display_node_01.js", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/browser_markup_display_node_02.js", "devtools/client/inspector/markup/views/element-editor.js"], "git_node": "54ef3f9f9c0089a69e3bef3f2e061b935cd81a00", "git_parents": ["f7763ffe866473baca446479e79b2710215b5d56"], "node": "7d87b1fb3a3cfbbeb6187a563ad0184687bf608f", "parents": ["ea30057cc197384f3303aaa9d6a70b21c9c9e7f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080658 - Remove unused Metropolis font files from Focus r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe metropolis font family and FocusTypography reference none of the italic or extra-light weights.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332768\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_blackitalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_bolditalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_extrabolditalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_extralighitalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_extralight.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_lightitalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_mediumitalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_regularitalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_semibolditalic.ttf", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/font/metropolis_thinitalic.ttf"], "git_node": "a25ddada1778760fbfe6261912e04b4cedc9d4d6", "git_parents": ["54ef3f9f9c0089a69e3bef3f2e061b935cd81a00"], "node": "349aed3fcfcc4f0db3ed20470841e8eeb753bf77", "parents": ["7d87b1fb3a3cfbbeb6187a563ad0184687bf608f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080621 - Bump cssparser to current main. r=supply-chain-reviewers,TYLin\n\nPicks a performance improvement from shrinking ParserState.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332743\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/cssparser/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/cssparser/src/parser.rs", "third_party/rust/cssparser/src/size_of_tests.rs", "third_party/rust/cssparser/src/tokenizer.rs"], "git_node": "8613e86d39d6d6845959a375fb9b928af9870147", "git_parents": ["a25ddada1778760fbfe6261912e04b4cedc9d4d6"], "node": "e3f8743b3643fd23096375ddc2a2fe113000e382", "parents": ["349aed3fcfcc4f0db3ed20470841e8eeb753bf77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Charlie Humphreys \u003cchumphreys@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072733: Add missing pref docs r=chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331292\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/docs/dev/preferences.md"], "git_node": "1e74fdf667550615b744e8af00b0119012507dce", "git_parents": ["8613e86d39d6d6845959a375fb9b928af9870147"], "node": "fe103983db646800778ede7b185128eb3def2e4b", "parents": ["e3f8743b3643fd23096375ddc2a2fe113000e382"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079900 - Wait for the discarded IPC dispatch in TestAudioTrackGraph.IOThreadDispatchDuringShutdown. r=pehrsons\n\nThe dispatch reaches the main thread through the IPC I/O thread, so a single\nProcessEventQueue() could return before it was discarded, leaving it to run\nduring the next test against an out-of-scope checkpoint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332352\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": "f5b41c2edef353e96513e37551054aec812c2dfd", "git_parents": ["1e74fdf667550615b744e8af00b0119012507dce"], "node": "b945d070b0ce725ca1f838b3c4208f48e1e16855", "parents": ["fe103983db646800778ede7b185128eb3def2e4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064552 - Make the jittest tasks on the macOS VMs tier 1. r=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/compiled.yml"], "git_node": "19ba058f25059a759fdde74bfc66d6d8576fe4bb", "git_parents": ["f5b41c2edef353e96513e37551054aec812c2dfd"], "node": "5400ee9489731ef4fe42b4c563be91444c697920", "parents": ["b945d070b0ce725ca1f838b3c4208f48e1e16855"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080654 - Fix some New Tab dialogs that are transparent when the train-hop is applied to Firefox 158 and 159 r=maxx\n\nEvery `--dialog-*` reference in the New Tab dialog styles now has a\nfallback, so the dialogs keep their background, border, corner radius\nand shadow when the train-hop is applied to Firefox 158 and 159.\nBug 2049387 moved these dialogs onto the `--dialog-*` tokens, which\nare available from Firefox 160 onwards.\n\nRather than restoring each dialog's old values, the fallbacks use the\n`--popup-*` and `--space-large` tokens that the `--dialog-*` tokens\nare built on. That way, Firefox 158 and 159 show the same dialogs as\nFirefox 160, including the Nova radius and border. The fallbacks are\nmarked `@backward-compat { version 160 }`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332771\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ConfirmDialog/_ConfirmDialog.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/ReportContent/ReportContent.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ModalOverlay/_ModalOverlay.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Weather/_Weather.scss"], "git_node": "d633f0015ff6965e7c70bac41776eec07248d90d", "git_parents": ["19ba058f25059a759fdde74bfc66d6d8576fe4bb"], "node": "5e1d487a37c6ea7cfd3ca1e2c5499d811c7dcd87", "parents": ["5400ee9489731ef4fe42b4c563be91444c697920"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071425 - Delete smart page from history - r=jlewis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332215\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AITabParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_actions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_page.js"], "git_node": "7191fe1946af9b7f5ca7edea4d9a0a2084e9f7e3", "git_parents": ["d633f0015ff6965e7c70bac41776eec07248d90d"], "node": "d66aebf2defdf079cd1bd28d87d1a2833680e2fc", "parents": ["5e1d487a37c6ea7cfd3ca1e2c5499d811c7dcd87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070576 - [customizable-menu] Show the extensions menu item in custom tabs menu r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332829\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuConfigurations.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuConfigurationsTest.kt"], "git_node": "92639d17dbeb0d20de03c72efc953fd9291d3d45", "git_parents": ["7191fe1946af9b7f5ca7edea4d9a0a2084e9f7e3"], "node": "e6a3d69d73ed7302a8149afcbcae8f5becfb066e", "parents": ["d66aebf2defdf079cd1bd28d87d1a2833680e2fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080589 - Fix for almost perma toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_bug1693577.js | test_search_input_popupshowing r=jsudiaman\n\nI was only using `await SidebarController.waitUntilStable()` for the updated bookmarks panel, but we need to do it either way\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332851\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_bug1693577.js"], "git_node": "3250594215e0385d857cc0549c9627b08ecffc2c", "git_parents": ["92639d17dbeb0d20de03c72efc953fd9291d3d45"], "node": "96dab965829db0e6ff94547023f17e720edd9973", "parents": ["e6a3d69d73ed7302a8149afcbcae8f5becfb066e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077605 - Fix minor nits in js/ after SOURCE_HEADERS change r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332446\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineJIT.cpp", "js/src/jit/IonGenericCallStub.h", "js/src/vm/GeckoProfiler.cpp"], "git_node": "af6b1cce1c70c837b3d246df1bbf41a5bc8d9043", "git_parents": ["3250594215e0385d857cc0549c9627b08ecffc2c"], "node": "41c2141fdffbe53014016b8ca2d77a1df57f3243", "parents": ["96dab965829db0e6ff94547023f17e720edd9973"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Link \u003cjlink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067318: Collapse runs of identical applicable declarations before building the rule path. r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nCascadeData::add_rule creates one Rule per selector in a selector list, all\nsharing a declaration block, so an element matching several members -- .a, .c {\n... } on an element carrying both classes -- collects an applicable declaration\nper match. for_rule_tree keeps only the source and the cascade priority, so\nthose entries contribute the same thing to the rule path, but each still gets\nits own rule node: ensure_child looks for the child among the children of the\nnode it just created, whose map is empty.\n\nDrop them as compute_rule_node consumes the list. The list is sorted by then, so\nsuch entries are adjacent; nothing earlier can do it, because which members\nmatch is a property of the element and the entries are not yet adjacent at\nmatching time.\n\n12.0% of applicable declarations on github.com/mozilla/gecko-dev are such\nduplicates. Utility-class frameworks group selectors this way and elements often\nmatch several members at once, so this is an authoring habit, not a site quirk.\n\nIn CI on top of bugs 2064258 and 2064900, Speedometer 3's total CPU time drops\n6-13% in the median on every desktop platform, while the score stays within a\nthird of a percent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325724\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/rule_tree/mod.rs"], "git_node": "6631dff4d22c1c6d45ee0dbed006e70ce853fb93", "git_parents": ["af6b1cce1c70c837b3d246df1bbf41a5bc8d9043"], "node": "59c02c6b2be832e81e1438ce7e804a8824348533", "parents": ["41c2141fdffbe53014016b8ca2d77a1df57f3243"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\naf -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nan -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nar -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nast -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\naz -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbe -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbg -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbn -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbo -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbqi -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbr -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbrx -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nbs -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nca -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nca-valencia -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\ncak -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nckb -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\ncs -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\ncy -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nda -\u003e 08ba6c5efaab334a66f766313533282a700d7804\nde -\u003e 08ba6c5e