ps://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/384\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/BackgroundServices.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/accounts/FxaWebChannelIntegration.kt"], "git_node": "69dbdb67b73d1ac6a28b6c9a87a89bb284628b81", "git_parents": ["e6870cd01c577df6e7a3c673cd4a990c94b06e69"], "node": "be02ffd245587ee130a34552555dcbe5ff290c31", "parents": ["09e1f835b4dbfd674469f3708c355fecd7baab23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067869 - Dismiss to snooze on PUWYLO resume cards - r=pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332467\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_resume_card.js"], "git_node": "d319d430548d219dad2411fd81abcd82906519c2", "git_parents": ["69dbdb67b73d1ac6a28b6c9a87a89bb284628b81"], "node": "207620fa13ef5bfecab25165430f860d807f660c", "parents": ["be02ffd245587ee130a34552555dcbe5ff290c31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fred Chasen \u003cfchasen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070663 - Add the moz-widget custom element. r=mconley,nina-py\n\n- Adds standard widget sizes and card styling.\n- Widget content can come from slotted elements or framed content loaded from `src`.\n- Loads framed content in a remote browser in chrome or iframe in content.\n- When using a browser element, extension content is loaded using the extension\u2019s browsing context group.\n- Adds Storybook documentation and chrome tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327912\n", "files": ["browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/storybook/.storybook/main.js", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.md", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/jar.mn", "browser/components/widgets/moz.build", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget.html"], "git_node": "ac0fa84c95fda8d4a08cc2e4059ad716841ef6f0", "git_parents": ["d319d430548d219dad2411fd81abcd82906519c2"], "node": "332681e47f62bcd007c383746c37bea906f10784", "parents": ["207620fa13ef5bfecab25165430f860d807f660c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fred Chasen \u003cfchasen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070684 - Add a header component and slot to moz-widget. r=nina-py\n\n- Adds a `moz-widget-header` component with a heading and `leading` and `trailing` slots\n- Adds a `header` slot to moz-widget for the `moz-widget-header`\n- Adds a `padded` attribute to moz-widget to inset and round the content\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328015\n", "files": ["browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget-header.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget-header.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.md", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/jar.mn", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget.html", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget_header.html"], "git_node": "52115c9954cad4b2a5667bf0839d4297d2b908f4", "git_parents": ["ac0fa84c95fda8d4a08cc2e4059ad716841ef6f0"], "node": "5b64c7a76d6f2e69706d0af3aa5429ac4f35d157", "parents": ["332681e47f62bcd007c383746c37bea906f10784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fred Chasen \u003cfchasen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070709 - Add WidgetManager to track the widgets registered by extensions. r=mconley\n\n- Adds a `WidgetManager` singleton that stores one widget per extension id.\n- Emits \"change\" at init and on register and unregister with the IDs of the updated widgets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329352\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "toolkit/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/widgets/WidgetManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/widgets/moz.build", "toolkit/components/widgets/tests/xpcshell/test_WidgetManager.js", "toolkit/components/widgets/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "7ed40ce763748089949cb7e9730748c4020cb714", "git_parents": ["52115c9954cad4b2a5667bf0839d4297d2b908f4"], "node": "c0e062a5e7abed1c95b33cd0273d415e624dd92a", "parents": ["5b64c7a76d6f2e69706d0af3aa5429ac4f35d157"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fred Chasen \u003cfchasen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074341 - Add ExtensionWidgetsFeed for widgets provided by extensions. r=mconley\n\n- Adds `src` and `extensionID` to the config for widgets.\n- Widgets with URL in `src` set will render using the `moz-widget` component with that src set on the internal iframe.\n- ExtensionWidgetsFeed updates on WidgetManager changes.\n- Extension widgets get `src` from WidgetManager.\n- Widgets without a registered extension widget aren't shown.\n- Extension widgets use the extension's name as their toggle label.\n- Applies the drag pointer-events and cell sizing rules to `moz-widget`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328690\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/bin/render-activity-stream-html.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/useWidgetLabels.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_WidgetWrapper.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/abouthomecache/page.html.template", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/ExtensionWidgetsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-debug.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-noscripts.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_ExtensionWidgetsFeed.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "799727a82fb566af9c5a4ec318c351993c57232f", "git_parents": ["7ed40ce763748089949cb7e9730748c4020cb714"], "node": "e4283ea318f9bfe48270027c4e81f5b8226b64f1", "parents": ["c0e062a5e7abed1c95b33cd0273d415e624dd92a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080876 - Log GMP service initialization and MediaCapabilities decoder support queries. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThis let us see the race clearly, but it's good anyway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332920\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPUtils.cpp", "dom/media/mediacapabilities/MediaCapabilities.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/PDMFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "f620c4f2ac2217563171bc7ec7f3df49da9f0d46", "git_parents": ["799727a82fb566af9c5a4ec318c351993c57232f"], "node": "7d308fd6833553075dbafe04bd3c16827241a67a", "parents": ["e4283ea318f9bfe48270027c4e81f5b8226b64f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080876 - Avoid deadlocking EME requests against GMP service initialization. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nA MediaCapabilities decoder probe can start creating the GMP service on a\nbackground thread and wait for main to initialize it. If an EME request\nthen calls HaveGMPFor on main, it waits for that pending service creation\nand prevents the initialization runnable from executing.\n\nFix this by moving EME's GMP support checks to the PDM thread pool, so main\nremains free to initialize the service. Assert that HaveGMPFor runs off\nmain to catch callers that could reintroduce the deadlock.\n\nTo consume those checks asynchronously, return a promise from\nGetKeySystemStatus and continue request processing on main when it\nresolves. Adapt CDM installation retries to await the status too, and\nignore results for requests that have expired or been shut down. Filter\nsupported key systems off main before assembling their configurations on\nmain; DOM promise settlement also stays on main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332938\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.cpp", "dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.h", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.cpp", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.h", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccessManager.cpp", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccessManager.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "b84f2e9c41d38d689cb1c99f19e04ea7410e67bb", "git_parents": ["f620c4f2ac2217563171bc7ec7f3df49da9f0d46"], "node": "8a061c2658ffada1e37927a5c42c9860dd35dd45", "parents": ["7d308fd6833553075dbafe04bd3c16827241a67a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074190. r=firefox-animation-reviewers,boris\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332961\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.h"], "git_node": "8884de243c8de3bcb3235379efa3f2b4583c38c7", "git_parents": ["b84f2e9c41d38d689cb1c99f19e04ea7410e67bb"], "node": "e918da2fd33a098a3cc7a158abca4cc039e1f50a", "parents": ["8a061c2658ffada1e37927a5c42c9860dd35dd45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080641 - More consistently deal with FontFaceSet promise resolution. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,boris\n\nDon't use the ready promise status as a proxy for \"do we need to\nschedule the resolve\".\n\nThis prevents .ready from resolving when other loads have started after\nthe fact already.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332819\n", "files": ["layout/style/FontFaceImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.h", "layout/style/FontFaceSetDocumentImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.h"], "git_node": "98c0c12d84b12c97053201d3da478bb4856d926a", "git_parents": ["8884de243c8de3bcb3235379efa3f2b4583c38c7"], "node": "058e5b7ac99a82247883c684a1014e72efcfa1a8", "parents": ["e918da2fd33a098a3cc7a158abca4cc039e1f50a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080640 - Teach nsDeviceContextSpecX to print via SkPDF for all print targets. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThis patch removes (behind a pref, just in case) our usage of\nPrintTargetCG. It was already dealing with printer output and file\noutput when it was dealing with PDF. Once this hits release I'll\nfollow-up with the relevant code removal.\n\nInteresting bits of code are:\n\n * PMPrintSettingsSetJobName handling gets ported over from\n   PrintTargetCG. We still need it there because it gets called before\n   the dev context one so if we're using PrintTargetCG, the dev context\n   call happens too late (the print job has started already). I believe\n   this might fix the job name for other SkPDF documents, but I don't\n   have a printer handy and I don't know where those are exposed in the\n   UI.\n\n * nsDeviceContextSpecX::DoEndDocument() gets de-indented and deals with\n   the new destinations:\n\n   * kPMDestinationProcessPDF uses PMWorkflowSubmitPDFWithSettings,\n     which gives the SkPDF generated document directly to the workflow.\n     This is nice, because it means things like links and accessibility\n     information is preserved with items like \"Send in Mail\".\n\n   * PrintPDFViaPrintSession() deals with the fallback cases (fax and\n     print to file to non-PDF output). It just replays the PDF into the\n     CGContext. Seems preferable than using a totally different painting\n     back-end.\n\nI tested this via \"Send in Mail\" items and \"Save as PostScript\" items,\nin the system print dialog, both working as expected. Note that if you\nwant to test the PostScript path you need to use an online viewer,\nPreview.app no longer deals with it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332761\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "widget/cocoa/nsDeviceContextSpecX.h", "widget/cocoa/nsDeviceContextSpecX.mm"], "git_node": "1d260ee1374cf8b2cf32b1d822c4c9b24517c09d", "git_parents": ["98c0c12d84b12c97053201d3da478bb4856d926a"], "node": "d7251047a29b3b25c5484c3e2f3583e68b3dafcc", "parents": ["058e5b7ac99a82247883c684a1014e72efcfa1a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080789 - Don't cache the interpreter entry offset when the assembler has run out of memory. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332884\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/bug2080789.js", "js/src/jit/InterpreterEntryTrampoline.cpp"], "git_node": "dc266692185e731c30220b8f513e3c7cc48ebaef", "git_parents": ["1d260ee1374cf8b2cf32b1d822c4c9b24517c09d"], "node": "e40f4b0d13b1f3899c542a7bcbad18b7820667be", "parents": ["d7251047a29b3b25c5484c3e2f3583e68b3dafcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066299 - Record outcome when about:sessionrestore and about:welcomeback are loaded. r=sessionstore-reviewers,jswinarton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331193\n", "files": ["browser/components/migration/content/aboutWelcomeBack.xhtml", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionMigration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/content/aboutSessionRestore.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/content/aboutSessionRestore.xhtml", "browser/components/sessionstore/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_aboutSessionRestore_telemetry.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_session_migration_show_reason.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.glean.d.ts"], "git_node": "ca334176f0f0a29606d6c12c3ec5d32a4786a6be", "git_parents": ["dc266692185e731c30220b8f513e3c7cc48ebaef"], "node": "624fd8df5a03975a5e9701af1450839f98ba3a32", "parents": ["e40f4b0d13b1f3899c542a7bcbad18b7820667be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074341, Bug 2070709, Bug 2070684, Bug 2070663 - Add ExtensionWidgetsFeed for widgets provided by extensions. r=mconley\" for causing mass failures @nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 799727a82fb566af9c5a4ec318c351993c57232f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070709 - Add WidgetManager to track the widgets registered by extensions. r=mconley\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7ed40ce763748089949cb7e9730748c4020cb714.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070684 - Add a header component and slot to moz-widget. r=nina-py\"\n\nThis reverts commit 52115c9954cad4b2a5667bf0839d4297d2b908f4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2070663 - Add the moz-widget custom element. r=mconley,nina-py\"\n\nThis reverts commit ac0fa84c95fda8d4a08cc2e4059ad716841ef6f0.\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/storybook/.storybook/main.js", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget-header.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget-header.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.md", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.stories.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/jar.mn", "browser/components/widgets/moz.build", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget.html", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget_header.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/bin/render-activity-stream-html.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/useWidgetLabels.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_WidgetWrapper.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/abouthomecache/page.html.template", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/ExtensionWidgetsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-debug.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-noscripts.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_ExtensionWidgetsFeed.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/widgets/WidgetManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/widgets/moz.build", "toolkit/components/widgets/tests/xpcshell/test_WidgetManager.js", "toolkit/components/widgets/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "586202ff7c9a12486a20269394e836259f76d6bb", "git_parents": ["ca334176f0f0a29606d6c12c3ec5d32a4786a6be"], "node": "cbfe9c972425d575b5a71b1da41e82c1409fbf24", "parents": ["624fd8df5a03975a5e9701af1450839f98ba3a32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080876 - Avoid deadlocking EME requests against GMP service initialization. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\" for causing gtest failures @GMPUtils.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit b84f2e9c41d38d689cb1c99f19e04ea7410e67bb.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2080876 - Log GMP service initialization and MediaCapabilities decoder support queries. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit f620c4f2ac2217563171bc7ec7f3df49da9f0d46.\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.cpp", "dom/media/eme/KeySystemConfig.h", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.cpp", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccess.h", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccessManager.cpp", "dom/media/eme/MediaKeySystemAccessManager.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPUtils.cpp", "dom/media/mediacapabilities/MediaCapabilities.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/PDMFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "db6bd4c86de475a5db4de7eb6ec078fbbf807538", "git_parents": ["586202ff7c9a12486a20269394e836259f76d6bb"], "node": "27c2b1d030844e5bb8cdb2e8434bd3479378105a", "parents": ["cbfe9c972425d575b5a71b1da41e82c1409fbf24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Rae Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@berkeley.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040774 - Wait for the urlbar to get focus after the native context menu closes in browser_test_focus_urlbar.js r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nWe can't reliably await a11y events on the native menu, but we should\nstill see a focus event land back on the url bar's input once the menu\nis closed. This patch ensures we await that focus event instead of the\n`popuphidden` alone, since this seems to be a better a11y signal.\n\nThis appears to fix the intermittent test issue tracked at both bug\n2040774 and 1883471.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332975\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/events/browser_test_focus_urlbar.js"], "git_node": "b641ff62e1ed3aa8211483df449861c4209d1001", "git_parents": ["db6bd4c86de475a5db4de7eb6ec078fbbf807538"], "node": "c8b2485f379f3a4bfa32fd1e4915d681f11a04de", "parents": ["27c2b1d030844e5bb8cdb2e8434bd3479378105a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071334 - Add plus and expand button to tab groups strip r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327153\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupsTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/TabGroupsStripContent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/redux/TabGroupsStripAction.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/redux/TabGroupsStripMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/redux/TabGroupsStripReducer.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/TabGroupsStripContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/strip/redux/TabGroupsStripReducerTest.kt"], "git_node": "bc2056b889ccc450a8a3705f7ac875f5f8742701", "git_parents": ["b641ff62e1ed3aa8211483df449861c4209d1001"], "node": "819b29e68fb52dc3815e50c9ad5d557bad41930d", "parents": ["c8b2485f379f3a4bfa32fd1e4915d681f11a04de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065579 - Allow a GeckoSession to be opened in an existing browsing context group and content process. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall,jonalmeida\n\nA session that clones a video from another session has to live in the same browsing context group and the same content process as that video, otherwise the video cannot be cloned into it.\n\nLet the embedder ask for that placement explicitly through two new session settings. When they are unset, remote type selection keeps falling back to ProcessIsolation's prediction, so this does not change how any existing session is opened.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320560\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/background.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-api.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-schema.json", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/SessionProcessPlacementTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/rule/GeckoSessionTestRule.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSessionSettings.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/shared/chrome/geckoview/geckoview.js", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/moz.build"], "git_node": "141f1800dd0df237e97bb5428071eef3a4503033", "git_parents": ["bc2056b889ccc450a8a3705f7ac875f5f8742701"], "node": "80dc1c2405942c633f943d78028fec9e3a15348f", "parents": ["819b29e68fb52dc3815e50c9ad5d557bad41930d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Let a GeckoSession host a picture-in-picture player. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324069\n", "files": ["mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPicturePlayerChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPicturePlayerParent.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/moz.build", "mobile/shared/chrome/geckoview/geckoview.js", "toolkit/actors/PictureInPictureChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn"], "git_node": "fbb2189ae83f8c31eed10b8b9ca2f340ce539f5c", "git_parents": ["141f1800dd0df237e97bb5428071eef3a4503033"], "node": "0f038d223a7ab6173ca22c1a0372d938c35e1db6", "parents": ["80dc1c2405942c633f943d78028fec9e3a15348f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Ask the embedder to open a picture-in-picture window for a playing video. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324070\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/rule/GeckoSessionTestRule.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PictureInPictureController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPictureSourceChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/moz.build", "mobile/shared/chrome/geckoview/geckoview.js", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "28900f6efec098f5afb657455aa902e5da39277c", "git_parents": ["fbb2189ae83f8c31eed10b8b9ca2f340ce539f5c"], "node": "ba3ce604a389f574df04d8c2fd80715bb3a35ee8", "parents": ["0f038d223a7ab6173ca22c1a0372d938c35e1db6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Clone the video once the picture-in-picture window's session is ready. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324071\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/TestSupportChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/background.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-api.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-schema.json", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/SessionProcessPlacementTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/rule/GeckoSessionTestRule.java", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d43de2c17d065727d48ff330a533aebc736961d4", "git_parents": ["28900f6efec098f5afb657455aa902e5da39277c"], "node": "fb10269b0ea7e602527479b2c548559174f34e4a", "parents": ["ba3ce604a389f574df04d8c2fd80715bb3a35ee8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Tell the embedder when to close the picture-in-picture window. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324072\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/www/video_in_iframe.html", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/BaseSessionTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PictureInPictureController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPicturePlayerParent.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "449b1d38b530c60e42bc866618a4cbd677a667cd", "git_parents": ["d43de2c17d065727d48ff330a533aebc736961d4"], "node": "a358ca7f29975baac8494e82106298dfabf69764", "parents": ["fb10269b0ea7e602527479b2c548559174f34e4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Let the embedder report that it closed the picture-in-picture window itself. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324073\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PictureInPictureController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b0a195b8fa94bf96fe6a82e12a05feea0cfc9a92", "git_parents": ["449b1d38b530c60e42bc866618a4cbd677a667cd"], "node": "9e3bf48633cd44ebfdbb25f894ac4ef2820db225", "parents": ["a358ca7f29975baac8494e82106298dfabf69764"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Keep the source tab alive while its video is in a picture-in-picture window. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall,kaya\n\nThe cloned video is painted from the source video, which stops painting once the source docShell is deactivated. The source session is deactivated when the user switches to another tab, and pages also commonly pause their video once they are hidden, so the picture-in-picture window would freeze.\n\nAdd SessionPictureInPicture.setKeepActive so the embedder can keep the source session active while its window shows one of that session's videos. GeckoView skips deactivating a session that has it set. Only the embedder knows when the window is gone and whether the session is still showing elsewhere, so once it clears the flag it is responsible for deactivating the session.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320563\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/GeckoViewTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoView.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PictureInPictureController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md"], "git_node": "b161794ba1253c1c78e6a390fd497998b02bc05c", "git_parents": ["b0a195b8fa94bf96fe6a82e12a05feea0cfc9a92"], "node": "57352ed869e3c3bb1a341dd3ca3d35f471dc3210", "parents": ["9e3bf48633cd44ebfdbb25f894ac4ef2820db225"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065587 - Implement picture-in-picture in GeckoView Example. r=ohall,geckoview-reviewers\n\nGeckoViewActivity answers the session's picture-in-picture delegate by opening the session Gecko asks for and starting PictureInPictureActivity, which renders it and puts itself into native picture-in-picture mode. Expanding the window returns to the tab the video was playing in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320565\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/GeckoViewActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PictureInPictureActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PipSessionHolder.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/res/values/strings.xml"], "git_node": "b36938fcaae6cf6e1f81f94f761a7b10c4cba011", "git_parents": ["b161794ba1253c1c78e6a390fd497998b02bc05c"], "node": "e61312d2f58cb9e2d8062218b2fe383c86130078", "parents": ["57352ed869e3c3bb1a341dd3ca3d35f471dc3210"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065581 - Drop picture-in-picture state when a session goes away. r=ohall,geckoview-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nA source session that went away without its window being closed first left GeckoView holding its browsing context group, which a later picture-in-picture session could be handed. Forget the source's state, or the player's, when its session is destroyed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324964\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/GeckoViewActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PictureInPictureActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PipSessionHolder.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/TabSessionManager.java", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c59277d4e6620c92476cb05ee075d7554f2ca540", "git_parents": ["b36938fcaae6cf6e1f81f94f761a7b10c4cba011"], "node": "cc41c15c3093a0bf817017c8ae0d88ab5cfe8b85", "parents": ["e61312d2f58cb9e2d8062218b2fe383c86130078"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072439 - Test the picture rect of a decoded VP8 frame with cropped rows r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nFrom dom/media/test, vp8-pixel-crop-rows.webm is generated with:\n  python3 generate_vp8_pixel_crop.py \\\n    --pixel-width 320 --pixel-height 240 \\\n    --pixel-crop-top 16 --pixel-crop-bottom 16 \\\n    --pixel-crop-left 0 --pixel-crop-right 0 \\\n    --timecode-scale 1000000 --duration 2000 \\\n    --block-timecode 0 --block-timecode 1000 vp8-pixel-crop-rows.webm\n\nCropping rows only keeps the wrong (0,16,320,240) rect inside the padded\ndecode buffer on every platform, so the test fails everywhere until the\ndecoder is fixed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326349\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/generate_vp8_pixel_crop.py", "dom/media/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/test/test_video_pixel_crop_picture_rect.html", "dom/media/test/vp8-pixel-crop-rows.webm"], "git_node": "7f523e883c783f101ae643ba35f5a085cb469fd3", "git_parents": ["c59277d4e6620c92476cb05ee075d7554f2ca540"], "node": "4e63e93f960b7f46a3a26980e7a2ec9b8fabf178", "parents": ["cc41c15c3093a0bf817017c8ae0d88ab5cfe8b85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072439 - Build the shared decode buffer's picture rect from the scaled image rect r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe rect combined the scaled image rect's origin with the codec context's\nfull size, so a cropped stream got a rect offset by the crop yet as large as\nthe coded frame: a 320x240 frame with 16 rows cropped at the top and bottom\ngot (0,16,320,240) instead of (0,16,320,208). Use the scaled image rect\nwhole, as the other paths do.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326350\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "a6b74127042947458079817a2a42861d870b0695", "git_parents": ["7f523e883c783f101ae643ba35f5a085cb469fd3"], "node": "2aa02f0b4f1ca431a8c8606313d11b7699f8a7b0", "parents": ["4e63e93f960b7f46a3a26980e7a2ec9b8fabf178"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076646 - Snap shadow contents relative to the content they shadow. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe display list builder desugars a shadow into copies of the shadowed items\ntranslated by the shadow offset. Each copy was snapped on its own, so at\nfractional device scales (where a 1 CSS px offset is fractional in layout\nspace) the visible offset flipped between whole pixels with the content's\nsub-pixel phase, for every shadowed item type.\n\nCarry the offset on the shadow's stacking context and keep that stacking\ncontext as a picture (a pass-through one when the shadow is unblurred). The\npicture's snapper snaps each copy's rect where the shadowed content is and\nthen moves it by the offset rounded to whole device pixels on the axes that\nsnap, which also holds under scale transforms and pinch zoom. Text runs apply\nthe same adjustment to their pens.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331837\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2076646-shadow-offset-snap-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2076646-shadow-offset-snap-scale-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2076646-shadow-offset-snap-scale.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2076646-shadow-offset-snap.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "b45d054b55f55a0dc537d56a39753a2694a53f59", "git_parents": ["a6b74127042947458079817a2a42861d870b0695"], "node": "7205ac1d7b81f0e90592b72b2085f13d66cf0efd", "parents": ["2aa02f0b4f1ca431a8c8606313d11b7699f8a7b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080923 - Only run test_crashreporter_appmem.js where RegisterAppMemory is implemented. r=crashreporting-reviewers,afranchuk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333014\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "1edcc4b0503b950d05c79e1d5b33ecf92d9b4f40", "git_parents": ["b45d054b55f55a0dc537d56a39753a2694a53f59"], "node": "af2d50b973d1005420a9855eaafcdaf652b8286f", "parents": ["7205ac1d7b81f0e90592b72b2085f13d66cf0efd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "na-g \u003cna-g@nostrum.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080949 - Set maintainer-phab: #webrtc-reviewers for drm;r=webrtc-reviewers,mjf\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333017\n", "files": ["third_party/drm/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "7fc59985b2afcf8cea928ceab213b1468adcec1f", "git_parents": ["1edcc4b0503b950d05c79e1d5b33ecf92d9b4f40"], "node": "70f613135a8d93b3b6519d41340e0fd943848c56", "parents": ["af2d50b973d1005420a9855eaafcdaf652b8286f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1854737 - Send filled border-images with empty edges to WebRender. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nWhen all border widths were zero, Gecko drew the whole source image instead\nof the sliced middle part, and fell back to a blob when only one axis was\nempty. WebRender handles both cases now, except that the unscaled middle image\nwas sized in source texels rather than nine-patch units, which is wrong when\nthe device pixel ratio isn't 1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332780\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-image-fill-zero-width-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-image-fill-zero-width.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/border-image-red-with-green-center.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/border-image-slice-fill-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "a0073bcaf742ceb522be14e42559dff0d55acea2", "git_parents": ["7fc59985b2afcf8cea928ceab213b1468adcec1f"], "node": "190b6a24b6855261b83a03ebbfe992f5811638e9", "parents": ["70f613135a8d93b3b6519d41340e0fd943848c56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078462 - Intern rectangles in the display list builder r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe first interned type, plus the machinery every primitive type shares.\nPrimitive keys hold the prim rect, local clip rect and flags, so an item is\nonly its spatial id, clip chain and handle, and the scene builder places the\ninstance from a PrimPlacement store (add_dl_prim). The two ids stay on the\nitem because content numbers them per build.\n\nSince an item no longer carries what its shadow copy needs, primitives pushed\nin a shadow scope record a CapturedKey that the desugar interns copies from.\nA handle-less rectangle in a finished list is a transparent checkerboard,\nkept only for its tile cache barrier.\n\nA fresh builder re-mints every uid, so an identical list from a new builder\nrepaints; test_invalidation covers it. wrshell's capture writer now emits\nplaceholder bounds and colour.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330955\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "d8906019c89f43a6ab58522c0ca99a8f2eaddc8a", "git_parents": ["a0073bcaf742ceb522be14e42559dff0d55acea2"], "node": "1bd64b21675dd806907c511753857194f7258004", "parents": ["190b6a24b6855261b83a03ebbfe992f5811638e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2065581, Bug 2065587, Bug 2065579 - Drop picture-in-picture state when a session goes away. r=ohall,geckoview-reviewers,jonalmeida\" for causing junit failures @ PictureInPictureTest\n\nThis reverts commit c59277d4e6620c92476cb05ee075d7554f2ca540.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065587 - Implement picture-in-picture in GeckoView Example. r=ohall,geckoview-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit b36938fcaae6cf6e1f81f94f761a7b10c4cba011.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Keep the source tab alive while its video is in a picture-in-picture window. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall,kaya\"\n\nThis reverts commit b161794ba1253c1c78e6a390fd497998b02bc05c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Let the embedder report that it closed the picture-in-picture window itself. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\"\n\nThis reverts commit b0a195b8fa94bf96fe6a82e12a05feea0cfc9a92.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Tell the embedder when to close the picture-in-picture window. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 449b1d38b530c60e42bc866618a4cbd677a667cd.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Clone the video once the picture-in-picture window's session is ready. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\"\n\nThis reverts commit d43de2c17d065727d48ff330a533aebc736961d4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Ask the embedder to open a picture-in-picture window for a playing video. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 28900f6efec098f5afb657455aa902e5da39277c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065581 - Let a GeckoSession host a picture-in-picture player. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\"\n\nThis reverts commit fbb2189ae83f8c31eed10b8b9ca2f340ce539f5c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2065579 - Allow a GeckoSession to be opened in an existing browsing context group and content process. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall,jonalmeida\"\n\nThis reverts commit 141f1800dd0df237e97bb5428071eef3a4503033.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/TestSupportChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/background.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-api.js", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/web_extensions/test-support/test-schema.json", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/www/video_in_iframe.html", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/BaseSessionTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/GeckoViewTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/PictureInPictureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/SessionProcessPlacementTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/rule/GeckoSessionTestRule.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSessionSettings.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoView.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/PictureInPictureController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/GeckoViewActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PictureInPictureActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/PipSessionHolder.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/TabSessionManager.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPicturePlayerChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPicturePlayerParent.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/GeckoViewPictureInPictureSourceChild.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/actors/moz.build", "mobile/shared/chrome/geckoview/geckoview.js", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewPictureInPicture.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/moz.build", "toolkit/actors/PictureInPictureChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/themes/mobile/global/jar.mn"], "git_node": "8270d266283a02ce1c39601cb6cd4823164273ac", "git_parents": ["d8906019c89f43a6ab58522c0ca99a8f2eaddc8a"], "node": "5f784af4bfe620853844eb49d8222f3427a73fec", "parents": ["1bd64b21675dd806907c511753857194f7258004"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009308 - Update libcubeb to 2e87c633. r=cubeb-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332909\n", "files": ["media/libcubeb/moz.yaml", "media/libcubeb/src/cubeb-jni-instances.h", "media/libcubeb/src/cubeb-jni.cpp", "media/libcubeb/src/cubeb-jni.h", "media/libcubeb/src/cubeb_opensl.cpp"], "git_node": "0d39b06f9c3b8d37fa78ffab5d1a1996881b8bfa", "git_parents": ["8270d266283a02ce1c39601cb6cd4823164273ac"], "node": "02e62bf72d5cc26ace4546fc7cb4387852b86143", "parents": ["5f784af4bfe620853844eb49d8222f3427a73fec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2009308 - Stop hardcoding cubeb's preferred sample rate and min latency for isolated content processes. r=geckoview-reviewers,cubeb-reviewers,padenot,ohall\n\nOn Android, CubebUtils.cpp calls\nGeckoAppShell.getAudioOutputFramesPerBuffer() and\nGeckoAppShell.getAudioOutputSampleRate() rather than\ncubeb_get_min_latency() and cubeb_get_preferred_sample_rate()\nrespectively. These usually call Android AudioManager APIs, which\nwould result in security exceptions being thrown in isolated\nprocesses. To avoid this, we currently hardcode return values rather\nthan query AudioManager when in an isolated process.\n\nThis patch avoids using hardcoded values by removing the\nandroid-specific path altogether, instead calling the cubeb functions\nas we do on other platforms. Cubeb's AAudio backend already\nimplemented these correctly, and the previous commit updated cubeb to\nimplement them for the OpenSL backend. This uses JNI to query the same\nAudioManager APIs previously called by GeckoAppShell. Thanks to\nAudioIPC, however, these calls are now made in the parent process,\nthereby avoiding the security exceptions.\n\nNote the Android-specific GetCubebMTGLatencyInFrames() implementation\nadditionally ensured the returned value was a minimum of 1024. This is\nno longer required as AudioIPC threads are now scheduled at real-time\npriority, so has been dropped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332484\n", "files": ["dom/media/CubebUtils.cpp", "dom/media/CubebUtils.h", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java"], "git_node": "1d3843d9948dbde57cf8138cd19aac1307ab1cf4", "git_parents": ["0d39b06f9c3b8d37fa78ffab5d1a1996881b8bfa"], "node": "f1cb965b2a0b18685fd64853aca96a60564e5118", "parents": ["02e62bf72d5cc26ace4546fc7cb4387852b86143"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079096 - Only promote rounded clips with a single non-zero corner radius to compositor clips. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nCoreAnimation can only apply one corner radius to a selection of corners, so\nNativeLayerCA used the largest radius for all of them. Compositor clip\npromotion relied on can_use_fast_path_in, which stopped requiring uniform\nradii in bug 1932736, so clips with mixed radii were being promoted once\nbug 1970028 enabled rounded compositor clips globally.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332764\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/rounded_rect_intersect.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/rounded_rect_intersect_mixed.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/per-corner-radius.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/single-radius-zero-corners-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/single-radius-zero-corners.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/two-clips-combined.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs"], "git_node": "f8537c10decfc38f4635ea3214eb829576755910", "git_parents": ["1d3843d9948dbde57cf8138cd19aac1307ab1cf4"], "node": "9bc3b3cfa8f87456293fdfd251c0846bcc27e68a", "parents": ["f1cb965b2a0b18685fd64853aca96a60564e5118"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080943 - Avoid some includes in PrintTargetSkPdf.h. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThis will be necessary when we remove PrintTargetPDF, and in general\nmakes the code a bit easier to reason about and less dependent on skia\nheaders.\n\nThe macOS change uses the same style as we use on windows / gtk.\n\nNo intended behavior change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332995\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.cpp", "gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.h", "widget/cocoa/nsDeviceContextSpecX.mm"], "git_node": "f62c1bdc233291dbcd7279060e5d3a871e6752e8", "git_parents": ["f8537c10decfc38f4635ea3214eb829576755910"], "node": "3843b60c02654379ea1636f12057934b31faa438", "parents": ["9bc3b3cfa8f87456293fdfd251c0846bcc27e68a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080102 r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332364\n", "files": ["image/AutoRestoreSVGState.h", "image/SVGDocumentWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "3a6acbe1080b01e8b390b7fecdf9696b6a50c914", "git_parents": ["f62c1bdc233291dbcd7279060e5d3a871e6752e8"], "node": "f58b10f0b57e085ca084648a3919320a3aee83b4", "parents": ["3843b60c02654379ea1636f12057934b31faa438"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074177 - Smart Window Monitor toolbar panel with HCM enabled r=ngrato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332907\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-panel/agent-monitor-panel.css"], "git_node": "33a1a2dcdfb28b06275b5b5afededa86abe3842a", "git_parents": ["3a6acbe1080b01e8b390b7fecdf9696b6a50c914"], "node": "796d9079e9f06414b39cb59bb107bfb28590998f", "parents": ["f58b10f0b57e085ca084648a3919320a3aee83b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072931 - Show the Google Lens button again when the search widget is redrawn. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332969\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/search/SearchWidgetProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/widget/SearchWidgetProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "66785ca21729d52638e54f852ba5bad028197669", "git_parents": ["33a1a2dcdfb28b06275b5b5afededa86abe3842a"], "node": "8ab1676a06a118ce55ab369d9ed1fda4c22f927f", "parents": ["796d9079e9f06414b39cb59bb107bfb28590998f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077880 [Linux][Vulkan Video] Keep H.264 DRM modifiers with height 1 on Blackwell with NVIDIA driver 610 or older. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nWhen codec is H264, on Blackwell with driver 610 or older, use DRM modifiers with height 1 to avoid corruption.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333028\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "7a9e93c429a1e26a7ca0715782792d9f948bf844", "git_parents": ["66785ca21729d52638e54f852ba5bad028197669"], "node": "5b5888c58f3f818fa4a03d48102a1cd8fb23481e", "parents": ["8ab1676a06a118ce55ab369d9ed1fda4c22f927f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vasish Baungally \u003cvbaungally@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079838 - Add Nimbus Preferences for Non-EN ATG Locales. r=Mardak\n\nThis patch only adds the Nimbus Preferences for non-en locales. A\nsubsequent patch will be created for handling model changes required\nas well as enabling for FR locale.\n\nThe functionality remains the same as before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332131\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGroupingSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_model.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_AutoTabGrouping.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "65ae946bb84af2bf6f64da19b5e162729c562ed1", "git_parents": ["7a9e93c429a1e26a7ca0715782792d9f948bf844"], "node": "2ef4c2cc9c7273b08d1fcd942229630dd0c540cb", "parents": ["5b5888c58f3f818fa4a03d48102a1cd8fb23481e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vasish Baungally \u003cvbaungally@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079849 - Add Handling for ATG non-EN Models. r=jlewis\n\nThis patch adds handling for non-EN locales for various models for ATG and\nenables FR expansion (adds fr to\nbrowser.smartwindow.autoTabGrouping.supportedLocales). The topic model\nfallback works only for English, so we only use the LLM for non-EN (FR). The\nclustering model is still being used.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332449\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGroupingSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_AutoTabGrouping.js"], "git_node": "25eac96b9ccdac240a2183263b6f84716884154e", "git_parents": ["65ae946bb84af2bf6f64da19b5e162729c562ed1"], "node": "29697ad915fec8dc404f5e4e791cac70e765cf38", "parents": ["2ef4c2cc9c7273b08d1fcd942229630dd0c540cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2078462 - Intern rectangles in the display list builder r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing mda crashes at mozglue_static\n\nThis reverts commit d8906019c89f43a6ab58522c0ca99a8f2eaddc8a.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "468f1edeaa346cbf2d27c921ce0ffa2420b02b39", "git_parents": ["25eac96b9ccdac240a2183263b6f84716884154e"], "node": "fd966ad73701020ad770e0983f1885ec107634eb", "parents": ["29697ad915fec8dc404f5e4e791cac70e765cf38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080641 - More consistently deal with FontFaceSet promise resolution. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,boris\" for causign mochitest failures @RecursiveMutex.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 98c0c12d84b12c97053201d3da478bb4856d926a.\n", "files": ["layout/style/FontFaceImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.h", "layout/style/FontFaceSetDocumentImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.h"], "git_node": "32451a79c238457fd30782f5b877f245631f9b98", "git_parents": ["468f1edeaa346cbf2d27c921ce0ffa2420b02b39"], "node": "baeaedbc243d61dece617c09f241148c5e95d517", "parents": ["fd966ad73701020ad770e0983f1885ec107634eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080943 - Avoid some includes in PrintTargetSkPdf.h. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for casuing wp failures.\n\nThis reverts commit f62c1bdc233291dbcd7279060e5d3a871e6752e8.\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.cpp", "gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.h", "widget/cocoa/nsDeviceContextSpecX.mm"], "git_node": "d67360df9fcbcc01c94cc94fbb73a294499af649", "git_parents": ["32451a79c238457fd30782f5b877f245631f9b98"], "node": "8053955bb2360e6e035e679c2ccc30fa9895c8d2", "parents": ["baeaedbc243d61dece617c09f241148c5e95d517"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074363 - The Add page button from the Monitor panel should not be displayed when there are 5 pages added r=yjamora\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332246\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js"], "git_node": "72dcb403e85b2ba4a9e89807b432dc4eb818f806", "git_parents": ["d67360df9fcbcc01c94cc94fbb73a294499af649"], "node": "a9902b21ce71f347e5aeb5ccc75e2f45f4d75e88", "parents": ["8053955bb2360e6e035e679c2ccc30fa9895c8d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1610213 - Annotate crash reports with what happens while InitializeMacApp() spins its run loop. r=emilio,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nSince bug 2055233 the startup run loop in InitializeMacApp() runs until the\nfirst idle instead of stopping in applicationDidFinishLaunching. Some reports\nshow the main thread still waiting in that loop when the user quits, but\nneither forcing a nested loop into it nor plain startups reproduce that.\n\nRecord the delegate callbacks, the observer firing and the stop together with\nthe run loop wake-ups in a MacStartupRunLoop annotation while the loop runs,\nand remove it once the loop returns. Early beta or earlier only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330481\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/CrashAnnotations.yaml", "toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.mm"], "git_node": "81faa8053892394dff4d8da5208beeec9e488a21", "git_parents": ["72dcb403e85b2ba4a9e89807b432dc4eb818f806"], "node": "23547174c5737723e6107f6d8fd86823f995c49d", "parents": ["a9902b21ce71f347e5aeb5ccc75e2f45f4d75e88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julie De Lorenzo \u003cjdelorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067130 - Surface error messages to the user r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,matt-tighe,parker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332250\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/ListenSheet.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayPauseButton.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlaybackControls.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlaybackUiState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayerCompact.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayerExpanded.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/VoiceSelection.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/ListenSheetTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlaybackUiStateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/listentopage/ListenSheetIntegration.kt"], "git_node": "8efd66b2b457265acca4e07f1e0f72c702a952a7", "git_parents": ["81faa8053892394dff4d8da5208beeec9e488a21"], "node": "f6f082dfa4b7394426427117b075a93752d95997", "parents": ["23547174c5737723e6107f6d8fd86823f995c49d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063414 - Improve PDF Tool Hide/Show Speed on Navigation r=android-reviewers,kaya\n\nPatch clears `isPdf` preemtively on page load change. The previous behavior could sometimes have the PDF toolbar linger too long on the next page for slow navigations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328569\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/reducer/ContentStateReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/ContentActionTest.kt"], "git_node": "559146bfbb7bfeedce97c4aaf7fcc1ea11fdafbb", "git_parents": ["8efd66b2b457265acca4e07f1e0f72c702a952a7"], "node": "7b030c3466dbc6e94817e5520506570a61383906", "parents": ["f6f082dfa4b7394426427117b075a93752d95997"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Peterson \u003ccpeterson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080697 - Use an explicit null check in SupportsInterface for C++23 compatibility. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nC++23 treats the returned local nsCOMPtr as an xvalue, selecting its\ndeleted rvalue pointer conversion. Compare against nullptr instead\nto return whether QueryInterface succeeded.\n\nerror: conversion function from 'const nsCOMPtr\u003cT\u003e' to 'T *' invokes a deleted function\n|   operator T*() const&& = delete;\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332800\n", "files": ["dom/navigation/Navigation.cpp"], "git_node": "61ff89cffd4be032b0307e1a3fbe3cd2900a0c96", "git_parents": ["559146bfbb7bfeedce97c4aaf7fcc1ea11fdafbb"], "node": "169ee71a6842956d013285c88891db1e0e370731", "parents": ["7b030c3466dbc6e94817e5520506570a61383906"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080978 - Move ANGLE vendoring README into Firefox Source Docs. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333038\n", "files": ["gfx/angle/README.md", "gfx/docs/VendoringANGLE.md", "gfx/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "05bb68aa64fad84b203c6e2944fe0dadae861727", "git_parents": ["61ff89cffd4be032b0307e1a3fbe3cd2900a0c96"], "node": "0699b4f64940a1117cc9e10e767f9be503ec9e21", "parents": ["169ee71a6842956d013285c88891db1e0e370731"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080981 - Add section for testing after vendoring ANGLE. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333040\n", "files": ["gfx/docs/VendoringANGLE.md"], "git_node": "e0a5beeaef81ed3178a7593dc3a8f7dafd499190", "git_parents": ["05bb68aa64fad84b203c6e2944fe0dadae861727"], "node": "679c32786bfe1526bcb4ab7520b7a4c1fc5467c0", "parents": ["0699b4f64940a1117cc9e10e767f9be503ec9e21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1959947 - Fix and re-enable browser_bouncetracking_tab_close.js for BTP stateless mode. r=manuel\n\nBTP sets the record's final host on the parent's top level STATE_STOP, which\ncan arrive after the content load event. The test closed the tab in between,\nso the destination was classified too. Wait for STATE_STOP before closing, and\nadd a task covering a tab closed while the destination is still loading, where\nclassifying the destination is expected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332940\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_tab_close.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/file_stalled_load.sjs", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "e77059b154691ae9a4feb8433bc3642dd507aabb", "git_parents": ["e0a5beeaef81ed3178a7593dc3a8f7dafd499190"], "node": "88ff68653270f2bf15375c7e924a93b3337930dd", "parents": ["679c32786bfe1526bcb4ab7520b7a4c1fc5467c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079897 - Update libyuv to 9456b062277d2809c97f4633c116ffa8d485afdd r=ng\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332151\n", "files": ["media/libyuv/libyuv/BUILD.gn", "media/libyuv/libyuv/CMakeLists.txt", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/compare_row.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/rotate_row.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/row.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/scale_row.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/libyuv.gyp", "media/libyuv/libyuv/libyuv.gypi", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/compare.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/compare_wasm.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/convert.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/convert_argb.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/convert_from.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/convert_from_argb.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/convert_to_argb.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/mjpeg_decoder.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/planar_functions.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/rotate.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/rotate_any.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/rotate_argb.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/rotate_wasm.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_any.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_gcc.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_neon.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_neon64.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_rvv.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_wasm.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/row_win.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_any.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_argb.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_common.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_rvv.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_uv.cc", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/scale_wasm.cc", "media/libyuv/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "71f05a4ba96fd13b6306c4bf04827abc55613dc7", "git_parents": ["e77059b154691ae9a4feb8433bc3642dd507aabb"], "node": "7cf49355296a5d49c8ffcad8c00eaf424c26ad1c", "parents": ["88ff68653270f2bf15375c7e924a93b3337930dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079897 - Apply mozilla patches for libyuv r=ng\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332152\n", "files": ["media/libyuv/libyuv/include/libyuv/row.h", "media/libyuv/libyuv/libyuv.gyp", "media/libyuv/libyuv/libyuv.gypi", "media/libyuv/libyuv/source/mjpeg_decoder.cc"], "git_node": "a3d005e0b7a3fa2fedae396e3f9006adbe3184dd", "git_parents": ["71f05a4ba96fd13b6306c4bf04827abc55613dc7"], "node": "639b6187a7ef9e8e468318fccec70942b5f432e1", "parents": ["7cf49355296a5d49c8ffcad8c00eaf424c26ad1c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068721 - Re-order newtab settings in about:preferences r=fluent-reviewers,maxx,bolsson\n\nThe Firefox Home section of `about:preferences#home` has been\nreordered to match the new design, and the per-widget toggles have\nbeen replaced with a \"Manage widgets\" link to\n`about:home#customize-widgets`, which the Base component now handles.\nMirroring the behaviour on the Customize panel, the link is hidden\nwhen the \"Widgets\" toggle is off.\n\nWith Nova on, Weather has its own row only when the widgets container\nis hidden; without Nova it keeps its row, as before. `prefsL10nId` and\nthe nine per-widget settings strings have been removed, and the new\nlink label is migrated from the Customize panel's \"Manage widgets\"\nbutton.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332817\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_both_off.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_tabs_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_windows_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_tab.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_window.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets_2.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2068721_newtab_manage_widgets_link.py"], "git_node": "064024f09721efa409141cd9e1e4fab38d592cde", "git_parents": ["a3d005e0b7a3fa2fedae396e3f9006adbe3184dd"], "node": "90a64774c96b43e8083d46c41136d812ec9f72b2", "parents": ["639b6187a7ef9e8e468318fccec70942b5f432e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071293 - Tell the documentation skill to check what a page claims against the code. r=sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332952\n", "files": [".agents/skills/documentation/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/documentation/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "c8641a25d99b4dc57715b11b7c59da69eb73ab94", "git_parents": ["064024f09721efa409141cd9e1e4fab38d592cde"], "node": "33bec123f2a84279fc6713003373c8e4320811ca", "parents": ["90a64774c96b43e8083d46c41136d812ec9f72b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079953 - Use `useWidgetTelemetry` in the Focus Timer widget. r=fchasen\n\nFocusTimer now uses `useWidgetTelemetry` for impressions and actions, like Weather. The hook still sends the legacy `WIDGETS_TIMER_*` events alongside the unified ones.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332521\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FocusTimer/FocusTimer.jsx"], "git_node": "94a3cd8c7744b72adb361745913be6c729496ce3", "git_parents": ["c8641a25d99b4dc57715b11b7c59da69eb73ab94"], "node": "a0d5f81cbf16f63a7acf9a558e449e57a0d0921d", "parents": ["33bec123f2a84279fc6713003373c8e4320811ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078941: Don't bother looking up PDF ids when it isn't useful. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331485\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "bee9cfa4bdb986b081bfa264282b202a96343910", "git_parents": ["94a3cd8c7744b72adb361745913be6c729496ce3"], "node": "f5e07a86b996081e774b8889868ba124345e1d57", "parents": ["a0d5f81cbf16f63a7acf9a558e449e57a0d0921d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076741 - Run WPT reftests/crashtests on GeckoView with fission. r=geckoview-reviewers,owlish\n\nAlso, no fission should be tier 2 and mozilla-central push only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331624\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-position/sticky/position-sticky-fractional-offset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.discrete.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.gamma.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.identity.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.linear.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/filters/2d.filter.canvasFilterObject.componentTransfer.table.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/text/canvas.2d.offscreen.worker.direction.html.ini"], "git_node": "4876ddadc46d511b9a593a149f8f0879b3d38efe", "git_parents": ["bee9cfa4bdb986b081bfa264282b202a96343910"], "node": "5136252856308f6c2b6b0d33fa399d59914ff664", "parents": ["f5e07a86b996081e774b8889868ba124345e1d57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1610213 - Annotate crash reports with what happens while InitializeMacApp() spins its run loop. r=emilio,crashreporting-reviewers\" for causing massive failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 81faa8053892394dff4d8da5208beeec9e488a21.\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/CrashAnnotations.yaml", "toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.mm"], "git_node": "53b0c1b254d9a4161354c139a2508df97e52907a", "git_parents": ["4876ddadc46d511b9a593a149f8f0879b3d38efe"], "node": "aa10d492865df55ab641a3ba3d4cc6830f97ef9c", "parents": ["5136252856308f6c2b6b0d33fa399d59914ff664"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Micah Killoran \u003cmtigley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079009 - Don't save the security code once it is unchecked in the credit card doorhanger. r=dimi\n\nThe security codes checkbox only turned off the CVV pref, so the record that\nwas captured while the pref was on still saved its security code. Leave the\nsecurity code out of the record to save when the pref is off, so that a new\ncard is saved without one and an update keeps the stored one.\n\nDepends on D331452\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331468\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_doorhanger_cvv.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "96b24c5931e6b9fd3f735b30f13731d3f189f342", "git_parents": ["53b0c1b254d9a4161354c139a2508df97e52907a"], "node": "003cf443778751eb1c5997bb964353a2f672427f", "parents": ["aa10d492865df55ab641a3ba3d4cc6830f97ef9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu/src/main/res/values-fa/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/pwa/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fa/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-is/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml"], "git_node": "9b374d1e6ad145bfbf3582afd30f661de187f072", "git_parents": ["96b24c5931e6b9fd3f735b30f13731d3f189f342"], "node": "87b3eed44aebea67eade70561e7a97feae5a6d38", "parents": ["003cf443778751eb1c5997bb964353a2f672427f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2068721 - Re-order newtab settings in about:preferences r=fluent-reviewers,maxx,bolsson\" for causing bc failures @browser_policy_firefoxhome.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 064024f09721efa409141cd9e1e4fab38d592cde.\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_both_off.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_tabs_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_windows_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_tab.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_window.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets_2.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2068721_newtab_manage_widgets_link.py"], "git_node": "38fb93e12efe9daa9e1dedfbc1f693b000f0c7b8", "git_parents": ["9b374d1e6ad145bfbf3582afd30f661de187f072"], "node": "ff772544924fd6ab50a0c0c67e70e3b2a4212334", "parents": ["87b3eed44aebea67eade70561e7a97feae5a6d38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073686 - Block scripts on ScrollbarActivity::BeginFade(). r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330626\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollbarActivity.cpp"], "git_node": "6772a78a107a79e9e8b181a1bd528364beaf3202", "git_parents": ["38fb93e12efe9daa9e1dedfbc1f693b000f0c7b8"], "node": "13992a42ca61c0853adf258bab2adc5b46cd137f", "parents": ["ff772544924fd6ab50a0c0c67e70e3b2a4212334"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cpchimento@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076943 - Write number directly into Latin1 StringBuilder in NumberValueToStringBuilder. r=iain\n\nWe can save some cycles in JSON.stringify() (as well as Array.p.join(),\netc.) by using the StringBuilder's buffer as the int32-to-string or\ndouble-to-string converter's buffer directly, if the StringBuilder has\nLatin1 chars. Previously, we'd write the string into a C string and then\ncopy that into the StringBuilder.\n\nI tried a few different ways of writing this and I think creating new\nversions of Int32ToCString, FracNumberToCString, and NumberToCString is\nprobably the cleanest way to go.\n\nI measured this on microbenchmarks of NumberValueToStringBuilder with\ndifferent sets of NumberValues, on 1-byte and 2-byte StringBuilders,\neither pre-reserved or not. 2-byte StringBuilders are unaffected, as\nyou might expect. 1-byte StringBuilders are improved in both\ncases (pre-reserved or not). The improvement is about 2-5 ns per\noperation in each case, and the percentage depends on how much of the\ntime the copy took up in the first place, about 5-20%.\n\nThe thing that microbenchmarks are probably not measuring is whether\nthere are any common workloads where the overallocate+write+shrink\ntechnique prematurely forces any StringBuilder from inline to\nheap-allocated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330072\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Number.cpp", "js/src/util/StringBuilder.h"], "git_node": "a7003ed0dbda6d845f4599e775999fe9f968a81a", "git_parents": ["6772a78a107a79e9e8b181a1bd528364beaf3202"], "node": "d3410503aae440fe9b62bd8f5cec7494defebac8", "parents": ["13992a42ca61c0853adf258bab2adc5b46cd137f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cpchimento@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076943 - Pre-count actual integer digits for AppendInt32ToStringBuilder. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nA pathological case in the previous commit is:\n\n    [\"a\".repeat(70), 1].join(\"\")\n\nBecause of overallocating to the maximum number length and then\nshrinking after writing the number to the buffer, we may force the\nStringBuilder to heap-allocate its buffer where otherwise it would have\nstayed inline.\n\nTurns out, it's not expensive to count the number of decimal digits in a\n32-bit integer:\n\nhttps://commaok.xyz/post/lookup_tables/\nhttps://lemire.me/blog/2025/01/07/counting-the-digits-of-64-bit-integers/\n\nSo we can just allocate the right number of digits in the first place,\nand avoid shrinking at the end.\n\nA similar pathological case still exists for writing non-int32-valued\nNumbers, which this patch does not affect.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331871\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Number.cpp"], "git_node": "3b50a44b3720111f696c6d41c0cea0aef341a957", "git_parents": ["a7003ed0dbda6d845f4599e775999fe9f968a81a"], "node": "35ad31009294bd383c96e63b18c5c0b76523648c", "parents": ["d3410503aae440fe9b62bd8f5cec7494defebac8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cpchimento@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076943 - Fall back to NumberValueToStringBuilder slow path if buffer would reallocate. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nCheck whether the StringBuilder's buffer would have to reallocate if we\ndid the direct-write trick. If it would, fall back to the old code,\nwhere we copy the string into the buffer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332222\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Number.cpp", "js/src/util/StringBuilder.h"], "git_node": "798b4111016b3c18b4a27412e9c8e976b476d5d6", "git_parents": ["3b50a44b3720111f696c6d41c0cea0aef341a957"], "node": "c12316bffa4103704e7da7934baac9c954b7c67a", "parents": ["35ad31009294bd383c96e63b18c5c0b76523648c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076943: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Number.cpp"], "git_node": "416d69d0912da45f90504e70593d252957fd8257", "git_parents": ["798b4111016b3c18b4a27412e9c8e976b476d5d6"], "node": "571af50048bcf47c603dc74bf2651cc8d607777f", "parents": ["c12316bffa4103704e7da7934baac9c954b7c67a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Grunbaum \u003cngrunbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080949 - set maintainer-phab: #webrtc-reviewers for libgbm;r=webrtc-reviewers,dbaker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333006\n", "files": ["third_party/gbm/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "ed5ba68994709a02ac7cc36f9d4fa375cbb0f82a", "git_parents": ["416d69d0912da45f90504e70593d252957fd8257"], "node": "62a1a5741e54a11193a3ef9822c5378c475c63e1", "parents": ["571af50048bcf47c603dc74bf2651cc8d607777f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Osmond Arnesto \u003coarnesto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022988 - Update toolbarbutton-icons.css to pass use-design-tokens r=desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,jules,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329028\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css", "stylelint-rollouts.config.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.tokens.json"], "git_node": "013a96bc7bcb6b889ca3338877809fc806a51350", "git_parents": ["ed5ba68994709a02ac7cc36f9d4fa375cbb0f82a"], "node": "7c97f40e03f4933389b39542b9e3ee56a44990c3", "parents": ["62a1a5741e54a11193a3ef9822c5378c475c63e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068721 - Re-order newtab settings in about:preferences r=fluent-reviewers,maxx,bolsson\n\nThe Firefox Home section of `about:preferences#home` has been\nreordered to match the new design, and the per-widget toggles have\nbeen replaced with a \"Manage widgets\" link to\n`about:home#customize-widgets`, which the Base component now handles.\nMirroring the behaviour on the Customize panel, the link is hidden\nwhen the \"Widgets\" toggle is off.\n\nWith Nova on, Weather has its own row only when the widgets container\nis hidden; without Nova it keeps its row, as before. `prefsL10nId` and\nthe nine per-widget settings strings have been removed, and the new\nlink label is migrated from the Customize panel's \"Manage widgets\"\nbutton.\n\nThe enterprise policy test for `FirefoxHome.Widgets.Blocked` now looks\nfor the blocked widget's toggle in the Customize panel, since settings\nno longer has per-widget toggles. The new link can open the \"Manage\nwidgets\" subpanel as the page loads, before the Customize panel checks\nfor locked prefs. To keep a blocked widget's toggle disabled in that\ncase, each toggle in the subpanel now applies the lock itself.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332817\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_firefoxhome.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_both_off.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_tabs_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_disabled_windows_on.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_tab.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_manage_widgets_opens_in_window.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home_widgets_2.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Nova/CustomizeMenu/WidgetsManagementPanel/WidgetsManagementPanel.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2068721_newtab_manage_widgets_link.py"], "git_node": "2eb39c91aa137483ecb8bafca2be0b8248265985", "git_parents": ["013a96bc7bcb6b889ca3338877809fc806a51350"], "node": "98f8e0a92a4a0a3768e057352718f897e6a6083f", "parents": ["7c97f40e03f4933389b39542b9e3ee56a44990c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079821 [wpt PR 63376] - Sanitizer: move parseHTML noscript tests into html5lib testcases, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSanitizer: move parseHTML noscript tests into html5lib testcases (#63376)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6ed734b654aa1dba8b6ee0274297dedc231156d\nwpt-pr: 63376\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/parsehtml-noscript.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-parseHTML.html"], "git_node": "798df143caa9cf37344a68dd41d955758e3d28b6", "git_parents": ["2eb39c91aa137483ecb8bafca2be0b8248265985"], "node": "fe54648402e52dc9583bd5457d3d89836b20c153", "parents": ["98f8e0a92a4a0a3768e057352718f897e6a6083f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079413 [wpt PR 63345] - [chromium-bidi] Fix element clip screenshot in scrolled viewport, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Fix element clip screenshot in scrolled viewport\n\n- Fix browsingContext.captureScreenshot with an element clip when the\n  page is scrolled, and add WPT test_clip_element_scroll_to.\n- Previously, #parseRect returned viewport-relative coordinates from\n  getBoundingClientRect() without adding the visual viewport scroll\n  offset, causing incorrect clipping or zero-dimension intersection\n  errors after scrolling.\n- Add visualViewport.pageLeft and visualViewport.pageTop to the element\n  bounding box to convert it to document coordinates per the WebDriver\n  BiDi specification.\n\nBug: 418765619\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: Ia0c25a27d0b36e30ede590d270c54f3e4ad4fe8e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520000\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714239}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 579fb95a4e5c283a1688220cb6fbafc862fd9758\nwpt-pr: 63345\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/capture_screenshot/clip.py"], "git_node": "072fa29099a13e6401aaaa6210aef987064c1857", "git_parents": ["798df143caa9cf37344a68dd41d955758e3d28b6"], "node": "68ec00744c4aadfb17bb2394ebb5fa4019a23c5c", "parents": ["fe54648402e52dc9583bd5457d3d89836b20c153"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079856 [wpt PR 63372] - Allowing declarative shadow roots should be scoped to the stream parser, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAllowing declarative shadow roots should be scoped to the stream parser\n\nInstead of calling Document::setAllowDeclarativeShadowRoots(true) on the\ntarget document in HTMLStream::Create (which leaked declarative shadow\nroot allowance to subsequent innerHTML and document.write() calls),\nenable include_shadow_roots on HTMLDocumentParser when\nroot_insertion_point is non-null.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: Ie7f034c85ffe24978d276a3878543b55c44d1757\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8498304\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714256}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 86e886fcd09ab67eb387f9f3f28d62d348a7865f\nwpt-pr: 63372\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-declarative-shadow-root.html"], "git_node": "c2f6b9b9aa4c0aaa4a30b7f497ba625382b0dab5", "git_parents": ["072fa29099a13e6401aaaa6210aef987064c1857"], "node": "5362c00da406f3a7109301bfda4d3b0a4c3e393d", "parents": ["68ec00744c4aadfb17bb2394ebb5fa4019a23c5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079856 [wpt PR 63372] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63372\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-with-declarative-shadow-root.html.ini"], "git_node": "2f28f8eea80719c41255807c78c77b4c41a12381", "git_parents": ["c2f6b9b9aa4c0aaa4a30b7f497ba625382b0dab5"], "node": "a4938d6928c7b86a2a369a442419673de06862d2", "parents": ["5362c00da406f3a7109301bfda4d3b0a4c3e393d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079940 [wpt PR 63382] - Fix custom element registry selection in HTMLStream::Create, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix custom element registry selection in HTMLStream::Create\n\nIn HTMLStream::Create:\n- Use shadow-\u003ecustomElementRegistry() when the target is a ShadowRoot\n  instead of using the shadow host's registry.\n- Keep registry as nullptr when the target is a \u003ctemplate\u003e content\n  DocumentFragment so top-level custom elements are not constructed in\n  the inert template document.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: Ifb71a5c7149d2c008c940b35d68a0ebb58370116\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8505239\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714260}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5adcbf6d673b077b57f551feeb1f1ab25f0919b7\nwpt-pr: 63382\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element.html"], "git_node": "e009f4663ebc095c01bab30f381ac7a30b4e0978", "git_parents": ["2f28f8eea80719c41255807c78c77b4c41a12381"], "node": "d9066d2f1c168a279d7808eb6a1e0ba29c239fdb", "parents": ["a4938d6928c7b86a2a369a442419673de06862d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079940 [wpt PR 63382] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63382\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-custom-element.html.ini"], "git_node": "c70c4b09f15e57228c0d08cb292db6e6ecfe5e52", "git_parents": ["e009f4663ebc095c01bab30f381ac7a30b4e0978"], "node": "364c9e0bbc3a0904a4591d3d800d749605b59964", "parents": ["d9066d2f1c168a279d7808eb6a1e0ba29c239fdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Rego \u003crego@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076734 [wpt PR 63093] - [aamtests] Adding new tests for \u003cabbr\u003e element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[aamtests] Adding new tests for \u003cabbr\u003e element (#63093)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0962bf0b291f0077095d4ba519194e6b535d79c0\nwpt-pr: 63093\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/aamtests/element/abbr.py"], "git_node": "2162a05eca18c2e5f45c539c8a252a0906c5bf2a", "git_parents": ["c70c4b09f15e57228c0d08cb292db6e6ecfe5e52"], "node": "23b2c15dc34ce733e77b304c443a97940b07e2dd", "parents": ["364c9e0bbc3a0904a4591d3d800d749605b59964"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080014 [wpt PR 63399] - Add bounds to LoAF style and layout durations, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd bounds to LoAF style and layout durations (#63399)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c8525d333367e1db0161011bce29a3f8333943d7\nwpt-pr: 63399\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-style-and-layout-duration-bounds.html"], "git_node": "70f92d97009dab5de301069d382f014961c90d0c", "git_parents": ["2162a05eca18c2e5f45c539c8a252a0906c5bf2a"], "node": "6c08279f671e1ce28c77537e1cfd6dc8552b0ada", "parents": ["23b2c15dc34ce733e77b304c443a97940b07e2dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ibrahim Bendebka \u003cibrahim.bendebka@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076481 [wpt PR 63052] - Fix corner-shape auto outline doubled offset and radii, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix corner-shape auto outline doubled offset and radii\n\nWhen an element had both `corner-shape` and `outline: auto`,\nchanging `outline-offset` resulted in a doubled offset and radii.\n\nThis occurred because the rect and radii used to define the\ncontour's origin_rect, were already outset adjusted.\n\nThis CL calculate the origin_rect radii from\nGetFocusRingCornerRadii at zero offset.\n\nBug: 556780780\nChange-Id: Id0516d151d383312278a69b7af68ada1fec6f0be\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8367406\nCommit-Queue: Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714279}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 04f9780fbf73b1630810aad450edbe7841d228c7\nwpt-pr: 63052\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-003.html"], "git_node": "723269485e58e9796e2a4c375f5c1902f4896b8b", "git_parents": ["70f92d97009dab5de301069d382f014961c90d0c"], "node": "cfd4ec369f6f463ca1329879f72fae41af201c8c", "parents": ["6c08279f671e1ce28c77537e1cfd6dc8552b0ada"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076481 [wpt PR 63052] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63052\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-auto-003.html.ini"], "git_node": "a06bc9ea4d7021875908886105b3825c902f3cba", "git_parents": ["723269485e58e9796e2a4c375f5c1902f4896b8b"], "node": "20d83de5913a0283b242241dada275ea139e937a", "parents": ["cfd4ec369f6f463ca1329879f72fae41af201c8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080016 [wpt PR 63401] - [chromium-bidi] Speed up pointer actions in input.performActions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Speed up pointer actions in input.performActions\n\n- Speed up pointer click and move actions in input.performActions by\n  ~3.4x (reducing 1000 clicks from ~16.7s to ~4.9s).\n- Previously, every input.performActions call evaluated\n  navigator.platform via CDP, scheduled setTimeout(0) on zero-duration\n  ticks, and awaited rAF-aligned CDP mouseMoved commands before sending\n  mousePressed, stalling each click on 60Hz VSync (~16.67ms).\n- Lazily evaluate and cache the macOS platform check only for keyDown\n  actions, skip setTimeout(0) on zero-duration ticks, and pipeline\n  subsequent non-move actions behind zero-duration hover mouseMoved\n  commands to flush the renderer event queue immediately.\n- Remove stale SlowTests entries and Chromium-only timeout=long metadata\n  for bidi/input/perform_actions WPTs, and update the\n  release_actions/queue.py expectation baselines.\n\nBug: 411434092\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I9317f17c6ab70b96e65b1b1286f42b51929bacbf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8522202\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714317}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: da1355b3fc629f97f8194884ab113da1ba3c7990\nwpt-pr: 63401\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/pointer_touch.py"], "git_node": "fb426d9df6b3ba09982b97f0dcc0bcb803c9336d", "git_parents": ["a06bc9ea4d7021875908886105b3825c902f3cba"], "node": "f1ba06d7c83b3def294e90be985583fcb1145650", "parents": ["20d83de5913a0283b242241dada275ea139e937a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080016 [wpt PR 63401] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63401\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/duration.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/key.py.ini"], "git_node": "c05b1e80bc5d8d7ae5fb4b63d11fce11eb4da59b", "git_parents": ["fb426d9df6b3ba09982b97f0dcc0bcb803c9336d"], "node": "05fea69fefae4b9147c5f67322dbd0fff019fe6d", "parents": ["f1ba06d7c83b3def294e90be985583fcb1145650"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080017 [wpt PR 63408] - Test moving element then using tree selects, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest moving element then using tree selectors (#63408)\n\nAlso test for moving an element into a display none tree.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b75d8b975a2dbcc731281ac0f5128365b8061f5\nwpt-pr: 63408\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-child-list-selector-invalidation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-into-display-none.html"], "git_node": "8e0312f6bd2ea2cc6c3e3f323160a1f46e6fd17f", "git_parents": ["c05b1e80bc5d8d7ae5fb4b63d11fce11eb4da59b"], "node": "30196756193706e65eb11826d992d3ab2d0a6223", "parents": ["05fea69fefae4b9147c5f67322dbd0fff019fe6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080017 [wpt PR 63408] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63408\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-child-list-selector-invalidation.html.ini"], "git_node": "6a297ca7a3fa864a03928b30f8205afa8bc78524", "git_parents": ["8e0312f6bd2ea2cc6c3e3f323160a1f46e6fd17f"], "node": "59973d7dc8686cdd87131beffbc6b59906e62050", "parents": ["30196756193706e65eb11826d992d3ab2d0a6223"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080020 [wpt PR 63407] - HTML parser: support #description in html5lib .dat tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML parser: support #description in html5lib .dat tests (#63407)\n\nA test may begin with a #description section, appended to its subtest name. Add descriptions to a few existing tests.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0e6e43503b0b00c8a5c8a69b1e0f3c634b14da76\nwpt-pr: 63407\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/README.md", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/search-element.dat", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/template.dat", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/test.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/tests19.dat", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/tests4.dat"], "git_node": "d9d7150617bc4ce6c87accf497a3ab69e476b8ac", "git_parents": ["6a297ca7a3fa864a03928b30f8205afa8bc78524"], "node": "e1bb84a0b976b7cce94df3c09f28001115aba699", "parents": ["59973d7dc8686cdd87131beffbc6b59906e62050"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077698 [wpt PR 63220] - Ensure page has focus at the start of change-focus-again-in-blur-during-intercept.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure page has focus at the start of the test\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 47b65690f1690ed993c9465d0e6703a290025a4b\nwpt-pr: 63220\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/focus-reset/change-focus-again-in-blur-during-intercept.html"], "git_node": "0416ac34d829638b676701f91a0ae75d9354bb79", "git_parents": ["d9d7150617bc4ce6c87accf497a3ab69e476b8ac"], "node": "60270777c5d9214f73cf30ed47956a9638b1e183", "parents": ["e1bb84a0b976b7cce94df3c09f28001115aba699"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079279 [wpt PR 63333] - Remove void element end tags from security and loading WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove void element end tags from security and loading WPTs\n\nimg, input, link, meta, embed, source and area have no end tag. Writing\ntheir end tag anyway is a parse error, and the parser drops the tag, so\nthe source suggests a structure the document never had. This CL removes\nthese end tags from\nthird_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/content-security-policy and\nsome other WPT tests.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: I943e45528f1a57d2cbad7aeb0e4c3803fcc8289b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8226705\nReviewed-by: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1712686}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: beba5cfdc940c47113a1f68d52ba9c1414c7725f\nwpt-pr: 63333\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/FileAPI/url/url_createobjecturl_file_img-manual.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/object-src/object-src-url-embed-allowed-img-src-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/object-src/object-src-url-embed-allowed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/object-src/object-src-url-embed-blocked.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/scripthash-basic-blocked-error-event.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/scripthash-changed-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/scripthash-changed-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/scriptnonce-changed-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/scriptnonce-changed-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/customized-built-in-constructor-exceptions.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/registries/element-mutation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/ParentNode-querySelector-case-insensitive.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/getElementsByClassName-30.htm", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-timing-002.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/import-maps/acquiring/modulepreload.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/service-workers/service-worker/resources/embed-image-is-not-intercepted-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/service-workers/service-worker/resources/embed-is-not-intercepted-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/Document-execCommand.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/block-Document-execCommand.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/trusted-types-from-literal.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-nfc/resources/support-iframe.html"], "git_node": "ad0c863dc9a22cb4d6dfcdb3c4602118905bc1ab", "git_parents": ["0416ac34d829638b676701f91a0ae75d9354bb79"], "node": "99ecccce0c7491f0bb6bf891029b85e7f981f37a", "parents": ["60270777c5d9214f73cf30ed47956a9638b1e183"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079279 [wpt PR 63333] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63333\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/postmessage.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/ServiceWorkerGlobalScope/unregister.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "942758842d55477ac33b510f4d709dbcd28d9d7e", "git_parents": ["ad0c863dc9a22cb4d6dfcdb3c4602118905bc1ab"], "node": "8af6a331bb6ee869fc26d3c2fd04cbc540ea1408", "parents": ["99ecccce0c7491f0bb6bf891029b85e7f981f37a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076288 [wpt PR 63024] - Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nKeep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\n\nAnchor the wavy pattern at the start of the decorating box instead of\neach fragment's own origin, so the wave phase no longer restarts at\ninline element boundaries like a nested \u003cem\u003e. Behind the default-on\nWavyDecorationContinuousPhase runtime feature as a kill switch.\n\nBug: 41287729\nChange-Id: Ia6ec134cdab6bbb3d2f7f64b631bc499bd9f4a56\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8456548\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714354}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 29099a8c15ed232af88aa20ca411dafe9f062e7d\nwpt-pr: 63024\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/reference/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001.html"], "git_node": "dd2c4876518ef9ffdbda8979c9af4611cb232423", "git_parents": ["942758842d55477ac33b510f4d709dbcd28d9d7e"], "node": "5d4d4699af1e431831189d7530cec6c7afcd994e", "parents": ["8af6a331bb6ee869fc26d3c2fd04cbc540ea1408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076288 [wpt PR 63024] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63024\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text-decor/crashtests/pseudo-element-text-decoration-under-pseudo-first-line-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text-decor/crashtests/text-decoration-animation-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "212a22748bb3b93a1e5167e55e9ab3e93414fce7", "git_parents": ["dd2c4876518ef9ffdbda8979c9af4611cb232423"], "node": "6f78f82ff2323dedb2e96a325e7033958cacf465", "parents": ["5d4d4699af1e431831189d7530cec6c7afcd994e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sampath Samaraweera \u003csampath.samaraweera@codimite.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080030 [wpt PR 63406] - Invalidate shapes' percentage `stroke-dashoffset` on viewport resize, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInvalidate shapes' percentage `stroke-dashoffset` on viewport resize\n\nFollow-up to https://crrev.com/c/8361775, which added\n`stroke-dasharray` to the ComputeStrokeHasRelativeLengths() helper\nbut left out `stroke-dashoffset`.\n\nA shape whose only percentage-based stroke property is\n`stroke-dashoffset` was therefore never flagged as\nviewport-dependent, so the viewport-change handling in\nSVGContentContainer skipped re-laying it out and the dash phase\nkept its stale value until some unrelated relayout recomputed it.\n\nAdd the missing case to ComputeStrokeHasRelativeLengths(). The dash\noffset is already resolved against the current viewport at paint\ntime, in SVGLayoutSupport::ApplyStrokeStyleToStrokeData(), so\nflagging the dependency is all that is required.\n\nFixed: 560379373\nChange-Id: Ifa3a6128ef600637cf614a09f4b29b2b5ad3f1aa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8423508\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714371}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4c3ecfb79e5fa5afe249969a6185d6b8642ee061\nwpt-pr: 63406\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dashoffset-line-viewbox-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dashoffset-path-viewbox-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/svg-percent-stroke-dashoffset-rect-viewbox-update.html"], "git_node": "091c9449bfd66bf582a808b6f600e612b58c276c", "git_parents": ["212a22748bb3b93a1e5167e55e9ab3e93414fce7"], "node": "e2d6b59d91a8cc8b1eb91aebed03c5d4daf048b0", "parents": ["6f78f82ff2323dedb2e96a325e7033958cacf465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080032 [wpt PR 63416] - Fix assert message for block-ellipsis-036.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix assertion message for block-ellipsis-036.html (#63416)\n\nThe previous assertion had been copied off of `block-ellipsis-033` and not updated to match the test.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 88d9816e5022b8802a6bba34f3fd32ee0c2ee630\nwpt-pr: 63416\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-036.html"], "git_node": "49558f8f8996840a9322de3fb4c91dbbf273b4e5", "git_parents": ["091c9449bfd66bf582a808b6f600e612b58c276c"], "node": "69234b46d6b318cc2f5ef407e36f4c9976276146", "parents": ["e2d6b59d91a8cc8b1eb91aebed03c5d4daf048b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080032 [wpt PR 63416] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63416\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-040-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "2899fd06bccecc08cf3d823594dcfda997b16eea", "git_parents": ["49558f8f8996840a9322de3fb4c91dbbf273b4e5"], "node": "43d256955f37aed0df7bb6419708887a3d9513c1", "parents": ["69234b46d6b318cc2f5ef407e36f4c9976276146"], "tags": []}, {"author": "wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079993 [wpt PR 63391] - Update CODEOWNERS, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAutomated update of CODEOWNERS\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e8a0386e6c8ec97605ad9552d75eff44c129f05a\nwpt-pr: 63391\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/CODEOWNERS"], "git_node": "b036b38cc340f052298592398bf3a88630c1f762", "git_parents": ["2899fd06bccecc08cf3d823594dcfda997b16eea"], "node": "5b36b0534b4bf2938e1412aa532c1c812aefac66", "parents": ["43d256955f37aed0df7bb6419708887a3d9513c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079603 [wpt PR 63365] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326689, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo not deserialize Window and DedicatedWorker-only types in other workers\n\nWebCodecs types, MediaStreamTrack, MediaStreamTrackHandle,\nMediaSourceHandle, RTCEncodedAudioFrame and RTCEncodedVideoFrame are\n[Exposed=(Window,DedicatedWorker)], but posting one to a shared worker\nor service worker delivered it there. Use the generated exposure check\nfrom 322966@main for these serialization tags, through\nisInterfaceExposedInGlobalObject() from 322979@main, so that those\nmessages fail to deserialize and result in a messageerror event.\n\nThe interfaces' [EnabledBySetting] now also applies when deserializing.\n\nVideoFrame, AudioData, MediaStreamTrack and MediaSourceHandle already\nfailed to deserialize there whenever the message crossed processes, as\ntheir data is not encoded for IPC. A shared worker can share the page's\nprocess though, so that was not reliable. The new tests cover them too.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326689\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e7352ab6762e7cf7f473879e52737b6813886093\nwpt-pr: 63365\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/dedicated-worker/mediasource-worker-handle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/dedicated-worker/mediasource-worker-handle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-streams/MediaStreamTrack-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-streams/MediaStreamTrack-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/serialization-to-shared-and-service-workers-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/serialization-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html"], "git_node": "411f9c86586b117943995ee1a0ebf91240b2b999", "git_parents": ["b036b38cc340f052298592398bf3a88630c1f762"], "node": "a5214d56344f630d0f1af558900f4bf9e3a6c248", "parents": ["5b36b0534b4bf2938e1412aa532c1c812aefac66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079603 [wpt PR 63365] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63365\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/dedicated-worker/mediasource-worker-handle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-streams/MediaStreamTrack-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/image-decoder-disconnect-readable-stream-crash.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "3881b9f7b7600a83112b5929e2a6a2b68ef98a79", "git_parents": ["411f9c86586b117943995ee1a0ebf91240b2b999"], "node": "6914a99d2f2e49b68624e5849e118444c2ed35df", "parents": ["a5214d56344f630d0f1af558900f4bf9e3a6c248"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079999 [wpt PR 63393] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326672, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove internals.markContextAsInsecure()\n\ninternals.markContextAsInsecure() turned a document created as a secure\ncontext into a non-secure one, which cannot happen otherwise: an API that\nrequires a secure context is either exposed or not. It also changed state only\nin its own process, so with site isolation other processes still saw a secure\ncontext.\n\nTests now get a real non-secure context from the WPT server, as localhost is\npotentially trustworthy. Tests that need nothing WebKit-specific become\nweb-platform tests:\n- orientation-event/device-orientation-events-unavailable-on-insecure-origins.html\n  is imported and replaces http/tests/events/device-orientation-motion-*.\n- speech-api/SpeechRecognition-non-secure-context.http.html is new and replaces\n  http/wpt/mediastream/speechrecognition-insecure.html.\n  SpeechRecognitionResultList is still exposed in non-secure contexts.\n- html/cross-origin-opener-policy/non-secure-to-secure-context-navigation.https.html\n  moves from http/wpt. Its popup now starts at\n  get_host_info().UNAUTHENTICATED_ORIGIN and navigates itself to the secure page.\n\nThe tests for the login status API, getGamepads() and geolocation's console\nmessage move to http/wpt and run from get_host_info().UNAUTHENTICATED_ORIGIN.\nThe login status test now checks navigator.setStatus() and\nnavigator.isLoggedIn() instead of navigator.setLoggedIn(), which no longer\nexists.\n\nFour tests are removed, as imported WPTs already cover them from a non-secure\ncontext:\n- fast/web-share/share-canShare-insecure.html, by web-share/canShare-insecure.http.html\n  and web-share/share-securecontext.http.html.\n- http/tests/notifications/notification-in-non-secure-context.html, by\n  notifications/permissions-non-secure.html.\n- http/tests/workers/worker-iframe-owner-isSecureContext.html, by\n  secure-contexts/basic-dedicated-worker.html.\n- http/wpt/crypto/historical.html, by WebCryptoAPI/historical.any.html.\n\nThis also removes the SecurityOrigin and Document setters that only the hook\nused.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326672\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc1f41278c3cd1be0dc6eae467a14bdb0ecf4c3e\nwpt-pr: 63393\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/non-secure-to-secure-context-navigation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/resources/non-secure-to-secure-context-navigation-popup.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speech-api/SpeechRecognition-non-secure-context.http.html"], "git_node": "fadef83c3cf5d398b31f5d204946bab6d12920e7", "git_parents": ["3881b9f7b7600a83112b5929e2a6a2b68ef98a79"], "node": "923a09658c4b9580fc086b09bdae89efeb7c8e55", "parents": ["6914a99d2f2e49b68624e5849e118444c2ed35df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080038 [wpt PR 63409] - Fix scrollLeft-of-scroller-with-wider-scrollbar, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix scrollLeft-of-scroller-with-wider-scrollbar\n\nThe test passed on content_shell but not headless_shell because\ncontent_shell disabled overlay scrollbars. The maximum value for\nscrollLeft is scrollWidth - clientWidth. When tested with overlay\nscrollbars enabled, clientWidth is non-zero, which affects the\nlimit.\n\nBug: 570397389\nChange-Id: Id0a012534e2b36b8ead3ee906e1ff1867561f830\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8527466\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714448}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 43ef4ddccb4bfd1ca2194d0a9a7dc86f8b7ffb21\nwpt-pr: 63409\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/scrollLeft-of-scroller-with-wider-scrollbar.html"], "git_node": "d2914443a3a1462e72dc9328fba29303bd7d8c71", "git_parents": ["fadef83c3cf5d398b31f5d204946bab6d12920e7"], "node": "e0ee2769ffd2178777c6bab015e1691ffd167e34", "parents": ["923a09658c4b9580fc086b09bdae89efeb7c8e55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080038 [wpt PR 63409] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63409\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/scrollLeft-of-scroller-with-wider-scrollbar.html.ini"], "git_node": "82a2eea623c1f9c808814bc5c33718ea2f2cc422", "git_parents": ["d2914443a3a1462e72dc9328fba29303bd7d8c71"], "node": "8d0c43db9100c9cdbab579b194a447e182a6a13b", "parents": ["e0ee2769ffd2178777c6bab015e1691ffd167e34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Awogbemila \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080039 [wpt PR 63413] - Update animation when setting currentTime with null timeline, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate animation when setting currentTime with null timeline\n\nWhen an animation has no timeline, setting currentTime leaves the\nanimation outdated without an active timeline to tick it. This can leave\nthe animation outdated until a later lifecycle phase (such as Paint)\nlazily queries its state, triggering an on-demand timing update and\nstyle invalidation mid-paint.\n\nThis CL eagerly updates the timing model and invalidates the effect in\nAnimation::setCurrentTime when timeline_ is null, matching the behavior\nin Animation::setTimeline.\n\nBug: 567645136\nChange-Id: I5b977331b3670a9b9d88e744d6a58049388a5868\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8517898\nCommit-Queue: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714449}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e9d3a761e4514ff7b266982f617fa4bcea2f0e4c\nwpt-pr: 63413\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/crashtests/null-timeline-backdrop-filter-crash.html"], "git_node": "de04dc8c748a394e02ce67b9817e80b996902e03", "git_parents": ["82a2eea623c1f9c808814bc5c33718ea2f2cc422"], "node": "e7192e6c4a6cec86e9ab4e80a9a6eeaf5e483275", "parents": ["8d0c43db9100c9cdbab579b194a447e182a6a13b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079825 [wpt PR 63369] - Reorganize Payment Method Manifest WPT files by pipeline stage, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReorganize Payment Method Manifest WPT files by pipeline stage\n\nAlign Payment Method Manifest Web Platform Test filenames and test\ngrouping with the specification pipeline stages (PMI, PMM, and WAM):\n\n   - Rename wam-ingestion.https.window.js to\n     pmm-default-applications.https.window.js to reflect that it tests\n     validation and parsing of the default_applications member of the\n     Payment Method Manifest (parallel to\n     pmm-supported-origins.https.window.js).\n   - Merge the non-HTTPS default_applications tests from\n     wam-non-https.https.sub.window.js into\n     pmm-default-applications.https.window.js (using get_host_info() and\n     options.origin on createWebAppManifestUrl).\n   - Move the Web App Manifest credentials omission test into\n     fetch-options.https.window.js alongside the PMI and PMM credentials\n     omission tests.\n\nBug: 552832440\nChange-Id: If86cac3bc67c4aa3e3dd0b84a718e72d8003541d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8480645\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Xuehui Chen \u003cxuehuichen@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714503}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0988598e7f9b83cf35024de90f1ba9198abda092\nwpt-pr: 63369\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/fetch-options.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmm-default-applications.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/wam-non-https.https.sub.window.js"], "git_node": "82941057e31f961bb9296dc978499a54f4aba5c9", "git_parents": ["de04dc8c748a394e02ce67b9817e80b996902e03"], "node": "552d66e2444b1e4e012f6501d675ee5f06f22a5c", "parents": ["e7192e6c4a6cec86e9ab4e80a9a6eeaf5e483275"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079825 [wpt PR 63369] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63369\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/fetch-options.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmm-default-applications.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-ingestion.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/wam-non-https.https.sub.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "0d296bd1b849fd13cfab32928985801ac56fc716", "git_parents": ["82941057e31f961bb9296dc978499a54f4aba5c9"], "node": "fb77e2f58f3fcf32b711cf986c79b684b331d3f7", "parents": ["552d66e2444b1e4e012f6501d675ee5f06f22a5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080043 [wpt PR 63417] - [css-scroll-snap] Use scrollBy() in scroll-snap-type-pair-007, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-scroll-snap] Use scrollBy() in scroll-snap-type-pair-007\n\nscroll-snap-type-pair-007 relied on a synthesized touch fling, but\nflings generated through ChromeDriver don't reach the compositor, so\nthe test can't reliably exercise fling behavior in WPT.\n\nReplace the fling with an instant 2D scrollBy(). scrollBy() snaps with\na displacement DirectionStrategy, which exercises the same 2D\ncosine-similarity conflict resolution under scroll-snap-type: pair,\nsynchronously and without testdriver. The step is kept small so that\nboth candidates remain mutually visible and compete.\n\nThe test passes under run_wpt_tests.py, including 100/100 runs of\nheadless_shell_wpt on Windows Swarming bots, so remove its flaky Win\nexpectation.\n\nBug: 542706103\nChange-Id: I3f67f2399724431ea34a3a4470bddefb2aa64e8e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8518797\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714538}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2810902e6a3a78789efe5de3376d4f082087041f\nwpt-pr: 63417\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-007.html"], "git_node": "cb0e2a5dff49070cac226d371ceb9ac6cc573a3b", "git_parents": ["0d296bd1b849fd13cfab32928985801ac56fc716"], "node": "da8791affee6974216f5cf15e22828fa4c4db601", "parents": ["fb77e2f58f3fcf32b711cf986c79b684b331d3f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080043 [wpt PR 63417] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63417\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/crashtests/fractional-covering-area-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-snap-type-pair-007.html.ini"], "git_node": "45860df2381aff714c8ece24c1e90bcd63c16909", "git_parents": ["cb0e2a5dff49070cac226d371ceb9ac6cc573a3b"], "node": "acbf9aa6d0043308ac24e62323fdd2a663abe5cc", "parents": ["da8791affee6974216f5cf15e22828fa4c4db601"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080045 [wpt PR 63415] - webgl: Return null from getUniformLocation for uniform block members, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Return null from getUniformLocation for uniform block members\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 96c8bb279c61ec8045e9b246b7b9a3cc127ca1a4\nwpt-pr: 63415\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/getUniformLocation-uniform-block-member.html"], "git_node": "2daa2d22ad80e2cf8c45f53de20465984ba5ff8d", "git_parents": ["45860df2381aff714c8ece24c1e90bcd63c16909"], "node": "3e4d871e7d5a1fcb25e6c42d8ba66a45190e9a81", "parents": ["acbf9aa6d0043308ac24e62323fdd2a663abe5cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080047 [wpt PR 63402] - layout: Don't paint fragment of inline box containing a block-level, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Don't paint fragment of inline box containing a block-level\n\nWhen an inline box gets split into multiple fragments because it has a\na block-level descendant, no browser paints a box shadow for the\nfragment of the inline box that only contains the block-level.\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b60c4b349d9d167bf354a40bc0d4cbed15174606\nwpt-pr: 63402\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/block-in-inline-fragmentation-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/block-in-inline-fragmentation-001.html"], "git_node": "c249c3567c580bcc7c874d5e8067544d0afd5340", "git_parents": ["2daa2d22ad80e2cf8c45f53de20465984ba5ff8d"], "node": "b25a87b036a0a6c8fa76639b4ea2acca941deddf", "parents": ["3e4d871e7d5a1fcb25e6c42d8ba66a45190e9a81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim van der Lippe \u003cTimvdLippe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079090 [wpt PR 63308] - Fix expectations for width attribute changes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix expectations for width attribute changes\n\nFollowing https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13033 that should\ntimeout instead of load, as no engine currently does that.\n\nAdditionally, this test flakes on Safari because all images are lazily\nloaded from the cache. To dedupe these cache hits, add a query\nstring to each of them to ensure they are all unique.\n--\nUpdate relevant-mutations-lazy.html\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15c04ca9d43b87c817fa74aeb5c7d9346bb8ca66, 71b4d5f0eb7628a5d5f7cd2ee868ce1b1b5dc010\nwpt-pr: 63308\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/relevant-mutations-lazy.html"], "git_node": "ab40d003d51d5144327f0cc2eb593daffdeba9f1", "git_parents": ["c249c3567c580bcc7c874d5e8067544d0afd5340"], "node": "87dbe27dad7ae6ab284bc83de6e7528e16d576d8", "parents": ["b25a87b036a0a6c8fa76639b4ea2acca941deddf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079090 [wpt PR 63308] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63308\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/document-destroyed-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/relevant-mutations-lazy.html.ini"], "git_node": "09b680c0fcf97582e6496a9277df2f39fd822744", "git_parents": ["ab40d003d51d5144327f0cc2eb593daffdeba9f1"], "node": "81b11e07b9b4ebe725c13fc7ab4e05717d0b450b", "parents": ["87dbe27dad7ae6ab284bc83de6e7528e16d576d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080205 [wpt PR 63428] - Revert \"Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\"\n\nThis reverts commit 198d0b60e4b380d9af19291d6f36813a808c675b.\n\nReason for revert:\nLUCI Bisection has identified this change as the cause of a test failure. See the analysis: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/bisection/test-analysis/b/5682156132106240\n\nSample build with failed test: https://ci.chromium.org/b/8668501104388031185\nAffected test(s):\n[://\\:blink_web_tests!webtest::fast/ruby#text-decoration.html](https://ci.chromium.org/ui/test/chromium/:%2F%2F%5C:blink_web_tests%21webtest::fast%2Fruby%23text-decoration.html?q=VHash%3Ab57e93f9ea8ad996)\n\nIf this is a false positive, please report it at http://b.corp.google.com/createIssue?component=1199205&description=Analysis%3A+https%3A%2F%2Fci.chromium.org%2Fui%2Fp%2Fchromium%2Fbisection%2Ftest-analysis%2Fb%2F5682156132106240&format=PLAIN&priority=P3&title=Wrongly+blamed+https%3A%2F%2Fchromium-review.googlesource.com%2Fc%2Fchromium%2Fsrc%2F%2B%2F8456548&type=BUG\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\n\u003e\n\u003e Anchor the wavy pattern at the start of the decorating box instead of\n\u003e each fragment's own origin, so the wave phase no longer restarts at\n\u003e inline element boundaries like a nested \u003cem\u003e. Behind the default-on\n\u003e WavyDecorationContinuousPhase runtime feature as a kill switch.\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 41287729\n\u003e Change-Id: Ia6ec134cdab6bbb3d2f7f64b631bc499bd9f4a56\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8456548\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714354}\n\u003e\n\nBug: 41287729\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: I4b5bb2b004bc749a841868b43fe1c4bc945efed6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8536782\nReviewed-by: Andy Phan \u003candyphan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andy Phan \u003candyphan@chromium.org\u003e\nOwners-Override: Andy Phan \u003candyphan@chromium.org\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714737}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: acd62d7e8b8e7ad080797555a8ce4dbfa9c75cd8\nwpt-pr: 63428\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/reference/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001.html"], "git_node": "4de9f8f080a613b99066e2fc980630f64570f454", "git_parents": ["09b680c0fcf97582e6496a9277df2f39fd822744"], "node": "da3d874d399dc504ebfa47806193e87a4cd74ab8", "parents": ["81b11e07b9b4ebe725c13fc7ab4e05717d0b450b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080211 [wpt PR 63423] - [html-in-canvas] Switch to canvas getter for element width/height, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Switch to canvas getter for element width/height\n\nElementImage violated [1] due to being a mix of static and live. This\npatch makes ElementImage static and moves the width/height data to a\ngetter on canvas, as the data depends on canvas width/height\nattributes.\n\n[1] https://w3ctag.github.io/design-principles/#live-vs-static\n\nChange-Id: I75edadd24f985b64b974392a5145fb00e5454fdd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8531547\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714586}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dcdb8e113ce06c809e3ae44c9731544168fbbd04\nwpt-pr: 63423\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/captureElementImage.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-different-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-different-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-display-none.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/element-image-fractional-size.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/error-conditions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage.tentative.html"], "git_node": "8d2d792c08d4aa0970e2c4e4f1d6a341609fa782", "git_parents": ["4de9f8f080a613b99066e2fc980630f64570f454"], "node": "7a3e359df97b6b61eea385764f9ce92bdc6505ee", "parents": ["da3d874d399dc504ebfa47806193e87a4cd74ab8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080211 [wpt PR 63423] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63423\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/captureElementImage.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-display-none.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/element-image-fractional-size.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "4b4d261a0ed86361d9dbfa89375bc30433680256", "git_parents": ["8d2d792c08d4aa0970e2c4e4f1d6a341609fa782"], "node": "8a59a6874fe45d12a31ef2aa45829ab8b0698e46", "parents": ["7a3e359df97b6b61eea385764f9ce92bdc6505ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Evan Stade \u003cevanstade@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080222 [wpt PR 63424] - BackgroundFetch: stop using Blobs during request lookup, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBackgroundFetch: stop using Blobs during request lookup\n\nWhen retrieving a request body from cache storage, don't wrap it in a\nBlob. The Blob is immediately redirected into a DataPipeGetter anyway\nwhen used by the browser for the upload/download. Registration of a\nBlobDataItem/BlobDataItemReader with the BlobContext is unnecessary\ncomplexity which uses extra mojo pipes and async steps. If the request\nis retrieved by the renderer with Match, the Blob wrapper is again\nunnecessary most of the time.\n\nThis change doesn't affect the lifetime of data: as with the\nBlobDataItem before it, the DataPipeGetter will stop working if the\ncache storage entry needs to be deleted.\n\n\"GetRequestBlob\" symbol names are changed to \"GetRequestBody\" in many\nplaces.\n\nAlso add WPT coverage for BgF uploads. (It seems like ReadableStream\nbody *should* be supported, but currently is not, so that's left out of\nthe test.)\n\nBypass-Check-License: file rename\nBug: 567175133\nChange-Id: Iba326621c2f6930d5d275bb1a95330fb70d69873\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444651\nReviewed-by: Tommy Nyquist \u003cnyquist@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Evan Stade \u003cevanstade@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rick Byers \u003crbyers@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni \u003crakina@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fergal Daly \u003cfergal@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714621}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1e4070e021b776ad9004e9db8d5f005f02517b77\nwpt-pr: 63424\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/background-fetch/match-request-body.https.window.js"], "git_node": "2ae87f0df44b283c99ea9be821ee04ceb3685916", "git_parents": ["4b4d261a0ed86361d9dbfa89375bc30433680256"], "node": "b64e65b7e0ea4d781510e0aef1191ea13da0ccea", "parents": ["8a59a6874fe45d12a31ef2aa45829ab8b0698e46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080234 [wpt PR 63405] - Remove void element end tags from HTML embedded and forms WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove void element end tags from HTML embedded and forms WPTs\n\nbase, img, input, embed, source, param and frame have no end tag.\nWriting their end tag anyway is a parse error, and the parser drops the\ntag so the source suggests a structure the document never had.\n\nThis CL removes those invalid end tags from\nthird_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/html/semantics/embedded-content\nand third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/html/semantics/forms.\n\nNo behavior change.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: I41f4e45c6e093e997533707a5afa8f411a1568a1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8227044\nReviewed-by: Andres Regalado Rosas \u003candresrega@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714639}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e9d67f958967c0fb2233ce74c388af3b1e50be7\nwpt-pr: 63405\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/document-getters-return-null-for-cross-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-hidden-attribute-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-hidden-attribute.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-in-object-fallback-image-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-in-object-fallback-image.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-represent-nothing-04.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-svg-navigation-resets-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-frame-element/document-getters-return-null-for-cross-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/decode/image-decode-with-quick-attach.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/image-compositing-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/image-compositing-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/image-compositing-large-scale-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/image-compositing-large-scale-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-object-element/object-remove-param-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/form-control-infrastructure/form_attribute.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/defaultSelection.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-form-element/resources/form-no-action-with-base.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-form-element/resources/form-with-action-and-base.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/input-submit-remove-jssubmit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/input-whitespace.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/range-setattribute-value-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-label-element/control-active-with-multiple-clicks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-label-element/label-attributes.sub.html"], "git_node": "25b03a5549c9305b3f57cd67ac3f8c07d35eb8df", "git_parents": ["2ae87f0df44b283c99ea9be821ee04ceb3685916"], "node": "97f04ca289c38cf6034799f88b35d6466721e294", "parents": ["b64e65b7e0ea4d781510e0aef1191ea13da0ccea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080241 [wpt PR 63426] - Preserve 'none' keywords across relative color resolution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve 'none' keywords across relative color resolution\n\nPer [1]:\n\n\u003e The component keywords return a \u003cnumber\u003e, or 'none'.\n\nFactor out a ToChannelValue() helper from UnresolvedRelativeColor's\nResolve() implementation and make it handle an expression that consists\nof only a component keyword reference. Pass std::optional\u003cfloat\u003e via\nEvaluationInput so that any 'none' keywords are preserved. Use\nColor::ConvertToColorSpaceForInterpolation() so that component keywords\nare carried forward through any conversion. Drop the explicit conversion\nfrom UnresolvedAlphaColor::Resolve() since it will be handled\ndownstream.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-5/#relative-syntax\n\nFixed: 569954059\nChange-Id: Iae2788a09ac775b32790205176100eeafa95d567\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8515517\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714679}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 66f9f7f3d4a6ceca604f9a0519860a16f7610834\nwpt-pr: 63426\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/alpha-color-computed.html"], "git_node": "0c6d47433e11b794b3134f18ddfa9fa0dc659bb0", "git_parents": ["25b03a5549c9305b3f57cd67ac3f8c07d35eb8df"], "node": "ef6ff5f181c5609bf9b0696eac16ba4b6d953c09", "parents": ["97f04ca289c38cf6034799f88b35d6466721e294"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080241 [wpt PR 63426] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63426\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/alpha-color-computed.html.ini"], "git_node": "4bcf36631b7540b4a7a0d589b33b4998b85aed2c", "git_parents": ["0c6d47433e11b794b3134f18ddfa9fa0dc659bb0"], "node": "86541d2144d0c206e606d3dbd20e2993f41ede3e", "parents": ["ef6ff5f181c5609bf9b0696eac16ba4b6d953c09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080246 [wpt PR 63420] - [Connection-Allowlist] Enforce WebRTC blocking in binders via no-op impls, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Connection-Allowlist] Enforce WebRTC blocking in binders via no-op impls\n\nPreviously, WebRTC blocking by the Connection Allowlist was decided in\nPopulateBinderMapWithContext(): when the enforced allowlist blocked\nWebRTC, the MdnsResponder and P2PSocketManager binders were never\nregistered. This had two problems:\n\n1. The wrong Connection Allowlist was checked. The binder map is built\n   once, when the BrowserInterfaceBroker is created: in\n   CreateRenderFrame() or FrameTree::AddFrame() for a new\n   frame, and again in DidCommitNavigation(). The commit path\n   rebuilds the broker before DidCommitNewDocument() installs the\n   new document's PolicyContainerHost, so the check saw the previous\n   document's policies (typically those of the initial empty document).\n\n2. Unregistered interfaces crashed the renderer. The renderer still\n   requests MdnsResponder and P2PSocketManager when it creates the peer\n   connection factory, which occurs in the RTCPeerConnection constructor.\n   With no binder registered, BrowserInterfaceBrokerImpl calls\n   ReportNoBinderForInterface(), which reports a bad message and kills the\n   renderer. This crash was mainly reproducible for nested about:blank and\n   about:srcdoc frames. Because they are created after the parent navigation\n   commit, they inherit the correct allowlist from their parent, which means\n   they never actually bind the interfaces when WebRTC is blocked.\n\nThis CL fixes both:\n\n- The Connection Allowlist check now runs inside the binder functions\n  (BindSocketManager() and RenderFrameHostImpl::CreateMdnsResponder()).\n  They run only when the renderer actually requests the interface,\n  which happens from script in an already-committed document, so the\n  check reads that document's policy container. Both binders are now\n  always registered, so the renderer can no longer be killed for\n  requesting them.\n\nHowever, this fix introduces another potential issue. Which is\nthat any IPC sent to these now-correctly-unbound interfaces will\nnever fire callbacks, leaving potential for hangs in renderer-side\ncode.\n\nNow, when WebRTC is blocked, the binders bind no-op implementations\ninstead of dropping the receiver:\n\n- NoOpP2PSocketManager reports an empty network list, returns no\naddresses from GetHostAddress(), and closes the pipes passed to\nCreateSocket(). It stays connected, so the renderer's\nP2PSocketDispatcher does not enter its reconnect loop.\n\n- NoOpMdnsResponder runs every reply callback with failure values\nand never registers or announces a name.\n\nSo calls from production code fail gracefully instead of hanging or\ncrashing, and no sockets are created and no mDNS names are registered,\nwhatever the renderer does.\n\nThis also removes the fenced-frame P2PSocketManager ban from the binder\nmap, as part of the ongoing removal of fenced frames.\n\nTests:\n- New content_unittests: NoOpMdnsResponderTest.*,\nNoOpP2PSocketManagerTest.*\n- New WPTs covering nested child about:blank / about:srcdoc frames under\na parent's Connection Allowlist, verifying they do not crash and\nproperly respect the WebRTC parameter of the inherited allowlist.\n- Existing virtual/connection-allowlist WebRTC WPTs continue to pass.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=e2464277-4d92-41dc-a35f-278d6b893a90\n\nBug: 565837691\nFixed: 565837691\nChange-Id: Id0aeb1a30b7b47163b74898ab11e8ddac37ad9ff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8485457\nReviewed-by: Giovanni Ortuno Urquidi \u003cortuno@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk \u003calexmos@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714691}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: eb1f17915b157f7c2449f4daccfaace3a5f49959\nwpt-pr: 63420\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/webrtc-local-scheme-allow.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/webrtc-local-scheme-allow.sub.window.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/webrtc-local-scheme-block.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/webrtc-local-scheme-block.sub.window.js.headers"], "git_node": "c965565ea871118215daea1906c5e06219cd3cf5", "git_parents": ["4bcf36631b7540b4a7a0d589b33b4998b85aed2c"], "node": "845a1bad667ef7afc7151558e860385ef599a6af", "parents": ["86541d2144d0c206e606d3dbd20e2993f41ede3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080246 [wpt PR 63420] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63420\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/webrtc-local-scheme-block.sub.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "cbdfe8c001e28d31c8f19c7a4a07174c0a27f13f", "git_parents": ["c965565ea871118215daea1906c5e06219cd3cf5"], "node": "76ea89409457e45f24a59ad516854adf8bfc492f", "parents": ["845a1bad667ef7afc7151558e860385ef599a6af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Becker \u003cstevebe@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080166 [wpt PR 63404] - [SVG] Make SVGPathElement::getPathSegmentAtLength() use the base value, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG] Make SVGPathElement::getPathSegmentAtLength() use the base value\n\n... instead of the animated value. This is consistent with other\nbrowsers. It's also consistent with `SVGPathElement::getPathData()`. The\nsegment returned by `getPathSegmentAtLength()` should exist in the\nsequence returned by `getPathData()`.\n\nBug: 40441025\nChange-Id: Ie531507395762cb89eef5eebeeb3a10d00440b7b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8534547\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Steve Becker \u003cstevebe@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714693}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e20cc479197289f01436bd9e319bf6d5cc7169c7\nwpt-pr: 63404\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathSegmentAtLength-during-animation.html"], "git_node": "1ec45063b9842560a054d493e4c01bf2f0892161", "git_parents": ["cbdfe8c001e28d31c8f19c7a4a07174c0a27f13f"], "node": "526780083265cb96017005c55dc4247875820ac3", "parents": ["76ea89409457e45f24a59ad516854adf8bfc492f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080172 [wpt PR 63422] - Fix flake in select-4-option-optgroup-display-none.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix flake in select-4-option-optgroup-display-none.html\n\nSet will-change: transform on :root in\nselect-4-option-optgroup-display-none.html and its reference file to\nprevent subpixel rendering differences on the rounded corners of the\n\u003cselect size=4\u003e elements, and remove the failure expectation.\n\nThe flake was reproduced using UTR against 'Linux Tests (dbg)(1)'\n(headless_shell_wpt_tests with --repeat-each=10), where 1 out of 10 runs\nfailed with a 1-channel-value difference on the rounded corner pixels.\nAfter adding will-change: transform, all 20 runs with --repeat-each=20\non 'Linux Tests (dbg)(1)' passed without any failures.\n\nFixed: 567713221\nChange-Id: I51b8519f4343aa997cc933a39aa748faf23d436b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8503877\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714719}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a9899331fe9eedee8669bca985ee58c1a7f6cc4\nwpt-pr: 63422\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/select-4-option-optgroup-display-none-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/select-4-option-optgroup-display-none.html"], "git_node": "0a7aedc4f9f63610c21bb3a2d160b4ba249888af", "git_parents": ["1ec45063b9842560a054d493e4c01bf2f0892161"], "node": "7eac7f8619e4949f0b34da500155d2e95a6ee6f9", "parents": ["526780083265cb96017005c55dc4247875820ac3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080181 [wpt PR 63431] - VT: Keep remembered size if style has contain-intrinsic-size: auto, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nVT: Keep remembered size if style has contain-intrinsic-size: auto\n\nThis patch ensures that we keep the VT remembered size if it needs one\noutside of the capture phase (ie the author style has\ncontain-intrinsic-size).\n\nR=freedebreuil@google.com\n\nChange-Id: I3bf6f935d69629a9bbebe39d6b5b695cac29ddd1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8519137\nReviewed-by: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714775}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: af6c5926d57293c3af16483726ef876c7a348b30\nwpt-pr: 63431\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-containment-keeps-author-remembered-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-containment-remembered-size.html"], "git_node": "dd16706185e8f6ad937d9d84418634fd8eadb0dc", "git_parents": ["0a7aedc4f9f63610c21bb3a2d160b4ba249888af"], "node": "06a72261d761320a3b53accb7b7ba866aeecfad8", "parents": ["7eac7f8619e4949f0b34da500155d2e95a6ee6f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080181 [wpt PR 63431] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63431\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-containment-keeps-author-remembered-size.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-containment-remembered-size.html.ini"], "git_node": "b7b093d1e4a9e93c69d7048ef5064cee2356fa37", "git_parents": ["dd16706185e8f6ad937d9d84418634fd8eadb0dc"], "node": "bbb2df6b539fef4c546d66f6a0a107247298c720", "parents": ["06a72261d761320a3b53accb7b7ba866aeecfad8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080188 [wpt PR 63430] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=311609, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG2] Implement the side attribute for SVG \u003ctextPath\u003e element (#63430)\n\nSVG2 adds the 'side' attribute to \u003ctextPath\u003e with values 'left' (default)\nand 'right' [1]. Per the spec, side=\"right\" lays the text out along the\nreversed path, which renders it on the opposite side of the curve. WebKit\ndid not expose the attribute on the DOM or honor it during layout.\n\nExpose 'side' as an SVGAnimatedEnumeration (SVGTextPathSideType, with the\nTEXTPATH_SIDETYPE_LEFT/RIGHT constants), mirroring the existing 'method'\nand 'spacing' enumerations, with 'left' as the lacuna value and invalid\nvalues reset to the initial value 'left' via the shared parseBaseVal\nhelper (matching method/spacing). The SVG WG resolved to add the side\nconstants to the SVGTextPathElement IDL [3].\n\nFor rendering, walking the reversed path at arc length t is equivalent to\nsampling the forward path at (pathLength - t) and rotating each glyph by\n180 degrees, so no path-reversal primitive is needed (WebCore::Path has\nnone). SVGTextLayoutEngine carries a reversed flag set from the textPath\nrenderer and applies the mirrored sampling and angle flip in the path\nlayout loop; the existing baseline/orientation math composes correctly\nbecause it operates on the reversed tangent angle.\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/single-page.html#text-TextPathAttributes\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/svgwg/issues/1086\n[3] https://www.w3.org/2026/04/23-svg-minutes.html\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=311609\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323115@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5717e380cdca8ed08a1f8e3bdd279beace9166da\nwpt-pr: 63430\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-right-startoffset-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-right-startoffset.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-right-subpaths-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textpath-side-right-subpaths.svg"], "git_node": "c752e2aac769a4ad081905c2be85555558cf92d8", "git_parents": ["b7b093d1e4a9e93c69d7048ef5064cee2356fa37"], "node": "00ee41333778ef39a80b858bdb14f0f7cc4ed8be", "parents": ["bbb2df6b539fef4c546d66f6a0a107247298c720"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080193 [wpt PR 63435] - [wpt] Fix webauthn add_credential/invalid.py null signCount expectation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Fix webauthn add_credential/invalid.py null signCount expectation\n\nThe test asserted that `signCount: null` must be rejected with\n\"invalid argument\". However, w3c/webauthn#2382 made signCount nullable\nto represent a credential without a signature counter, and ChromeDriver\nimplements this (see crrev.com/c/fc0cd539d551b \"[chromedriver] Support\nnull signature counters\"). The sibling set_credential_properties/set.py\ntest already treats `None` as a valid signCount, so invalid.py was\ninternally inconsistent with the rest of the suite. This made\ntest_sign_count_invalid_type[None] fail deterministically on all\nplatforms.\n\nRemove `None` from the invalid-type cases and add a positive test in\nadd.py asserting that a credential with a null signCount is accepted\nand read back with `signCount == null`.\n\nRemoves the [ Failure ] expectation. Both add.py and invalid.py pass\nlocally with run_wpt_tests.py (36 subtests).\n\nBug: 533056772\nChange-Id: Ia8cecaf642a11dcfeab2ddf7830de6d4331be7a1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8540564\nReviewed-by: Martin Kreichgauer \u003cmartinkr@google.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Martin Kreichgauer \u003cmartinkr@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714914}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 385f52fe54bdea1383e8621675ce6727be9d076b\nwpt-pr: 63435\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/add.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/invalid.py"], "git_node": "4ae6c8f558b444e8fd9586b80baadea8037cc3d4", "git_parents": ["c752e2aac769a4ad081905c2be85555558cf92d8"], "node": "f8801424e7b052e198cca112aa1b14b29e2b7413", "parents": ["00ee41333778ef39a80b858bdb14f0f7cc4ed8be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080193 [wpt PR 63435] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63435\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/add.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/invalid.py.ini"], "git_node": "fbb2c54f81f938f65a5b4f57a3a3b9bb34d01275", "git_parents": ["4ae6c8f558b444e8fd9586b80baadea8037cc3d4"], "node": "9f4936952535fcee06d442097040c847df618d12", "parents": ["f8801424e7b052e198cca112aa1b14b29e2b7413"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080079 [wpt PR 63400] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326793, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo not deserialize RTCCertificate in workers\n\nRTCCertificate is [Exposed=Window], but posting one to a dedicated,\nshared, or service worker delivered it there. Use the generated exposure\ncheck, through isInterfaceExposedInGlobalObject() from 322979@main, so\nthat those messages fail to deserialize and result in a messageerror\nevent.\n\nRTCCertificate can also be stored in IndexedDB, and reading one back in a\nworker used to deliver it there too. Now that it fails to deserialize,\nIDBRequest's result, IDBCursorWithValue's value, and IDBRecord's value\nwould be null, silently losing the record. Align with Firefox instead:\nthe request succeeds and reading the value throws. Throw a DataCloneError\nrather than Firefox's InvalidStateError, as proposed in\nhttps://github.com/w3c/IndexedDB/issues/391\n\n(Chromium deserializes as null, which seems less useful.)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326793\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 10ccd8604683524790a9493d68965c2878107afe\nwpt-pr: 63400\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/value-not-exposed-in-worker-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/value-not-exposed-in-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCCertificate-postMessage-to-workers-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCCertificate-postMessage-to-workers.https.html"], "git_node": "fc03e8e43c42db0d49e2f0cc1103a657a751e49f", "git_parents": ["fbb2c54f81f938f65a5b4f57a3a3b9bb34d01275"], "node": "71951445ca7be778d88c61c572221fcc183bad6c", "parents": ["9f4936952535fcee06d442097040c847df618d12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080079 [wpt PR 63400] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63400\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/IndexedDB/value-not-exposed-in-worker.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "b2be584994687d82b351f51151682b85240832f7", "git_parents": ["fc03e8e43c42db0d49e2f0cc1103a657a751e49f"], "node": "6cddc25be6d1bc98c18ea59bb397e08acb208ed1", "parents": ["71951445ca7be778d88c61c572221fcc183bad6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080134 [wpt PR 63437] - [SAH] Remove stale expectation and harden storage-access-headers WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SAH] Remove stale expectation and harden storage-access-headers WPT\n\nstorage-access-headers.tentative.https.sub.window.html has been marked\n[ Failure Timeout ] since the storage-access-api WPTs started running\nagainst Chrome (via ChromeDriver) instead of content_shell, because the\nStorage Access API is implemented in the //chrome layer. The causes of\nthose failures have since been fixed (ChromeDriver's SetPermission frame\norigin, the test assuming cross-site cookies are blocked by default, and\nSetFirstPartyCookie's `{ once: true }` listener being detached by stray\nmessages), and the test now passes reliably, so remove the expectation.\n\nAlso clean up the test itself:\n\n* Run areCrossSiteCookiesAllowedByDefault() inside promise_setup()\n  instead of an unawaited async IIFE. Previously the first three\n  promise_tests started running while the probe frame was still being\n  loaded and messaged, so the probe ran concurrently with subtests that\n  create cross-site frames and set storage-access permissions for the\n  same origin.\n\n* Remove the responder iframes created by the probe and by five\n  subtests once they are no longer needed. These frames load\n  testharness.js and post a `{type: \"complete\"}` message to every\n  ancestor when their 10s harness timeout fires, and keeping them\n  around leaves cross-site frames alive for the remainder of the test.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=0d875fba-fe1a-401b-9481-9a9d918e0eca\n\nBug: 366530634\nChange-Id: I058f027f2890290c5fbd4539310b966010f49523\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520603\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Chris Fredrickson \u003ccfredric@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714977}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1214c0bce69b13d746f0324ae59a0ceee7382469\nwpt-pr: 63437\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/storage-access-api/storage-access-headers.tentative.https.sub.window.js"], "git_node": "b09fe2d1d3ef0ca34c53917ff02813d29e2930c1", "git_parents": ["b2be584994687d82b351f51151682b85240832f7"], "node": "3360647fba4ebcd5fb1492ebf8d4c37bf3bdcea6", "parents": ["6cddc25be6d1bc98c18ea59bb397e08acb208ed1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080134 [wpt PR 63437] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63437\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-cross-site-iframe.sub.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "110b7ec694764a3c1499ccd52ab91694b73ba392", "git_parents": ["b09fe2d1d3ef0ca34c53917ff02813d29e2930c1"], "node": "db08eb0b074cfd5dc09aad33e0cf9c3695c1b294", "parents": ["3360647fba4ebcd5fb1492ebf8d4c37bf3bdcea6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080137 [wpt PR 63436] - Don't hold a reference to the id attribute across UpdateId(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't hold a reference to the id attribute across UpdateId()\n\nElement::InsertedInto() took a reference into the element's attribute\nstorage via GetIdAttribute() and passed it to UpdateId(). UpdateId()\nnotifies id target observers, and those can update style and layout.\nFor example, a focused \u003cinput list\u003e whose datalist became usable\nrebuilds its shadow tree and calls RevealSelection(). If that update\nbuilds a \u003cuse\u003e instance tree that clones the element, cloning\nserializes the element's dirty style attribute and appends it to the\nattribute storage. When that reallocates the storage, the reference\ndangles, and the remaining reads of the id in UpdateId() access freed\nmemory.\n\nThis CL copies the id into a local AtomicString before calling\nUpdateId(). RemovedFrom() passes the id to UpdateId() the same way, so\nit gets the same change. Recent fixes for similar bugs in\nElementRuleCollector and HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink()\nused the same approach.\n\nFixed: 567638392\nChange-Id: I1ebac072098091e5dc9d8898f2bced3cf0c3bbcc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8517119\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715019}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d7f802deee5455c0ea0ab7553b2f2b3a14cf666e\nwpt-pr: 63436\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-datalist-element/list-id-insertion-crash.html"], "git_node": "65376da465368d415defe78cd2f4e676fc5b251a", "git_parents": ["110b7ec694764a3c1499ccd52ab91694b73ba392"], "node": "f8c97d113091cfee912184ff221185bb550f0c51", "parents": ["db08eb0b074cfd5dc09aad33e0cf9c3695c1b294"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080137 [wpt PR 63436] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63436\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-datalist-element/list-id-insertion-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "6a4367de2c612a10825eb695cc8d7129aa4b3d56", "git_parents": ["65376da465368d415defe78cd2f4e676fc5b251a"], "node": "b757af37b669c9bf512026c867229a50acb818ce", "parents": ["f8c97d113091cfee912184ff221185bb550f0c51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080140 [wpt PR 63439] - [WebCodecs] Fix fractional display size scaling on visibleRect override, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCodecs] Fix fractional display size scaling on visibleRect override\n\nCast default_display_size.width() and default_display_size.height() to\ndouble before dividing by default_visible_rect dimensions in\nParsedVideoFrameInit(). Previously, integer division truncated\nnon-integer display-to-visible ratios to integers, producing incorrect\ndisplay dimensions for fractional scales \u003e 1 and throwing spurious\nTypeErrors when scales \u003c 1 truncated to zero.\n\nFixed: 562847603\nChange-Id: I63cabd61bdc1a38d3599114288e59d0c82431694\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8540370\nReviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715044}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9fd55a8464bf08be2f2b9a8415a5e42d362aac9a\nwpt-pr: 63439\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-construction.any.js"], "git_node": "289eaffb32035f6bbed126967397db8828429103", "git_parents": ["6a4367de2c612a10825eb695cc8d7129aa4b3d56"], "node": "7294efaea66e9fb46e0bd8875aa0bef98f8675c9", "parents": ["b757af37b669c9bf512026c867229a50acb818ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080199 [wpt PR 63447] - Deflake cdata-001.xhtml and cdata-002.xhtml by waiting for Ahem, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake cdata-001.xhtml and cdata-002.xhtml by waiting for Ahem\n\n`wpt/html/rendering/cdata-001.xhtml` and\n`wpt/html/rendering/cdata-002.xhtml` are flaky due to not waiting for\nAhem to load. When the tests are run by themselves, the flakiness is\nconsistently reproducible without this patch and goes away with this\npatch, which waits for the font to be ready. This patch has a small\nspecial-case because the fonts may not load until the non-empty xhtml\nwith the Ahem font is present, so a second await is needed.\n\nBug: 568337130\nChange-Id: Ic739279bde8f84527bd8c9225ab63d78c3c1e430\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8542234\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715116}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 05d3e3785d1c6983cf65af0d6b36f37cf8843f5b\nwpt-pr: 63447\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/cdata-001.xhtml", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/cdata-002.xhtml"], "git_node": "19f9674591d7269301c4d630eec462b4532adf27", "git_parents": ["289eaffb32035f6bbed126967397db8828429103"], "node": "f3f126ebe9399db3a12b363f077168ab5231fb79", "parents": ["7294efaea66e9fb46e0bd8875aa0bef98f8675c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dan Murphy \u003cdmurph@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080202 [wpt PR 63442] - [Notifications] SW popup capability delegation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Notifications] SW popup capability delegation\n\nWhen handling a notification click, a Service Worker may need an\nexisting client window to open a popup (e.g. an email preview or chat\ncompose). Currently, window.open() in the client is blocked by the popup\nblocker because the client window lacks transient user activation.\n\nThis CL allows the Service Worker to delegate popup capability to a\nsame-origin WindowClient via client.postMessage(msg, {delegate:\n'popup'}). Upon receipt, the client window receives a 1-second transient\npopup token enabling window.open(). This is decoupled from window\ninteraction and gated behind the CapabilityDelegationPopup feature flag.\n\nSee https://chromestatus.com/feature/5091965583622144\n\nBug: 542314185, b:529458813\nTest: http/tests/serviceworker/clients-capability-delegation.html\nTest: external/wpt/html/capability-delegation/\nTest: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=WebFrameTest.CapabilityDelegation*\nChange-Id: I43dcdbf25b6585f9fcdb8a49f9810037136aec5e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8069089\nReviewed-by: Marijn Kruisselbrink \u003cmek@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Murphy \u003cdmurph@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nasko Oskov \u003cnasko@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715121}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83381e6080f07d775a4fc9d33adc4bffbd13186c\nwpt-pr: 63442\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/capability-delegation/frame-capability-delegation-popup-blocked.tentative.html"], "git_node": "ffc650d78a87d7879123dbf842c734fa52e04527", "git_parents": ["19f9674591d7269301c4d630eec462b4532adf27"], "node": "5b379cdddde09e5865cb090bd6b4b9b1878d8a70", "parents": ["f3f126ebe9399db3a12b363f077168ab5231fb79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080202 [wpt PR 63442] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63442\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/capability-delegation/frame-capability-delegation-popup-blocked.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "1c6ce167c3befb474c2bcbaaa8e7b0cb461eb698", "git_parents": ["ffc650d78a87d7879123dbf842c734fa52e04527"], "node": "2b654630ac0c35efbe73c82a7356747ee6acc9b3", "parents": ["5b379cdddde09e5865cb090bd6b4b9b1878d8a70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080206 [wpt PR 63443] - [html-in-canvas] Remove blink-specific terms in WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Remove blink-specific terms in WPTs\n\nThis patch removes some blink-specific implementation terms in the\ndraw-element-image tests.\n\nChange-Id: I9d303a0984a4c8a51230846b67a3f34af36da1db\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8545050\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715139}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e22fa4e75778f91795fda7e14c82f067fb2a156\nwpt-pr: 63443\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/compositing-descendant-filter-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/compositing-descendant-filter.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/descendant-filter-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/descendant-filter.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/invalidation-during-onpaint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/moved-webgl-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted-moveBefore.tentative.html"], "git_node": "da22645ad205151564b8edd5faaf1e0da0ab4b76", "git_parents": ["1c6ce167c3befb474c2bcbaaa8e7b0cb461eb698"], "node": "b4f35094287bbcf44ad52c91861e28f8515fefaa", "parents": ["2b654630ac0c35efbe73c82a7356747ee6acc9b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Bowman-Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080001 [wpt PR 63394] - flex: Consider precomputed min/max_main size when doing layout on indefinite sizing item of flex:column, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Run CSS fetching tests (#48716)\n\nThese changes enable a new subdirectory and fix some problems that were\ncausing the tests to timeout.\n\nTesting: New passing subtest\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e\n\n--\nadded wpt test for this scenario\n\nSigned-off-by: rayguo17 \u003ctin.tun.aung1@huawei.com\u003e\n\n--\nchange EOL to LF\n\nSigned-off-by: rayguo17 \u003ctin.tun.aung1@huawei.com\u003e\n\n--\naddress comment\n\nSigned-off-by: rayguo17 \u003crayguo17@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e5eca838839adb2cc0c04a7959d6be602325fa00, 6d1e51c31bfd62f89ec36a433eb1d652a75f9389, 1317e80115b1df439f420d8ddc16aa587d72729b, e4a9e438d3542b0ca9e6e56f9fa838ed30ba72d7\nwpt-pr: 63394\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/column-flex-child-center-with-indefinite-height.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/reference/column-flex-child-center-with-indefinite-height-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/fetching/fetch-resources.sub.html"], "git_node": "6e331301101ca4372a73df48de958f92cb192c1e", "git_parents": ["da22645ad205151564b8edd5faaf1e0da0ab4b76"], "node": "a59043779d99d968a1798f1711bd583c79e10927", "parents": ["b4f35094287bbcf44ad52c91861e28f8515fefaa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003c69349599+sadym-chromium@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075273 [wpt PR 62938] - [testdriver] Add test_driver.bidi.emulation.set_viewport_meta_override, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[testdriver] Add test_driver.bidi.emulation.set_viewport_meta_override (#62938)\n\nSpec: https://w3c.github.io/webdriver-bidi/#command-emulation-setViewportMetaOverride\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d191fa8bbab9d678b76e31f243fabcf5530e40f2\nwpt-pr: 62938\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/docs/writing-tests/testdriver.md", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/metadata/infrastructure/testdriver/bidi/emulation/set_viewport_meta_override.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/testdriver/bidi/emulation/set_viewport_meta_override.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resources/testdriver.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/asyncactions.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/executorwebdriver.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/protocol.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/testdriver-extra.js"], "git_node": "1ffb716382dd48eda702d8e8a6d2738118c24c41", "git_parents": ["6e331301101ca4372a73df48de958f92cb192c1e"], "node": "d81f00303c0fbfff2d7553911e0433e620cfa3e4", "parents": ["a59043779d99d968a1798f1711bd583c79e10927"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075273 [wpt PR 62938] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62938\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/infrastructure/testdriver/bidi/emulation/set_viewport_meta_override.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "7ccbda94085e1be449caafd94b529a7bf1e21ce8", "git_parents": ["1ffb716382dd48eda702d8e8a6d2738118c24c41"], "node": "5fdcaec5aca276c58bec18597fcc46f839e96cfb", "parents": ["d81f00303c0fbfff2d7553911e0433e620cfa3e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "github-actions[bot] \u003c41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079648 [wpt PR 63368] - Sync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.85.1, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSync interfaces/ with @webref/idl 3.85.1 (#63368)\n\nCo-authored-by: wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 72048bce931b8c75165ab661b0f16ef7c7b7460e\nwpt-pr: 63368\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/html.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/install-element.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/prompt-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/push-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/wasm-js-api.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webcodecs.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webmcp.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webrtc-stats.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/webtransport.idl"], "git_node": "191f2a24db4c817393198ed6ef813f3dcff7dac6", "git_parents": ["7ccbda94085e1be449caafd94b529a7bf1e21ce8"], "node": "bb0a51a754a48cc8dbac1eb53ab79c4ad515edb5", "parents": ["5fdcaec5aca276c58bec18597fcc46f839e96cfb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079648 [wpt PR 63368] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63368\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/api/credentials/cookies.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/dynamic-mozilla-162063.xhtml.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/touch-events/hover-state-caused-by-compatibility-mouse-events.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/uievents/mouse/mouseenter-mouseleave-on-drag.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-unconnected-outputs.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/accept_alert/accept.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/add_cookie/add.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/new_session/unhandled_prompt_behavior.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/send_alert_text/send.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/idlharness.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpTransceiver.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "a94826289a8d10a4c1dc6372150b7d815991bcc2", "git_parents": ["191f2a24db4c817393198ed6ef813f3dcff7dac6"], "node": "596148cd880b2d15dda1695fb8ab161513f299c5", "parents": ["bb0a51a754a48cc8dbac1eb53ab79c4ad515edb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080177 [wpt PR 63449] - [html-in-canvas] Remove legacy getElementTransform API, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Remove legacy getElementTransform API\n\nThis patch removes the legacy 2-argument `getElementTransform(element,\ndraw_transform)` method from `HTMLCanvasElement` and `OffscreenCanvas`,\nretaining the 1-argument `HTMLCanvasElement.getElementTransform(element)`\nmethod that reads the stored element canvas transform.\n\nTransform calculation test coverage from the removed legacy tests (such\nas canvas/CSS pixel scaling, zoom, CTM transforms, `transform-origin`,\nand source rect offsets) has been migrated to `canvas-transform-update`\nand `canvas-transform-update-worker` via `drawElementImage()`.\n\nFixed: 571496925\nChange-Id: Ie9484247714ef6a621132c27da60bb043f088208\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8542152\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715079}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b59184b6ef85a5cb29a96a64351dc9228d85bc9e\nwpt-pr: 63449\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-different-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/draw-element-image-different-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/error-conditions.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/get-element-transform.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/getElementTransform-worker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage.tentative.html"], "git_node": "7b19ecdad367125501ae9af702e383326ef7430c", "git_parents": ["a94826289a8d10a4c1dc6372150b7d815991bcc2"], "node": "1dbcaa6c6afa8015a8ed2e2b97782e6e20939cc2", "parents": ["596148cd880b2d15dda1695fb8ab161513f299c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080177 [wpt PR 63449] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63449\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/get-element-transform.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update-worker.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/getElementTransform-worker.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "fbf5fe5f68f3667b14cb855eb8697471c72eba91", "git_parents": ["7b19ecdad367125501ae9af702e383326ef7430c"], "node": "2f7635e052917524ebc9d8907e6f9dbcf5feea6b", "parents": ["1dbcaa6c6afa8015a8ed2e2b97782e6e20939cc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080212 [wpt PR 63450] - [focus-without-user-activation] Fix label forwarding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[focus-without-user-activation] Fix label forwarding\n\nPreserve the calling frame when a label forwards focus to its associated\ncontrol, both for label.focus() and scripted click activation. Losing\nthe caller caused these paths to check the target document's permissions\npolicy instead.\n\nForward FocusParams::initiator_frame from HTMLLabelElement::Focus(). For\nuntrusted click events, use the incumbent window's frame as the\ninitiator, matching Element::focusForBindings(). Trusted clicks (user\ninput, accessibility, UA-simulated) still use the label's frame.\n\nThe new WPT is tentative while initiator attribution is specified:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12032\n\nBug: 523708065\nChange-Id: I2e4ac1ba4a6b836594512105e21ed03e5668a528\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464353\nReviewed-by: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715143}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9914cd827be802c83201eddedfe51beb3bb4d7c0\nwpt-pr: 63450\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/experimental-features/focus-without-user-activation-label-click.tentative.html"], "git_node": "b16b2570b1e0bcf5880f0ddaf37c8e9adb23e938", "git_parents": ["fbf5fe5f68f3667b14cb855eb8697471c72eba91"], "node": "2a4c5992764b6661ab44922faa67582e47b4439a", "parents": ["2f7635e052917524ebc9d8907e6f9dbcf5feea6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080212 [wpt PR 63450] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63450\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/experimental-features/focus-without-user-activation-label-click.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "3fb814cfd914aba903897c212cf139169131a12c", "git_parents": ["b16b2570b1e0bcf5880f0ddaf37c8e9adb23e938"], "node": "919db18aebc62e6b9d2b2ccd94ceca396f899dd2", "parents": ["2a4c5992764b6661ab44922faa67582e47b4439a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jingyun Liu \u003cjingyun@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080233 [wpt PR 63440] - LanguageModel.prompt() returns a sequence\u003cLanguageModelMessageContent\u003e if expecting tool call output, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLanguageModel.prompt() returns a sequence\u003cLanguageModelMessageContent\u003e\nif expecting tool call output\n\n- https://github.com/webmachinelearning/prompt-api/pull/162#discussion_r4154198219\n- previously it returns dynamic types (DOMString if no tool call,\nsequence if has tool call)\n- Now if expectedOutput expects tool call, prompt() will return sequence\n regardless of current model output\n- Update WPT and unit tests to cover the new resolution behavior.\n\nChange-Id: I2d091e22a7d6dd235256b6976d817c760b59fca3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8504744\nCommit-Queue: Jingyun Liu \u003cjingyun@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Tom Sepez \u003ctsepez@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715202}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2acf56c32a7b70e88dcec7cc30cfe56bd681196b\nwpt-pr: 63440\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/language-model-tool-use.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "1e87a526ebcdf88cd4502e21ca9997e0d6c19955", "git_parents": ["3fb814cfd914aba903897c212cf139169131a12c"], "node": "7a5d62c0f0505466f612bd191631aa1861b2adfb", "parents": ["919db18aebc62e6b9d2b2ccd94ceca396f899dd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079988 [wpt PR 63390] - Add MutationObserver transient registered observer and callback order tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd MutationObserver transient registered observer and callback order tests\n\nA MutationObserver observing a subtree keeps observing a node removed from that subtree, until mutation observers are notified. Test that this happens, also after takeRecords(), for children removed by replaceChildren(), and for nodes moved out of the subtree by moveBefore(), and that it stops:\n\n* when mutation observers are notified, even if no record was queued for the observer or its callback was not invoked;\n* when disconnect() is invoked, without affecting other observers;\n* when observe() replaces the options of the registered observer it originates from, without affecting other registered observers.\n\nEach of these is also tested for nodes removed from an already removed subtree.\n\nAlso test that observe() on a node in a removed subtree registers an observer that remains after mutation observers are notified, that removing a node from an observed subtree queues the mutation observer microtask while other mutations only do so once a record is queued for an observer, and that mutation observers are notified in the order they were created.\n\nFor https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1507\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 37db47b966754e6ad7cf20d6d43fa0375db4080d\nwpt-pr: 63390\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/MutationObserver-callback-order.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/MutationObserver-transient-registered-observers.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/mutation-observer-moved-subtree.window.js"], "git_node": "2d8886e3a15faa971e6d37fbcfae50a3283deefb", "git_parents": ["1e87a526ebcdf88cd4502e21ca9997e0d6c19955"], "node": "cce45a1e114c22962eda03cee006572c9f94ce9f", "parents": ["7a5d62c0f0505466f612bd191631aa1861b2adfb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079988 [wpt PR 63390] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63390\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/DOMImplementation-createDocument-with-null-browsing-context-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "0bea67dbed39154e925788dbfb8a640d1c54d2f5", "git_parents": ["2d8886e3a15faa971e6d37fbcfae50a3283deefb"], "node": "fec40359def7ad6d3948bcdb1b0d661a9b5dd301", "parents": ["cce45a1e114c22962eda03cee006572c9f94ce9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080239 [wpt PR 63452] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326946, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo not deserialize FileSystemHandle in non-secure contexts\n\nFileSystemHandle is [SecureContext], but posting one to a non-secure\ncontext of the same origin, such as an https frame inside an http page,\ndelivered it there. Use the generated exposure check, through\nisInterfaceExposedInGlobalObject() from 322979@main, so that those\nmessages fail to deserialize and result in a messageerror event.\n\nFileSystemHandle can also be stored in IndexedDB, but a non-secure\ncontext never shares a storage partition with a secure context of the\nsame origin, so there is no IndexedDB equivalent to test.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326946\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc4dce436b08d0bfcec2da90a433b26dc5323870\nwpt-pr: 63452\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fs/FileSystemBaseHandle-postMessage-insecure-context.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/fs/resources/insecure-context-message-host.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fs/resources/insecure-context-message-target.html"], "git_node": "759bdd446bfcdb982a49e58f95011c711600e48f", "git_parents": ["0bea67dbed39154e925788dbfb8a640d1c54d2f5"], "node": "edfc71fbc83532c7059b401b158d1438fc4dde27", "parents": ["fec40359def7ad6d3948bcdb1b0d661a9b5dd301"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080239 [wpt PR 63452] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63452\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fs/FileSystemBaseHandle-postMessage-insecure-context.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "0554a2f3050dccb9e35cdf9324e42dc89dbc7dbd", "git_parents": ["759bdd446bfcdb982a49e58f95011c711600e48f"], "node": "65ae912c9a59e2f9ecde364925debdfc59226df6", "parents": ["edfc71fbc83532c7059b401b158d1438fc4dde27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080440 [wpt PR 63459] - Fix and re-enable highlight-painting-shadows-vertical.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix and re-enable highlight-painting-shadows-vertical.html\n\n`external/wpt/css/css-pseudo/highlight-painting-shadows-vertical.html`\nfailed consistently due to not waiting for Ahem to load. This patch\nfixes this issue by waiting for Ahem to load, removes the failing\nTestExpectations entry, and double-checks that the test is no longer\nflaky.\n\nBug: 568337130, 431033198\nChange-Id: Ic61a9178bb533ccc8117695b628c7c97c5526ab5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8541574\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715330}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83559739b4d540fed1178267b23bf0f99ce702bc\nwpt-pr: 63459\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-painting-shadows-vertical-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-painting-shadows-vertical.html"], "git_node": "1b9d87b34359fa50063dfd477bd939e000e1f0d3", "git_parents": ["0554a2f3050dccb9e35cdf9324e42dc89dbc7dbd"], "node": "56041774872311837b8798af3e7a1c5c85d22951", "parents": ["65ae912c9a59e2f9ecde364925debdfc59226df6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Martinez \u003camartinez55@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080452 [wpt PR 63433] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324766, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nElements using background image from currentColor doesn't repaint when current color changes\n\nisEquivalentForPainting() only checked background-color for currentColor. currentColors inside background images, like linear-gradient()\ndid not trigger repaints when the objects changed.\n\nStyle::Image::containsCurrentColor() now checks for currentColors in gradients, image, crossfade, filter, and image-set.\nEvery background layer is checked in BackgroundData::backgroundContainsCurrentColor().\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324766\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bf7d032062962e28907a9421e67613e6fbc6eab5\nwpt-pr: 63433\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-image-gradient-currentcolor-self-repaint-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-image-gradient-currentcolor-self-repaint.html"], "git_node": "cc64a45eb5c2336f98b576bd8301746881a5e583", "git_parents": ["1b9d87b34359fa50063dfd477bd939e000e1f0d3"], "node": "42d9532d38da6abe8a3ecff079f3a81ee386e3fe", "parents": ["56041774872311837b8798af3e7a1c5c85d22951"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080455 [wpt PR 63462] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326790, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMediaList writes are silently dropped after its owner rule or stylesheet is destroyed (#63462)\n\nA MediaList wrapper does not keep its owning CSSMediaRule, CSSImportRule\nor CSSStyleSheet alive. When the owner is destroyed while script still\nholds the MediaList, the owner's destructor calls detachFromParent(), which\nsnapshots the queries into m_detachedMediaQueries and clears both parent\npointers.\n\nReads were served from that snapshot, but MediaList::setMediaQueries() only\nwrote through the parent pointers. Both are null by then, so the mediaText\nsetter, appendMedium() and deleteMedium() became silent no-ops, and the list\nkept reporting its old value. Whether a write took effect depended on GC\ntiming.\n\nStore writes into m_detachedMediaQueries when the list is detached.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326790\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323203@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 384004d0601b26a8e09ca3fb252d142f8c438f82\nwpt-pr: 63462\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/medialist-mutation-after-owner-gc.html"], "git_node": "1383e7cfb0b3700314156c417b59b4dd6441126a", "git_parents": ["cc64a45eb5c2336f98b576bd8301746881a5e583"], "node": "f2579068b4377926d784d20eb4a9d0f4ccb44158", "parents": ["42d9532d38da6abe8a3ecff079f3a81ee386e3fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080462 [wpt PR 63456] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326652, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSetting src to the empty string on a connected script element does not fire an error event (#63456)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox.\n\nThe script element's attribute change steps [1] say:\n\n    \"If localName is src, value is not null, and element is connected, then\n    run the script HTML element post-connection steps, given element.\"\n\nScriptElement::handleSourceAttribute() returned early when the value was\nempty rather than null, so setting src to \"\" on a connected script element\nthat had not yet started never prepared it, and the error event required by\n\"If src is the empty string, then queue an element task on the DOM\nmanipulation task source given el to fire an event named error at el, and\nreturn.\" was never fired.\n\nCheck isNull() instead. SVGScriptElement passes href(), which can be the\nempty string when the attribute is removed, so keep its existing behavior by\nskipping the call for an empty href.\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script-processing-model\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326652\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323200@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0c8e6e9999057f167da1947a1bea58b08348c4b3\nwpt-pr: 63456\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/fetch-src/empty-set-while-connected.html"], "git_node": "e95b2975a15adb9ba72b653ade089614eeaf239a", "git_parents": ["1383e7cfb0b3700314156c417b59b4dd6441126a"], "node": "860db5bf3efc7de7900516401b98f5ce02643db5", "parents": ["f2579068b4377926d784d20eb4a9d0f4ccb44158"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080474 [wpt PR 63455] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326650, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nModule script elements with an empty or invalid src fire the error event synchronously (#63455)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\n\"Prepare the script element\" [1] says:\n\n    \"If src is the empty string, then queue an element task on the DOM\n    manipulation task source given el to fire an event named error at el,\n    and return.\"\n\n    \"If url is failure, then queue an element task on the DOM manipulation\n    task source given el to fire an event named error at el, and return.\"\n\nThese steps run before the switch on el's type, so they apply to classic\nand module scripts alike.\n\nrequestClassicScript() already queues the task, but requestModuleScript()\ncalled dispatchErrorEvent() directly, so for module scripts the error event\nfired synchronously inside appendChild(). Use the same\nqueueTaskKeepingObjectAlive() pattern as the classic path.\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#prepare-the-script-element\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326650\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323198@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dcdb122e7425b76d3a1f7d477639115c16669646\nwpt-pr: 63455\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/src-empty-or-invalid-error-event-queued.html"], "git_node": "954c1e99a364219eb30c03417b06c18eeb86fda1", "git_parents": ["e95b2975a15adb9ba72b653ade089614eeaf239a"], "node": "2c1d3b117b27b4acd13280d2e25a417ed658935a", "parents": ["860db5bf3efc7de7900516401b98f5ce02643db5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076766 [wpt PR 63102] - Fix and extend cross-origin WebAssembly.Module sharing tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix and extend cross-origin WebAssembly.Module sharing tests\n\nSame-site documents share an agent cluster unless they are origin-keyed, and\nthe WebAssembly Web API only rejects a WebAssembly.Module whose agent cluster\ndiffers from the target's. Documents in non-secure contexts, which most of\nthese tests use, cannot be origin-keyed.\n\ncross-origin-module-sharing-fails.html used OTHER_ORIGIN for its \"different\nagent cluster\" subtest, but that origin is same site. Use\nHTTP_NOTSAMESITE_ORIGIN instead. Its HTTPS_ORIGIN subtest claimed the same\nagent cluster, but the scheme makes that origin a different site, so describe\nit accurately. Also cover a sandboxed iframe, whose opaque origin is only same\nsite with itself, and rename the test to window-cross-site-failure.html.\n\nshare-module-cross-origin-fails.sub.html expected sharing with a same-site\ncross-origin document to fail, contradicting\nwindow-similar-but-cross-origin-success.sub.html. That restriction is proposed\nin https://github.com/WebAssembly/spec/issues/1303 but is not part of the\nWebAssembly Web API. Replace it with window-same-site-success.sub.html, which\nexpects sharing with iframes on another host and on another port to succeed,\nwithout using document.domain.\n\nAdd window-cross-origin-isolated.https.sub.html. Cross-origin isolation keys\nagent clusters by origin, so sharing with a same-site cross-origin iframe fails\nthere while sharing with a same-origin iframe succeeds.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1c54118ac3bc08bc4292d14da0cc8daea302fd07\nwpt-pr: 63102\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/cross-origin-module-sharing-fails.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/share-module-cross-origin-fails.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/window-cross-origin-isolated.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/window-cross-origin-isolated.https.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/window-cross-site-failure.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wasm/serialization/module/window-same-site-success.sub.html"], "git_node": "32187686445b8b4d433c7c1ca0c912471098b8a2", "git_parents": ["954c1e99a364219eb30c03417b06c18eeb86fda1"], "node": "e0062498e1715106b4ddc897355601fd3793c1e2", "parents": ["2c1d3b117b27b4acd13280d2e25a417ed658935a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076766 [wpt PR 63102] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63102\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/serialization/module/cross-origin-module-sharing-fails.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/serialization/module/share-module-cross-origin-fails.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "0c6503d1ad775c24ad0b3aceddafefd4f0537bd3", "git_parents": ["32187686445b8b4d433c7c1ca0c912471098b8a2"], "node": "0cfe54f0b514e3e4d7c0f0ab406bfcf59fe81e57", "parents": ["e0062498e1715106b4ddc897355601fd3793c1e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1839958 [wpt PR 40709] - Make encrypt_after_connect support work, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake encrypt_after_connect support work (#40709)\n\n* Make the HTTP server also act as an HTTPS proxy\n\nEnable encrypt_after_connect on the plain HTTP server when SSL is\navailable, so that a PAC file can route https:// requests through it.\nAlways compute an SSL config when certificates are available, even if\nthe SSL environment is not otherwise enabled.\n\nAlso pass the CA certificate path for the pregenerated certificates so\nthat an SSL config is produced by default, and fall back to plain HTTP\nin start_http_server when there is no SSL config.\n\nExtend infrastructure/server/test-pac to cover an https:// request\nthrough the proxy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\n* Clean up wptserve's handling of connections encrypted after CONNECT\n\nClose TLS connections set up after a CONNECT request in finish(),\nsending a close_notify first. socketserver only closes the socket it\naccepted, which wrap_socket() detaches, so the TLS socket was left\nopen. This replaces shutting down every connection that is marked to\nbe closed, which ended TLS connections without a close_notify.\n\nTrack the scheme per connection, so that requests sent through a\nCONNECT tunnel have an https URL instead of the HTTP server's scheme.\n\nExplain why the connection is kept open after a CONNECT request.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b8aed1e7cd75850921d452b7d9a3e5c59cb5ac0\nwpt-pr: 40709\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/metadata/infrastructure/server/test-pac.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/metadata/infrastructure/server/test-pac.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/server/resources/proxy.sub.pac", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/server/test-pac.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/server/test-pac.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/serve.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptserve/tests/test_request.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptserve/wptserve/config.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptserve/wptserve/request.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptserve/wptserve/server.py"], "git_node": "5ef61465323e4bc5fe3cd1ae683d3e339a929009", "git_parents": ["0c6503d1ad775c24ad0b3aceddafefd4f0537bd3"], "node": "43bb9952b26d0659ac578948e5a07b140f2469ff", "parents": ["0cfe54f0b514e3e4d7c0f0ab406bfcf59fe81e57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1839958 [wpt PR 40709] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 40709\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/infrastructure/server/test-pac.html.ini"], "git_node": "f9d09095aafaafe2cc41a487715cca5b8aa0c011", "git_parents": ["5ef61465323e4bc5fe3cd1ae683d3e339a929009"], "node": "7a5f7c5e2e8a65164e6c7fb748bfe832de1ae474", "parents": ["43bb9952b26d0659ac578948e5a07b140f2469ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080344 [wpt PR 63466] - [chromium-bidi] Serialize input.releaseActions on the actions queue, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Serialize input.releaseActions on the actions queue\n\n- Serialize parallel input.performActions and input.releaseActions\n  commands on the top-level browsing context's actions queue, and relax\n  the WPT parallel pointer test to accept any integer detail on\n  mousemove.\n- Previously, input.releaseActions bypassed the actions queue and\n  deleted the InputState instance along with its mutex, while\n  input.performActions mutated input state before entering the queue,\n  causing pipelined commands to race and drop release events.\n- Build action ticks and dispatch release actions inside the top-level\n  InputState queue, and reset active input sources and cancel actions in\n  place while preserving the queue mutex.\n\nBug: 411434092\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I674f9899ba35afa1585edaf7ffd22c7a5dd436fd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8538847\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715405}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6471ef0635a21c6d482c1eb4880f011b08c187f6\nwpt-pr: 63466\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/queue.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/release_actions/queue.py"], "git_node": "49d89288627093331d88b87a82a61489a4eb4360", "git_parents": ["f9d09095aafaafe2cc41a487715cca5b8aa0c011"], "node": "964add7fa3f84d05766f1f9c261f56a63158a95b", "parents": ["7a5f7c5e2e8a65164e6c7fb748bfe832de1ae474"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080381 [wpt PR 63471] - [wpt] Mark scroll-to-text-fragment-security.sub.html as timeout=long, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Mark scroll-to-text-fragment-security.sub.html as timeout=long\n\nThe test opens five popups/iframes to a cross-origin (or noopener)\ntarget page, each of which requires spawning a new renderer process,\nloading the page, waiting two animation frames and round-tripping\nresults through the WPT stash. Locally this takes a steady ~4s against\nthe 6s default timeout, so it intermittently times out on loaded bots.\nSibling tests using the same pattern (scroll-to-text-fragment.html,\nscroll-to-text-fragment-security-replacestate.sub.html) already declare\n\ntimeout=long; do the same here and drop the flaky-timeout expectation.\n\nBug: 40818984\nChange-Id: I1c445ffda4f0c2a8ce23b538d31c5e9401b67a23\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8544211\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715434}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b69fbe9e40d48c3193a133bcb3aa6b8c2df0d571\nwpt-pr: 63471\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/scroll-to-text-fragment-security.sub.html"], "git_node": "890fc5d652a893866b85e3599b6be84454e445e3", "git_parents": ["49d89288627093331d88b87a82a61489a4eb4360"], "node": "b418a43013bab341c11a93e3b66fe8793ce9a2de", "parents": ["964add7fa3f84d05766f1f9c261f56a63158a95b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080382 [wpt PR 63472] - [wpt] Make clear-site-data/executionContexts test fail fast, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Make clear-site-data/executionContexts test fail fast\n\nexecutionContexts.sub.html waits unconditionally for an iframe to be\nreloaded by a 'Clear-Site-Data: \"executionContexts\"' response. Chromium\ndoes not implement the 'executionContexts' type (it is ignored with an\n'Unrecognized type' console warning, and '*' does not include it), and\nneither does any other shipping engine: Firefox removed it, and\nw3c/webappsec-clear-site-data#59 proposes dropping it from the spec. The\ntest therefore always runs into the harness timeout (and a content_shell\nkill) on every bot.\n\nBound each wait with test.step_timeout(1000) so unsupported\nimplementations produce a deterministic per-subtest FAIL in a few\nseconds, only start the clock once the response carrying the header has\nbeen received, remove each subtest's iframe on cleanup so a late message\ncannot leak into the next subtest, mark the test as timeout=long so the\ntwo sequential negative waits have ample headroom on slow bots, and drop\nthe no-op assert_true(true) calls. Add the Chromium baseline and remove\nthe [ Timeout ] expectation.\n\nBug: crbug.com/40475877\nChange-Id: I73c2a4794c6a209f59122851b01796df3740c4d7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8544830\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715435}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e779fd61e08ec7b11462cc160bae1ff263cb81f9\nwpt-pr: 63472\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/clear-site-data/executionContexts.sub.html"], "git_node": "a6faabd865f4df9c20efb14df0ee0ba403638b09", "git_parents": ["890fc5d652a893866b85e3599b6be84454e445e3"], "node": "84fb5536ac9c2515eb47bb3da0ea501741f9ab59", "parents": ["b418a43013bab341c11a93e3b66fe8793ce9a2de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080384 [wpt PR 63473] - [wpt] Make clear-cache.https.html deterministic, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Make clear-cache.https.html deterministic\n\nThe cache-clearing subtests compare random per-response tokens (uuid4\nstrings / random PNG dimensions). When a subtest fails,\nassert_not_equals embeds the token in its failure message, so the\nbaseline could never match and the test was marked '[ Failure ]  # Flaky\noutput'.\n\nAdditionally, clear-cache.https.html runs 13 sequential promise_tests\nthat open 32 popups sequentially (~8.3s), which previously caused it to\nalso time out against the 6s default timeout on Linux, Win, and Mac bots\n(it was marked '[ Failure Timeout ]  # Flaky output' on those platforms\nbefore https://crrev.com/c/7910841 consolidated the platform lines).\n\nAssert on the equality result instead so the failure message is stable,\nadd \u003cmeta name=\"timeout\" content=\"long\"\u003e, update the baseline, and drop\nthe flaky-output expectation lines.\n\nThe three Image/CSS/JS subtests still fail deterministically:\nClear-Site- Data: 'cache' clears the HTTP cache but does not evict the\nrenderer's in-process MemoryCache for the cleared origin, so same-origin\npopups keep reusing the cached resources (the fetch()-based subtests\npass because fetch() bypasses the MemoryCache).\n\nBug: none\nChange-Id: Ifd25b85f4c3dea88161cb1cd627008ee12336dff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8544790\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715436}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 521d168d63dbd206ea7fbe0b74ddd5760e6e668e\nwpt-pr: 63473\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/clear-site-data/clear-cache.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/clear-site-data/support/clear-cache-helper.sub.js"], "git_node": "c7cd0b85774dd934d567938bc420f648552af2b6", "git_parents": ["a6faabd865f4df9c20efb14df0ee0ba403638b09"], "node": "97036ea7d6242b4168f4d56168d6bac95d6d9008", "parents": ["84fb5536ac9c2515eb47bb3da0ea501741f9ab59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080370 [wpt PR 63469] - [wpt] sttf: don't assume text fragment scrolls within 2 frames, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] sttf: don't assume text fragment scrolls within 2 frames\n\nThe scroll-to-text-fragment-security-replacestate target page reports\nits scroll position two animation frames after load. Blink may\nlegitimately defer processing a cross-document text fragment until the\nbrowser confirms the browsing context group state\n(NotifyRelatedPagesFinalized, sent after DidCommit is processed) or\nuntil the newly opened popup's page visibility and layout lifecycle\nsettle, and the spec allows UAs to delay the search. On a busy bot this\noccasionally lands after the 2-rAF measurement, so the noopener 'sanity'\nsubtests flakily observe scrollY=0 and fail with 'Expected text fragment\ndirective to activate with noopener, but got scrollPosition=top'.\n\nPoll the scroll position across up to 10 animation frames before\nreporting scrollY=0 instead of sampling at a fixed 2-frame point.\nPositive cases report on the exact frame the scroll lands; the 'must not\nactivate' cases now wait 10 frames before reporting, which also makes\nthem a stronger check. Remove the Failure Pass expectation.\n\nBug: 552768634\nChange-Id: I3a0c9d6220352b7ef2c076c5e9e32a6ca0831625\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8542876\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715498}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9f868fd730423a984c45f32e6d524db9da9e21a5\nwpt-pr: 63469\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/scroll-to-text-fragment-security-replacestate-target.html"], "git_node": "99503718d42fb15cc5dda7ec94f41993b17f132f", "git_parents": ["c7cd0b85774dd934d567938bc420f648552af2b6"], "node": "6332aaead39c91cc80b10dd77c81acae08621ac4", "parents": ["97036ea7d6242b4168f4d56168d6bac95d6d9008"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080405 [wpt PR 63477] - Deflake html5-tree/dynamic-href-001.html by waiting for Ahem, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake html5-tree/dynamic-href-001.html by waiting for Ahem\n\n`wpt/mathml/relations/html5-tree/dynamic-href-001.html` is flaky due to\nnot waiting for Ahem to load. When the test is run by itself, the\nflakiness is consistently reproducible without this patch and goes away\nwith this fix, which waits for the font to be ready.\n\nBug: 568337130\nChange-Id: I32438cc59ade149082fb889b620ae42173356c9f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8541197\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715548}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d86e829895c95cb931038cda4e24968108f7d09c\nwpt-pr: 63477\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/dynamic-href-001.html"], "git_node": "e036451721e1ee97bd69289f94acacc874ac6266", "git_parents": ["99503718d42fb15cc5dda7ec94f41993b17f132f"], "node": "1b911f3e3b7e5a146bd6c2707f3628a664457aa0", "parents": ["6332aaead39c91cc80b10dd77c81acae08621ac4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080433 [wpt PR 63481] - [Masonry] Fragment nested dense-packed items, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Fragment nested dense-packed items\n\nFragmented grid-lanes iteration previously walked only each lane's root\nitem vector. Items stored above another item by dense packing were\nskipped, and spanners whose entries had different nested paths in each\nlane could not be resumed consistently.\n\nUse lane-local item index paths to walk nested storage in physical\nstacking order. Normal columns and rows visit dense children before\ntheir parent, while fill-reverse columns visit the recursively reversed\nparent first.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I7f25d568b0c375220ea0f3ceba09f9bd9471118d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8527177\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715671}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c8482945c1e2209f9668c3acf33908979fe54ff0\nwpt-pr: 63481\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-015.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-016-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-016.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-017.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-018-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-018.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-019.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-020-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-020.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-017.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-018.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-019-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-019.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-020.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-021-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-021.html"], "git_node": "5b833c6d323b5c5ab16600c027a7e1807f3e506a", "git_parents": ["e036451721e1ee97bd69289f94acacc874ac6266"], "node": "e9e659b864a4d62cb2452ac511311e296053bb29", "parents": ["1b911f3e3b7e5a146bd6c2707f3628a664457aa0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080433 [wpt PR 63481] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63481\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-017.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-019.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-020.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-017.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-018.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-019.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-020.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-021.html.ini"], "git_node": "fd2a10f37c8f8c7078be2e749760b0d8eac1fc43", "git_parents": ["5b833c6d323b5c5ab16600c027a7e1807f3e506a"], "node": "6d45e3b282abd8007b06075c8849fab3d4454468", "parents": ["e9e659b864a4d62cb2452ac511311e296053bb29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080431 [wpt PR 63480] - [FragmentedOofInCb] Relayout self-collapsed on BFC block-offset change., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[FragmentedOofInCb] Relayout self-collapsed on BFC block-offset change.\n\nInside block fragmentation, if there are any OOFs inside a\nself-collapsing block whose initial BFC block-offset estimate was wrong,\nwe need to relayout, just like we already do for adjoining floats. This\nis not an issue for non-FragmentedOofInCb, since then all OOF layout is\ndelayed until right before finishing layout of the outermost\nfragmentation context root.\n\nThe two tests included would fail when run as\nvirtual/fragmented-oof-in-cb/.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: I8b8c170084d43c7e2630443d72ead99e83a25ebe\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8548955\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715696}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b525d59a7ac82e619640d97ff49e6cc8ff973f39\nwpt-pr: 63480\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/oof-in-self-collapsing-block-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/oof-in-self-collapsing-block-002.html"], "git_node": "ad18dce3502488083676f7db2066d35342ba20de", "git_parents": ["fd2a10f37c8f8c7078be2e749760b0d8eac1fc43"], "node": "de48bbd9d6a2d5e4585841e01d0d7d20aebc95f3", "parents": ["6d45e3b282abd8007b06075c8849fab3d4454468"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079995 [wpt PR 63392] - Set WebSocketCommon state to kClosed when WebSocketStream aborts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSet WebSocketCommon state to kClosed when WebSocketStream aborts\n\nWhen WebSocketStream::OnAbort() cancelled the handshake and reset\nchannel_ to nullptr, it left common_ in the kConnecting state. Calling\nclose() afterwards passed a null channel_ to\nWebSocketCommon::CloseInternal() while in kConnecting, causing a null\npointer dereference in WebSocketChannelImpl::Fail().\n\nSimilarly, when WebSocketStream::Connect() returned early due to an\nalready-aborted signal, common_ remained in kConnecting and channel_ was\nnot cleared, keeping HasPendingActivity() true and causing subsequent\nclose() calls to fail an unconnected channel.\n\nSet common_ to kClosed and clear channel_ in both abort paths, and clear\nchannel_ and abort_handle_ when Connect() fails asynchronously.\n\nFixed: 432920899\nChange-Id: I2a827bba93ee1aa7e1743b2b28c9a0654478a315\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8522181\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715697}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dbb5468a70bbd3d64600cff8915b116d289d4954\nwpt-pr: 63392\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/websockets/stream/tentative/abort.any.js"], "git_node": "391c1eb82b782b7e753d1f5762283147c3b25174", "git_parents": ["ad18dce3502488083676f7db2066d35342ba20de"], "node": "90bf0ffd660d2b69d6d2af41ea70d2f23f9b641c", "parents": ["de48bbd9d6a2d5e4585841e01d0d7d20aebc95f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079995 [wpt PR 63392] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63392\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/websockets/stream/tentative/abort.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "7a140ecad888c5430210c72cfd454a50fa44299e", "git_parents": ["391c1eb82b782b7e753d1f5762283147c3b25174"], "node": "36d8d870f23b6a0057998b305a2c9142e21d5993", "parents": ["90bf0ffd660d2b69d6d2af41ea70d2f23f9b641c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "fantasai \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080509 [wpt PR 63500] - [css-text-3] Fix test metadata, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-3] Fix test metadata\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c0aad05975c9d3a25e03203057682dc80fad695e\nwpt-pr: 63500\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-008.html"], "git_node": "a755bb87d72d3b5262f42c4e5e5dde5fb6fdfe17", "git_parents": ["7a140ecad888c5430210c72cfd454a50fa44299e"], "node": "b7184350132c73c6a1df62461163a9612ddd90be", "parents": ["36d8d870f23b6a0057998b305a2c9142e21d5993"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080515 [wpt PR 63446] - Handle displaced reference node and stop parsing on write error in HTMLStream, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHandle displaced reference node and stop parsing on write error in HTMLStream\n\nWhen the reference node (next_child) is removed or moved out of its\nexpected parent mid-chunk (e.g. by a streamed inline script), drop\nsubsequent nodes, text, and foster-parented children instead of hitting\na DCHECK in ContainerNode::ParserInsertBefore or appending to the old\nparent.\n\nAlso call parser_-\u003eStopParsing() in HTMLSink::write before throwing on\nchunk string conversion failure or a displaced reference node, matching\nthe spec's writeSteps abort behavior.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: If4bd1f1b6aa1c9fbd1ca7040899131815102bda2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8498307\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715744}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 91a04631ef17ee6648110bddf8fe7b60e4ef5d9c\nwpt-pr: 63446\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-insertion-logic.html"], "git_node": "b49086a39f1c40206d5d119f9835f8ea59f93e30", "git_parents": ["a755bb87d72d3b5262f42c4e5e5dde5fb6fdfe17"], "node": "2ba2766f239634acbf5c61b11d686b2497f820ae", "parents": ["b7184350132c73c6a1df62461163a9612ddd90be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080515 [wpt PR 63446] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63446\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-insertion-logic.html.ini"], "git_node": "73c22c6456b3148949baf83ca9cc60c47560db93", "git_parents": ["b49086a39f1c40206d5d119f9835f8ea59f93e30"], "node": "e176df5de5f03d9a632f5c27cce64b7a7ef38bf7", "parents": ["2ba2766f239634acbf5c61b11d686b2497f820ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080516 [wpt PR 63434] - Flush pending text at the end of each chunk for HTMLStream, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFlush pending text at the end of each chunk for HTMLStream\n\nFlush pending text (including kTextMode) at the end of each chunk and before StopParsing() for fragment parsers, so written text is in the DOM when write() resolves and no text is left buffered in HTMLConstructionSite when a writer is dropped, aborted, or its write() rejects.\n\nFixed: 568820698\nChange-Id: I79c3302e2dd8a2f2999dfdda0f30019a18d0544e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8529649\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715746}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bcfb7996295b002bf8fc3f475594a47cd7c5c6c2\nwpt-pr: 63434\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html-unsafe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-append-html.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html.html"], "git_node": "649c2bffbdde511ee7486a2829e847b45c4c2f53", "git_parents": ["73c22c6456b3148949baf83ca9cc60c47560db93"], "node": "6f074cee6a53740f94e65aca5530801017e54081", "parents": ["e176df5de5f03d9a632f5c27cce64b7a7ef38bf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080516 [wpt PR 63434] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63434\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html.ini"], "git_node": "70f9c54400fd16787eddd495927d80ceaeb7b190", "git_parents": ["649c2bffbdde511ee7486a2829e847b45c4c2f53"], "node": "0a5b459633bae4c880ac3bc0a6f7de90a830c019", "parents": ["6f074cee6a53740f94e65aca5530801017e54081"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080454 [wpt PR 63485] - Let CSSParser::ParseFont() parse the shorthand directly, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLet CSSParser::ParseFont() parse the shorthand directly\n\nThis drops support for CSS wide keywords and pending substitution\nvalues, which were already being dropped after parsing.\n\nAvoids arbitrary declaration parsing in @supports which may access\ncross thread access to static Persistent in GetUACounterStyleMap().\n\nThis fixes a UAF issue when the singleton was created on an off-main\nthread and later accessed from the main thread.\n\nBug: 568832157\nChange-Id: I8793cee34fc032c43918599acc52f65a5ed1c039\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8525429\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715776}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c0f453e5ef5e3b4d468a11c734acbe1167fce27d\nwpt-pr: 63485\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/text/2d.text.font.parse.invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/text/2d.text.font.parse.invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/text/2d.text.font.parse.invalid.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/tools/yaml/text.yaml"], "git_node": "a1e22128962552eb8163127b9669662885b97456", "git_parents": ["70f9c54400fd16787eddd495927d80ceaeb7b190"], "node": "b83e1ff265a06f6b2f00f2380157d7025ea8ffaf", "parents": ["0a5b459633bae4c880ac3bc0a6f7de90a830c019"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Awogbemila \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080518 [wpt PR 63502] - Do not paint focus ring for display-locked \u003carea\u003e elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDo not paint focus ring for display-locked \u003carea\u003e elements\n\nWhen painting an \u003cimg\u003e with an associated focused \u003carea\u003e element,\nImagePainter::PaintAreaElementFocusRing calls EnsureComputedStyle() on\nthe \u003carea\u003e to check for outlines.\n\nIn the linked bug, Blink attempts to paint a display-locked \u003carea\u003e\nelement. This triggers a style update mid-paint which leads to a\nuse-after-free.\n\nThis CL skips painting the focus ring if the \u003carea\u003e is display-locked.\n\nBug: 570743446\nChange-Id: I6c2677fce30feb1e4a46e901a69c02084159c8b0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8551233\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715794}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 054a941a8e1d87613e173c8d74bfb1adae9d9091\nwpt-pr: 63502\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/crashtests/area-focus-in-hidden.html"], "git_node": "24bf7fca002bb86243547ae5164902b4fdebc4a5", "git_parents": ["a1e22128962552eb8163127b9669662885b97456"], "node": "777d5bdcee15c7b6b136d9cb7f68676822c29fc5", "parents": ["b83e1ff265a06f6b2f00f2380157d7025ea8ffaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080520 [wpt PR 63503] - [masonry] Test per-segment rule visibility, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Test per-segment rule visibility\n\nThe CSSWG resolved that rule visibility applies per segment in grid\nlanes. Our current implementation uses whole-lane occupancy, which can\nleave rules visible beside empty portions of a lane.\n\nMost of the coverage we had was with `rule-break: none`, which is not\naffected by the resolution. So this CL adds coverage for `rule-break:\nintersection`, and converts a test we had for `none` to be for\n`intersection`. These are marked as failing, the implementation CL will\nfollow.\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14489.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ia16e07c5c58479ca2742faf05c66fc2a6dce8c57\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8496106\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715798}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dd8f1fc24a4a1bb61decf449c7da8704b67a4db9\nwpt-pr: 63503\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010.html"], "git_node": "f2f0dbbd8ebb847b47e1bced3d1464c5dd023866", "git_parents": ["24bf7fca002bb86243547ae5164902b4fdebc4a5"], "node": "bcaa84418ae1e2fdbb06706e389c108f763b2060", "parents": ["777d5bdcee15c7b6b136d9cb7f68676822c29fc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080520 [wpt PR 63503] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63503\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-004.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-around-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-007.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-008.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/row-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-010.html.ini"], "git_node": "c5bd0da64f708d8aeaaba25c78f3b23a9481a8c6", "git_parents": ["f2f0dbbd8ebb847b47e1bced3d1464c5dd023866"], "node": "c829a25d3c80d315e0a5e38a24a8bfcf3d119b9a", "parents": ["bcaa84418ae1e2fdbb06706e389c108f763b2060"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080521 [wpt PR 63504] - [wpt] Fix guaranteed timeout in COOP access-reporting/reporting-observer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Fix guaranteed timeout in COOP access-reporting/reporting-observer\n\nThe last subtest (\"Access from cross-site iframe\") expects *no*\ncoop-access-violation report and calls `receive(this_window_token, 2000)`\nexpecting it to resolve with \"timeout\". However, dispatcher.js's\n`receive()` only takes a uuid and polls the dispatcher forever; the 2000\nis silently ignored. Because Chromium correctly never dispatches a report\nhere, the subtest can never complete and the whole test always hits the\nharness timeout (150s in Debug) and gets its content_shell killed.\n\nUse the directory's existing `receiveReport()` helper from\nreporting-common.js instead, which races the dispatcher against a 3s\nstep_timeout and returns \"timeout\" when nothing arrives, so the subtest\ncompletes in a few seconds. The test now passes deterministically on\nLinux, so drop the [ Pass Timeout ] expectation.\n\nBug: 40180286\nChange-Id: Ia92e732d80c25b46e66d8520b5e9b7b67d14ebe0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8547071\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715811}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 49692c66145b38c42b762de2236e30a8fc97ce6d\nwpt-pr: 63504\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/reporting/access-reporting/reporting-observer.html"], "git_node": "67f2ca92ceb4b681516cbc5b3283a760bf738a12", "git_parents": ["c5bd0da64f708d8aeaaba25c78f3b23a9481a8c6"], "node": "e091649219baacc4e8a52e780079b2d73bc5b761", "parents": ["c829a25d3c80d315e0a5e38a24a8bfcf3d119b9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Jansen \u003cjohnjansen@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080526 [wpt PR 63506] - [WPT] Fix img-sizes-auto test to use attribute selector, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPT] Fix img-sizes-auto test to use attribute selector\n\nThe test's \"!important\" subtest compares a real \u003cimg sizes=auto\nclass=test-important\u003e element against a synthetic \"expected\" clone\ncreated via createElementNS() in a non-HTML namespace.\n\nThe test's author rule `img.test-important { contain-intrinsic-size:\n30px 15px }` was meant to apply to that expected clone so the ref's\ncomputed style reflects the author-overridden value. Due to a Chromium\nbug (https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41276987), the class selector\nfails to match elements created in a non-HTML namespace, so the rule\nnever applied to the expected clone and the subtest compared against the\nwrong reference value.\n\nSwitch to the equivalent attribute selector\n`img[class~=\"test-important\"]`, which is not affected by this bug and\nmatches the expected clone correctly, so the subtest asserts against the\ncorrect reference value.\n\nBug: 571158508\nTest: Ran run_web_tests.py for img-sizes-auto.html; manually verified all 24 subtests pass in Firefox.\nChange-Id: Ia7a8d8fbff0a4515ec99370a4fa933f90a00b7ff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8539079\nCommit-Queue: John Jansen \u003cjohnjansen@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Jackson \u003cmjackson@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715829}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e131722122caf6b3649c01120fb29e32da53a42c\nwpt-pr: 63506\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/replaced-elements/images/img-sizes-auto.html"], "git_node": "2ea2a80034beafba0ae987c30aec1dc76adb59d4", "git_parents": ["67f2ca92ceb4b681516cbc5b3283a760bf738a12"], "node": "e2a1a39b729dbc03a88c2feb6cec8e4c4677086e", "parents": ["e091649219baacc4e8a52e780079b2d73bc5b761"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080536 [wpt PR 63508] - Preserve durations for unset or duplicate timestamps during encoding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve durations for unset or duplicate timestamps during encoding\n\nVideoEncoder previously tracked per-frame metadata in a base::flat_map\nkeyed by timestamp, defaulted unset frame durations to 0\n(base::TimeDelta()), and left DecoderBuffer duration at its default of 0\ninstead of media::kNoTimestamp when duration was zero or unset. This\ncaused input frames without a duration to produce EncodedVideoChunks\nwith duration 0 instead of null, and caused frames with duplicate or\nreordered timestamps to overwrite or misassociate metadata. Pending\nmetadata was also not cleared on reset().\n\nDefault unset frame durations to media::kNoTimestamp, store\nFrameMetadata in input order in a Vector, consume the first matching\nentry in CallOutputCallback() while evicting unmatched entries older\nthan the 16-frame reordering window, and clear pending metadata on\nreset().\n\nFixed: 561828156\nChange-Id: Ie05a8d1556a7651542c9076b71d39e3824fc7c08\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8537870\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715855}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: afc65f299c72f9a2133c547af46bb9e6951acdfd\nwpt-pr: 63508\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/video-encoder.https.any.js"], "git_node": "12c45e51b11d27da0a2f3d59781e8b609158131e", "git_parents": ["2ea2a80034beafba0ae987c30aec1dc76adb59d4"], "node": "d1286a4ce2da6b9129a15e21d35d0e57fa702532", "parents": ["e2a1a39b729dbc03a88c2feb6cec8e4c4677086e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080536 [wpt PR 63508] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63508\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "2ecd9bd70cd52dfbc8a3b5ee53d4f8a836d0fa5c", "git_parents": ["12c45e51b11d27da0a2f3d59781e8b609158131e"], "node": "f613bdbb9b251c5efbad23817847520e36e25438", "parents": ["d1286a4ce2da6b9129a15e21d35d0e57fa702532"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080294 [wpt PR 63465] - WebTransport: Implement WebTransport keying material export, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebTransport: Implement WebTransport keying material export\n\nImplement the current three-argument exportKeyingMaterial() API and\nscope TLS exporter output to the WebTransport CONNECT stream. Queue\nrequests made while connecting, reject requests after closure, and\nvalidate inputs at both the Blink and network-service boundaries.\n\nThe current Web IDL requires label, context, and outputLength; calls\nwith missing arguments reject with TypeError. Construct the HTTP/3\nexporter context in Chromium's dedicated WebTransport client using\nQUICHE's span-based QuicDataWriter API so the buffer size and storage\ncannot become inconsistent.\n\nExpose the API through the generated, disabled-by-default Blink\nWebTransportExportKeyingMaterial base feature.\n\nChromeStatus: https://chromestatus.com/feature/4860330806214656\nSpec: https://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransport-exportkeyingmaterial\n\nBug: 556304550\nChange-Id: Id925aa5633c8d0ae39fc59e0630ff1b214bbe9e6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8272125\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Gough \u003cajgo@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nidhi Jaju \u003cnidhijaju@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Monica Chintala \u003cmonicach@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715849}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 084bc83409ed15c241773281fe39902aef9bed9e\nwpt-pr: 63465\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/export-keying-material.https.any.js"], "git_node": "c5c825a57a4392e2d0a7f29287341bc518bd6090", "git_parents": ["2ecd9bd70cd52dfbc8a3b5ee53d4f8a836d0fa5c"], "node": "128bb4bf16decd3c761eccbe861c5b93963e265e", "parents": ["f613bdbb9b251c5efbad23817847520e36e25438"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080294 [wpt PR 63465] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63465\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/export-keying-material.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "843afa4c4361bc0d173c13f45c7953760fb4acd4", "git_parents": ["c5c825a57a4392e2d0a7f29287341bc518bd6090"], "node": "cd52a0804db7d65b9d1103bea2a510d34f44f30f", "parents": ["128bb4bf16decd3c761eccbe861c5b93963e265e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080412 [wpt PR 63463] - Reland \"Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\"\n\nThis is a reland of commit 198d0b60e4b380d9af19291d6f36813a808c675b\n\nThe original change was reverted because fast/ruby/text-decoration.html\nfailed on win11-arm64-rel-tests. It had added a win11-arm64-specific\nbaseline from a stale try run; the bot's actual output is byte-identical\nto the updated platform/win baseline. This reland drops the win11-arm64\nbaseline so the test falls back to the matching win one, and runs the\nCI-only suites on CQ via Include-Ci-Only-Tests to verify before landing.\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Keep wavy text decorations continuous across fragments\n\u003e\n\u003e Anchor the wavy pattern at the start of the decorating box instead of\n\u003e each fragment's own origin, so the wave phase no longer restarts at\n\u003e inline element boundaries like a nested \u003cem\u003e. Behind the default-on\n\u003e WavyDecorationContinuousPhase runtime feature as a kill switch.\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 41287729\n\u003e Change-Id: Ia6ec134cdab6bbb3d2f7f64b631bc499bd9f4a56\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8456548\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714354}\n\nBug: 41287729\nChange-Id: I1040cb7c219339dfb27166d953417e96ddd31272\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8537549\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715952}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7bcd699b26b51fb7ec8f49a46bf8d6d704fff358\nwpt-pr: 63463\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/reference/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-wavy-phase-across-elements-001.html"], "git_node": "055f06f9308b1761fa6c087d73ab91ae01696aef", "git_parents": ["843afa4c4361bc0d173c13f45c7953760fb4acd4"], "node": "29ccb4252916867875196691ebf5f8c67db4a672", "parents": ["cd52a0804db7d65b9d1103bea2a510d34f44f30f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080558 [wpt PR 63512] - [COOP] Fix top navigation and expectation in navigate-top-to-aboutblank, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[COOP] Fix top navigation and expectation in navigate-top-to-aboutblank\n\nnavigate-top-to-aboutblank.https.html has been marked [ Failure ] since\nCL 2565243 switched the iframe top-navigation from sandbox to\ntest_driver.bless(). Because the iframe is inside a COOP popup window\nwith no opener reference to the main testharness window, calling\ntest_driver.bless() inside the iframe fails in both wptrunner ('Tried to\nrun in a non-testharness window without a call to set_test_context') and\ncontent_shell, preventing the navigation to about:blank from ever\noccurring.\n\nFix this by setting sandbox=\"allow-top-navigation allow-scripts\nallow-same-origin\" on the iframe so it can navigate top without a user\ngesture while preserving its origin. Also update the third subtest\n(opener with COOP: same-origin-allow-popups navigated to about:blank by\na cross-origin iframe) to expect expect_opener_closed = true, as\nsame-origin-allow-popups only relaxes browsing context group switches\nwhen navigating from an initial empty document, not when navigating the\ntop-level document itself to COOP: unsafe-none.\n\nRemove the [ Failure ] expectation from TestExpectations.\n\nBug: 40734373\nChange-Id: Ie938eaa3fc741e0ba24eb3b22cbe44772f26eca4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549095\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715959}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1fb0000432983e7668ddaddd5e9fad7baec1b187\nwpt-pr: 63512\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/navigate-top-to-aboutblank.https.html"], "git_node": "c0f6c3742dda963335415b23313f5a9600baa3fa", "git_parents": ["055f06f9308b1761fa6c087d73ab91ae01696aef"], "node": "a0996e288840508ac91d51463d7811b1e28cb986", "parents": ["29ccb4252916867875196691ebf5f8c67db4a672"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080558 [wpt PR 63512] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63512\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/navigate-top-to-aboutblank.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "4c3c567ce174d5378c875c72266c4da1170ab78d", "git_parents": ["c0f6c3742dda963335415b23313f5a9600baa3fa"], "node": "25a4705da8fa5da7dfc42feddfff6efbb7e39364", "parents": ["a0996e288840508ac91d51463d7811b1e28cb986"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080522 [wpt PR 63505] - Deflake WPT COOP iframe-popup-same-origin-to-* tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake WPT COOP iframe-popup-same-origin-to-* tests\n\nIn resources/iframe-test.js:\n\n1. Run subtests sequentially with promise_test instead of\npromise_test_parallel, and clean up each subtest's iframe and popup\nvia t.add_cleanup (waiting for the popup to acknowledge before\nclosing) instead of add_completion_callback. Previously, all 6\nsubtests in a variant ran concurrently and kept all 6 iframes and 6\npopups alive polling /common/dispatcher/dispatcher.py until the entire\ntest file completed, saturating the 6-socket-per-origin HTTP/1.1 pool.\n2. In the 'severed' opener state with window_open, poll popup.closed in\nthe iframe up to 2.5s instead of relying on a fixed 500ms timer that\ncould race cross-process WindowProxy detachment IPC under load.\n3. Remove the obsolete unparameterized [ Skip Timeout ] entries for\niframe-popup-same-origin-to-unsafe-none.https.html and\niframe-popup-same-origin-to-same-origin.https.html, as well as the\nLinux [ Failure Pass ] entry for\niframe-popup-same-origin-to-unsafe-none.https.html?*, from\nTestExpectations.\n\nBug: 40815983, 539889938\nChange-Id: Idad1867ad8befaac0306f5834f51062f0d8b158e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8550153\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715814}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5a21b581e48eff9dc5cce62205d773cf2dbf2bf1\nwpt-pr: 63505\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/resources/iframe-test.js"], "git_node": "62f5ac56b2f3a234b326df54a70d07bf1e6be360", "git_parents": ["4c3c567ce174d5378c875c72266c4da1170ab78d"], "node": "74b7b6e83d7c9d159feb1dfab914868c1819015e", "parents": ["25a4705da8fa5da7dfc42feddfff6efbb7e39364"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080570 [wpt PR 63517] - [html-in-canvas] Keep MailboxTextureBacking single-threaded, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Keep MailboxTextureBacking single-threaded\n\nIn nested html-in-canvas scenarios, GetCanvasSnapshot recorded a nested\ncanvas snapshot without first making it unaccelerated. When transferred\nto worker threads via ElementImage, a single-threaded\nMailboxTextureBacking object bound to the main thread's GPU context\ncould be used on worker threads, causing multiple threads to\nsimultaneously use the main thread's unsynchronized\nRasterContextProvider. This patch ensures GetCanvasSnapshot only draws\nan unaccelerated snapshot, similar to the non-nested case in\nHTMLCanvasElement::PaintInternal.\n\nTo harden against this issue, the existing MailboxTextureBacking thread\nchecks have been converted to CHECKS, and have been expanded.\n\nFixed: 569129173\nChange-Id: Ide09e9375da36ba55bf3dca69d5eb1d2811112c7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549355\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716006}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d9984257b41603887635b9d841ac41e3a870bd6e\nwpt-pr: 63517\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/offscreen/manual/draw-element-image/offscreenCanvas-drawElementImage-worker.tentative.html"], "git_node": "0590fdc3ac0fbfe8df87a24f033cb5fd421f3f66", "git_parents": ["62f5ac56b2f3a234b326df54a70d07bf1e6be360"], "node": "1ea9c9a0b4a5c2078c8c3cd056c4a396b3e39b42", "parents": ["74b7b6e83d7c9d159feb1dfab914868c1819015e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080571 [wpt PR 63518] - [wpt] Make integrity-policy/style.https.html?reporting=true fail fast, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Make integrity-policy/style.https.html?reporting=true fail fast\n\nWhen a policy violation is expected, the ?reporting=true variant awaited\nthe ReportingObserver promise with no bound. Chromium only implements\nIntegrity-Policy for the script destination (IntegrityPolicyScript), so\nfor style no 'integrity-violation' report is ever dispatched and the\nvery first subtest hangs until the harness timeout, which is why the\nvariant has been [ Skip Timeout ] since it was imported.\n\nRace the report promise against a timer in both branches (1s when a\nreport is expected, keeping the existing 100ms when one is not). The\nstyle has already finished loading by this point, so a conforming\nimplementation still observes the report immediately, while a\nnon-conforming one now gets a deterministic per-subtest FAIL (\"Expected a\npolicy violation report\") in about a second instead of a timeout.\n\nAdd the Chromium baseline for ?reporting=true, which mirrors the existing\n?reporting=false baseline plus the report-only case, and drop the\n[ Skip Timeout ] expectation so the variant runs on the bots again.\n\nBug: 431034515\nChange-Id: Iaa024bc977d407cee48ba5fc25c1a55f69e391a1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8547072\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716020}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5cc2dd894eeb0b0cd25a3165fd872a6a5b025cac\nwpt-pr: 63518\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/subresource-integrity/integrity-policy/style.https.html"], "git_node": "ad96e7ab9c6db192af9ff271c79a348d41e59f0e", "git_parents": ["0590fdc3ac0fbfe8df87a24f033cb5fd421f3f66"], "node": "603f13188b64d67a2df29ce95f67dd0a919fb1a1", "parents": ["1ea9c9a0b4a5c2078c8c3cd056c4a396b3e39b42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080548 [wpt PR 63511] - Clean up open elements and pending scripts on HTMLStream abort and EOF, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nClean up open elements and pending scripts on HTMLStream abort and EOF\n\nAlign HTMLDocumentParser, HTMLTreeBuilder, ScriptLoader, and PendingScript with the WHATWG HTML spec for fragment parser abort and EOF:\n- On StopParsing() for fragment parsers ('abort a parser', fragment case), mark open \u003cscript\u003e elements already-started, pop all open elements so elements like \u003cstyle\u003e finish parsing children, and cancel pending parser-blocking and deferred scripts.\n- At EOF in the 'text' insertion mode, mark an unclosed \u003cscript\u003e already-started for fragment parsers, so it never runs even if it is later connected.\n\nBug: 491743369\nChange-Id: I92f8b6e1fc762a28de590ed32ff98b3e33c6e628\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8529650\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716036}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3d17e5ead7f00f8a5cb25c8574175d7a5d5ddc82\nwpt-pr: 63511\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/resources/slow.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-abort-unblocks-rendering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-parser-blocking-script.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/stream-html.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/tentative/unclosed-script-already-started.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/dynamic-markup-insertion/html-unsafe-methods/setHTMLUnsafe-runScripts.html"], "git_node": "093b8947f7af15418af3efdd3482ef78bb5ad968", "git_parents": ["ad96e7ab9c6db192af9ff271c79a348d41e59f0e"], "node": "c5b132d33413670349461b626c5fc37065e646de", "parents": ["603f13188b64d67a2df29ce95f67dd0a919fb1a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080548 [wpt PR 63511] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63511\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-abort-unblocks-rendering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-parser-blocking-script.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html-unsafe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/stream-html.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/domparsing/tentative/unclosed-script-already-started.html.ini"], "git_node": "d69c820c03735b4f1bdcc5045c09a4949cfd6ddf", "git_parents": ["093b8947f7af15418af3efdd3482ef78bb5ad968"], "node": "4bc83d92a22da5a963665cc5977075c74622eaae", "parents": ["c5b132d33413670349461b626c5fc37065e646de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080560 [wpt PR 63514] - [masonry] Fix paint order in reference, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Fix paint order in reference\n\nThe test was failing because in the reference, the third item's text was\npainting over the fifth item's text. This change addresses the paint\norder issue.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ib21d7960ba26cf450a2c6d77eeeab8252551c729\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8548915\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716054}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4910ef70cf457f143ebb7f86198134ebd2571882\nwpt-pr: 63514\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/column-negative-margin-003-ref.html"], "git_node": "4e8e21921e78e8d6d136ec4400d6dcb61c06ae36", "git_parents": ["d69c820c03735b4f1bdcc5045c09a4949cfd6ddf"], "node": "f5286dcb81cdb20b8db2f90ea173f07bb66027cc", "parents": ["4bc83d92a22da5a963665cc5977075c74622eaae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080547 [wpt PR 63509] - [Masonry] Preserve item end margins during fragmentation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Preserve item end margins during fragmentation\n\nGrid-lanes items include their block-end margins during initial\nplacement, but the per-fragment placement pass only used the fragment\nborder-box end. When a column item finished in a fragmentainer, this\ncould make the container fragment intrinsic block size too small and\nincorrectly carry trailing space into another fragment.\n\nPersist each resolved block-end margin in the shared item placement\ndata. Include it when the item first reaches its block end, then clear\nit so parallel-flow continuations cannot apply it again.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Idd1987b184dbe85f7ba5b3213cac563d753c5a1f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8532867\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716062}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 84fb58b58270525a849fd852e9a70029b6b7e30b\nwpt-pr: 63509\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-single-lane-fragmentation-005.html"], "git_node": "88974fa85b18c044c60091dfba3f03191cf27966", "git_parents": ["4e8e21921e78e8d6d136ec4400d6dcb61c06ae36"], "node": "040dc8b08cf3a5f68ad562f31f14f0388e40ebd4", "parents": ["f5286dcb81cdb20b8db2f90ea173f07bb66027cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080547 [wpt PR 63509] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63509\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-single-lane-fragmentation-005.html.ini"], "git_node": "e91b4aec6ab1927edc2905705494ef61c9ec9546", "git_parents": ["88974fa85b18c044c60091dfba3f03191cf27966"], "node": "f158691aaec85e9eea6d40abdb6a939ea588fbae", "parents": ["040dc8b08cf3a5f68ad562f31f14f0388e40ebd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080563 [wpt PR 63516] - [WebAudio] Test malformed AudioWorklet process() (Part 1 of 2), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Test malformed AudioWorklet process() (Part 1 of 2)\n\nRename audioworkletprocessor-no-process-function.https.html to\naudioworkletprocessor-malformed-process.https.html and expand it to\ncover undefined process(), a non-callable data property (42), a getter\nreturning a non-callable value (42), and a process getter throwing an\nError.\n\nAdd a subtest that assigns process after construction and before\nrendering, verifying that process is read in the rendering loop rather\nthan at registration or construction.\n\nCheck in the trunk failure baseline to be resolved in Part 2.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=a00f6083-3709-4d5a-a95e-434c28d1ecc1\n\nBug: 413259648\nTest: audioworkletprocessor-malformed-process.https.html\nChange-Id: Ica5ecafba0b76304df9a2f99506e9867e245c6a5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8520321\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716111}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2b92da0cf11fdf4a65f83d195a62544186047fe2\nwpt-pr: 63516\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-malformed-process.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-malformed-process.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-no-process-function.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-no-process.js"], "git_node": "8eaf47fe7ffc265aa5a23163b458c5dd590cda81", "git_parents": ["e91b4aec6ab1927edc2905705494ef61c9ec9546"], "node": "dd04c78c01b92ecdeb7ed763290ba3a9f879e69e", "parents": ["f158691aaec85e9eea6d40abdb6a939ea588fbae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080563 [wpt PR 63516] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63516\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-no-process-function.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "dd75ebbe56742d31f7ec424bc500bf216a01f855", "git_parents": ["8eaf47fe7ffc265aa5a23163b458c5dd590cda81"], "node": "7c92e19e2a62ff2e888064f03bb00c6039a10896", "parents": ["dd04c78c01b92ecdeb7ed763290ba3a9f879e69e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroshige Hayashizaki \u003chiroshige@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080561 [wpt PR 63515] - [PermissionsPolicy] Fix Allowlist::Contains() to match opaque origins for '*', a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[PermissionsPolicy] Fix Allowlist::Contains() to match opaque origins for '*'\n\nThis CL makes `PermissionsPolicy::Allowlist::Contains()` return true\nfor `matches_all_origins_` (`*` policies) even for opaque origins, so\nthat a wildcard allowlist '*' matches all origins, including opaque\norigins (e.g. sandboxed iframes or data: URL frames).\n\nThis new behavior aligns with:\n- The spec: https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-permissions-policy/#matches\n- `FeaturePolicy::Allowlist::Contains()` before\n  https://crrev.com/c/1430588 (which moved the '*' fallback after the\n  opaque origin early return)\n- `ParsedPermissionsPolicyDeclaration::Contains()`\n\nThe check order changes in this CL are:\n\n- Check `matches_all_origins_` first. This intentionally changes the\n  behavior as specified, which is covered by the added unit tests and\n  WPTs.\n- Check opaque origins before `allowed_origins_`. This doesn't change\n  the behavior, because `DoesMatchOrigin()` always returns false for\n  opaque origins.\n\nThis CL also updates\n`PermissionsPolicyTest.TestSandboxedFrameFromHeaderPolicy` to properly\npass an empty container policy, matching its comments and ASCII diagram.\n\nUnit tests in `permissions_policy_unittest.cc` (which mostly corresponds\nto the tests to be deleted in https://crrev.com/c/8464750) and WPT tests\nfor wildcard '*' container policies with sandboxed and data: URL frames\nare added.\n\nThis also fixes the behavior of Worker permissions policy\n(crbug.com/562705553) around `data:` workers, as\n`PermissionsPolicy::Allowlist::Contains()` can be called e.g. from\n`ExecutionContext::IsFeatureEnabled()` from\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8426410/10/third_party/blink/renderer/core/workers/shared_worker.cc#298\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=c5b4675c-907b-4a62-821b-dc605b21d806\n\nBug: 565859110, 562705553\nChange-Id: Ife867aba7e8309f499ffdce3304b288dfc50508d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464749\nCommit-Queue: Hiroshige Hayashizaki \u003chiroshige@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716126}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d5a765f1089ce6d3f72300281481edf3dddff7f3\nwpt-pr: 63515\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/policy-extends-to-data-url-all.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/policy-extends-to-sandbox-all.html"], "git_node": "e665f57ae8805c856e55f4888d3edab9c2cf0d61", "git_parents": ["dd75ebbe56742d31f7ec424bc500bf216a01f855"], "node": "7a0147e0d388d0bec761f847663fff37cf35d408", "parents": ["7c92e19e2a62ff2e888064f03bb00c6039a10896"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079563 [wpt PR 63353] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326665, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSeparate same-origin documents with a different Document-Isolation-Policy into different agent clusters\n\nSame-origin documents can now be in different agent clusters, so an origin\ncheck no longer tells whether one document can reach another. Building on\n322736@main, the UI process assigns each document an AgentClusterIdentifier,\nminted per browsing context group from the agent cluster key: site or origin,\nplus the cross-origin isolation key where one applies.\n\nThe identifier, origin keying, and policy travel as an AgentClusterAssignment.\nA preliminary one is made at navigation action time and replaced at response\ntime, when the policy headers are parsed. Loads that continue in another\nprocess get theirs through LoadParameters and GoToBackForwardItemParameters,\nand the injected bundle can no longer skip the response decision for\ndocuments that need it. Loads without a response decision now also record\ntheir historical agent cluster keying. The WebContent process no longer needs\nthe BrowsingContextGroupIdentifier.\n\nisPlatformObjectSameOrigin() adds the agent cluster check to\nisSameOriginDomain() wherever one document can reach another's objects or run\nscript in it, including javascript: URLs and the navigate event's\nsourceElement. Universal access bypasses it. The initial about:blank Window is\nnot reused across agent clusters, and javascript: URL and XSLT results keep\nthe identifier of the document they replace.\n\nSee https://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/11\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326665\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d6713be63025929a1e8d8af45baaff0744b5e50d\nwpt-pr: 63353\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/getter-special-cases/javascript-url-no.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/getter-special-cases/javascript-url-yes.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/header-parsing.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/resources/header-parsing-frame.py"], "git_node": "80473049a645c845146f4d0825c04f7af3c190b4", "git_parents": ["e665f57ae8805c856e55f4888d3edab9c2cf0d61"], "node": "38567c6dfac0bfd41c67e3380203f0f474b08175", "parents": ["7a0147e0d388d0bec761f847663fff37cf35d408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079563 [wpt PR 63353] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63353\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/header-parsing.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "03a76a59168bbeccd32575ee48a3ac1733fb9247", "git_parents": ["80473049a645c845146f4d0825c04f7af3c190b4"], "node": "a3bd336635abe16c2a78d3a77c1b4d9282027bd0", "parents": ["38567c6dfac0bfd41c67e3380203f0f474b08175"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080504 [wpt PR 63496] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326925, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nadoptedStyleSheets keeps applying removed sheets after length is shrunk, and stops picking up changes to a sheet after its duplicate is removed (#63496)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nCSSStyleSheetObservableArray::shrinkTo() dropped sheets from m_sheets without\ndetaching them from the tree scope, so `adoptedStyleSheets.length = n` never\ninvalidated style and the truncated sheets stayed applied. Overwriting an entry\nvia `adoptedStyleSheets[i] = sheet` likewise never detached the replaced sheet.\n\nCSSStyleSheet tracks its adopting tree scopes in a WeakHashSet with no\nmultiplicity, so when a sheet appeared more than once (e.g. [s, s]), removing a\nsingle occurrence via pop() removed the tree scope from the sheet entirely.\nSubsequent mutations of the still-adopted sheet (replaceSync(), insertRule())\nthen failed to invalidate that scope, leaving stale styles.\n\nReplace willRemoveSheet() with didRemoveSheet(), which runs after m_sheets has\nbeen updated and only detaches the tree scope when the sheet no longer appears\nin the array. Call it from shrinkTo(), removeLast(), the overwrite path in\nsetValueAt(), and setSheets().\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326925\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323233@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f9792821a217de2c3bd740ece725d59f2f75d1c2\nwpt-pr: 63496\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/adoptedstylesheets-observablearray-removal.html"], "git_node": "5e7366f3823ca856cb70d9adcfaea054296c212d", "git_parents": ["03a76a59168bbeccd32575ee48a3ac1733fb9247"], "node": "c9ba63820725378ea1c54efb2bb18f64b83088d7", "parents": ["a3bd336635abe16c2a78d3a77c1b4d9282027bd0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080614 [wpt PR 63453] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326655, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nExternal scripts blocked by 'strict-dynamic' do not fire an error event (#63453)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nWhen a CSP policy contains 'strict-dynamic', WebKit checks external scripts\nearly via ContentSecurityPolicy::allowScriptForStrictDynamic(). If that check\nfailed, requestClassicScript() and requestModuleScript() returned without\nfiring an error event at the script element.\n\nPer \"prepare the script element\" [1], a script blocked by CSP is a network\nerror, so el's result is null and \"execute the script element\" says:\n\n    \"If el's result is null, then fire an event named error at el, and\n    return.\"\n\nThis is also what WebKit already does when CSP blocks a script without\n'strict-dynamic', since the fetch is refused in the loader. For classic\nscripts, fall through to the existing queued error event; for module\nscripts, queue one on the DOM manipulation task source. Blocked inline\nscripts are unchanged, as the spec returns without firing an error event\nfor those.\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#prepare-the-script-element\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326655\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323191@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6a3c46c7c119fc84a80a1082fc8d21f9f5c24e66\nwpt-pr: 63453\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/script-src-strict_dynamic_parser_inserted_error_event.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/script-src-strict_dynamic_parser_inserted_error_event.html.headers"], "git_node": "59c04986d90655f408304af1a69f8ab4f26052db", "git_parents": ["5e7366f3823ca856cb70d9adcfaea054296c212d"], "node": "f081e0a1a56026c7bc6d2dbd3bba2d15af479f2c", "parents": ["c9ba63820725378ea1c54efb2bb18f64b83088d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080496 [wpt PR 63486] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326937, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplicit @scope in a constructed stylesheet adopted by a document matches nothing (#63486)\n\nPer [1], \"if no such element exists and the containing node tree is a shadow\ntree, then the scoping root is the shadow host. Otherwise, the scoping root is\nthe root of the containing node tree.\" For a constructed stylesheet adopted by\na document, that is the Document. ElementRuleCollector only produced implicit\nscoping roots for shadow root adopters, so nothing in such a sheet matched.\n\nUse the Document as the scoping root. Since scoped selectors are relative, \"with\nthe scoping root and descendant combinator implied at the start\" [2],\nSelectorChecker's descendant and child combinator walks now treat reaching a\nDocument scoping root as matching a lone :scope (or :where(:scope), which is\nwhat & resolves to). Every element \"that is an inclusive descendant of the\nscoping root\" [3] is therefore in scope, including the root element, while\n:scope itself still matches no element.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scope-limits\n[2] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoped-rules\n[3] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scope-atrule\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326937\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323237@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9ec154ff43db468923997c08bb08f905ceab62a5\nwpt-pr: 63486\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/scope-implicit-constructed-document.html"], "git_node": "2ddd918c3798192a3c1444a4deb1d8aedceef5f3", "git_parents": ["59c04986d90655f408304af1a69f8ab4f26052db"], "node": "0f7003931e917a15f98ac8cf8e2ad4c82ce5a3d4", "parents": ["f081e0a1a56026c7bc6d2dbd3bba2d15af479f2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080496 [wpt PR 63486] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63486\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-cascade/scope-implicit-constructed-document.html.ini"], "git_node": "ad7d3abc68f82e0200b37e32e10d860c32341047", "git_parents": ["2ddd918c3798192a3c1444a4deb1d8aedceef5f3"], "node": "bcc74f0eede6991fbe18a740c5fc1cc193b2a9f2", "parents": ["0f7003931e917a15f98ac8cf8e2ad4c82ce5a3d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080588 [wpt PR 63523] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327061, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAllow transferring streams to an AudioWorklet\n\nReadableStream, WritableStream, and TransformStream are [Exposed=*], but\ntransferring one to an AudioWorkletProcessor failed to deserialize there,\nbecause these serialization tags were special-cased to be unavailable in\nAudioWorkletGlobalScope until transfer there was tested.\n\nThe transfer receiving steps only need a JSDOMGlobalObject and a\nMessagePort, both of which AudioWorkletGlobalScope has. Use the\ngenerated exposure checks through isInterfaceExposedInGlobalObject()\nfrom 322979@main instead, and add a test.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327061\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f73756f43450758c18c6db2224d6348a2c908cef\nwpt-pr: 63523\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/streams/transferable/audioworklet.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/streams/transferable/resources/audioworklet-stream-processor.js"], "git_node": "7c2abfd83d57e8e46e5649185d549c37c40eda1b", "git_parents": ["ad7d3abc68f82e0200b37e32e10d860c32341047"], "node": "e18820b953bd7775ee4dddaa00e8864ade2660c2", "parents": ["bcc74f0eede6991fbe18a740c5fc1cc193b2a9f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080527 [wpt PR 63507] - layout: Don't treat `display: contents` as `none` on replaced elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Don't treat `display: contents` as `none` on replaced elements\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2f17dec1f36194d1c236120fd38b3556be466072\nwpt-pr: 63507\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-replaced-content.html"], "git_node": "41151a5af0cf6559f0f1fb9350e3ce792daad778", "git_parents": ["7c2abfd83d57e8e46e5649185d549c37c40eda1b"], "node": "5c845aa0f2f9bf1810cee630fea84d1198666484", "parents": ["e18820b953bd7775ee4dddaa00e8864ade2660c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "fantasai \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080620 [wpt PR 63535] - [css-text-3] Add line breaking regression test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-3] Add line breaking regression test\n\nSee\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325487\nhttps://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/76548\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 97501e6fb049952f915ba11b808cef154b63be5e\nwpt-pr: 63535\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-text-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-text-001.html"], "git_node": "f17065d709c82be59bd4d56f1440c340fd37e9b3", "git_parents": ["41151a5af0cf6559f0f1fb9350e3ce792daad778"], "node": "698658d335975bd594cb2b0f67dac790870bcef4", "parents": ["5c845aa0f2f9bf1810cee630fea84d1198666484"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080620 [wpt PR 63535] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63535\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/line-breaking/line-breaking-text-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "5796ef9b9a0f7032bdd1c404e74a281b39459459", "git_parents": ["f17065d709c82be59bd4d56f1440c340fd37e9b3"], "node": "bcbb6b1866ab1f77ea80dace8557b65e69042bff", "parents": ["698658d335975bd594cb2b0f67dac790870bcef4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079608 [wpt PR 63366] - Don't let `appearance` change `display` on non-widget elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't let `appearance` change `display` on non-widget elements\n\nOnly adjust `display` for elements with a native widget appearance.\nNon-widget elements keep their specified `display`, while widgets such\nas buttons still get the adjustment when author styles suppress their\neffective appearance.\n\nThis also restores markers on \u003cdetails\u003e and \u003cli\u003e with `appearance:\nauto`. Remove FixMarkerSuppressionForAppearanceAuto, which is superseded\nby this change.\n\nUpdate editing tests for the new layout: preserve the original input of\nthe table crash test but update its expected result; specify `display`\nin the span test; update the colgroup caret expectation.\n\nBug: 568576344, 408002786\nChange-Id: Ie59ec5c844c2450cedfb75703db6940cc6d29f7f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8498586\nAuto-Submit: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716385}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c999c58338ee1d223df5ad62e48be1202ced0d37\nwpt-pr: 63366\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/appearance-display-001.html"], "git_node": "0798aab5f6e3202b3fdfc63b09fb86bc5845acf7", "git_parents": ["5796ef9b9a0f7032bdd1c404e74a281b39459459"], "node": "d3aaf41d003cb802c18a176f530a78dc95fabcc2", "parents": ["bcbb6b1866ab1f77ea80dace8557b65e69042bff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080623 [wpt PR 63532] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327038, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainer size queries truncate fractional container sizes to integers (#63532)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nThe width, height, inline-size and block-size container features\nunzoomed the container's content box size with\nStyle::unapplyingZoom\u003cint\u003e, which converted the LayoutUnit to an int\nbefore comparing it with the query. On a 100.5px container,\n(width \u003e 100px) did not match and (width \u003c= 100px) did. Under zoom \u003e 1,\nthe int code path in unapplyingZoom adds 1 before dividing, so a 100.5px\ncontainer with zoom: 2 was evaluated as 101px and matched\n(width \u003e 100.5px).\n\nUnzoom as a LayoutUnit instead. evaluateLengthFeature already takes a\nLayoutUnit, so the int conversion only lost precision. The aspect-ratio\nand orientation features already used the unrounded LayoutUnit sizes.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327038\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323328@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1674c98db18f4486af07f03e8ceaae60cb33076a\nwpt-pr: 63532\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/size-feature-fractional.html"], "git_node": "1ddb9c4442911a32de546268ccb3ad7bb674c3c4", "git_parents": ["0798aab5f6e3202b3fdfc63b09fb86bc5845acf7"], "node": "335a7a2b4f288a304f21a2accb31734093bb5d8f", "parents": ["d3aaf41d003cb802c18a176f530a78dc95fabcc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080623 [wpt PR 63532] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63532\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini"], "git_node": "48b05be90ecb21c07ce1eb642048e38354320440", "git_parents": ["1ddb9c4442911a32de546268ccb3ad7bb674c3c4"], "node": "f578f01d3043e42e782638d332714ed38d228abf", "parents": ["335a7a2b4f288a304f21a2accb31734093bb5d8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080627 [wpt PR 63542] - Add tests that were left out of three WebKit exports, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest that Document-Isolation-Policy is ignored in an HTTPS iframe in an HTTP page\n\nAn HTTPS document embedded in an HTTP page is not a secure context, so its\nDocument-Isolation-Policy has no effect and a no-cors fetch of a resource\nwithout CORP still succeeds. This is the counterpart of\nhtml/cross-origin-embedder-policy/no-secure-context-https-iframe.html, which\n#63282 added. It was left out of that export.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326351\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322838@main\n\n--\nTest that MediaStreamTrackHandle cannot be transferred to shared and service workers\n\nMediaStreamTrackHandle is [Exposed=(Window,DedicatedWorker)], so transferring\none to a shared worker or service worker results in a messageerror event. This\ncovers the type that was left out of #63365, which tested the other Window and\nDedicatedWorker-only types.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326689\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323120@main\n\n--\nTest that a popup keeps its Document-Isolation-Policy across a browsing context group switch\n\nA popup whose response has Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin, opened by\na page without one, is moved to a new browsing context group. Its\nDocument-Isolation-Policy has to apply there as well: the popup is in an\norigin-keyed agent cluster and its no-cors fetch of a resource without CORP is\nblocked. This subtest was left out of #63353.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326665\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323290@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4f673b848fad8e9c1fea6e8edd676c6d2303a475, 00f17864cad00587bb01237d09f409f7f4fd2ec1, 561228c9c38619665d9956c74086c45ec4960e9c\nwpt-pr: 63542\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/no-secure-context-https-iframe.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-insertable-streams/MediaStreamTrackHandle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-insertable-streams/MediaStreamTrackHandle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html"], "git_node": "8e296b72a9e75e7bfbbdba342d89a39a507b320a", "git_parents": ["48b05be90ecb21c07ce1eb642048e38354320440"], "node": "b56099b64e1fb6a8c2a9023f2edaf37090f62d5c", "parents": ["f578f01d3043e42e782638d332714ed38d228abf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080627 [wpt PR 63542] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63542\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-insertable-streams/MediaStreamTrackHandle-transfer-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "90158cd3d291b08476fe7561411b0ce4f58af75c", "git_parents": ["8e296b72a9e75e7bfbbdba342d89a39a507b320a"], "node": "22b9856e837d200a5acefa87ece9ffaa6ef6b8b1", "parents": ["b56099b64e1fb6a8c2a9023f2edaf37090f62d5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080643 [wpt PR 63541] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327130, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPicking the selected option of a single-select deselects it\n\nThe pick an option algorithm only sets the selectedness of an option to true, so users cannot\ndeselect the option of a single-select, as with a native list box. Yet activating the selected\noption of a base appearance single-select list box deselected it, and so did assistive technology\nthere. The HTML standard defines the access key of an option to pick it, or toggle it in a select\nwith multiple, but unless the select had a base appearance picker it went through\nHTMLSelectElement::accessKeySetSelectedIndex(), which toggled it in any select. That also left the\nselectedOptions collection stale, and focused and clicked the select first.\n\nRemove the deselection from pickOrToggleOption(), and have HTMLOptionElement::accessKeyAction() and\nHTMLOptionElement::setSelectedByUser() use it regardless of appearance, so that\naccessKeySetSelectedIndex() can go. pickOrToggleOption() now only hides a base appearance picker.\n\npickOrToggleOption() still only sets the dirtiness of the option for base appearance. Picking and\ntoggling set it regardless of appearance, but no native user interaction sets it yet, not the\nnative popup nor mouse and keyboard input, so neither should the access key or assistive\ntechnology. Setting it for all of native appearance is left for a separate change.\n\ncustomizable-select-listbox-mouse-behavior.html expected the deselection, so update it.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327130\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be3ccb802967a8de6f237796c4c4fbe0612ce679\nwpt-pr: 63541\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select-listbox/customizable-select-listbox-mouse-behavior.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interactive-elements/commands/option/option-accesskey.html"], "git_node": "c753fc7b4dc0d7362e0be7a3859b65dc59c989a6", "git_parents": ["90158cd3d291b08476fe7561411b0ce4f58af75c"], "node": "4fbf7fd359a3125f4a635c2ed04cc7fa5d3a878a", "parents": ["22b9856e837d200a5acefa87ece9ffaa6ef6b8b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080643 [wpt PR 63541] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63541\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/commands/option/option-accesskey.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a5ec3c027760a54ca9ac59ce15ba60279c1f94b", "git_parents": ["c753fc7b4dc0d7362e0be7a3859b65dc59c989a6"], "node": "5a22c7e23ad784bb0391067b8b955055685f6e9e", "parents": ["4fbf7fd359a3125f4a635c2ed04cc7fa5d3a878a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072219 [wpt PR 62706] - [selectors] Test featureless matching with the shadow host as the subject, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSelectors: improve :host coverage\n\nA couple of these tests might need to be changed based on the outcome of https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14504\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 924c07ca386054695fbca532213a808a51a75d29\nwpt-pr: 62706\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/featureless-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/selectors/featureless-007.html"], "git_node": "c64b6907d64ab7d6dea8b1f3097287802d9e7c8e", "git_parents": ["9a5ec3c027760a54ca9ac59ce15ba60279c1f94b"], "node": "fe55651cc798f3669a2a509c920d16549d9f4cdd", "parents": ["5a22c7e23ad784bb0391067b8b955055685f6e9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072219 [wpt PR 62706] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62706\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/selectors/featureless-006.html.ini"], "git_node": "ec62a67a56cc3ee93871f884edf3ba13ff5bc5c7", "git_parents": ["c64b6907d64ab7d6dea8b1f3097287802d9e7c8e"], "node": "4392a2ff7352d74d01bd6618b512fd0d89db46aa", "parents": ["fe55651cc798f3669a2a509c920d16549d9f4cdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080592 [wpt PR 63524] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327062, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDOMException and QuotaExceededError should be exposed everywhere\n\nWeb IDL defines DOMException and QuotaExceededError as [Exposed=*], but\nWebKit only exposed them in windows and workers. Expose them in\nAudioWorkletGlobalScope and PaintWorkletGlobalScope too.\n\nSince 323229@main, deserialization checks the [Exposed] values of these\ninterfaces, so they can now also be posted to an AudioWorkletProcessor.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327062\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ddb25fdfff7766af4cd75eac3fb3b6ac206140ce\nwpt-pr: 63524\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebIDL/ecmascript-binding/es-exceptions/DOMException-audioworklet-processor.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/WebIDL/ecmascript-binding/es-exceptions/DOMException-audioworklet.https.html"], "git_node": "d24a903cc7779f6913377c7ad7bafb77cf762277", "git_parents": ["ec62a67a56cc3ee93871f884edf3ba13ff5bc5c7"], "node": "e129878a83d67848833edca81c8f14bbcd6e11b5", "parents": ["4392a2ff7352d74d01bd6618b512fd0d89db46aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080592 [wpt PR 63524] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63524\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/WebIDL/ecmascript-binding/es-exceptions/DOMException-audioworklet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "a038980745a345c6d1e7ace523edb1cec6a99108", "git_parents": ["d24a903cc7779f6913377c7ad7bafb77cf762277"], "node": "463ea818936e8a11cfb9582f07260c07eed249d1", "parents": ["e129878a83d67848833edca81c8f14bbcd6e11b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080651 [wpt PR 63534] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327090, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlob documents created by a document with an opaque origin lose its Document-Isolation-Policy\n\nA blob: document inherits the policy container of the document that created\nit, which BlobResourceHandleBase reflects as a Document-Isolation-Policy\nheader on the response. Since 323290@main the UI process applies that\nheader only in a secure context, which it computes from the response's\norigin. For a blob URL created by an opaque origin, such as a sandboxed\ndocument, the UI process can't recover the creator's origin, so the\npolicy was ignored and the blob document could load cross-origin\nresources that don't opt in through CORP.\n\nTreat the header on a blob: response as inherited: it is only present when\nthe creator's policy, obtained in a secure context, included it.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327090\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 87b5d13099c8bc2f9047ce1d29c963a3e0a246f6\nwpt-pr: 63534\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/blob-document-inherits-policy.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/resources/blob-creator-frame.html"], "git_node": "856e84a650bf043b77d7f1e066b24324ffd0c9c2", "git_parents": ["a038980745a345c6d1e7ace523edb1cec6a99108"], "node": "d03b9b780b0862218dc067c96e3f39227e42d48c", "parents": ["463ea818936e8a11cfb9582f07260c07eed249d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080651 [wpt PR 63534] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63534\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/blob-document-inherits-policy.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "c66c7b2104a1ba28e4047c876d139d58cff61761", "git_parents": ["856e84a650bf043b77d7f1e066b24324ffd0c9c2"], "node": "5b304fa76775ab25f7e303b6521a8a7ed058d5ed", "parents": ["d03b9b780b0862218dc067c96e3f39227e42d48c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080791 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to fea973d923cafb504cdca781c77fb782553d1459, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: fea973d923cafb504cdca781c77fb782553d1459\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/background-fetch/match-request-body.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/clipboard-copy-selection-line-break.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-on-self-origin-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https