], "user": "smolnar@mozilla.com"}, "45556": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging fc7b5f0153f851eecfbdd5567e5f1de8bb3a0584 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_159_0b2_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "5cbd6e771f20cb1316edac62c76b45450f3dbaa3", "git_parents": ["edc00968cc98b41b48c66bb3b00331fcc0213957"], "node": "a16686b76a686cb6f3896cd7100ec3b1ad57133d", "parents": ["efc7aa16e0a4b9b8bf41b78454c2d3dd0d09aaa5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983293, "git_changesets": ["5cbd6e771f20cb1316edac62c76b45450f3dbaa3"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45557": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging fc7b5f0153f851eecfbdd5567e5f1de8bb3a0584 with FIREFOX_159_0b2_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "4807cf82620b63962441550c82ccf93f52677f0b", "git_parents": ["5cbd6e771f20cb1316edac62c76b45450f3dbaa3"], "node": "20bf686faf047d6cbbf747fdf9cbdf3579b0e6f4", "parents": ["a16686b76a686cb6f3896cd7100ec3b1ad57133d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983417, "git_changesets": ["4807cf82620b63962441550c82ccf93f52677f0b"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45558": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging fc7b5f0153f851eecfbdd5567e5f1de8bb3a0584 with DEVEDITION_159_0b2_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "b66feef7e3c153f062d9a27e675e5c8f8cc1aed0", "git_parents": ["4807cf82620b63962441550c82ccf93f52677f0b"], "node": "199fb22c8a3c1aa493a6b0348f277aa487d5be69", "parents": ["20bf686faf047d6cbbf747fdf9cbdf3579b0e6f4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983530, "git_changesets": ["b66feef7e3c153f062d9a27e675e5c8f8cc1aed0"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45559": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging fc7b5f0153f851eecfbdd5567e5f1de8bb3a0584 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_159_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "78aeecafb3fdf0079b0b8f67359c4da3ab2272f1", "git_parents": ["b66feef7e3c153f062d9a27e675e5c8f8cc1aed0"], "node": "0dee593e7e121ea3a83768625a51849f3b4370c8", "parents": ["199fb22c8a3c1aa493a6b0348f277aa487d5be69"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791984916, "git_changesets": ["78aeecafb3fdf0079b0b8f67359c4da3ab2272f1"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45560": {"changesets": [{"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011842 - A GTest. r=botond\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300227\n", "files": ["widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetTouchEventIPC.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "c5704e119658f6d8b9b18b3f8c2881e4d4e91be3", "git_parents": ["3934f7874da5d43c3eac71e6f44e0afe79d9071f"], "node": "71af2d9270df1c4cfafdf14f57dda14c9967671a", "parents": ["3273685a4dab39957e6dcb403d1c12c52403a8c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067842 - Copy the untrimmed URL from the urlbar in popup windows r=adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333423\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_readOnly.js"], "git_node": "0b6f2d015b93b103ab901faa66e16838093844d2", "git_parents": ["c5704e119658f6d8b9b18b3f8c2881e4d4e91be3"], "node": "3923be6536e971292e1afc4fb08e80271b3f9ad0", "parents": ["71af2d9270df1c4cfafdf14f57dda14c9967671a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078481: Refactor CssAltContent into nsCoreUtils::GetCssAltContent. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nSince bug 1986641 removed attribute handling, CssAltContent no longer needs to be a class.\nGetCssAltContent returns Maybe\u003cnsString\u003e, where Nothing means no CSS alt content was specified and an empty string means it was explicitly specified as empty.\n\nMost of this is a straight move, but note the following:\n\n- mRealElement and mPseudoElement are now a single pseudoElement local variable, since the only remaining purpose of the real element was to check that the pseudo-element has a parent.\n- The non-pseudo-element case now returns early with a single combined condition instead of assigning mRealElement.\n- Alt text is appended with AppendUTF8toUTF16 instead of via a temporary NS_ConvertUTF8toUTF16.\n- ShouldCreateImgAccessible uses valueOr(u\"\"_ns) so that unspecified and explicitly empty alt content are still both treated as empty.\n- Callers now use the returned string directly instead of copying it via AppendToString; e.g. BundleFieldsForCache moves it into the field.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330963\n", "files": ["accessible/base/CssAltContent.cpp", "accessible/base/CssAltContent.h", "accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/base/moz.build", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.h", "accessible/base/nsTextEquivUtils.cpp", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "d600cdbf872ac0bd73717948b05fe71436cf5808", "git_parents": ["0b6f2d015b93b103ab901faa66e16838093844d2"], "node": "5ec3f6fb83c70c17987a6646849302a1280671ec", "parents": ["3923be6536e971292e1afc4fb08e80271b3f9ad0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1609953: Cache the text of list bullets rather than querying layout whenever the text is needed. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nPreviously, HTMLListBulletAccessible computed its text from layout on demand, including while computing text offsets during DOM mutations, when style might be dirty.\nIt is now a TextLeafAccessible which caches its text.\nThe text is set when the bullet is created and updated in NotificationController::WillRefresh when the marker's text is reflowed, both of which happen with clean layout.\n\nThe bullet remains a single Accessible backed by the ::marker element, rather than exposing the marker's generated text nodes as normal TextLeafAccessibles.\nThis is because a marker can have several text nodes (e.g. content: counter(list-item) \") \"), which would produce several list item marker Accessibles, but other code (e.g. line boundary handling in TextLeafRange and the Mac text marker code) assumes a bullet is a single Accessible.\nAlso, the spoken text (counter-style speak-as or list-style-image) can differ from the rendered text, which would break the assumption that a TextLeafAccessible's text matches its text frame when computing offsets and character bounds.\n\nThe bullet has its own AccType so that IsTextLeaf() returns false, since code which checks IsTextLeaf() assumes a DOM text node, text frame, character bounds, etc.\nAsTextLeaf() still works so that SetText, TextUpdater and nsAccUtils::TextLength work.\n\nRegarding the test, the !StylistNeedsUpdate() assertion only fires when a counter style lookup misses the cache while the stylist is dirty.\nNothing else resolves a speak-as reference to another counter style until the spoken text is requested, so the test uses this to cause a cache miss.\nIt replaces and flushes the stylesheet defining the referenced counter style, which evicts it from the cache, and then removes an unrelated stylesheet to dirty the stylist without flushing it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331503\n", "files": ["accessible/base/AccTypes.h", "accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/base/nsAccUtils.cpp", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/basetypes/Accessible.h", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible-inl.h", "accessible/generic/TextLeafAccessible.h", "accessible/html/HTMLListAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLListAccessible.h", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_treeupdate_list.js", "accessible/tests/browser/text/browser_text.js"], "git_node": "449af23c64e97dde189a74aa708f8525521223b4", "git_parents": ["d600cdbf872ac0bd73717948b05fe71436cf5808"], "node": "c547a8c85aa90322f64ebe3cc77eadfaaa05e985", "parents": ["5ec3f6fb83c70c17987a6646849302a1280671ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075119: Use CSS alt content for list bullets. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nList bullets get their text from layout via a separate code path, so they didn't support CSS alt content.\nHTMLListBulletAccessible::ComputeText now uses the alt content if there is any, and otherwise falls back to the spoken marker text.\n\nnsCoreUtils::GetCssAltContent normally ignores alt content on pseudo-elements with children, since it gets exposed on those children instead.\nHowever, a bullet is a single Accessible for the ::marker pseudo-element and its children are never exposed, so we now make an exception for ::marker.\n\nAs with other text, we don't create a bullet if its text is empty; e.g. because the alt content is empty.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331504\n", "files": ["accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLListAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLListAccessible.h", "accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_css_alt.js", "testing/web-platform/meta/accname/name/comp_name_from_pseudo_content_marker.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "e94d430ea00032551b0e924be8785f145a3dd3c3", "git_parents": ["449af23c64e97dde189a74aa708f8525521223b4"], "node": "6746c55c1468f19b3d2010a4a82c71a695814504", "parents": ["c547a8c85aa90322f64ebe3cc77eadfaaa05e985"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1609953, 2075119, 2078481: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLListAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "9f68694342352e5533964937a07cdd7f8b5db25c", "git_parents": ["e94d430ea00032551b0e924be8785f145a3dd3c3"], "node": "c931ded6246926d6b1ba9a8b55a9abe77f087e02", "parents": ["6746c55c1468f19b3d2010a4a82c71a695814504"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081138. Remove the branches from qcms's clamp_u8. r=jrmuizel\n\nIn a profile of decoding an HDR JXL image clamp_u8 went from 6.7% to 2.1% of the qcms work.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333165\n", "files": ["gfx/qcms/src/transform.rs"], "git_node": "d7b8e8d7ee395c771e8f154abcd2098736010b7b", "git_parents": ["9f68694342352e5533964937a07cdd7f8b5db25c"], "node": "b3269d3a6e8efa417601532cd2cab57b83cfdb03", "parents": ["c931ded6246926d6b1ba9a8b55a9abe77f087e02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080814 - [devtools] Add getSourceContentForResource to the window global target actor r=devtools-reviewers,devtools-backward-compat-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332867\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/sources/loadSourceText.js", "devtools/client/fronts/source.js", "devtools/client/fronts/targets/target-mixin.js", "devtools/server/actors/targets/window-global.js", "devtools/shared/specs/targets/window-global.js"], "git_node": "9b48d86d8ed4f54e19b50d298f355460a31ae477", "git_parents": ["d7b8e8d7ee395c771e8f154abcd2098736010b7b"], "node": "1d54c7d98bf7e90e9223b479611d1238a74b0af7", "parents": ["b3269d3a6e8efa417601532cd2cab57b83cfdb03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077502 - Fix stale threading comments in netwerk/protocol/http. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nCorrect the comments on nsHttpTransaction::mResponseHeadTaken, nsAHttpTransaction::RequestHead, the nsHttpHandler Alt-Svc functions, and the nsHttpConnectionMgr main thread section.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330416\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsAHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h"], "git_node": "58cd067213341f72192dda27b486031be4a602ba", "git_parents": ["9b48d86d8ed4f54e19b50d298f355460a31ae477"], "node": "ceb2725484e9cc460dcf7c86bb0ef3be2c80ee72", "parents": ["1d54c7d98bf7e90e9223b479611d1238a74b0af7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077501 - Assert that the Digest and NTLM authenticators are used on the main thread. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nBoth are singletons that keep per-call state in members, which is only safe because nsHttpChannelAuthProvider calls them on the main thread.  Assert that in ChallengeReceived and GenerateCredentials and note it on the members.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330415\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpDigestAuth.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpDigestAuth.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.cpp"], "git_node": "c8d58d16f9b5791b05f1f0cfd28df4327ab113f3", "git_parents": ["58cd067213341f72192dda27b486031be4a602ba"], "node": "f6036f72e960a832b377c83560b0f6e559d44e6f", "parents": ["ceb2725484e9cc460dcf7c86bb0ef3be2c80ee72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2011842 - A GTest. r=botond\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit c5704e119658f6d8b9b18b3f8c2881e4d4e91be3.\n", "files": ["widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetTouchEventIPC.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "1c54ef408048ff89c4bfe3b0440b6f87c45b01cb", "git_parents": ["c8d58d16f9b5791b05f1f0cfd28df4327ab113f3"], "node": "b3607c10dffa5304c4a531a80f891831a9d7f99c", "parents": ["f6036f72e960a832b377c83560b0f6e559d44e6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011842 - A GTest. r=botond\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300227\n", "files": ["widget/tests/gtest/TestWidgetTouchEventIPC.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "10df05cbd9ece9a84393678cec1bf4b1336aa89a", "git_parents": ["1c54ef408048ff89c4bfe3b0440b6f87c45b01cb"], "node": "892e98c21ebee39fd326f70d6fdcaa461bcb571e", "parents": ["b3607c10dffa5304c4a531a80f891831a9d7f99c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077499 - Document the shared request head in nsHttpTransaction and cancel the transaction if the pump cannot be created. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nThe transaction points at the channel's request head rather than copying it, so that the headers the socket thread adds or removes are what the channel reports as sent.  The channel normally outlives the transaction because the pump holds it until the transaction closes the pipe.  The exception was a failure creating that pump after the transaction had been handed to the connection manager, so cancel the transaction there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330414\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/TRRServiceChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h"], "git_node": "5329709268f84f5a2b4ff9ccd38fac483cd8ec91", "git_parents": ["10df05cbd9ece9a84393678cec1bf4b1336aa89a"], "node": "c8bb761c703e282477bceea6f50726caf955d15e", "parents": ["892e98c21ebee39fd326f70d6fdcaa461bcb571e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077502 - Fix stale threading comments in netwerk/protocol/http. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\" for causing build bustages at nsHttpTransaction.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 58cd067213341f72192dda27b486031be4a602ba.\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsAHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h"], "git_node": "e82a0dddc4aa8e4d34c94d11af8b3091527bd94a", "git_parents": ["5329709268f84f5a2b4ff9ccd38fac483cd8ec91"], "node": "e54907f24233a7efe2f60621e3439f7512c3782a", "parents": ["c8bb761c703e282477bceea6f50726caf955d15e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1831048 - Part 7: Fix \u003e100 'misc-unused-parameters' warnings under /accessible r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie\n\nhttps://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc/unused-parameters.html\n\nEverything found by ./mach static-analysis was manually inspected and changed if needed, before --fix commented out the rest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332243\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/atk/ApplicationAccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/atk/Platform.cpp", "accessible/atk/UtilInterface.cpp", "accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceAction.cpp", "accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceEditableText.cpp", "accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceTable.cpp", "accessible/base/AccAttributes.cpp", "accessible/base/AccAttributes.h", "accessible/base/DocManager.cpp", "accessible/base/TextAttrs.cpp", "accessible/base/TextLeafRange.cpp", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/generic/ApplicationAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/BaseAccessibles.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/ImageAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/OuterDocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLElementAccessibles.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLFormControlAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLImageMapAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLImageMapAccessible.h", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/xpcom/xpcAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/xpcom/xpcAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULElementAccessibles.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULListboxAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULMenuAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULTabAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULTreeAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULTreeAccessible.h", "accessible/xul/XULTreeGridAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "97065839d5157efc32a7f69bbd0e0a431b0b8f6f", "git_parents": ["e82a0dddc4aa8e4d34c94d11af8b3091527bd94a"], "node": "442774e012f0a0641c57f1999b9244ccc10b8716", "parents": ["e54907f24233a7efe2f60621e3439f7512c3782a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080272 - Make `IMContextWrapper::DispatchCompositionChangeEvent` check `mContentSelection.isSome()` at collapsing selection to expected position r=m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332722\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "a7ab07e4ee507a64590607e95c4dcccb1cb5ae38", "git_parents": ["97065839d5157efc32a7f69bbd0e0a431b0b8f6f"], "node": "cc0405c825c627d9a269fa7fe2eace66d7033167", "parents": ["442774e012f0a0641c57f1999b9244ccc10b8716"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050878 - Match the custom-car toolchain tasks by label, so that try pushes reuse the mozilla-central builds. r=perftest-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,kshampur,bhearsum\n\nThe job transforms remove a task's name before the custom_car transform runs, so that transform never matched a task. As a result, the mozilla-central builds were never indexed, and try pushes always built Chromium-as-Release again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333388\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/custom_car.py"], "git_node": "516b6f93ec5b1287a5e4247662f0e268a2aad147", "git_parents": ["a7ab07e4ee507a64590607e95c4dcccb1cb5ae38"], "node": "7af9c68caac82977ebb2e38e7e13ac90804594d6", "parents": ["cc0405c825c627d9a269fa7fe2eace66d7033167"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 1: SkPDF: Support specifying namespace for structure elements. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nWe need this in order to support tagging MathML in PDF, which requires that we specify the MathML namespace.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329544\n", "files": ["gfx/skia/skia/include/docs/SkPDFDocument.h", "gfx/skia/skia/src/pdf/SkPDFTag.cpp", "gfx/skia/skia/src/pdf/SkPDFTag.h"], "git_node": "16620648ab11592dccd1513f309439d75f99c6f0", "git_parents": ["516b6f93ec5b1287a5e4247662f0e268a2aad147"], "node": "634657fde0cd283ab2b74f0f840f92c8041fb3eb", "parents": ["7af9c68caac82977ebb2e38e7e13ac90804594d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 2: PdfStructTreeBuilder: Map MathML to PDF. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329545\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.h", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_structTree.js"], "git_node": "331ce59001582e5ff8324c495bc00c340aa26cc9", "git_parents": ["16620648ab11592dccd1513f309439d75f99c6f0"], "node": "c7a94d21edcb2388a11bc1335038f914d77500a7", "parents": ["634657fde0cd283ab2b74f0f840f92c8041fb3eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 3: Don't associate nsMathMLChar with an accessibility node if the character is implicitly drawn for the element (e.g. square root). r=layout-reviewers,accessibility-platform-reviewers,dshin,eeejay\n\nFor \u003cmsqrt\u003e and \u003cmenclose notation=\"longdiv\"\u003e, the characters are drawn implicitly for the element.\nIn these cases, the element itself is the semantic representation for accessibility; the character is purely presentational.\nThus, it should not be associated with an accessibility node and should be treated as an artifact in tagged PDF output.\n\nIn contrast, nsMathMLChar can also be used for \u003cmo\u003e in some cases.\nIn these cases, the character is necessary for meaning; \u003cmo\u003e by itself is meaningless.\nThus, we must ensure the character is associated with an accessibility node.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329546\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.h", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_artifacts.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_structTree.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/generate_pdfTest_font.py", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/head.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf^headers^", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.h", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmencloseFrame.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmoFrame.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmrootFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "e9d47b7670ce7b8e2d906069755f20b5c7ac9464", "git_parents": ["331ce59001582e5ff8324c495bc00c340aa26cc9"], "node": "3b8494218f05f154122b2295134197be040bc88a", "parents": ["c7a94d21edcb2388a11bc1335038f914d77500a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 4: Add glyph source text support to Moz2D and the Skia backend. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\ngfx::GlyphBuffer now has optional per-glyph source text and cluster fields, and DrawTarget has a new SupportsGlyphSourceText() method.\nFactory::CreateDrawTargetWithSkCanvas now takes a new argument which specifies whether the target supports this.\nPrintTargetSkPDF sets this for the PDF page canvas.\nWhen this is set and a caller supplies source text/cluster data, DrawTargetSkia uses SkTextBlobBuilder::allocRunTextPos instead of allocRunPos, falling back to the existing behaviour otherwise.\nWhen splitting glyphs into batches, it avoids splitting glyphs which share a cluster, since each batch only includes the source text for its own glyphs.\nNothing populates the new fields yet, so this is not a behaviour change on its own.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329547\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/2D.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetSkia.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetSkia.h", "gfx/2d/Factory.cpp", "gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.cpp"], "git_node": "ed9e04a238a43ccf417d1410a6ddd663907efdd1", "git_parents": ["e9d47b7670ce7b8e2d906069755f20b5c7ac9464"], "node": "bdd4a323eec7f8ef439dc03b5dd04c56f06be381", "parents": ["3b8494218f05f154122b2295134197be040bc88a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 5: Add a way for gfxTextRun::PropertyProvider to supply per-character source text. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nPropertyProvider has a new GetSourceText virtual method, which fetches the source text a range of the textrun was shaped from, as exactly one UTF-16 code unit per textrun character.\nThe default implementation returns false.\nnsTextFrame::PropertyProvider implements it by mapping back to the original DOM text via the skip-chars iterator, even for a transformed textrun, since text-transform must not affect a plain text copy.\nThe DOM text is never masked, so for a transformed textrun, it explicitly returns false for masked password characters.\nNot yet called from anywhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329548\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.h", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.h"], "git_node": "568491dafb4da7bb1d564fc83d14847f6765de43", "git_parents": ["ed9e04a238a43ccf417d1410a6ddd663907efdd1"], "node": "5c97b574d545469526c037ce128ab252435e5834", "parents": ["bdd4a323eec7f8ef439dc03b5dd04c56f06be381"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 6: Feed per-glyph source text into GlyphBuffer when drawing text. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\ngfxTextRun::Draw determines once per run whether to collect source text, based on whether there is a provider and whether DrawTarget::SupportsGlyphSourceText() says the target might be able to use it.\nIf so, gfxTextRun::DrawGlyphs fetches the source text for the range being drawn from the provider, converts it to UTF-8 along with a mapping from textrun characters to byte offsets, and passes these to gfxFont via TextRunDrawParams, just as it already does for spacing.\nThe conversion to UTF-8 happens here rather than in the provider because that is what Skia expects (as does cairo's equivalent API), whereas layout deals in UTF-16.\ngfxFont::DrawGlyphs maps each glyph to the source text of the character it was drawn for, plus any following characters that have no glyphs of their own.\nFor example, a ligature glyph maps to the text of all the characters it replaced.\nGlyphBufferAzure records a cluster offset for each glyph it buffers and passes the relevant slice of the source text to the DrawTarget whenever it flushes, which can happen part way through a run.\nThis fixes incorrect /ToUnicode mapping in PDF output for glyphs reached via OpenType substitution, such as MathML sub/superscript styling, when printing directly to SkPDF.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329549\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_sourceText.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/generate_pdfTest_font.py", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/head.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp"], "git_node": "8347bcc75b493d3d1ac36b1f326e5e05f10e4f8c", "git_parents": ["568491dafb4da7bb1d564fc83d14847f6765de43"], "node": "9f203fef7f16236bb3e612dfa61077f36a9d6b33", "parents": ["5c97b574d545469526c037ce128ab252435e5834"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 7: Plumb glyph source text from content processes to the parent process via DrawTargetRecording. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nRecordedDrawGlyphs, and the RecordedFillGlyphs/RecordedStrokeGlyphs events derived from it, now take the whole GlyphBuffer rather than just a glyph array and count.\nThey serialize the buffer's optional source text/cluster fields when present.\nBecause recordings can come from a less privileged process, the clusters are validated when an event is read, before they can be used to index into the text.\nDrawTargetRecording::SupportsGlyphSourceText defers to its recorder, since the target the recording will eventually be replayed against isn't known at record time.\nRecorders opt in via DrawEventRecorderPrivate::SetSupportsGlyphSourceText.\nThis is done for the recorder used for printing in a content process, and for CrossProcessPaint when painting out-of-process iframes for printing, since those are replayed directly into the print target.\nOther recording consumers such as remote canvas and WebRender blob images don't opt in, so they don't pay for this.\nThis is required for the fix in the previous patch to take effect when printing a document in a content process, since content process drawing is recorded and only replayed against the real target (e.g. a tagged SkPDF document) in the parent process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329550\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_sourceText.js", "gfx/2d/DrawEventRecorder.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.h", "gfx/2d/RecordedEventImpl.h", "gfx/ipc/CrossProcessPaint.cpp", "widget/nsDeviceContextSpecProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "268ef93f4a44a5489779e302f15a21f844a4af62", "git_parents": ["8347bcc75b493d3d1ac36b1f326e5e05f10e4f8c"], "node": "d14abaebd461dfa398c13ec9c5383d0a01091931", "parents": ["9f203fef7f16236bb3e612dfa61077f36a9d6b33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 8: Fix outline titles now that glyph source text is provided to SkPDF. r=gfx-reviewers,accessibility-platform-reviewers,lsalzman,eeejay\n\nWhen PDF outline generation was implemented in bug 1950656, source text wasn't passed to SkPDF.\nThat meant that SkPDF couldn't accumulate heading names for the outline from the source text.\nTo work around that, I tweaked Skia slightly to optionally use the alt text as the heading name without exposing the name as the alt attribute in the struct tree.\n\nNow that we pass source text to SkPDF thanks to the earlier patches in this stack, this previous support is redundant and causes duplicate text.\nInstead, in most cases, we now allow SkPDF to accumulate heading names from the source text.\nWhere a heading's name is overridden (e.g. using aria-label), we continue to pass it as alt text.\nHowever, we don't want to expose both alt text and source text, so this tweaks Skia to avoid accumulating heading names from the source text if alt text is explicitly specified for a heading.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329551\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "gfx/skia/skia/include/docs/SkPDFDocument.h", "gfx/skia/skia/src/pdf/SkPDFTag.cpp"], "git_node": "eecd30d8e7e2b8b7a2d9e3815957650649c39745", "git_parents": ["268ef93f4a44a5489779e302f15a21f844a4af62"], "node": "ecb74933bec64c14e23e523af89c74796e1269f5", "parents": ["d14abaebd461dfa398c13ec9c5383d0a01091931"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081545 - Update PDF.js to 288892aadaa27f03ed0cd4724edf678c6bda8e61 r=calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333472\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.renderer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/wasm/openjpeg.wasm", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/wasm/openjpeg_nowasm_fallback.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "62fcf3f5411f22404d8428ba2643611c352ba7d5", "git_parents": ["eecd30d8e7e2b8b7a2d9e3815957650649c39745"], "node": "69b96b76143abecb9f23045410dca963ed87d279", "parents": ["ecb74933bec64c14e23e523af89c74796e1269f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2077501 - Assert that the Digest and NTLM authenticators are used on the main thread. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\" for causing xpc failures @ nsHttpNTLMAuth.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit c8d58d16f9b5791b05f1f0cfd28df4327ab113f3.\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpDigestAuth.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpDigestAuth.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.cpp"], "git_node": "89de575fa346a585d32f68bab2b188e05d2f6cff", "git_parents": ["62fcf3f5411f22404d8428ba2643611c352ba7d5"], "node": "9e5483c9af09559e35aa724cb49f16f568d5bcf1", "parents": ["69b96b76143abecb9f23045410dca963ed87d279"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079053 - Make sure that `HTMLEditor::CreateAnonymousElement` and `HTMLEditor::GetPositionAndDimensions` won't handle different document's node r=m_kato\n\nIf the target node of resizers etc was moved into another document\nwhile we're initializing the native anonymous nodes, we may start to\nput some anonymous nodes into the new target's owner document.\nTherefore, the methods should return error in the case to make the\ncaller abort the initialization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332618\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLAnonymousNodeEditor.cpp"], "git_node": "8d2b3da7e72c0d2f6ceb26e56424240ec29d7f4b", "git_parents": ["89de575fa346a585d32f68bab2b188e05d2f6cff"], "node": "9004520450257c251472fd90ea99c01a670b86ac", "parents": ["9e5483c9af09559e35aa724cb49f16f568d5bcf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\naf -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nan -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nar -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nast -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\naz -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbe -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbg -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbn -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbo -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbqi -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbr -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbrx -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nbs -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nca -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nca-valencia -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\ncak -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nckb -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\ncs -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\ncy -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nda -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f44280e51424bd8\nde -\u003e 15d56609608c4fabd55708b79f442