 "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/aes-ocb.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/chacha20-poly1305.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/ed448.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/hybridkem.tentative.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/kmac.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/mldsa.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/serialization/x448.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/sign_verify/eddsa_curve448.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/sign_verify/kmac.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/sign_verify/mldsa.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/supports-modern.tentative.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/WebCryptoAPI/supports.tentative.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "ae5c6ff884ac0d3249e0e87815a95fd5e210f795", "git_parents": ["8dda403be18545d421ca35b299c6719751a0ff3a"], "node": "5e29cf0ebf788214c5c88909eb52cc9ca88e93ad", "parents": ["91502998c3bb5cc3bae8d134e4f90de9c6ad9e31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080864 [wpt PR 63558] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327184, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSizesAttributeParser::parse recurses per leading \"auto,\" entry, so a long sizes=\"auto,auto,\u2026\" exhausts the stack (#63558)\n\nWhen parsing a sizes attribute, each leading \"auto,\" entry was handled by\ntail-recursing into parse(). The call is not tail-call-optimized (the frame\ncarries locals and copies the token range), so an attribute such as\n\"auto,auto,auto,\u2026\" grows the stack one frame per entry and crashes the web\nprocess once it is large enough \u2014 around 27,000 entries in a Release build.\n\nConsume the leading \"auto\" entries iteratively instead. The behavior is\notherwise unchanged: \"auto\" followed by end-of-input or a comma sets the\nauto flag (and, for a comma, parsing continues with the remainder); any\nother token restores the saved range and falls through to the normal\n(media-condition, length) pair parsing.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327184\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323414@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c7bbc237dc396576b7486224a40a2ae2fa6d1141\nwpt-pr: 63558\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-many-commas-crash.html"], "git_node": "039209c709f2483874b700055c0338a2ec25f43b", "git_parents": ["ae5c6ff884ac0d3249e0e87815a95fd5e210f795"], "node": "2105a79c35ea2fb38bba18d7439661485ac5ae9a", "parents": ["5e29cf0ebf788214c5c88909eb52cc9ca88e93ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080864 [wpt PR 63558] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63558\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-many-commas-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "dcd9d244e3552b8d00c147da9efead129b589a94", "git_parents": ["039209c709f2483874b700055c0338a2ec25f43b"], "node": "9bf957f2ced64d908fc547502b7e2d7a57509a02", "parents": ["2105a79c35ea2fb38bba18d7439661485ac5ae9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Felipe Piubello \u003cpiubellofelipe97@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080983 [wpt PR 63571] - [chromium-bidi] Limit accessibility locator results across start nodes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Limit accessibility locator results across start nodes\n\nApply maxNodeCount to the accumulated accessibility-locator result when multiple start nodes are provided. Stop querying later roots after reaching the global limit.\n\nExtend the existing multi-root WPT across locator types, boundary counts, and both start-node orders.\n\nBug: 562178175\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: Ia904cba46aeaa5f8f12447764262a59b5ab52f33\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8411532\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716725}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 38d608e1005d6d7f0fecefb3b7b14109ab3c3b1d\nwpt-pr: 63571\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/max_node_count.py"], "git_node": "643a783c3a371072618c8ef20d445d2a0c91026e", "git_parents": ["dcd9d244e3552b8d00c147da9efead129b589a94"], "node": "13fa9c2f411ca492484b24ebbc1802309a4356af", "parents": ["9bf957f2ced64d908fc547502b7e2d7a57509a02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080983 [wpt PR 63571] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63571\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/locate_nodes/max_node_count.py.ini"], "git_node": "b5a8ae4a59565fcd94e06ddc5af0eaff354891d1", "git_parents": ["643a783c3a371072618c8ef20d445d2a0c91026e"], "node": "3e464b0a9383790ac9668b9f187cc6cf36065bd1", "parents": ["13fa9c2f411ca492484b24ebbc1802309a4356af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080979 [wpt PR 63570] - [ListMarker] Skip marker layout in locked items, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[ListMarker] Skip marker layout in locked items\n\nUsually, a \u003cli\u003e with content-visibility: hidden, skips its contents and\nwe put a display lock on it, so we don't update their style, and layout\ntreats it as if it has no children.\n\nThe outside ::marker was the exception. It gets to layout through a\nseparate path, and that path did not check the display lock. So we laid\nout a marker with an old style and if list-style-type changed from a\nstring to a counter style while the item was hidden, the marker still\nhad the string, and ListStyleTypeData::GetCounterStyleName() failed its\nCHECK.\n\nThis actually resulted in blink having a web visible bug: Where a hidden\nlist item would be as tall as its outside marker.\n\nThis CL adds the display lock check to\nLayoutInputNode::ListMarkerBlockNodeIfListItem(), which is the function\nthat feeds that path. We allow child layout only when it also allows\nchild style updates, so a marker that is laid out always has a current\nstyle.\n\nThis removes the known cause of the mismatch, so this CL also changes\nthe `DCHECK`s in ListStyleTypeData back to CHECKs, which reverts\nCL:8409749.\n\nThis also fixes the web-visbile bug. We follow CSS Containment spec,\nwhere content-visibility: hidden turns on size containment [1], and a\nbox with size containment is sized as if it has no content, not even a\n::marker [2].\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-contain-2/#skips-its-contents [2]\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-contain-2/#containment-size\n\nFixed: 559127243, 562119519\nChange-Id: I80a43d5b8c23d1abed1335b617ded8acc0e856c2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8444016\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716778}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9e69210455fe0c58e7e90c6b01d3131ed8166f7b\nwpt-pr: 63570\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-hidden-list-item-marker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/crashtests/list-item-marker-list-style-type-change-crash.html"], "git_node": "c39faa2f2f4ea3afd3748aa84b521d5d50f68606", "git_parents": ["b5a8ae4a59565fcd94e06ddc5af0eaff354891d1"], "node": "8ee1608d51ac7610a5391407bd3eb8de833fd6c9", "parents": ["3e464b0a9383790ac9668b9f187cc6cf36065bd1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080979 [wpt PR 63570] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63570\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-auto-applied-to-th-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/content-visibility/content-visibility-auto-selection-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "5dcd25da3a21bfc8d6c9669f2df50f68a00fc32e", "git_parents": ["c39faa2f2f4ea3afd3748aa84b521d5d50f68606"], "node": "8d2a3d5564c3d55c4068e7e379e7a0cab13c5681", "parents": ["8ee1608d51ac7610a5391407bd3eb8de833fd6c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "J\u00falio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080376 [wpt PR 63470] - Blur directly focused temporal input hosts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlur directly focused temporal input hosts\n\nBlurring a temporal input can close its picker or blur a shadow field\nwithout releasing focus on the input itself. This leaves coarse-pointer\ndate/time inputs focused after WebDriver Clear.\n\nThe views now call DefaultBlur() if the host was focused before cleanup\nand is still focused afterward, preserving focus moved by event handlers.\nTemporalInputHostBlur is a default-enabled kill switch.\n\nThe coarse-pointer suite adds 20 WPT variants on Android and Linux.\nAndroid covers touch devices; Linux exercises a pointer configuration\nthat its default fine-pointer runs miss. This configuration needs\npermanent regression coverage, so the suite has no expiry. It explicitly\nenables InputMultipleFieldsUIWithPointerChecks independently of rollout.\nThe ordinary variants also run in Headless after removing their\nContentShell exclusion.\n\nBug: 541316137\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: Ifa670b2edbf0af66b983518bae31d093e905e400\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8175546\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716806}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 785dad555f07facc855ea9f30676c957859ca3f6\nwpt-pr: 63470\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/focus-dynamic-type-change-on-blur.html"], "git_node": "c188caa2ad484ebf40729d4d59409d1f40759cb3", "git_parents": ["5dcd25da3a21bfc8d6c9669f2df50f68a00fc32e"], "node": "1af3524dd2d2b74e238fbda122423efbc98a63f1", "parents": ["8d2a3d5564c3d55c4068e7e379e7a0cab13c5681"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080434 [wpt PR 63482] - Implement OfflineAudioContext close(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement OfflineAudioContext close()\n\nThis CL implements OfflineAudioContext::close, which is part of the\nwebAudio specification.\n\nTo make sure that the OfflineAudioContext can dispose of the used\nresources properly, a synchronization mechanism was implemented to\ncoordinate the main and audio threads. By setting the atomic to true and\nposting OADH::AcknowledgeRenderStop on the audio thread, we make sure\nthat all previously posted render tasks in the audio thread will have\ntime to run and respond to the close request.\n\nThe close() sequence should be:\nMain thread:\n- Script calls OAC::close()\n- Set OAC internal state to closed\n- sets the atomic OADH::stop_requested_ to true\n- Posts OADH::AcknowledgeRenderStop on the audio thread\n- Returns the close promise\n\nAudio thread:\n- During OADH::DoOfflineRendering check OADH::stop_requested_ and stops rendering between rendering quanta.\n- Eventually, OADH::AcknowledgeRenderStop will execute and post OADH::NotifyRenderStopped on the main thread. No more chunks should be expected after that.\n\nMain thread:\n- Execute OAC::OnRenderStopped\n- Calls OAC::CloseInternal to clean up resources\n- Resolves the returned close promise.\n\nBug: 530596178\nChange-Id: I80b6af1ed58dda746f9b11318cee5af2022ca94c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8371474\nReviewed-by: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716918}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2edc3ef1eb8ef417e04fc77ce2abc14fe0ecd23d\nwpt-pr: 63482\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-offlineaudiocontext-interface/offlineaudiocontext-close.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-offlineaudiocontext-interface/offlineaudiocontext-incremental-rendering.html"], "git_node": "b49a699ee64dfc62d2a3b85750027aa6d01e37c9", "git_parents": ["c188caa2ad484ebf40729d4d59409d1f40759cb3"], "node": "ef03723a270a1d5066d87cb4e3d169d4b0c395f0", "parents": ["1af3524dd2d2b74e238fbda122423efbc98a63f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080434 [wpt PR 63482] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63482\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-offlineaudiocontext-interface/offlineaudiocontext-close.html.ini"], "git_node": "c40f706eacb860207fd054609b6053eda2380b7d", "git_parents": ["b49a699ee64dfc62d2a3b85750027aa6d01e37c9"], "node": "2fda96ccaeb193bd842109e1681d8d043525e87d", "parents": ["ef03723a270a1d5066d87cb4e3d169d4b0c395f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "wpt-pr-bot \u003cwpt-pr-bot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080593 [wpt PR 63525] - Update CODEOWNERS, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAutomated update of CODEOWNERS\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3381cffb7b36f5a8351c0dbb89a589d343799c26\nwpt-pr: 63525\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/CODEOWNERS"], "git_node": "3fcf10fb51b3be5cd2e580ac65a78741631e2bd1", "git_parents": ["c40f706eacb860207fd054609b6053eda2380b7d"], "node": "a04585ee336db085844a1e6c71994e3071458dd6", "parents": ["2fda96ccaeb193bd842109e1681d8d043525e87d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081000 [wpt PR 63575] - [VIZ] Prevent render pass backing padding from bleeding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[VIZ] Prevent render pass backing padding from bleeding\n\nRender pass backing textures can be larger than their logical content\nbecause allocation sizes are rounded or backings are reused.\n\nSkiaRenderer previously treated the entire physical image as valid\ncontent. When a render pass was upscaled with linear filtering, sampling\ncould reach transparent allocation padding and expose content underneath\nalong the right or bottom edge.\n\nConstrain valid texture sampling to the referenced source render pass's\noutput_rect. Apply the same bounds to regular render pass drawing and\nrender pass overlay preparation.\n\nRebaseline affected pixel tests to account for the corrected render-pass\nedge sampling.\n\nGate the behavior behind the RenderPassBackingLogicalBounds feature flag\nenabled by default to provide a kill switch.\n\nBug: 566909185\nChange-Id: I6cb840fae83963996a2f1093f6b99dd641ba27f9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8456389\nReviewed-by: Xiaoqian Dai \u003cxdai@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Michael Tang \u003ctangm@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vasiliy Telezhnikov \u003cvasilyt@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717060}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ca5384f99ee37dcabfe8078f5afaf419bd4784c0\nwpt-pr: 63575\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/render-pass-backing-logical-bounds-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/render-pass-backing-logical-bounds.html"], "git_node": "71f4bb3a92a79160a104ccc337dd465f27aae52f", "git_parents": ["3fcf10fb51b3be5cd2e580ac65a78741631e2bd1"], "node": "0c77a6034089d05bd4e142ae6aff26c264986818", "parents": ["a04585ee336db085844a1e6c71994e3071458dd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081036 [wpt PR 63578] - Implement the focusreset event (behind a flag), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement the focusreset event (behind a flag)\n\nThe focusreset event fires when we remove a focused element, with a\nsingle microtask delay to avoid firing synchronously inside a removal\nstep.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12842\n\nBug: 572677865\nChange-Id: I74f5516bcd70a72619092ee7b43aaae0722de5bd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8549440\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717162}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 68bb72601d35a8be5959cf4976cc85f916b70b6b\nwpt-pr: 63578\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-basic.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-cancelled-by-focus-update.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-iframe.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-moveBefore.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-removal-variants.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-timing.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/support/focusreset-helpers.js"], "git_node": "988e049de602c452d3e5275fad878679a92e4f23", "git_parents": ["71f4bb3a92a79160a104ccc337dd465f27aae52f"], "node": "2065c00e3f84871ea8bfd316c9dd83a3c3af74a5", "parents": ["0c77a6034089d05bd4e142ae6aff26c264986818"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081036 [wpt PR 63578] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63578\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-basic.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-cancelled-by-focus-update.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-iframe.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-moveBefore.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-removal-variants.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusreset/focusreset-timing.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "d43cf4083923234eaa56432f5a3f675cfa21baf5", "git_parents": ["988e049de602c452d3e5275fad878679a92e4f23"], "node": "68c9221bcf1246859ec37117d9ae412d330e6655", "parents": ["2065c00e3f84871ea8bfd316c9dd83a3c3af74a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081038 [wpt PR 63579] - [menu a11y] Give violated menus a list role, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[menu a11y] Give violated menus a list role\n\nWhen a page violates the menu elements' content model, we previously\nexposed the toplevel menu as an ARIA dialog and submenus as ARIA lists.\nDialog didn't do well in empirical testing; the keyboard focus behavior\ndidn't match. When the outer-most menubar was focused and announced as a\ndialog, pressing escape left focus on the menubar, which is not what a\nscreen reader user would expect. They expect the dialog to close and\nfocus to go somewhere else. But we can't close a menubar.\n\nSo now every violated menu owner, toplevel or not, is exposed as a\nlist.\n\nWe don't leave menuitem elements as menuitem roles inside the list. When\nwe tried that with plain menuitems, NVDA over-announced the word \"menu\".\nWe expect checkable menuitems left as menuitemcheckbox/menuitemradio to\nbehave the same way, so they aren't left as menu roles either. Plain\nmenuitems become listitems. Checkable menuitems become checkbox and\nradio, because ARIA doesn't allow listitem to have a checked state,\nwhich is kind of critical for checkable stuff.\n\nSubtle points around setsize/posinset that arose in implementation:\n\n- Once menuitems became listitems, the \"X of Y\" count would have counted\n  each menuitem's own contents, such as its text, as extra items of the\n  menu. This CL makes the counting skip the inside of a menuitem when\n  the list comes from a violated menu. Gecko does the same: when it\n  looks for an item's siblings, it never searches inside another item.\n\n- Once the menu became a list, all menuitems wrapped in a fieldset, even\n  in different fieldsets, were counted together, separate from the rest\n  of the menu. Instead, this CL counts menuitems wrapped in a fieldset\n  along with the rest of the menu's items. E.g. Copy, Invalid, and\n  Checkbox are announced as X of 3:\n  \u003cmenulist id=\"menu\"\u003e\n    \u003cmenuitem\u003eCopy\u003c/menuitem\u003e\n    \u003cbutton\u003eInvalid\u003c/button\u003e\n    \u003cfieldset checkable=\"multiple\"\u003e\n      \u003cmenuitem\u003eCheckbox\u003c/menuitem\u003e\n    \u003c/fieldset\u003e\n  \u003c/menulist\u003e\n\nOnly the behavior of menu elements is intended to change in this CL.\n\nBug: 425682466\nChange-Id: I8ee43b8f6ee5d37ee4245fbcd22e17c59a0d7f3f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8502151\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Lucas Radaelli \u003clucasradaelli@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717188}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 98a60676ce1e0e821aaca347bc7fdf26359cfb53\nwpt-pr: 63579\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-violation-mode-focus.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/reparent-with-pending-violation-microtask.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/valid-submenu-invalid-root.html"], "git_node": "75928ab77b59e2949428ecb6add2c0a0d6bc4d89", "git_parents": ["d43cf4083923234eaa56432f5a3f675cfa21baf5"], "node": "cab93512d1180421ac144b72353cab13c2718917", "parents": ["68c9221bcf1246859ec37117d9ae412d330e6655"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081038 [wpt PR 63579] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63579\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-violation-mode-focus.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/reparent-with-pending-violation-microtask.html.ini"], "git_node": "280970a983582d2c2b239534d390d822f92f2160", "git_parents": ["75928ab77b59e2949428ecb6add2c0a0d6bc4d89"], "node": "570a2e2a6b1343af4a147990657e5cdd7fbd4db7", "parents": ["cab93512d1180421ac144b72353cab13c2718917"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081065 [wpt PR 63441] - Preserve durations for non-unique/reordered timestamps during decoding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve durations for non-unique/reordered timestamps during decoding\n\nVideoDecoder previously tracked per-chunk durations in a base::flat_map\nkeyed by timestamp and erased [begin(), it + 1) upon producing an\noutput. This caused chunks with duplicate timestamps to overwrite\nearlier entries, and caused non-monotonic output timestamps (e.g.\ndecode-order timestamps with B-frame reordering) to erase pending\nentries for lower timestamps before they were output. Pending metadata\nwas also not cleared on reset().\n\nStore ChunkMetadata in input order in a Vector, consume the first\nmatching entry in MakeOutput() while evicting unmatched entries older\nthan the 16-frame reordering window, and clear pending metadata on\nreset().\n\nFixed: 561828151\nChange-Id: Iffd2e1734162ef5c9c7d22ccb91483e9fd1c8638\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8543332\nReviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717190}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d0e2802b0a2daa4ba26f7e4a52eba3ae89e66ec8\nwpt-pr: 63441\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js"], "git_node": "9a22f0c5aac80327db925896afa544f6f8fbfabe", "git_parents": ["280970a983582d2c2b239534d390d822f92f2160"], "node": "da934d58943606ab3ae2d7778f931955c98157d9", "parents": ["570a2e2a6b1343af4a147990657e5cdd7fbd4db7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081065 [wpt PR 63441] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63441\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoDecoder-codec-specific.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "9c4a31e00a662306d2649d3e0bdc76b43030bfc7", "git_parents": ["9a22f0c5aac80327db925896afa544f6f8fbfabe"], "node": "f2d723079d4be94d0f4149f1c483bb797e8b6f13", "parents": ["da934d58943606ab3ae2d7778f931955c98157d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexander Kyereboah \u003cakyereboah@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081085 [wpt PR 63585] - Add AccentColor keyword resolution WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd AccentColor keyword resolution WPTs\n\nAdd WPT coverage for AccentColor and AccentColorText resolution,\nanimation, cycles, forced colors, registered properties, and Canvas 2D.\nThe tests are expected to fail until the dependent implementation CL\nlands.\n\nBug: 536420071\nChange-Id: Id0a2eec50a0cde37ead7c4df75ee52847dc58e93\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8546693\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alexander Kyereboah \u003cakyereboah@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717217}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1b67fafba1d46d158b45a831bb604d86c9b5c5a8\nwpt-pr: 63585\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-cyclic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-resolution.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/accent-color-text-keyword-resolution.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/forced-colors-mode/accent-color-keyword-forced-colors.html"], "git_node": "92f86531c581c9eaff8b7a0a48903ba39cdc34f6", "git_parents": ["9c4a31e00a662306d2649d3e0bdc76b43030bfc7"], "node": "e861fac45d1283293d7cfa69ddf177be05bc4d84", "parents": ["f2d723079d4be94d0f4149f1c483bb797e8b6f13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081085 [wpt PR 63585] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63585\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-animation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-cyclic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/accent-color-keyword-resolution.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/accent-color-text-keyword-resolution.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/forced-colors-mode/accent-color-keyword-forced-colors.html.ini"], "git_node": "5c8b90d245635c1b6b0f38be0061af4d93f0d8fc", "git_parents": ["92f86531c581c9eaff8b7a0a48903ba39cdc34f6"], "node": "53113a279fb8b70662a4277b936c12156a174272", "parents": ["e861fac45d1283293d7cfa69ddf177be05bc4d84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081058 [wpt PR 63581] - [COEP] Deflake reporting-subresource-corp.https.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[COEP] Deflake reporting-subresource-corp.https.html\n\nreporting-subresource-corp.https.html has been flaking with both\ntimeouts and unexpected assertion failures on debug and Mac bots:\n\n1. resources/reporting-worker.js started a 200ms setTimeout before\nevaluating the fetch() script and unconditionally disconnected the\nReportingObserver when the timer fired. On slower bots, cross-origin or\nredirected worker fetches and ReportingObserver delivery can take longer\nthan 200ms, causing the worker to return fewer reports than expected.\n\n2. observeReports() in reporting-subresource-corp.https.html\nunconditionally slept 500ms in every subtest even after receiving all\nexpected reports (adding 5.5s of fixed sleep across the 11 frame/script\nsubtests), and started the timer before fetch() completed when\nexpected_count == 0.\n\nFix this by awaiting the evaluated script in reporting-worker.js and\nwaiting for expected_count reports when expected_count \u003e 0 (only using\nthe 200ms settle wait when expected_count is 0 or unspecified), and by\nawaiting the fetch promise in observeReports() and skipping the extra\ndelay once expected_count \u003e 0 reports have arrived. Remove the [ Pass\nTimeout ] entry from TestExpectations.\n\nBug: 40211077\nChange-Id: I9b7a64f93a5b11ec133a18405bf6d1c797a6f2f5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8547819\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717200}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 949615b58d896fc4838b43f8d63c9e0cec7b9298\nwpt-pr: 63581\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/cache-storage-reporting-dedicated-worker.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/cache-storage-reporting-service-worker.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/cache-storage-reporting-shared-worker.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/reporting-subresource-corp.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/resources/reporting-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore"], "git_node": "5a30147750a7c34bc10dcc8050a730f86165a60e", "git_parents": ["5c8b90d245635c1b6b0f38be0061af4d93f0d8fc"], "node": "264886cfb6c2dd75a6a5fd89d3ee1b2925aaab74", "parents": ["53113a279fb8b70662a4277b936c12156a174272"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Wojciech Bielawski \u003cwojciech.bielawski@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081067 [wpt PR 63582] - WebXR: Tolerate incomplete plane detection updates, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebXR: Tolerate incomplete plane detection updates\n\nXRPlaneManager assumes that plane IDs omitted from updated plane data are already present in its cache. After tracking data is temporarily unavailable, the cache can be cleared before the device resumes sending unchanged IDs. This causes a renderer CHECK failure.\n\nIgnore IDs that have neither updated data nor a cached XRPlane. A subsequent complete update can recreate the plane normally. This keeps malformed or temporarily inconsistent device deltas from terminating the renderer.\n\nTest: autoninja -C out/Default content_shell\n\nTest: autoninja -C out/Default blink_tests\n\nTest: third_party/blink/tools/run_web_tests.py --no-xvfb --no-show-results --no-manifest-update --additional-driver-flag=--headless=new -t Default external/wpt/webxr/plane-detection/xrFrame_detectedPlanes_incomplete_update.https.html\n\nTest: third_party/blink/tools/run_web_tests.py --no-xvfb --no-show-results --no-manifest-update --additional-driver-flag=--headless=new -t Default external/wpt/webxr/plane-detection/\n\nBug: none\n\nWebXR: Handle infinite far planes in projection matrices\n\nWebXR permits depthFar to be positive infinity. The existing projection calculations divide by near - far and later multiply the result by far. When far is infinity, this produces NaN entries in the projection matrix.\n\nCalculate the depth scale and translation separately before constructing the matrix. For an infinite far plane, use the analytical limits required by each clip-space convention:\n\nWebGL [-1, 1]: z_scale = -1, z_translate = -2 * near\nWebGPU [0, 1]: z_scale = -1, z_translate = -near\nApply this handling to both field-of-view and aspect-based projection calculations. Keep the existing finite-far formulas unchanged.\n\nAdd focused coverage for WebGL and WebGPU through both projection paths. Each test checks the complete matrix and verifies that every component is finite. Retain finite-far coverage to guard against changes to existing projection results.\n\nChange-Id: I0446c4d108d99e56689ab37e5b429ff01df27e1a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8523814\nCommit-Queue: Brandon Jones \u003cbajones@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Wojciech Bielawski \u003cwojciech.bielawski@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Brian Sheedy \u003cbsheedy@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Brandon Jones \u003cbajones@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717211}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cd1d8aa5bfebc15d1af2af230c7ff95f9e582a4c\nwpt-pr: 63582\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resources/chromium/webxr-test.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/plane-detection/xrFrame_detectedPlanes_incomplete_update.https.html"], "git_node": "c93afa4d47cfaa4f2c424d7243a715ff3df11368", "git_parents": ["5a30147750a7c34bc10dcc8050a730f86165a60e"], "node": "642742c9cabfc8abbbe409d9c12b9975364b6b56", "parents": ["264886cfb6c2dd75a6a5fd89d3ee1b2925aaab74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081067 [wpt PR 63582] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63582\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/plane-detection/xrFrame_detectedPlanes_incomplete_update.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "c57a444559e78f60c6ef3cf09875f37e13d18dc3", "git_parents": ["c93afa4d47cfaa4f2c424d7243a715ff3df11368"], "node": "aa4f5716f7d44c6ca3029449b2b89a4789737a06", "parents": ["642742c9cabfc8abbbe409d9c12b9975364b6b56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Hargett \u003cplaztiksyke@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076939 [wpt PR 63120] - Cover cast precision in composed graphs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCover cast precision in composed graphs (#63120)\n\n* Cover composed float16 cast rounding and NaN comparisons\n\n* Extend exact cast coverage to same-type float32 values\n\n* Cover exact float16 widening across tensor layouts\n\n* Keep NaN checks independent of float16 ordering fixes\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0bb6051de0901c7dcdc19f4b2a75d1195f649984\nwpt-pr: 63120\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/cast_rounding.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/helper-validation.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/resources/utils.js"], "git_node": "ba592837a78f61678c042d4346b3c64bfa7841a0", "git_parents": ["c57a444559e78f60c6ef3cf09875f37e13d18dc3"], "node": "8f97b3e1b02661c0fb85c18c3133cc79e2a21e17", "parents": ["aa4f5716f7d44c6ca3029449b2b89a4789737a06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081071 [wpt PR 63584] - Prevent Range::expand() from crossing shadow boundaries, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent Range::expand() from crossing shadow boundaries\n\nRange::expand() computes word, sentence, block, and document boundaries\nusing editing position utilities that can traverse the flat tree across\nshadow boundaries and return positions in a different TreeScope. Passing\nthose unadjusted positions to Range::setStart() and Range::setEnd()\ncauses the Range to collapse into the target shadow tree, exposing nodes\ninside closed or user-agent shadow roots.\n\nAdjust the positions in Range::expand() so that they remain within the\nRange's initial TreeScope, clamping positions that cross into a child\nshadow tree to before or after the shadow host and clamping positions\nthat cross out of a shadow tree to the start or end of the shadow root.\n\nFixed: 567936269\nChange-Id: I1d873ef6ed07998eae08f8d4c2644b424a035830\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8519883\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717233}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc3129961ca1225186fd69037d3e99dd976107bd\nwpt-pr: 63584\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/Range-expand-shadow.tentative.html"], "git_node": "ce6ed10a9d57ebd241abba5b1349b63561d91f49", "git_parents": ["ba592837a78f61678c042d4346b3c64bfa7841a0"], "node": "9365a548211e660818c2863c2b558c2d5c8abb05", "parents": ["8f97b3e1b02661c0fb85c18c3133cc79e2a21e17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081071 [wpt PR 63584] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63584\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/ranges/Range-expand-shadow.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "f2347db884761461512c5e307396efdafe75655a", "git_parents": ["ce6ed10a9d57ebd241abba5b1349b63561d91f49"], "node": "624745a2eb4486c9cfc5d0387fde1b33a4ba4aa6", "parents": ["9365a548211e660818c2863c2b558c2d5c8abb05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081093 [wpt PR 63587] - [HiC] Fix backdrop-filter combined with mix-blend-mode, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Fix backdrop-filter combined with mix-blend-mode\n\nSkia does not apply the backdrop filter when there is a\nblend mode also present on the layer, though it may depend\non exactly which blend mode. This was preventing CSS\nbackdrop-filter from functioning when a CSS mix-blend-mode\nwas also active.\n\nFix the issue by saving another layer for the blend mode.\nThe fix is complicated by the use of kDstIn blend mode to\nimplement masks, which still requires the blend mode on\nthe backdrop save layer.\n\nFixed: 567613565\nChange-Id: I3086e3747c70b8a0ebed2d3dde5d1c2a5b1b2ebd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8560238\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717273}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e723d22ab267e578885d1d546011f6b326b046d1\nwpt-pr: 63587\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-and-mask-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-and-mask.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-with-mix-blend-mode-and-opacity-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-with-mix-blend-mode-and-opacity.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-with-mix-blend-mode-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-backdrop-filter-with-mix-blend-mode.tentative.html"], "git_node": "cdb4af7d60f2531ab509f62328eb9c11c41b2d72", "git_parents": ["f2347db884761461512c5e307396efdafe75655a"], "node": "1406f6f7c9c0ed52765058f9d889f554f8e5dd87", "parents": ["624745a2eb4486c9cfc5d0387fde1b33a4ba4aa6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081097 [wpt PR 63588] - [HiC] Invalidate filters when an element moves into canvas, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Invalidate filters when an element moves into canvas\n\nTypically compositor filter operations are not rebuilt unless the style\nfilter value changes, regardless of paint invalidation. With this change\ncompositor filter operations will be aggressively rebuilt whenever\ncontent moves into a canvas.\n\nFixed: 572598342\nChange-Id: I4ea26b5c4974088b53fe5cfe96c6d316f81f7882\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8558681\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717279}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a7242745c4bb73eba4060a8ba1d7494292bb11e1\nwpt-pr: 63588\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/box-reflect-images-in-iframe-moved-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html"], "git_node": "3a9d74b3428fbb81d3d22ccca5d1a94da4463a11", "git_parents": ["cdb4af7d60f2531ab509f62328eb9c11c41b2d72"], "node": "792a4dbbbd506b17374adf0cf13a020dedb8e134", "parents": ["1406f6f7c9c0ed52765058f9d889f554f8e5dd87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081097 [wpt PR 63588] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63588\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/box-reflect-images-in-iframe-moved-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "83b201984ca7d3791e281707635ff258d9570cce", "git_parents": ["3a9d74b3428fbb81d3d22ccca5d1a94da4463a11"], "node": "74d1995c430c25c1662fafec3d47d2efc02abc7b", "parents": ["792a4dbbbd506b17374adf0cf13a020dedb8e134"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Wonik Choi \u003cchoiwonik91@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081092 [wpt PR 63586] - [Blink] Expose ProgressEvent in service workers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Blink] Expose ProgressEvent in service workers\n\nThe XHR specification exposes ProgressEvent to Window and Worker, but\nBlink currently omits service workers. Expose the existing\nimplementation there behind ProgressEventInServiceWorker, enabled by\ndefault with stable status while retaining a Finch kill switch.\n\nConvert the constructor WPT to .any.js to cover Window, dedicated,\nshared and service workers. Update the default and virtual/stable\nservice worker interface listings.\n\nBug: 332663431\nChange-Id: I07d53c1240fc35e0548e052ed00212d45e6e899b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8425503\nReviewed-by: Kentaro Hara \u003charaken@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kentaro Hara \u003charaken@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717288}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e1bc767ac9e91dcc0add5a1c0f82cd34ce048f7\nwpt-pr: 63586\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/progressevent-constructor.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/progressevent-constructor.html"], "git_node": "e699432449c4da8720add48660d544da68dabdb0", "git_parents": ["83b201984ca7d3791e281707635ff258d9570cce"], "node": "ec76667c0c7edcdb836436b60c90cb8be100dd16", "parents": ["74d1995c430c25c1662fafec3d47d2efc02abc7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Hargett \u003cplaztiksyke@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077116 [wpt PR 63165] - WebNN: test instance normalization with zero epsilon, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: test instance normalization with zero epsilon (#63165)\n\n* Test WebNN instance normalization with zero epsilon\n\n* Write literal zero-epsilon normalization expectations\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c14eda5b978ae32616b5856ef5747a7e64575654\nwpt-pr: 63165\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/instance-normalization-zero-epsilon.https.any.js"], "git_node": "ec90e0ac1a1f6d0e623185054068b6e6b6fe4c50", "git_parents": ["e699432449c4da8720add48660d544da68dabdb0"], "node": "6d3076387c04a304403179c8ec898d2d69f84244", "parents": ["ec76667c0c7edcdb836436b60c90cb8be100dd16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Hargett \u003cplaztiksyke@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077027 [wpt PR 63148] - WebNN: cover NHWC normalization affine operands, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: cover NHWC normalization affine operands (#63148)\n\n* WebNN: cover NHWC normalization affine operands\n\n* Use explicit expected normalization outputs\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6c99968b9aea04bc6d5f61194a200387505d41d9\nwpt-pr: 63148\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/instance-normalization-affine-layout.https.any.js"], "git_node": "4bbe37e51c213baaa87e777d878ea365e08de53b", "git_parents": ["ec90e0ac1a1f6d0e623185054068b6e6b6fe4c50"], "node": "20ed72f3c001783c371fa1f365089de67b43c3bd", "parents": ["6d3076387c04a304403179c8ec898d2d69f84244"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080594 [wpt PR 63418] - layout: Treat preserved tabs as conditionally hanging under `white-space: pre-wrap`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Treat preserved tabs as conditionally hanging under `white-space: pre-wrap`\n\nThe [specification] says that preserved tabs must hang conditionally\nwhen `white-space` is `pre-wrap`. This change does that, but\nincorporating this idea into inline content sizing, white space\ntrimming, and inline layout line breaking.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\nCo-authored-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c0105093437fa7c1e75910d508af0b4ba64c01db\nwpt-pr: 63418\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/hanging-whitespace-005.html"], "git_node": "2d9e1e7aadb7d982a218d64d459ff88b4c682e93", "git_parents": ["4bbe37e51c213baaa87e777d878ea365e08de53b"], "node": "5a7e5f410f0c12903a96d41fb9d1a15ae5bcaf7e", "parents": ["20ed72f3c001783c371fa1f365089de67b43c3bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080594 [wpt PR 63418] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63418\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/white-space/nowrap-wbr-and-space-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "dd0d7bd59d12c6b612cdb3d57ffa10c4cd1cb520", "git_parents": ["2d9e1e7aadb7d982a218d64d459ff88b4c682e93"], "node": "882be7d62eae3a34383a29d6314bdcdc0887e2cb", "parents": ["5a7e5f410f0c12903a96d41fb9d1a15ae5bcaf7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Skrzypczak \u003cglenn.skrzypczak@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080987 [wpt PR 63573] - script: set checked element state when cloning input element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: correctly update checked element state when cloning an input element\n\nSigned-off-by: Glenn Skrzypczak \u003cglenn.skrzypczak@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2c3d0bce856e4b6f63bcbd5c904657c25ef9d23c\nwpt-pr: 63573\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/selectors/pseudo-classes/checked-after-clone.html"], "git_node": "abdc7c728ea6a61d0ecf8b9ccb247e6b2371b008", "git_paren