om/D331927\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/XULPopupElement.webidl", "dom/xul/XULMenuParentElement.cpp", "dom/xul/XULMenuParentElement.h", "dom/xul/XULPopupElement.cpp", "dom/xul/XULPopupElement.h", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menu_accesskey_conflicts.xhtml", "toolkit/content/widgets/auto-accesskey.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "3356bc273eed89ca7ade4b9133142f5277532371", "git_parents": ["ac8be2fb0d0b9e0d8919c6a3341d6a1ed04c851b"], "node": "58f72244c88aa7b5a7d385d181f3bbc34a084395", "parents": ["0eed9551f71917ddd9c1dfb36a882f9681cec5c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076174 - Let typing a letter in an open menu select an item with a label that starts with punctuation or an emoji. r=dom-core-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331928\n", "files": ["dom/xul/XULMenuParentElement.cpp", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menu_typeahead_label_start.xhtml", "toolkit/content/widgets/auto-accesskey.mjs"], "git_node": "51d9d5566e456e3c571635048fd7079bb228763b", "git_parents": ["3356bc273eed89ca7ade4b9133142f5277532371"], "node": "e77b40218d48a0d0bcbf24a7911baf7985f49d56", "parents": ["58f72244c88aa7b5a7d385d181f3bbc34a084395"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081230: revert head_rev overriding from bug 2026291 r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nThis was done to address some Try-specific issues, but has caused real problems in production. We can probably do this in a smarter way, but in the near term let's revert it.\n\nI've left the `run_nightly` action changes made in that bug, as that is a try-specific action with no downsides to production.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333655\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/release_promotion.py"], "git_node": "1676fe802334e1360e5b9aa8392f6ccda206f1fa", "git_parents": ["51d9d5566e456e3c571635048fd7079bb228763b"], "node": "2eebb45ec05267e75c45b2b6d261844b5a9320df", "parents": ["e77b40218d48a0d0bcbf24a7911baf7985f49d56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080179 - P1. Vendor application-services bf6e952d for credit card CVV storage r=joschmidt\n\nVendor application-services bf6e952d3, which merges pull requests #7631 and\n#7648. #7631 (bug 2076154) keeps an optional CVV in the credit card store,\nencrypted like the number: UpdatableCreditCardFields.cc_cvv in, CreditCard.cc_cvv\nout, and a schema upgrade adding the column. #7648 (bug 2074008) exposes\nStore.credit_cards_bridged_engine(), which nothing uses yet;\nCreditCardsBridgedEngine is declared AsyncWrapped beside AddressesBridgedEngine.\n\nThe revision also carries the upstream changes since f22774fb: search-config-v3\nwork on the search engine selector (bugs 2063260, 2063272, 2061724 and 2050097),\nand the Glean error ping on iOS (bug 2011695), after which error-support builds\nGlean bindings with glean-build from glean v70.2.0, so its git source moves to\nthat tag.\n\nThis also includes the file changes from `./mach uniffi generate`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332402\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "docs/rust-components/api/js/autofill.md", "docs/rust-components/api/js/search.md", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/sql/create_shared_schema.sql", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/autofill.udl", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/credit_cards.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/models/credit_card.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/schema.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/store.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/lib.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/bridge.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/credit_card/incoming.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/credit_card/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/places/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/configuration_types.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/environment_matching.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/error.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/filter.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/selector.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/sort_helpers.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/test_helpers.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/types.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/support/error/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/support/error/build.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/support/error/src/error_tracing.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/support/error/src/lib.rs", "third_party/application-services/examples/autofill-utils/src/autofill-utils.rs", "third_party/application-services/megazords/ios-rust/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/moz.yaml", "third_party/application-services/testing/sync-test/src/autofill.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/autofill/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/autofill/autofill.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/search/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/search/search.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustAutofill.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustBreachAlerts.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustContextId.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustDbCrypto.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustFilterAdult.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustFxcontainers.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustLogins.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustRelevancy.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustRemoteSettings.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustSearch.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustSuggest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustTabs.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustViaduct.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustWebextstorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/config.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTests.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTestsCollision.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTestsExternalTypes.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-js/GeneratedScaffolding.cpp"], "git_node": "2c4c70cd841cf9d6d14294c78d609fa0e07adc1f", "git_parents": ["1676fe802334e1360e5b9aa8392f6ccda206f1fa"], "node": "496ed32b429d7bc8d0c25f9c81767d68eb914571", "parents": ["2eebb45ec05267e75c45b2b6d261844b5a9320df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080179 - P2. Store the credit card security code in the Rust store on Desktop r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin,joschmidt\n\nThe Rust credit card adapter gets its own valid fields, the ones its store has\na column for, so it adds cc-csc, mapped to the encrypted ccCvv, and drops\nbillingAddressGUID. cc-csc then counts in matching like any other field: a\nsaved card submitted with a new code is not a match, so the update doorhanger\noffers to save the code.\n\nStorage keeps the security code whatever the CVV prefs, and hides it from its\nconsumers while CVV is disabled. CreditCardRecord.normalizeFields drops cc-csc\nthen, so neither store writes one through add() or update(), and both strip it\nfrom every non-raw read through CreditCardRecord.stripSecurityCodeWhenDisabled.\nSync and the migration go through neither path and carry the code as stored.\nThe JSON store's getDuplicateRecords now yields cleaned copies, so that read is\nstripped too rather than handing out the store's own records. normalizeFields\nalso trims the code and drops one that is not 3 or 4 digits.\n\nThe Rust adapter's getSavedFieldNames reads raw, so a hidden code still counts\nas a saved field: the saved field names are recomputed only when the store\nchanges, so turning CVV on would otherwise offer no code until the next change.\nWhether the code is offered is decided where it would be filled.\n\nupdate() in the Rust adapter keeps the stored code when the record it is given\nomits cc-csc, and only an empty value clears it, which is what the JSON store\ndoes with cc-csc as an unknown field. The edit dialog has no security code\nfield while CVV is disabled, so saving a card from it keeps the code. update()\nmerges against a raw read so the hidden code is not lost; for addresses that\nalso keeps a country without metadata, as the JSON store does.\n\nThe migration carries the code into the Rust store but not back: the JSON\nstore would keep it in the clear. The copy back leaves cc-csc out, and the\nmigration no longer compares it. The CVV browser tests no longer skip under the\nRust store.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332403\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_capture_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_doorhanger_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_editCreditCardDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_manageCreditCardsDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_paymentsList_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAdapterBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/CreditCardRecord.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "91939a039c4e153afa02121fd079e9c2943f04c3", "git_parents": ["2c4c70cd841cf9d6d14294c78d609fa0e07adc1f"], "node": "17bbdb9133a3c1de0dce8bce9cde1aa670ab9823", "parents": ["496ed32b429d7bc8d0c25f9c81767d68eb914571"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080179 - P3. Only support credit card security codes while the Rust store is serving r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nisAutofillCreditCardCVVSupported now also requires the Rust credit card store\nto be active: the JSON store would keep the code in the clear. While it serves,\nno CVV option is offered and no new code is stored, and a code it already holds\nstays hidden. A profile with a primary password is never migrated, so it does\nnot get the feature.\n\nThe CVV browser tests switch to the Rust store through the new\nswitchCreditCardStore helper, and new tasks check the JSON store offers none of\nit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333604\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_capture_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_cvvPreference.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_doorhanger_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_editCreditCardDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_manageCreditCardsDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_paymentsList_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_creditCardCVVPrefs.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofill.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5d41bc07dec206ad511c2689f4b01ab74516c308", "git_parents": ["91939a039c4e153afa02121fd079e9c2943f04c3"], "node": "db4ce13b2efa0a4757d6bc771c280fb7c00b63fa", "parents": ["17bbdb9133a3c1de0dce8bce9cde1aa670ab9823"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080179 - P3. Only support credit card security codes while the Rust store is serving r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\" for causing documentation failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 5d41bc07dec206ad511c2689f4b01ab74516c308.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2080179 - P2. Store the credit card security code in the Rust store on Desktop r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin,joschmidt\"\n\nThis reverts commit 91939a039c4e153afa02121fd079e9c2943f04c3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2080179 - P1. Vendor application-se