], "git_node": "f1c69afb89ba3c13fabf778f79a8edb1351e97ff", "git_parents": ["43f1e88bb918c4ef69d190b6e5df6954862d3c19"], "node": "8ad1ce99e899cfdf678a84c7229eec4b5f2363ef", "parents": ["18400e1cbb5b2d1230c1642509ff56b1243d5540"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 2: PdfStructTreeBuilder: Map MathML to PDF. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329545\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.h", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_structTree.js"], "git_node": "592517211441ebf0343b336667fa37f354d2c43f", "git_parents": ["f1c69afb89ba3c13fabf778f79a8edb1351e97ff"], "node": "fb950509071c7a2aade449984babe7f66e3d44b3", "parents": ["8ad1ce99e899cfdf678a84c7229eec4b5f2363ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 3: Don't associate nsMathMLChar with an accessibility node if the character is implicitly drawn for the element (e.g. square root). r=layout-reviewers,accessibility-platform-reviewers,dshin,eeejay\n\nFor \u003cmsqrt\u003e and \u003cmenclose notation=\"longdiv\"\u003e, the characters are drawn implicitly for the element.\nIn these cases, the element itself is the semantic representation for accessibility; the character is purely presentational.\nThus, it should not be associated with an accessibility node and should be treated as an artifact in tagged PDF output.\n\nIn contrast, nsMathMLChar can also be used for \u003cmo\u003e in some cases.\nIn these cases, the character is necessary for meaning; \u003cmo\u003e by itself is meaningless.\nThus, we must ensure the character is associated with an accessibility node.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329546\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.h", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_artifacts.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_structTree.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/generate_pdfTest_font.py", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/head.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf^headers^", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.h", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmencloseFrame.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmoFrame.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLmrootFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "6a9512e66467093ce30ce95dbd1a8417046aa85b", "git_parents": ["592517211441ebf0343b336667fa37f354d2c43f"], "node": "ceb7b606668eb5fabdde3a0e680dbe33c2fa031e", "parents": ["fb950509071c7a2aade449984babe7f66e3d44b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 4: Add glyph source text support to Moz2D and the Skia backend. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\ngfx::GlyphBuffer now has optional per-glyph source text and cluster fields, and DrawTarget has a new SupportsGlyphSourceText() method.\nFactory::CreateDrawTargetWithSkCanvas now takes a new argument which specifies whether the target supports this.\nPrintTargetSkPDF sets this for the PDF page canvas.\nWhen this is set and a caller supplies source text/cluster data, DrawTargetSkia uses SkTextBlobBuilder::allocRunTextPos instead of allocRunPos, falling back to the existing behaviour otherwise.\nWhen splitting glyphs into batches, it avoids splitting glyphs which share a cluster, since each batch only includes the source text for its own glyphs.\nNothing populates the new fields yet, so this is not a behaviour change on its own.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329547\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/2D.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetSkia.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetSkia.h", "gfx/2d/Factory.cpp", "gfx/thebes/PrintTargetSkPDF.cpp"], "git_node": "c8c2d8354d01d3dbd02cf237aae0a32827cab2f2", "git_parents": ["6a9512e66467093ce30ce95dbd1a8417046aa85b"], "node": "0aafde3019dc283ad53fa791f5eba18e031d2976", "parents": ["ceb7b606668eb5fabdde3a0e680dbe33c2fa031e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 5: Add a way for gfxTextRun::PropertyProvider to supply per-character source text. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nPropertyProvider has a new GetSourceText virtual method, which fetches the source text a range of the textrun was shaped from, as exactly one UTF-16 code unit per textrun character.\nThe default implementation returns false.\nnsTextFrame::PropertyProvider implements it by mapping back to the original DOM text via the skip-chars iterator, even for a transformed textrun, since text-transform must not affect a plain text copy.\nThe DOM text is never masked, so for a transformed textrun, it explicitly returns false for masked password characters.\nNot yet called from anywhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329548\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.h", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.h"], "git_node": "b1a2dec0ac5d95926b0b5c111bb7367819a6961d", "git_parents": ["c8c2d8354d01d3dbd02cf237aae0a32827cab2f2"], "node": "b3cd849abe186d6223e55ea0d96891897dc36da2", "parents": ["0aafde3019dc283ad53fa791f5eba18e031d2976"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 6: Feed per-glyph source text into GlyphBuffer when drawing text. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\ngfxTextRun::Draw determines once per run whether to collect source text, based on whether there is a provider and whether DrawTarget::SupportsGlyphSourceText() says the target might be able to use it.\nIf so, gfxTextRun::DrawGlyphs fetches the source text for the range being drawn from the provider, converts it to UTF-8 along with a mapping from textrun characters to byte offsets, and passes these to gfxFont via TextRunDrawParams, just as it already does for spacing.\nThe conversion to UTF-8 happens here rather than in the provider because that is what Skia expects (as does cairo's equivalent API), whereas layout deals in UTF-16.\ngfxFont::DrawGlyphs maps each glyph to the source text of the character it was drawn for, plus any following characters that have no glyphs of their own.\nFor example, a ligature glyph maps to the text of all the characters it replaced.\nGlyphBufferAzure records a cluster offset for each glyph it buffers and passes the relevant slice of the source text to the DrawTarget whenever it flushes, which can happen part way through a run.\nThis fixes incorrect /ToUnicode mapping in PDF output for glyphs reached via OpenType substitution, such as MathML sub/superscript styling, when printing directly to SkPDF.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329549\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_sourceText.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/generate_pdfTest_font.py", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/head.js", "accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/pdfTest.ttf", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp"], "git_node": "b807edd9820819e20fcb01af7ca851775984bb91", "git_parents": ["b1a2dec0ac5d95926b0b5c111bb7367819a6961d"], "node": "89d79e18c5b6612fdeced3169659d148f7f12134", "parents": ["b3cd849abe186d6223e55ea0d96891897dc36da2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 7: Plumb glyph source text from content processes to the parent process via DrawTargetRecording. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nRecordedDrawGlyphs, and the RecordedFillGlyphs/RecordedStrokeGlyphs events derived from it, now take the whole GlyphBuffer rather than just a glyph array and count.\nThey serialize the buffer's optional source text/cluster fields when present.\nBecause recordings can come from a less privileged process, the clusters are validated when an event is read, before they can be used to index into the text.\nDrawTargetRecording::SupportsGlyphSourceText defers to its recorder, since the target the recording will eventually be replayed against isn't known at record time.\nRecorders opt in via DrawEventRecorderPrivate::SetSupportsGlyphSourceText.\nThis is done for the recorder used for printing in a content process, and for CrossProcessPaint when painting out-of-process iframes for printing, since those are replayed directly into the print target.\nOther recording consumers such as remote canvas and WebRender blob images don't opt in, so they don't pay for this.\nThis is required for the fix in the previous patch to take effect when printing a document in a content process, since content process drawing is recorded and only replayed against the real target (e.g. a tagged SkPDF document) in the parent process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329550\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/pdfOutput/browser_sourceText.js", "gfx/2d/DrawEventRecorder.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.h", "gfx/2d/RecordedEventImpl.h", "gfx/ipc/CrossProcessPaint.cpp", "widget/nsDeviceContextSpecProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "31fced352fbf9ab2155b87237b3773b3e4ca030f", "git_parents": ["b807edd9820819e20fcb01af7ca851775984bb91"], "node": "3d6be35d4d2fa2824bb1d1c6e8efcf9d46c124e0", "parents": ["89d79e18c5b6612fdeced3169659d148f7f12134"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055405 part 8: Fix outline titles now that glyph source text is provided to SkPDF. r=gfx-reviewers,accessibility-platform-reviewers,lsalzman,eeejay\n\nWhen PDF outline generation was implemented in bug 1950656, source text wasn't passed to SkPDF.\nThat meant that SkPDF couldn't accumulate heading names for the outline from the source text.\nTo work around that, I tweaked Skia slightly to optionally use the alt text as the heading name without exposing the name as the alt attribute in the struct tree.\n\nNow that we pass source text to SkPDF thanks to the earlier patches in this stack, this previous support is redundant and causes duplicate text.\nInstead, in most cases, we now allow SkPDF to accumulate heading names from the source text.\nWhere a heading's name is overridden (e.g. using aria-label), we continue to pass it as alt text.\nHowever, we don't want to expose both alt text and source text, so this tweaks Skia to avoid accumulating heading names from the source text if alt text is explicitly specified for a heading.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329551\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp", "gfx/skia/skia/include/docs/SkPDFDocument.h", "gfx/skia/skia/src/pdf/SkPDFTag.cpp"], "git_node": "77140fd08a321811c0df4e342ac9afec22489bfc", "git_parents": ["31fced352fbf9ab2155b87237b3773b3e4ca030f"], "node": "ec20add222aa55bc8a5bc2e51e496038c35c9244", "parents": ["3d6be35d4d2fa2824bb1d1c6e8efcf9d46c124e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081738 - Create a new verifyBookmarksOnHomeScreenTest regression UI test r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333696\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/HomeSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/BookmarksTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsHomepageTest.kt"], "git_node": "eec7eec3973cc9ba878694f341eecb764de6cce1", "git_parents": ["77140fd08a321811c0df4e342ac9afec22489bfc"], "node": "d3b1252ee997207acf9c1a3d7b51f32e0c764247", "parents": ["ec20add222aa55bc8a5bc2e51e496038c35c9244"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077570 - Name the shutdown phase in nsTerminator's shutdown hang profile line. r=florian\n\nTreeherder searches for bugs by the field after the TEST-UNEXPECTED-FAIL\nprefix. For the line naming the uploaded shutdown hang profile that field was\n\"shutdown hang\" for every hang, so all of them got the same suggestions. Put\nthe shutdown phase the hang happened in there instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328767\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/terminator/nsTerminator.cpp"], "git_node": "a51fa38932b30304bf0fec6e91ac6f82c0780c95", "git_parents": ["eec7eec3973cc9ba878694f341eecb764de6cce1"], "node": "a43e4e918c79bfb1a394d4142269d343f50f7bcc", "parents": ["d3b1252ee997207acf9c1a3d7b51f32e0c764247"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080894 - Prevent instantiation of std::default_type for specific types r=nika\n\nTypes which specialize mozilla::DefaultDeleter should never be passed as\na parameter of std::default_delete, because they have a custom deletion\nprocess.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332926\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/xulstore/XULStore.h"], "git_node": "91590e139d447a2093bd60b7feb831e6cae49147", "git_parents": ["a51fa38932b30304bf0fec6e91ac6f82c0780c95"], "node": "107a15a4ad1e1381b2c8c4e5ebd4442ac3aac223", "parents": ["a43e4e918c79bfb1a394d4142269d343f50f7bcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071503 - Add a totals bar (tab count, RAM, CPU) to about:processes?groupby=tab. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nAdds open-tab count and aggregate RAM and CPU to the tab-view footer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328417\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.html", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "c2fc381c9b4d94f34347cb34723ce0310503469e", "git_parents": ["91590e139d447a2093bd60b7feb831e6cae49147"], "node": "e16cf3c2c69d4991ca86f9632287139257cd2641", "parents": ["107a15a4ad1e1381b2c8c4e5ebd4442ac3aac223"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2002879 - Serialize style attribute from parsed inline declaration block and drop opacity property when copying; r=masayuki\" for causing build bustages at nsHTMLContentSerializer\n\nThis reverts commit ad98bb5162192f820453dd98b5d885e58943ab81.\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.cpp", "dom/serializers/nsHTMLContentSerializer.h", "dom/serializers/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/serializers/tests/mochitest/test_htmlcopyencoder_inlinestyle.html", "dom/serializers/tests/mochitest/test_htmlcopyencoder_inlinestyle_opacity.html", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/tests/clipboard-apis/clipboard-copy-selection-style-opacity.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/clipboard-apis/resources/user-activation.js"], "git_node": "7af714a88dec5f297bb2918ffea9834bfd8acd75", "git_parents": ["c2fc381c9b4d94f34347cb34723ce0310503469e"], "node": "5e17d6363baa54407e176ea9b55f174de36ef29a", "parents": ["e16cf3c2c69d4991ca86f9632287139257cd2641"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - docs: improve some of the glossary r=ahal,firefox-source-docs-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333875\n", "files": ["d