"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080839 - [devtools] Wait for mutation if getDefaultNodeForSelection returned null r=devtools-reviewers,devtools-backward-compat-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332958\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js", "devtools/client/inspector/compatibility/actions/compatibility.js", "devtools/client/inspector/inspector.js", "devtools/server/actors/inspector/walker.js", "devtools/shared/specs/walker.js"], "git_node": "41d75b3bf86deb7930b0d81e87996769bb6c1cf2", "git_parents": ["42d81ac17e740355f9c709620e68367c25faebe5"], "node": "94fa19aa52b1941570eb01a53670382c44b63ef5", "parents": ["93fcf8a3eaea3b2c5d52e990cbab81ed46ee64de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080839 - [devtools] Add test for inspector crash on document without root r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332959\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/test/browser_inspector_document_without_root.js"], "git_node": "d1b255514841b29e60cfc27f8412da67bb6233d7", "git_parents": ["41d75b3bf86deb7930b0d81e87996769bb6c1cf2"], "node": "c0a6b10c28123016ede1c857bbded1a951300283", "parents": ["94fa19aa52b1941570eb01a53670382c44b63ef5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082309 - Add D3D11Checks::DoesRenderTargetViewNeedRecreating() failure handling r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nD3D11 api call failure means that D3D device does not work as expected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334007\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/D3D11Checks.cpp", "gfx/thebes/D3D11Checks.h", "gfx/thebes/DeviceManagerDx.cpp"], "git_node": "dd4e18e8fec180b63c1bd1cfc7488795b0f9ba86", "git_parents": ["d1b255514841b29e60cfc27f8412da67bb6233d7"], "node": "48755ef5e29c51fec2f869b8621949fdca639642", "parents": ["c0a6b10c28123016ede1c857bbded1a951300283"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076775 - Fall back to the document's referrer policy for speculation rules prefetch. r=necko-reviewers,sunil\n\nAn empty policy resolved to the browser default instead of the document's policy.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333391\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/referrer-policy-from-rules.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/referrer-policy.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "a3ab57ab548ac25acceede41494b82c3efa25757", "git_parents": ["dd4e18e8fec180b63c1bd1cfc7488795b0f9ba86"], "node": "85cd1059b01d3b7d015a396a408e097b1446425a", "parents": ["48755ef5e29c51fec2f869b8621949fdca639642"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1772590 - Remove redundant code from StorageAccessAPIHelper::AllowAccessFor helpers. r=emz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330743\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/StorageAccessAPIHelper.cpp"], "git_node": "3276a7deccd953b91b9058eb5597bfdb859b6794", "git_parents": ["a3ab57ab548ac25acceede41494b82c3efa25757"], "node": "d58e96f47a298922be856e9840962fb9a5e3a1ad", "parents": ["85cd1059b01d3b7d015a396a408e097b1446425a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082072 - Bring back the old annotation for window.screen, r=webidl,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334035\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/Window.webidl"], "git_node": "cf96653694e300ac808e392d39111bb927227075", "git_parents": ["3276a7deccd953b91b9058eb5597bfdb859b6794"], "node": "4c358d9ab9e853ffe9ff5c444b978c9366b85fed", "parents": ["d58e96f47a298922be856e9840962fb9a5e3a1ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082221 - Relax threading assertion to allow us to check parent runtime's atoms zone state r=spidermonkey-reviewers,yulia\n\nWe don't do anything with the zone except check it's GC state via\nshouldMarkInZone(). This state is always NoGC for the parent runtime's shared\natoms zone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334026\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Marking.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2082221.js"], "git_node": "36a839120e4655ee34e6f760520bf27a0406047b", "git_parents": ["cf96653694e300ac808e392d39111bb927227075"], "node": "0b0b4781a8afdef8d9609f3845444b48a40b9380", "parents": ["4c358d9ab9e853ffe9ff5c444b978c9366b85fed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1898145 - Credential Management API shouldn't allow method calls on non-fully active docs r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316231\n", "files": ["dom/credentialmanagement/CredentialsContainer.cpp", "dom/credentialmanagement/CredentialsContainer.h", "dom/webauthn/tests/test_webauthn_store_credential.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/credential-management/non-fully-active.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/create-non-fully-active.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/get-non-fully-active.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "4ae0409c73709de938d4985d11bf0062c7c15837", "git_parents": ["36a839120e4655ee34e6f760520bf27a0406047b"], "node": "832b9022b3b5da638080673d171c3639f93214ff", "parents": ["0b0b4781a8afdef8d9609f3845444b48a40b9380"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1733835 - Fix new tab showing \"about:privatebrowsing\" as title in permanent private browsing mode r=timhuang,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nWhen in permanent private browsing mode, new private tabs are normal tabs. On Windows new private tabs are opened using the --private-window\ncommand line when opened from the task bar.\nMake sure that in permanent private browsing mode it opens the correct blank tab in this case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316481\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-tabs/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-tabs/browser_tab_title.js", "browser/base/moz.build", "browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/tests/marionette/test_private_window_cli_startup.py"], "git_node": "5293454f7e68e351eddcc9ce242e7eb9aa7a00e4", "git_parents": ["4ae0409c73709de938d4985d11bf0062c7c15837"], "node": "330198ce82cafc41ab4710320f7be8056c9f4501", "parents": ["832b9022b3b5da638080673d171c3639f93214ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059405 - Remove legacy application reputation probes r=timhuang,janerik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317398\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/reputationservice/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/reputationservice/test/unit/head_download_manager.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": "36fb92e0d2b7e19f3c6c82bac0634e6637614eac", "git_parents": ["5293454f7e68e351eddcc9ce242e7eb9aa7a00e4"], "node": "70804d06bb29dc9091513eca0fd1424b0d3de537", "parents": ["330198ce82cafc41ab4710320f7be8056c9f4501"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059407 - Remove legacy urlclassifier probes r=emz,TravisLong\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317413\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "4af4cbd34d1b060b9b1134c9bff7566a630b131d", "git_parents": ["36fb92e0d2b7e19f3c6c82bac0634e6637614eac"], "node": "02f0b2e6cb3174a784c73b49ab63b9f78d736971", "parents": ["70804d06bb29dc9091513eca0fd1424b0d3de537"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007038 - [devtools] Store destroyed state in NetworkThrottleQueue to avoid race r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy\n\nThe intermittent failures from browser_net_throttling_disable_unblocks_requests.js occur because the feature itself is racy.\nBasically the current implementation only unthrottles requests which are already in `#throttleListeners`. But requests are only pushed in this array when the first batch of data is \"sent\". So there is a time window where requests might not be registered in the array yet, and won't be unthrottled.\n\nInstead here we move the state to the NetworkThrottleQueue and \"unthrottle\" all requests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333542\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkThrottleManager.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/test/xpcshell/test_throttle.js"], "git_node": "fb351be5aa813e646a59b85ad787e0022cc74683", "git_parents": ["4af4cbd34d1b060b9b1134c9bff7566a630b131d"], "node": "05d7029d0cf543bf01fd7d407a2d6208f2da8cee", "parents": ["02f0b2e6cb3174a784c73b49ab63b9f78d736971"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059414 - Remove legacy cookie purging probes r=emz,chumphreys\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317441\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/xpcshell/test_purge_trackers_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "9fd20fd06d9336b64b95d723fd034e3034e41607", "git_parents": ["fb351be5aa813e646a59b85ad787e0022cc74683"], "node": "2ae82770569b6fdf5d73cc323db1c126d91c736d", "parents": ["05d7029d0cf543bf01fd7d407a2d6208f2da8cee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1945659 - Add shim for SendToNews embed on usmagazine.com r=webcompat-reviewers,emz,twisniewski\n\nusmagazine.com embeds SendToNews videos which are classified as\ntrackers. Add shim to be able to unblock them like the TikTok\nembed on the same pages.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324564\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteProtections.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/data/shims.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/sendtonews-embed.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/shims/video-embed.svg"], "git_node": "ac077b28c2efdd26274e4a4da78e60243859e41b", "git_parents": ["9fd20fd06d9336b64b95d723fd034e3034e41607"], "node": "40492c2f978eaa6a6b01153d9ba9675b603491ed", "parents": ["2ae82770569b6fdf5d73cc323db1c126d91c736d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072546 - Report resource timing when the redirect target does not report it r=extension-reviewers,timhuang,valentin,robwu,necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nWhen an extension redirects a request to a moz-extension: channel, the target channel\ndoes not report timing information.\nScripts that use performance.getEntriesByName then cannot find entries for this request\nand might think that the request was blocked.\n\nFix this by reporting timing information on channels that redirect to channels that do\nnot report timing information.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326918\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_webRequest_redirect_resource_timing.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell-common.toml"], "git_node": "ede3516fecee61d47df83cd9ef2b1585760f9d93", "git_parents": ["ac077b28c2efdd26274e4a4da78e60243859e41b"], "node": "ca97b891a8266097885ca4bd52036a71dd4877e4", "parents": ["40492c2f978eaa6a6b01153d9ba9675b603491ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072546 - Shim Amazon ad system bid requests made with fetch r=webcompat-reviewers,timhuang,twisniewski\n\nInstead of blocking make requests to the Amazon Ad system from Javascript use the shim.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331083\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/shims.js"], "git_node": "a5d9c14474a0be1fc77104c696d3ce52561e1d9b", "git_parents": ["ede3516fecee61d47df83cd9ef2b1585760f9d93"], "node": "3810a4d985cda3e320ccca140fd64cdac48edbc8", "parents": ["ca97b891a8266097885ca4bd52036a71dd4877e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068410 - Update the initialized length before the length in ArraySetLength. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334008\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Array.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/arrays/set-length-oom.js", "js/src/vm/ArrayObject.h"], "git_node": "bf82d965a621cc4d7bd91b546347a8d491a71bf2", "git_parents": ["a5d9c14474a0be1fc77104c696d3ce52561e1d9b"], "node": "ce1e0dbac128415078139e51a9714c46023ce110", "parents": ["3810a4d985cda3e320ccca140fd64cdac48edbc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068395 - Make densifySparseElements update the initialized length infallibly. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,yulia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334009\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/Iteration.cpp", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.cpp", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.h", "js/src/vm/Shape.cpp"], "git_node": "b8032b08e3f65822ab9be50d7f8a6f00a0b3eec2", "git_parents": ["bf82d965a621cc4d7bd91b546347a8d491a71bf2"], "node": "d3a2e8ff1e2b5b51cfab1ea625ec7940188e2332", "parents": ["ce1e0dbac128415078139e51a9714c46023ce110"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068395 - Call the add-property hook before densifying sparse elements. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,yulia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334010\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/arrays/densify-sparse-oom.js", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.cpp"], "git_node": "40efda3cb0542d8c8c9741b20d3351f3e658ee23", "git_parents": ["b8032b08e3f65822ab9be50d7f8a6f00a0b3eec2"], "node": "db04ca696b34b163cc026355039cadbf3e4ccbb9", "parents": ["d3a2e8ff1e2b5b51cfab1ea625ec7940188e2332"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1765317 - Part 1 - Move the anti-tracking heuristics into their own folder r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330100\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/AntiTrackingRedirectHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/AntiTrackingRedirectHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/DynamicFpiNavigationHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/DynamicFpiNavigationHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/DynamicFpiRedirectHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/DynamicFpiRedirectHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingRedirectHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingRedirectHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/DynamicFpiNavigationHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/DynamicFpiNavigationHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/DynamicFpiRedirectHeuristic.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/DynamicFpiRedirectHeuristic.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/moz.build", "toolkit/components/antitracking/moz.build"], "git_node": "b4a0aea7494a9c8e8a85704d771b5569c0efd38e", "git_parents": ["40efda3cb0542d8c8c9741b20d3351f3e658ee23"], "node": "b591696aacc562c40a44bef9de17e77c45e6d5b1", "parents": ["db04ca696b34b163cc026355039cadbf3e4ccbb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1765317 - Part 2 - Move the opener heuristic from Document into the anti-tracking component r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330101\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingOpenerHeuristics.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingOpenerHeuristics.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/moz.build"], "git_node": "5ba6e41d70183fc0edc6826042df7e96fac0d459", "git_parents": ["b4a0aea7494a9c8e8a85704d771b5569c0efd38e"], "node": "b68a1ec8c9b071e450d803974b0f700c9c527a99", "parents": ["b591696aacc562c40a44bef9de17e77c45e6d5b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Raiber \u003cmraiber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1765317 - Part 3 - Move the window.open heuristic from nsGlobalWindowOuter into the anti-tracking component r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330102\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingOpenerHeuristics.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/heuristics/AntiTrackingOpenerHeuristics.h"], "git_node": "af6222b8200a0c67c30fcc1a96aba08c0af29b33", "git_parents": ["5ba6e41d70183fc0edc6826042df7e96fac0d459"], "node": "21fb5ec6df879b214284c9fe3ccd1a4335f1ef11", "parents": ["b68a1ec8c9b071e450d803974b0f700c9c527a99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064720 - Remove search engine overrides test from test_userInstalledConfigEngine.js as it is no longer supported. r=search-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333275\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_userInstalledConfigEngine.js"], "git_node": "4cd928a53ab4e326c8524e57c0ccf0fef3bad7f9", "git_parents": ["af6222b8200a0c67c30fcc1a96aba08c0af29b33"], "node": "560255b455e791105717b398d29136bc598b742d", "parents": ["21fb5ec6df879b214284c9fe3ccd1a4335f1ef11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064720 - Support loading search-config-v3 within the SearchService when the flag is enabled. r=search-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nThis handles hooking up loading of the configuration using the new application services APIs, as well as adjusting the partner code and telemetry suffix handling for V3.\n\nThis also fixes most of the toolkit/components/search tests (when application-services is updated as well), however some still fail and will be handled in follow-up commits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333276\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/ConfigSearchEngine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/SearchEngine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/SearchTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/head_search.js", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_engine_selector_subvariants.js", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_engine_selector_variants.js", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_getSubmission_partnerCode.js"], "git_node": "ab4c0f886b40c3dac4d8ca37c69704a5afa9d987", "git_parents": ["4cd928a53ab4e326c8524e57c0ccf0fef3bad7f9"], "node": "05065d8f3c9e535a5f06de27fa580300600fa80c", "parents": ["560255b455e791105717b398d29136bc598b742d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064720 - Apply the platform to the application name when loading search-config-v3. r=search-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333277\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_engine_selector_environment.js"], "git_node": "5f67fa0ce727a5e29166f53970943d6352b64833", "git_parents": ["ab4c0f886b40c3dac4d8ca37c69704a5afa9d987"], "node": "1e42b75d6b6915dd5aa67ebc0037253d377779cd", "parents": ["05065d8f3c9e535a5f06de27fa580300600fa80c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fabio Kaminski \u003cfabiokaminski@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841326 Colorspace property added and correctly managed in CanvasRenderingContext2d and ImageData r=gfx-reviewers,webidl,emilio,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332911\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "dom/canvas/ImageData.cpp", "dom/canvas/ImageData.h", "dom/webidl/CanvasRenderingContext2D.webidl", "dom/webidl/ImageData.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-ImageData.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-canvas.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-pattern-canvas.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.p3.rgba.unorm8.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.srgb.rgba.unorm8.html.ini"], "git_node": "76d008734a82091bcf84ad70e4d4e796322c38c4", "git_parents": ["5f67fa0ce727a5e29166f53970943d6352b64833"], "node": "c5919052f2257375ddb2308710885abb54a09257", "parents": ["1e42b75d6b6915dd5aa67ebc0037253d377779cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072290 - Start the HTTP/3 backup timer for transactions added before the handshake completes, r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332341\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/MockNetworkLayer.cpp", "netwerk/base/MockNetworkLayerController.cpp", "netwerk/base/MockNetworkLayerController.h", "netwerk/base/nsIMockNetworkLayerController.idl", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "netwerk/test/unit/test_http3_ipv6_send_would_block.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "1c025575e14d5c9ed790261ca9deb829d5dedbd9", "git_parents": ["76d008734a82091bcf84ad70e4d4e796322c38c4"], "node": "1458ce347053f5ad31917fcd69079a60cb77268b", "parents": ["c5919052f2257375ddb2308710885abb54a09257"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081760 - Tweak transition cascade order. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nAdd a pref + test to make sure that transitions can't override UA\nimportant cascade level.\n\nSee bug 2077756 for context.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333700\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "servo/components/style/applicable_declarations.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_tree/level.rs", "servo/components/style/rule_tree/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/style_resolver.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/ua-important.tentative.html"], "git_node": "ac51083513159497668f423ed72eaabba1ef6961", "git_parents": ["1c025575e14d5c9ed790261ca9deb829d5dedbd9"], "node": "7b734024246d68e63fcc6f0d82757f72f0cfb6da", "parents": ["1458ce347053f5ad31917fcd69079a60cb77268b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081765 - Add InspectorUtils method to know if a given rule supports declarations. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,webidl.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333662\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/CSSRule.webidl", "layout/inspector/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "layout/inspector/tests/chrome/test_CSSRule_supportsDeclarations.html", "layout/style/Rule.cpp", "layout/style/Rule.h", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/mod.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "c10ba6044e709b6338da6e3920b1848d79f3fcb4", "git_parents": ["ac51083513159497668f423ed72eaabba1ef6961"], "node": "daab1b1e4e33ceaf67c79c405403c0f3f2dae10f", "parents": ["7b734024246d68e63fcc6f0d82757f72f0cfb6da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081924 - Allow Suggest features to show results in the zero prefix view through UrlbarProviderQuickSuggest. r=adw,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333927\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderQuickSuggest.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/AmpSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/SuggestBackendMerino.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/SuggestBackendMl.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/WikipediaSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_amp.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_dynamicSuggestions.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_merino.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_wikipedia.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_yelp_ml.js"], "git_node": "4a4b3f949d72ab7f08e7109b8491eb9b4698fd21", "git_parents": ["c10ba6044e709b6338da6e3920b1848d79f3fcb4"], "node": "648e0e66753440ff54e5215166eaaae13283a48a", "parents": ["daab1b1e4e33ceaf67c79c405403c0f3f2dae10f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1610213 - Annotate crash reports with what happens while InitializeMacApp() spins its run loop. r=emilio,crashreporting-reviewers\n\nSince bug 2055233 the startup run loop in InitializeMacApp() runs until the\nfirst idle instead of stopping in applicationDidFinishLaunching. Some reports\nshow the main thread still waiting in that loop when the user quits, but\nneither forcing a nested loop into it nor plain startups reproduce that.\n\nRecord the delegate callbacks, the observer firing and the stop together with\nthe run loop wake-ups in a MacStartupRunLoop annotation while the loop runs,\nand remove it once the loop returns. Early beta or earlier only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330481\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/CrashAnnotations.yaml", "toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.mm"], "git_node": "a70d3d43100fb5df2dd5f35d2d47a004d6d66c99", "git_parents": ["4a4b3f949d72ab7f08e7109b8491eb9b4698fd21"], "node": "421411d622165a28e9d6619d646031b69445983f", "parents": ["648e0e66753440ff54e5215166eaaae13283a48a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1325609 - Don't make TestBlockingProcess depend on inherited stdin. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nTestBlockingProcess blocked by reading a byte from stdin, so it only actually\nblocks when the inherited descriptor blocks. The xpcshell harness launches\nxpcshell without setting stdin, so fd 0 is inherited from whatever ran the\nharness; in automation it can be at end-of-file, in which case the helper\nreturns 0 within milliseconds of exec.\n\ntest_nsIProcess.js then races: if the monitor thread reaps the child before\nkill() runs, kill() fails and the test sees an uncaught NS_ERROR_FAILURE from\nnsIProcess.kill, and if kill() signals the zombie first it succeeds but the\nprocess had already exited with 0, so the observer is notified with\nprocess-finished instead of process-failed. Both are observed in CI.\n\nBlock on a bounded sleep instead, so the helper can only be terminated by the\nsignal. The bound stops a stray helper outliving the harness if a kill is ever\nlost, and returning 0 keeps such a case visible as a test failure.\n\nHave test_notify_killed check that the helper is still running some time after\nit was started, so that a helper that does not block fails deterministically\nrather than only when it loses the race.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314903\n", "files": ["xpcom/tests/TestBlockingProcess.cpp", "xpcom/tests/unit/test_nsIProcess.js"], "git_node": "54ae3a73cdd5bbdd4a532bf77476de8b31e629c3", "git_parents": ["a70d3d43100fb5df2dd5f35d2d47a004d6d66c99"], "node": "2f151492a84930f537d6ca8f8b1a60ba84d5e4b1", "parents": ["421411d622165a28e9d6619d646031b69445983f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1325609 - Re-enable test_nsIProcess.js on Android. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe Android skip dates from when the helper programs did not link there (bugs\n676998 and 1631671). They link and run today, and the test passes.\n\nThe linux 22.04 wayland condition never applied, because xpcshell sets\nrun-on-projects to nothing for wayland test platforms.\n\nWindows stays skipped, because Kill() reports a process it terminated as having\nexited cleanly, so the test fails on every run there. That is bug 749717, which\nre-enables it. The Windows condition cited this bug only because the\nini-to-toml migration split a single condition that cited four bugs together and\nshifted the numbers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314904\n", "files": ["xpcom/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "fdede2c3c42cb61d6efeb5b0bd35111197cf511e", "git_parents": ["54ae3a73cdd5bbdd4a532bf77476de8b31e629c3"], "node": "86196017f322eb61f9e0ac8c4d5900295c1a244e", "parents": ["2f151492a84930f537d6ca8f8b1a60ba84d5e4b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2072964 - [wdspec] Add tests for WebDriver BiDi sessions restricted to a single container r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\" for causing wd failures @container_isolation.py.\n\nThis reverts commit a00b1f5c545d50c45ea3b58c48a977fc8631f58f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2072964 - [bidi] Restrict browsing context access to a single container r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\"\n\nThis reverts commit 48441653d19ce12ac86cc6d90345e0edc2d2b942.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2072964 - [bidi] Use a shared helper to resolve user context ids in BiDi modules r=webdriver-reviewers,Sasha\"\n\nThis reverts commit cd720b544931a5635e780a4ee4250be7a837a840.\n", "files": ["remote/shared/TabManager.sys.mjs", "remote/shared/test/browser/browser_TabManager.js", "remote/shared/webdriver/Session.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/RootBiDiModule.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/_configuration.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/browser.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/browsingContext.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/network.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/permissions.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/script.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/session.sys.mjs", "remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/storage.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browser/set_download_behavior/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/activate/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/activate/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/create/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/get_tree/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/navigate/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/reload/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/set_viewport/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browsing_context/traverse_history/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/conftest.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/emulation/set_locale_override/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/external/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/external/permissions/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/external/permissions/set_permission/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/external/permissions/set_permission/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/input/perform_actions/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/network/add_data_collector/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/network/add_intercept/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/network/set_extra_headers/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/network/set_extra_headers/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/script/add_preload_script/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/script/add_preload_script/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/script/evaluate/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/session/subscribe/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/session/subscribe/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/storage/get_cookies/container_isolation.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/support/container_isolation.py"], "git_node": "d809a3834f25c38505bfffafcd88d4538f3f6db0", "git_parents": ["fdede2c3c42cb61d6efeb5b0bd35111197cf511e"], "node": "1a27ac2fe4192fb12b86665be9439dd3b779f666", "parents": ["86196017f322eb61f9e0ac8c4d5900295c1a244e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1733835 - Fix new tab showing \"about:privatebrowsing\" as title in permanent private browsing mode r=timhuang,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\" for causing marionette failures @test_private_window_cli_startup.py.\n\nThis reverts commit 5293454f7e68e351eddcc9ce242e7eb9aa7a00e4.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-tabs/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-tabs/browser_tab_title.js", "browser/base/moz.build", "browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/tests/marionette/test_private_window_cli_startup.py"], "git_node": "cfc20bf9116825b46a51d0b2f296f6e21bccf85e", "git_parents": ["d809a3834f25c38505bfffafcd88d4538f3f6db0"], "node": "f79f95b2eafba5b9e8ed779f6aae2a5d374cad1a", "parents": ["1a27ac2fe4192fb12b86665be9439dd3b779f666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Perf AI Bot \u003cperf-ai-bot@bmo.tld\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071848 - Construct non-empty atomized HTML attribute values directly through the parser atom table instead of routing them through the general newStringFromBuffer portability helper. r=hsivonen,dom-core-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325847\n", "files": ["parser/html/javasrc/Tokenizer.java", "parser/html/nsHtml5Tokenizer.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TokenizerHSupplement.h"], "git_node": "d9b9e9adbf7effde9c42575cb72609356add5636", "git_parents": ["cfc20bf9116825b46a51d0b2f296f6e21bccf85e"], "node": "14eae155539c3f5b166876dccb4b2c9b3741f5cb", "parents": ["f79f95b2eafba5b9e8ed779f6aae2a5d374cad1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081218 - Go back to logging to stderr when logging.config.LOG_FILE is cleared, r=xpcom-reviewers,nika.\n\nClearing the pref calls SetLogFile(nullptr), which expanded the empty file name to \".moz_log\" and opened it relative to the current directory. On Windows, browser/components/shell/test/unit/test_taskbarPinningPolicy.js clears the pref in its cleanup function, which created a .moz_log file in its test directory. about:logging clears the same pref when logging is stopped, leaving a stray .moz_log file in the directory Firefox was started from.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333298\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/Logging.cpp", "xpcom/base/Logging.h", "xpcom/tests/unit/test_logFilePrefReset.js", "xpcom/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "dc0b34e58b250e78b8d26a1ffd690bee7c2c50e1", "git_parents": ["d9b9e9adbf7effde9c42575cb72609356add5636"], "node": "10807b79bd18d42d24d9d7cf51b6cd7b16104ea2", "parents": ["14eae155539c3f5b166876dccb4b2c9b3741f5cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 1: Refactor nursery active chunk range r=jonco\n\nWe can't just start allocating in any chunk; we can either start from\nthe beginning, after evicting a space or when switching spaces, or we\ncan continue with the next chunk.\n\n- Refactor to better name the range of chunks used for allocation since\n  the last collection.  Allow a space to have *no* active chunks; this is\n  the case in the promote-only nursery configuration.\n\n- Add a Space::chunk accessor that ensures the chunk is in the active\n  range.\n\n- Don't bother ensuring that fromspace has an current chunk.\n\n- Don't eagerly flip the gckind of a space's allocated but inactive\n  pages; lazily flip them just before allocation.\n\n- Simplify poisoning under generational GC zeal.\n\n- Simplify nursery growth/shrinkage under generational GC zeal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325424\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "8086ce6118532c1aad3528297676bab4db1065be", "git_parents": ["dc0b34e58b250e78b8d26a1ffd690bee7c2c50e1"], "node": "c5be8e0e94dd25b38b6e37c90e8f0d08a27f3f01", "parents": ["10807b79bd18d42d24d9d7cf51b6cd7b16104ea2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 2: Implement contiguous nursery mode r=jonco\n\nShould speed up chunk acquisition / release and isInside checks.\nEnabled if -DJS_CONTIGUOUS_NURSERY.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325425\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery-inl.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.cpp"], "git_node": "1772659cd869d331d7fa59989d61be4969c31fa6", "git_parents": ["8086ce6118532c1aad3528297676bab4db1065be"], "node": "c354480864692a2ad8e545fc45af8092596839db", "parents": ["c5be8e0e94dd25b38b6e37c90e8f0d08a27f3f01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740752 - Part 3: Use contiguous nursery on 64-bit platforms r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325427\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": "03d6b98b1681b6487b97f90f00198e14ad59f606", "git_parents": ["1772659cd869d331d7fa59989d61be4969c31fa6"], "node": "6b3ca98c9a46295f71eb9