StateKtTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/accounts/MozillaAccountMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/header/MozillaAccountMenuItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuNavigationMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/accounts/MozillaAccountMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "898450b886620ea9842f7295e7622046394759db", "git_parents": ["c218f96f98812239013bf9b2d33b9430c69014d1"], "node": "86559551efaeced4310699bfabc8237983a86645", "parents": ["24d94946939a3e45b3c5ca3d1b3c4b9c0ac886c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brad Frost \u003cbfrost@squarespace.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005072 - Implement proposed loading attribute for video and audio elements. r=dom-core-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,webidl,layout-reviewers,smaug,emilio,pehrsons,alwu,jjaschke\n\nAdd support for the `loading` attribute on \u003cvideo\u003e and \u003caudio\u003e\nelements, mirroring the existing behavior for \u003cimg\u003e and \u003ciframe\u003e. The\nattribute accepts `eager` (default) and `lazy`. When `loading=\"lazy\"`\nis set, loading of the media resource and poster image, as well as\nautoplay, is deferred via an intersection observer until the element is\nnear the viewport. Gated behind the media.lazy_loading.enabled pref.\n\nSpec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#attr-media-loading\nSpec PR: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11980\n\nCo-authored-by: Scott Jehl \u003csjehl@squarespace.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D278547\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMIntersectionObserver.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.h", "dom/webidl/HTMLMediaElement.webidl", "layout/generic/nsVideoFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsVideoFrame.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-autoplay-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-disconnected.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-not-rendered.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-source-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-to-eager.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-lazy-window-onload.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-load-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-load-preload-auto-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element/audio-loading-load-preload-metadata-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-autoplay-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-autoplay-when-visible.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-below-viewport-load-event.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-disconnected.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-load-when-visible.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-not-rendered.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-poster-when-visible.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-resume-on-loading-attribute-change.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-source-inserted-load-event.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-source-poster-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-to-eager.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-lazy-window-onload.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-load-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-load-preload-auto-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-load-preload-metadata-deferred.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video-loading-poster-deferred.html.ini"], "git_node": "23845b380086ad3f1bed87301b46033a733e5118", "git_parents": ["898450b886620ea9842f7295e7622046394759db"], "node": "d1ef6f26f579ea71b34a22cb8997b819d0a6d0e7", "parents": ["86559551efaeced4310699bfabc8237983a86645"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mcarare \u003c48995920+mcarare@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082301 - Fix crash fragment layout positioning related to the toolbar. r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nAlso improve theming for crash fragment.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334236\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_browser.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_crash_reporter.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-night/colors.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml"], "git_node": "5a357839f82b968d1bd35d3efecc76f4adfe8c3a", "git_parents": ["23845b380086ad3f1bed87301b46033a733e5118"], "node": "2b63e22088db6aa2a2dc7cf4980f35f99843bcbc", "parents": ["d1ef6f26f579ea71b34a22cb8997b819d0a6d0e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078138 - Open the tab group when its Smart Window chip is clicked. r=yjamora\n\nA tab group chip has no URL, and every chip click only sent AIChatContent:OpenLink, so clicking one did nothing. Tab group chips in the context chips, the grouped chips panel and inline mentions now send AIChatContent:OpenTabGroup. The parent then calls select() on the group in that window, which expands it and selects its first tab.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332313\n", "files": ["browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AIChatContentChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/AIChatContentParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-message/ai-chat-message.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-grouped-chip-container/ai-grouped-chip-container.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_message.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_grouped_chips.js"], "git_node": "267351349d4a816a697c6e2a501c8866ceef7267", "git_parents": ["5a357839f82b968d1bd35d3efecc76f4adfe8c3a"], "node": "6cbf9b7e624ee64cbad0feb58837bf31a4e46118", "parents": ["2b63e22088db6aa2a2dc7cf4980f35f99843bcbc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Remove the boilerplate `toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/Makefile.in` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe only comment in `toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/Makefile.in` pointed at\n`updater-xpcshell/Makefile.in`, which no longer exists.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328996\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/Makefile.in"], "git_node": "b5beca248fb3ef298a9520ba932e57fa00e34884", "git_parents": ["267351349d4a816a697c6e2a501c8866ceef7267"], "node": "bc16298ad7d78b19400f27fa419c7d29da87c48b", "parents": ["6cbf9b7e624ee64cbad0feb58837bf31a4e46118"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the host C++ link decision from `rules.mk` to the backend r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe emitter already decides that a host linkable needs the C++ driver, but that\nnever reached the backend, so `rules.mk` worked it out again from\n`HOST_CPPSRCS`. Host simple programs used a second test that also read\n`USE_HOST_CXX`, which nothing in the tree assigns, so that variable goes too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329007\n", "files": ["config/rules.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/conly-cpplib/d.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/conly-cpplib/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/conly/b.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/conly/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/cpp/a.cpp", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/cpp/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/cpplib/c.cpp", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/cpplib/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/simple/host_asimple.cpp", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/host-cpp-link/simple/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "77781751b18a86d9f75ca45793c88a57dac783e3", "git_parents": ["b5beca248fb3ef298a9520ba932e57fa00e34884"], "node": "daa8f877793891b81f0222dfa83db0ac7a1d06f1", "parents": ["bc16298ad7d78b19400f27fa419c7d29da87c48b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Add backend target resolution and use it for `mach gtest` r=mjf\n\nCommands asked the build for make tier names such as `recurse_gtest`, and a\ntier is a make concept that other backends do not have. `BuildDriver` now\npasses every requested target through `BuildBackend.resolve_targets()`, so a\ncommand asks for a backend neutral name and each backend maps that name to its\nown targets. The make backend maps `gtest` to `recurse_gtest` and `syms` to\n`recurse_syms`, which `loop-ff.py` and `autospider.py` now ask for. A backend\nbuilds any name it does not map as given, so an explicit\n`mach build recurse_gtest` still works.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329016\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/third_party_build/loop-ff.py", "js/src/devtools/automation/autospider.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/base.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "7f30f992f9d8143b4070d52727dacb0ff72d3887", "git_parents": ["77781751b18a86d9f75ca45793c88a57dac783e3"], "node": "858ef5524f49b6addf255109a1cebeff3eb8039c", "parents": ["daa8f877793891b81f0222dfa83db0ac7a1d06f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the static analysis export build from `_run_make` to `mach build` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe export now runs through the configured backend instead of always through\nmake. It asks for `analysis-prereqs`, which the make backend resolves to\n`pre-export`, `export` and `pre-compile`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329017\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/code_analysis/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/code_analysis/test_mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "f8ef0c56c8cd1baf21a89dd123e99a70c4de2429", "git_parents": ["7f30f992f9d8143b4070d52727dacb0ff72d3887"], "node": "17fe243d4953dbaaf5d5001b0ad53d9fde749ee1", "parents": ["858ef5524f49b6addf255109a1cebeff3eb8039c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the `mach cargo` export prerequisites from make tier names to `rust-prereqs` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe make backend maps `rust-prereqs` to `pre-export` and `export`, and\n`uniffi-target` to `recurse_uniffi-target`. `./mach uniffi generate` asks for\nboth.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329019\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "d0ea86476f04f971f250b9df378cb8fb2ad82142", "git_parents": ["f8ef0c56c8cd1baf21a89dd123e99a70c4de2429"], "node": "dd06761e4a68d862159f9b7a61002b2b1294298f", "parents": ["17fe243d4953dbaaf5d5001b0ad53d9fde749ee1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the `mach rusttests` targets from make tier names to `rust-prereqs` and `rusttests` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329020\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "testing/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "dd35dc22b43f50b03c6891ad3ef448118f2b603b", "git_parents": ["d0ea86476f04f971f250b9df378cb8fb2ad82142"], "node": "5be91652a85b847463ecdc7229e16461c74af56d", "parents": ["dd06761e4a68d862159f9b7a61002b2b1294298f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the Rust test library staging from `rust.mk` to `run_cargo` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe backend stops writing `RUST_LIBRARY_CARGO_PROFILE_SUFFIX` into `backend.mk`,\nbecause the staging was the last thing that read it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329472\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/rust.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/run_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/rust_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/action/test_run_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_rust_commands.py"], "git_node": "bb816757ae1029c40ed19bf84706d1aadcb6efed", "git_parents": ["dd35dc22b43f50b03c6891ad3ef448118f2b603b"], "node": "27df3ade02e8001a9192f88cc6b0f07b913f70e3", "parents": ["5be91652a85b847463ecdc7229e16461c74af56d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the Rust networking check from `rust.mk` to `run_cargo` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe library spec now names the library file, and the backend stops writing\n`RUST_LIBRARY_LTO`, which only the check read. `check_binary` reads the build\nconfiguration when it is imported, so it is imported where it is used.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329473\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/rust.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/run_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/rust_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/action/test_run_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_rust_commands.py"], "git_node": "337261eefe2ab68fad86c8b8c30f8fab0d272598", "git_parents": ["bb816757ae1029c40ed19bf84706d1aadcb6efed"], "node": "824af20736d75f925ba807dc510c1e4097bf739a", "parents": ["27df3ade02e8001a9192f88cc6b0f07b913f70e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the big endian ICU data edges from `recurse.mk` to `GeneratedFile` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\n`data.py` now treats a generated `.dat` as a compile input, because\n`icu_data.S` reads it with `.incbin`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329009\n", "files": ["config/external/icu/data/moz.build", "config/recurse.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/data/convert.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/data/data.S", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/data/little.dat", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/data/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/tool/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files-host-tool/tool/tool.c", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "d21ea628b741038a53c30de09a8ca7f941b1365b", "git_parents": ["337261eefe2ab68fad86c8b8c30f8fab0d272598"], "node": "05f62b6a89ef5f53ad5cbc7482e6781cb8eec9de", "parents": ["824af20736d75f925ba807dc510c1e4097bf739a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Add per source `object_deps` to `SOURCES` and use it for the libopus arm assembly r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nAssembly is built without a dependency file, so an object only reassembles when\na file it pulls in with `.include` changes if that file is declared. The backend\nwrites the source as the object's first prerequisite, because the compile rules\nin `rules.mk` build `$\u003c`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329023\n", "files": ["media/libopus/Makefile.in", "media/libopus/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/context.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/per-source-object-deps/generate.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/per-source-object-deps/included.inc", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/per-source-object-deps/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/per-source-object-deps/plain.s", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/per-source-object-deps/static.s", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps-missing/generate.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps-missing/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps-missing/plain.s", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps/generate.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps/included.inc", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/data/per-source-object-deps/plain.s", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/test_emitter.py"], "git_node": "32e96b9033e7c19ffc5c037abbab399982d9c25c", "git_parents": ["d21ea628b741038a53c30de09a8ca7f941b1365b"], "node": "e460f6d7769a9f04d5001e3207c9122187596c90", "parents": ["05f62b6a89ef5f53ad5cbc7482e6781cb8eec9de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038789 - Move the libvpx arm assembly dependency from `media/libvpx/Makefile.in` to `SOURCES` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe make rule also named `idct8x8_add_neon` and `idct16x16_add_neon`, which are\nno longer in `LINUX_ARM_SOURCES`, so only `idct4x4_add_neon` declares the\ndependency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329024\n", "files": ["media/libvpx/Makefile.in", "media/libvpx/moz.build"], "git_node": "84193240666e18d78284eb3f7cd081d6cca54819", "git_parents": ["32e96b9033e7c19ffc5c037abbab399982d9c25c"], "node": "3c2fe01b963c08f1541cf8c0f7ff37a2c0549f31", "parents": ["e460f6d7769a9f04d5001e3207c9122187596c90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082541 - Don't create remote decoders with a CDM whose process crashed. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nIf the process hosting a remote CDM crashes, the CDM is terminated, but\nMediaFormatReader may still try to create new decoders with it once the\nprocess is recreated. Sending the dead CDM actor would trigger a release\nassertion, so fail to create the decoder instead. The page must create a new\nCDM to recover.\n\nThis recovery is done by the page through the signalling provided via\nMediaKeys::Terminated. This is already in place on Android through the\nRemoteCDMChild::ActorDestroy call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334182\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteAudioDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "b6d2ef4ba1ec7aad4c299beb063c4441d7795e29", "git_parents": ["84193240666e18d78284eb3f7cd081d6cca54819"], "node": "16fe636eda816483cfd13ec71d947373b7e48d07", "parents": ["3c2fe01b963c08f1541cf8c0f7ff37a2c0549f31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1981478 - Flip prefs to switch to NDK decoding/encoding on Android on nightly. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D260149\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "c0e99674dd93f531223294a546dd0ba14aac975e", "git_parents": ["b6d2ef4ba1ec7aad4c299beb063c4441d7795e29"], "node": "4d0a2bb684c4305f94f147af6219abd31f821975", "parents": ["16fe636eda816483cfd13ec71d947373b7e48d07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Rubino \u003cdrubino@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1996158 - Clear the read-only attribute when removing the empty backup folder. r=hsohaney\n\nOneDrive can mark the folders it syncs as read-only, so removing the empty backup folder failed with NS_ERROR_FILE_ACCESS_DENIED. The retryReadonly option that handles this was misspelled, so IOUtils never retried.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334002\n", "files": ["browser/components/backup/BackupService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/backup/tests/xpcshell/test_BackupService.js"], "git_node": "86eedd053a6e8f193cb81a44f592f7350af2dfb0", "git_parents": ["c0e99674dd93f531223294a546dd0ba14aac975e"], "node": "445719a1d0aa27e008238f509c33902d968738f4", "parents": ["4d0a2bb684c4305f94f147af6219abd31f821975"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082436 - Run the partials and partials-signing kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe partials, partials-signing kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are partial MAR generation and signing tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334130\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/partials-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/partials/kind.yml"], "git_node": "98b67e62c75ccc2f28664a5c35d6a95bc33ce251", "git_parents": ["86eedd053a6e8f193cb81a44f592f7350af2dfb0"], "node": "f0416f3dbfb6344ee42126683243833ff12b32ab", "parents": ["445719a1d0aa27e008238f509c33902d968738f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082347 - Run the balrog and mar-signing kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe balrog, release-balrog-submit-toplevel, mar-signing, mar-signing-l10n\nand mar-signing-autograph-stage kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\ntheir tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it\nonly changes scheduling: these scriptworker tasks have no checkout. The\n`task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only content.\n\nVerified on hg try on Oct 14 with the guard-free kind files:\n`mach try scriptworker balrog-submit --release-type beta` ran balrog and\nrelease-balrog-submit-toplevel (push 57ef248f132e, all green), and\n`mach try scriptworker linux-signing` ran mar-signing (push 1d990d6384bd,\ngreen). mar-signing-l10n and mar-signing-autograph-stage use the same\nsigning scriptworker path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334039\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/balrog/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mar-signing-autograph-stage/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mar-signing-l10n/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mar-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-balrog-submit-toplevel/kind.yml"], "git_node": "fa8bea49589c5fbc7de1d9e3c88167ad40df196f", "git_parents": ["98b67e62c75ccc2f28664a5c35d6a95bc33ce251"], "node": "223a4e17fdb39a2d91ff9d62fee6498a760432db", "parents": ["f0416f3dbfb6344ee42126683243833ff12b32ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082435 - Run the post-* dummy kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe post-balrog-dummy, post-beetmover-checksums-dummy, post-beetmover-components-dummy, post-beetmover-dummy, post-langpack-dummy, post-signing-dummy, post-update-verify-dummy, upload-generated-sources-dummy kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are dummy tasks on the built-in succeed worker that only group dependencies, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334131\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/post-balrog-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-beetmover-checksums-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-beetmover-components-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-beetmover-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-langpack-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-signing-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/post-update-verify-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/upload-generated-sources-dummy/kind.yml"], "git_node": "d49e2c06d199c3c8c86e0914890f050820027385", "git_parents": ["fa8bea49589c5fbc7de1d9e3c88167ad40df196f"], "node": "438d1b28a0e66b968cf3c40da12b70b674d7aab8", "parents": ["223a4e17fdb39a2d91ff9d62fee6498a760432db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082437 - Run the beetmover kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe beetmover-android-app, beetmover-apt, beetmover-checksums, beetmover-components, beetmover-geckoview, beetmover-repackage, beetmover-source kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are beetmover scriptworker tasks that upload build artifacts, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334129\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-android-app/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-apt/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-checksums/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-components/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-geckoview/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-repackage/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-source/kind.yml"], "git_node": "9098a3ec613cc29d1fc761ee8a36b482c88c249b", "git_parents": ["d49e2c06d199c3c8c86e0914890f050820027385"], "node": "3224939c98a0a6da1b934d1098bcf2d2afa2d4d2", "parents": ["438d1b28a0e66b968cf3c40da12b70b674d7aab8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082433 - Run the bouncer kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-bouncer-aliases, release-bouncer-sub, release-partner-repack-bouncer-sub, bouncer-locations kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are bouncer scriptworker tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334133\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/bouncer-locations/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-bouncer-aliases/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-bouncer-sub/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-bouncer-sub/kind.yml"], "git_node": "e9b9909912060fc5659a3c63f28bb412ef25f895", "git_parents": ["9098a3ec613cc29d1fc761ee8a36b482c88c249b"], "node": "45b69b96f79e5d04533439a649df2c7578f9296a", "parents": ["3224939c98a0a6da1b934d1098bcf2d2afa2d4d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Leritte \u003cjleritte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076799 - Record fire button exposure at the first startup after enrollment, in every branch. r=nimbus-reviewers,beth\n\nExposure on press could never fire in the control branch, which has no\nbutton. The enrollment is remembered in a pref because the button is only\ncreated or left out at startup, so the session that enrolls must not count.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332203\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableWidgets.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_fireButton.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "81c35398c176e1210407c0a1f70a5e819b248768", "git_parents": ["e9b9909912060fc5659a3c63f28bb412ef25f895"], "node": "b9e5554602404fd82bd4f136aea83f8103fa7a94", "parents": ["45b69b96f79e5d04533439a649df2c7578f9296a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080331 - Retry network errors when fetching resource usage profiles for test timings, r=ahal.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332580\n", "files": ["testing/timings/profile-worker.js"], "git_node": "5a6791cd8402c9a720de58f71ea3f27aa874c34b", "git_parents": ["81c35398c176e1210407c0a1f70a5e819b248768"], "node": "afe11795d38310e55e4cf9beb3ac24b091b1377e", "parents": ["b9e5554602404fd82bd4f136aea83f8103fa7a94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080632 - Build the libdmg-hfsplus dmg and hfsplus tools for macOS. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThey will be used to extract DMGs without mounting them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332754\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-dmg-hfsplus-macosx.sh", "tools/lint/toolchain-parity/exclusions.yml"], "git_node": "a8789871ff7043cdc92aaee408c9c5a1a14f4a66", "git_parents": ["5a6791cd8402c9a720de58f71ea3f27aa874c34b"], "node": "4fbba7bc21051e11f31dbc8e6abbcc0f97e9ded9", "parents": ["afe11795d38310e55e4cf9beb3ac24b091b1377e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080632 - Make mozinstall extract DMGs with libdmg-hfsplus when available instead of mounting them. r=mozbase-reviewers,ahal\n\nMounting needs access to /Volumes, which sandboxes can deny. Mounting stays as\nthe fallback, as mozinstall is also used where the tools aren't available, e.g.\nby mozregression.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332755\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozinstall/mozinstall/mozinstall.py", "testing/mozbase/mozinstall/tests/test_install.py"], "git_node": "b3a883c7c51ec2bd84e58cf1034108b6d007511d", "git_parents": ["a8789871ff7043cdc92aaee408c9c5a1a14f4a66"], "node": "665072f2ba11593e9a2a4f33a6acc4f72798adeb", "parents": ["4fbba7bc21051e11f31dbc8e6abbcc0f97e9ded9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080632 - Fetch the dmg tools in macOS test tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332756\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/other.py"], "git_node": "f2cfd1be2b5549109a5ec77326b58412d50dd00f", "git_parents": ["b3a883c7c51ec2bd84e58cf1034108b6d007511d"], "node": "63d19475d6ebf10fe3bf835905e45e835eab08ce", "parents": ["665072f2ba11593e9a2a4f33a6acc4f72798adeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080632 - Bootstrap the dmg tools for macOS artifact builds. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nMounting the DMG fails in sandboxes that deny access to /Volumes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332757\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/bootstrap.py"], "git_node": "d37e4bac07963b9e92a3621c6da650f44918f4ff", "git_parents": ["f2cfd1be2b5549109a5ec77326b58412d50dd00f"], "node": "46f15d5b362b5c48e76a6e43bb8c19c9a9dee07c", "parents": ["63d19475d6ebf10fe3bf835905e45e835eab08ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080632 - Update libdmg-hfsplus to e18579b391950589b9ed16ee630c54ce4319bb29. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis version decompresses DMG runs in parallel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332758\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "8e3f3987e84f4fb1036f4cfeb7ed7bd7525d8c6e", "git_parents": ["d37e4bac07963b9e92a3621c6da650f44918f4ff"], "node": "7f73e62d273712cec2fc34e7a1bafdefcfba8ad8", "parents": ["46f15d5b362b5c48e76a6e43bb8c19c9a9dee07c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ali Sayed Salehi \u003ca.s.salehi.95@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055854 - Part 2: Target every push-based perf task in the perf batching shadow schedulers. r=taskgraph-reviewers,perftest-reviewers,sparky,ahal\n\nThe SS(perf_*_batch_*) shadow schedulers re-run optimization with the\ndecision task's parameters, so they inherit the `autoland_tasks` target\nmethod. On non-backstop pushes that method drops every test against a\nshippable build before optimization runs, which covers nearly all perf\ntasks (talos, awsy, shippable browsertime desktop, android-hw-a55). The\nbatching strategies therefore only got to judge the ~220 perf tasks\nagainst non-shippable builds instead of the ~850 that autoland targets\non a backstop push, and their batch pushes almost never coincide with a\nbackstop. Since the point of the evaluation is to replace the backstop,\nthe shadow schedulers must target perf tasks independently of it.\n\nAdd an `autoland_perf_shadow_scheduler_tasks` target method that behaves\nlike `autoland_tasks` except that tasks optimized through a\nperf-cadence-* strategy are always targeted, leaving the decision to the\nstrategy under evaluation. The shippable-test filter is factored out of\n`autoland_tasks`, whose behavior is unchanged.\n\n`mach taskgraph` only accepts a whole parameters set via `-p`, so the\nperf shadow schedulers derive one from the decision task's with a small\nscript (taskcluster/scripts/misc/shadow-scheduler-parameters.py) that\nreplaces `target_tasks_method` with\n`autoland_perf_shadow_scheduler_tasks`, and pass that file to `-p`. The\nderived file is uploaded as an artifact so a run can be reproduced\nlocally. The shadow scheduler task defaults switch from `run.using:\nmach` to the equivalent `run-task` command so the perf tasks can chain\nthe two steps; the bugbug shadow schedulers' task definitions are\nunchanged, and production scheduling is not affected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326296\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/shadow-scheduler.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/shadow-scheduler-parameters.py"], "git_node": "252eca5d6edd7f171f872e762c5a910ca571ac3b", "git_parents": ["8e3f3987e84f4fb1036f4cfeb7ed7bd7525d8c6e"], "node": "7dff6db3d0fed9a70d79e8e9a95ceca9af362d80", "parents": ["7f73e62d273712cec2fc34e7a1bafdefcfba8ad8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Baker \u003cdbaker@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072722 - Don't start early media reception when the receive track has no early codecs. r=webrtc-reviewers,pehrsons\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333964\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepTrack.h", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest_peerconnection.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_earlyMediaNoCodecs.html"], "git_node": "6cd3b582ca319ac4e00f80585ad6b850e052f057", "git_parents": ["252eca5d6edd7f171f872e762c5a910ca571ac3b"], "node": "3ded3473998c57cf24fb1f84196b889ad1951dd6", "parents": ["7dff6db3d0fed9a70d79e8e9a95ceca9af362d80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082551 - Add new telemetry for inclusions count and rule_applied - r=ip-protection-reviewers,sstreich\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334253\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPChannelFilter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPSiteRuleProviders.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPChannelFilter.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPPermissionRuleProvider.js"], "git_node": "001320c597b752858b0adcfd3677a80c4a5d68d6", "git_parents": ["6cd3b582ca319ac4e00f80585ad6b850e052f057"], "node": "076b5611947575d218327d172361b7db3c48048d", "parents": ["3ded3473998c57cf24fb1f84196b889ad1951dd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082409 - Update NSS to c0f712e69d86526338a885288c2b6668a6d8252d. UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE r=nss-reviewers,jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334090\n", "files": ["security/nss/cmd/libpkix/pkix_pl/module/manifest.mn", "security/nss/cmd/libpkix/pkix_pl/module/test_httpdefaultclient.c", "security/nss/cmd/libpkix/pkixutil/pkixutil.c", "security/nss/doc/src/build.md", "security/nss/doc/src/legacy_extracts/asn1.md", "security/nss/doc/src/legacy_extracts/structure.md", "security/nss/gtests/ssl_gtest/ssl_0rtt_unittest.cc", "security/nss/lib/libpkix/pkix_pl_nss/module/pkix_pl_httpdefaultclient.c", "security/nss/lib/libpkix/pkix_pl_nss/module/pkix_pl_httpdefaultclient.h", "security/nss/lib/ssl/tls13con.c", "security/nss/moz.yaml", "security/nss/tests/libpkix/pkix_pl_tests/module/runPLTests.sh"], "git_node": "3544a7d7996ea569dc98ea97fd9561cca338ad37", "git_parents": ["001320c597b752858b0adcfd3677a80c4a5d68d6"], "node": "e0ac3ff8e9429152b031f7291dfe362fd721b610", "parents": ["076b5611947575d218327d172361b7db3c48048d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077958 - Include filter inflation in the rect used to pick a surface's sub-slice. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nOtherwise a picture whose inflated coverage overlaps a compositor surface is\ndrawn in a later sub-slice than its children record their dependencies in, and\nits tiles are never invalidated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333938\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/surface_sub_slice_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/surface_sub_slice_2.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs"], "git_node": "50b1b969f719942b26866be47ff2c71c022a8a2f", "git_parents": ["3544a7d7996ea569dc98ea97fd9561cca338ad37"], "node": "c7bdbae6a733f8149b28e24f967254e2c2a9c7c1", "parents": ["e0ac3ff8e9429152b031f7291dfe362fd721b610"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081481: Use megamorphic cache for toJSON in JSON.stringify fast path r=mgaudet\n\nThe main potential downside of this is that it could theoretically pollute the megamorphic property cache, but I think on balance it should do more good than harm.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333775\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/JSON.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/JSON/stringify-toJSON-cache.js", "js/src/vm/Caches.h"], "git_node": "5c941bc94cb2e84420ed90210daa5a6389e8a19b", "git_parents": ["50b1b969f719942b26866be47ff2c71c022a8a2f"], "node": "193110741db928e9e8da81125bbca3c1a237fcab", "parents": ["c7bdbae6a733f8149b28e24f967254e2c2a9c7c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070278 - Match the Your clocks list hover to Stocks and drop the outline on open. r=nina-py\n\nOpening \u201cYour clocks\u201d no longer shows a focus ring: the panel takes focus instead of the back button. Clock rows now use the same 8px corners as Stocks rows, rather than a pill shape.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333399\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks/EditClocksPanel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks/_Clocks.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/EditClocksPanel.test.jsx"], "git_node": "84ef3855d3d1b23649435a907e7bfbce788972e2", "git_parents": ["5c941bc94cb2e84420ed90210daa5a6389e8a19b"], "node": "461b8192273637e6b6458b1b424f580887176376", "parents": ["193110741db928e9e8da81125bbca3c1a237fcab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082428 - Run the release tagging, push and source-signing kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-mark-as-shipped, release-version-bump, release-early-tagging, release-flatpak-push, release-msix-push, release-push-langpacks, release-source-signing, release-source-checksums-signing kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are release tagging, version bump, store push and source signing tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334158\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-early-tagging/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-flatpak-push/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-mark-as-shipped/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-msix-push/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-push-langpacks/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-source-checksums-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-source-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-version-bump/kind.yml"], "git_node": "9768d611c380b53a67bcf6fb08b27e2d2c5aea80", "git_parents": ["84ef3855d3d1b23649435a907e7bfbce788972e2"], "node": "c30d45171ae7e8fffbaf90cd6f7cc806765846d4", "parents": ["461b8192273637e6b6458b1b424f580887176376"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082430 - Run the release-partner kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-partner-attribution-beetmover, release-partner-repack-beetmover, release-partner-repack-chunking-dummy, release-partner-repack-mac-notarization, release-partner-repack-mac-signing, release-partner-repack-repackage, release-partner-repack-repackage-signing kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are partner repack signing, notarization and upload tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334156\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-attribution-beetmover/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-beetmover/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-chunking-dummy/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-mac-notarization/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-mac-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-repackage-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack-repackage/kind.yml"], "git_node": "a4b19509915a0c5fbf2b63141dfe9b98634b02e5", "git_parents": ["9768d611c380b53a67bcf6fb08b27e2d2c5aea80"], "node": "640928cae91acefbcc63f051d4f59805fbfe6b87", "parents": ["c30d45171ae7e8fffbaf90cd6f7cc806765846d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082431 - Run the release-eme-free-repack kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-eme-free-repack-beetmover, release-eme-free-repack-beetmover-checksums, release-eme-free-repack-mac-notarization, release-eme-free-repack-mac-signing, release-eme-free-repack-repackage, release-eme-free-repack-repackage-signing kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are EME-free repack signing, notarization and upload tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334155\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-beetmover-checksums/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-beetmover/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-mac-notarization/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-mac-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-repackage-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack-repackage/kind.yml"], "git_node": "b25faf33db6d58608499dcfac180434150a1ddd5", "git_parents": ["a4b19509915a0c5fbf2b63141dfe9b98634b02e5"], "node": "11666b3fa8d2c8acb90b8584fc1bf5a08fa64dfd", "parents": ["640928cae91acefbcc63f051d4f59805fbfe6b87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081313 - Don't assume non-overlay scrollbars are opaque. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThey might very well not be due to scrollbar-color.\n\nThis came up during mini-window development, where we might want to\npaint non-overlay visual-viewport-only scrollbars with overlay style.\nBut it seems like a relatively minor optimization.\n\nWe still need to subtract the scrollbar from the visual viewport etc\nthough (my first version of this patch didn't use to), otherwise we\nmight make content unreachable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333318\n", "files": ["layout/base/ViewportUtils.cpp", "layout/base/ViewportUtils.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/viewport-transparent-scrollbar-zoomed-ref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/viewport-transparent-scrollbar-zoomed.html"], "git_node": "d17b7ddb482e133699d0b66e626d36378fc1248c", "git_parents": ["b25faf33db6d58608499dcfac180434150a1ddd5"], "node": "0bdcb3404900c121e30b4c2583f2cbc78e8b9c30", "parents": ["11666b3fa8d2c8acb90b8584fc1bf5a08fa64dfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082429 - Run the release update-verify and balrog-scheduling kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-update-verify, release-update-verify-next, release-balrog-scheduling, release-update-product-channel-version, release-final-verify kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are update verification and balrog scheduling tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334157\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-balrog-scheduling/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-final-verify/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-product-channel-version/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-verify-next/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-verify/kind.yml"], "git_node": "b806a649c80bdb2db113a8e756c2e763d0ab3278", "git_parents": ["d17b7ddb482e133699d0b66e626d36378fc1248c"], "node": "b2aad02680638deb3a005a0ba65d5c8a97235be2", "parents": ["0bdcb3404900c121e30b4c2583f2cbc78e8b9c30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082432 - Run the release beetmover and checksums kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-beetmover-push-to-release, release-beetmover-signed-langpacks, release-beetmover-signed-langpacks-checksums, release-beetmover-source-checksums, release-generate-checksums-beetmover, release-generate-checksums-signing kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are release beetmover and checksums signing tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334154\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-beetmover-push-to-release/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-beetmover-signed-langpacks-checksums/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-beetmover-signed-langpacks/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-beetmover-source-checksums/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-generate-checksums-beetmover/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-generate-checksums-signing/kind.yml"], "git_node": "75a36b3229eb50ea7a3063fb93c9434ada907d2a", "git_parents": ["b806a649c80bdb2db113a8e756c2e763d0ab3278"], "node": "ced674774f8e5f3e91400ecc0a7691f34930ad4d", "parents": ["b2aad02680638deb3a005a0ba65d5c8a97235be2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082434 - Run the release-notify kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe release-notify-av-announce, release-notify-promote, release-notify-push, release-notify-ship, release-notify-started kinds carry `run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so\nthe tasks are dropped from the graph of a git-backed push. Removing it only\nchanges scheduling: these are release notification tasks, with no source\ncheckout. The `task-defaults:` key is removed where the guard was its only\ncontent.\n\nChain of Trust verification for scriptworker tasks is one shared code path\nthat is already verified on git-backed pushes (bug 2081108), so no per-kind\ntry run is needed. The generated task graph was checked locally against main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334132\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-av-announce/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-promote/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-push/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-ship/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-started/kind.yml"], "git_node": "788c6254454687c0552bb6edcc72cd4dd0cec7e5", "git_parents": ["75a36b3229eb50ea7a3063fb93c9434ada907d2a"], "node": "2c96776fffae1c39f58a6f3e84c3289885e0917b", "parents": ["ced674774f8e5f3e91400ecc0a7691f34930ad4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1981478 - Flip prefs to switch to NDK decoding/encoding on Android on nightly. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\" for causing mda failures in test_hevc_playback.html.\n\nThis reverts commit c0e99674dd93f531223294a546dd0ba14aac975e.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "4e877b82a9e05c14f2e1404ee1e2dea786f17f6a", "git_parents": ["788c6254454687c0552bb6edcc72cd4dd0cec7e5"], "node": "d58a824aa262ae32758f2fdca38b884a2be6e9e5", "parents": ["2c96776fffae1c39f58a6f3e84c3289885e0917b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2079902, Bug 2079981 - Newtab spaces preview modal on hover over tab bar r=jbrown\" for causing lint failures @ _Spaces.scss\n\nThis reverts commit ecf6b702d06eebf3244fcdb67dbeae65b04d916b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2079981 - Keep the New Tab thematic spaces frame within the page width - r=thecount\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3560e6051067f5cecdee555e1ec8016f9f4a7181.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2079981 - Show the first-slot widget in thematic spaces and let the config name the widget catch-all - r=thecount\"\n\nThis reverts commit a7ee5e6ee486ee3afb1ceb0c0cb04f94e15afd89.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2079981 - Show Recent activity in the thematic space marked for it - r=thecount\"\n\nThis reverts commit fa3e31940389a456640e5dd1285ca6a68e776708.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2079981 - Show edge arrows with the switcher and keep spaces without stories in New Tab thematic spaces - r=thecount\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7212785c2194f02907ce3c096f5823d7230cbe1e.\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/PageLayoutVariants.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase/DiscoveryStreamBase.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/Spaces.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/_Spaces.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-activity.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-activity.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-stories.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-widgets.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-stories.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-widgets.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/common/PageLayoutVariants.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Spaces.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/selectLayoutRender.test.js"], "git_node": "157b60a1a9e0ed71390792af671b6dc6c3a4a0f1", "git_parents": ["4e877b82a9e05c14f2e1404ee1e2dea786f17f6a"], "node": "a0a2dd6805e59fb51ddd985a8977a37fb5a1c916", "parents": ["d58a824aa262ae32758f2fdca38b884a2be6e9e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "af5eb65a07f95f38958889352ec720763aa12f46", "git_parents": ["157b60a1a9e0ed71390792af671b6dc6c3a4a0f1", "e08a96ae6182d44d58846ce56551dbbaf339ee66"], "node": "873eb8c4d76b6470ca6c56da268139a496bb9cf1", "parents": ["a0a2dd6805e59fb51ddd985a8977a37fb5a1c916", "f73cc5160274b37e6023f57c07f362f4be289b34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2081313 - Don't assume non-overlay scrollbars are opaque. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\" for causing bc tests failures\n\nThis reverts commit d17b7ddb482e133699d0b66e626d36378fc1248c.\n", "files": ["layout/base/ViewportUtils.cpp", "layout/base/ViewportUtils.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/viewport-transparent-scrollbar-zoomed-ref.html", "layout/reftests/css-scrollbars/viewport-transparent-scrollbar-zoomed.html"], "git_node": "202b025207ef5778d52c31bce31e037c7cc5f7ec", "git_parents": ["af5eb65a07f95f38958889352ec720763aa12f46"], "node": "40204ff2b5e3f6fc87ca652946708fb1ec15e118", "parents": ["873eb8c4d76b6470ca6c56da268139a496bb9cf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044804 - add support for dragging and dropping entries from the sidebar history panel into the tab strip. r=sidebar-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333442\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-history.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-tab-list.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_history_sidebar_drag_and_drop.js"], "git_node": "d762b0e2b0a646704a7472349a88a4a547a71a78", "git_parents": ["202b025207ef5778d52c31bce31e037c7cc5f7ec"], "node": "87cff9028ed7f4630b7874dbb88f9f9bef9c933d", "parents": ["40204ff2b5e3f6fc87ca652946708fb1ec15e118"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079992 - Report unexpected assertion counts in the error summary. r=ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332244\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/errorsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_errorsummary.py"], "git_node": "f54ef24ce7975c097a3721d556d299660b30f2e1", "git_parents": ["d762b0e2b0a646704a7472349a88a4a547a71a78"], "node": "3f41654ac1b94145a306c547bbf236f80d86ef49", "parents": ["87cff9028ed7f4630b7874dbb88f9f9bef9c933d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082609 - add Nightly default on for aitab r=Mardak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334279\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "b773aea25c9a1419ce9df99afcf29e71ff0e566c", "git_parents": ["f54ef24ce7975c097a3721d556d299660b30f2e1"], "node": "e508b84dce148be90c698cc917754aa6b83e5899", "parents": ["3f41654ac1b94145a306c547bbf236f80d86ef49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079283 - Add newtabpreview.ftl file. r=mconley,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331604\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/bin/render-activity-stream-html.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/abouthomecache/page.html.template", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/remote-renderer-host.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-debug.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream-noscripts.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/prerendered/activity-stream.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/moz.build", "browser/locales-preview/newtabPreview.ftl", "browser/locales/jar.mn"], "git_node": "a3e65c8d4a574d0bd57e3a4ae550ce9cc9e4033e", "git_parents": ["b773aea25c9a1419ce9df99afcf29e71ff0e566c"], "node": "9d6733a5397d031aa4e42480b3b320ace4641d9f", "parents": ["e508b84dce148be90c698cc917754aa6b83e5899"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings mobile-experiments mobile-merino-manifest ct-logs - r=release-managers,dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334287\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-manifest/src/main/assets/manifest/manifest.json", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin.meta.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/softblocks-addons-mlbf.bin", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/softblocks-addons-mlbf.bin.meta.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json", "toolkit/components/certviewer/content/components/logNameTable.mjs"], "git_node": "14378a311267d17d43375a84678c4096edbbcf2a", "git_parents": ["a3e65c8d4a574d0bd57e3a4ae550ce9cc9e4033e"], "node": "23547d664db11dd13debe9146df90219bf75fbcb", "parents": ["9d6733a5397d031aa4e42480b3b320ace4641d9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Devota Aabel \u003cdaabel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081918 - Extract the homepage toolbars and wallpaper background out of HomeFragment.initComposeHomepage. r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\ninitComposeHomepage built the Scaffold's top and bottom bar contents and the\nwallpaper background inline, which made it too complex for detekt once more\nhomepage logic is added. Move them into private composables: HomeTopBar,\nHomeBottomBar (split into HomeNavigationBottomBar and HomeToolbarBottomBar\nfor the two toolbar positions) and WallpaperBackground. The bar composables\ntake a modifier so callers can observe the slot sizes.\n\nNo behavior change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333838\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt"], "git_node": "4948db2cf9a225157f155c8c3aa31778d818b8be", "git_parents": ["14378a311267d17d43375a84678c4096edbbcf2a"], "node": "bd1a92dad9659c9ecf9a8a9490494050bc651db0", "parents": ["23547d664db11dd13debe9146df90219bf75fbcb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Devota Aabel \u003cdaabel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076899 - Add gradient scrims behind the homepage toolbars with universal edge-to-edge wallpapers. r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nWith the universal edge-to-edge wallpapers setting, the homepage toolbars are\ntransparent and their icons can lack contrast on busy wallpapers. The scrims are\ndrawn in a full-screen layer behind the Scaffold rather than inside the toolbar\nslots, so that they start inside the status bar and system navigation bar, and\ntheir heights follow the measured toolbar slots.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330057\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/WallpaperToolbarScrim.kt"], "git_node": "57227dfc692f7726028458a30aff89cbd6f376c0", "git_parents": ["4948db2cf9a225157f155c8c3aa31778d818b8be"], "node": "e789f845bf18ec4f1095222c351466695b37fdb3", "parents": ["bd1a92dad9659c9ecf9a8a9490494050bc651db0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Devota Aabel \u003cdaabel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076931 - Show the homepage tab strip over the toolbar scrim with universal edge-to-edge wallpapers. r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nThe tab strip kept its opaque gradient background, and the same gradient behind\nthe status bar, while the toolbars around it sit on the scrim. The tab strip\ncontent colors move into TabStripColors so the content drawn directly on the\nscrim can use the wallpaper text color, matching the toolbar icons.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330071\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/tabstrip/TabStrip.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/tabstrip/TabStripColors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/theme/StatusBarColorManager.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/theme/StatusBarColorManagerTest.kt"], "git_node": "d8d4b5017dc5033f1b81cba0eedb5746398d0d7a", "git_parents": ["57227dfc692f7726028458a30aff89cbd6f376c0"], "node": "5b799ff82fb26c249a70de6fb2b5bc1edb922f71", "parents": ["e789f845bf18ec4f1095222c351466695b37fdb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Devota Aabel \u003cdaabel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082151 - Enable universal edge-to-edge wallpapers by default. r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nTurn on the universal-edge-to-edge-wallpapers Nimbus feature by default on all\nchannels. The secret setting still overrides it locally, and Nimbus can still\nturn it off remotely.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333904\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "e3dc348a9938237455d76445c2dc690c1bca36a9", "git_parents": ["d8d4b5017dc5033f1b81cba0eedb5746398d0d7a"], "node": "5acc728ebd8740e1746524459afed0e3f5e9ebfc", "parents": ["5b799ff82fb26c249a70de6fb2b5bc1edb922f71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079432 - Disable the Widevine/PlayReady EME WPTs in test-verify. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThe test-verify jobs run without the network access or CDM configuration\nthe Widevine/PlayReady tests depend on, so they cannot pass there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331874\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-encryption-scheme.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-initdata-type.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-status-for-hdcp.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-events-session-closed-event.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-events.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-expiration.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-generate-request-disallowed-input.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-invalid-license.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses-multiple-sessions.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-clear-encrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-encrypted-clear-sources.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-encrypted-clear.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-events.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-expired.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey-sequential-readyState.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey-sequential.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multisession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration-keystatus.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-after-src.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-after-update.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-immediately.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-onencrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-two-videos.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-waitingforkey.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-requestmediakeysystemaccess.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-reset-src-after-setmediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-again-after-playback.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-again-after-resetting-src.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-at-same-time.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-multiple-times-with-different-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-multiple-times-with-the-same-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-to-multiple-video-elements.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeysession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeysystemaccess.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-unique-origin.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-waiting-for-a-key.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-not-callable-after-createsession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/encrypted-media/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "6ee1c7753ad2ae62b19d0b663cebd0663d60f530", "git_parents": ["e3dc348a9938237455d76445c2dc690c1bca36a9"], "node": "2268cf302c5e0f46adb4db6fa982c90221c03fd5", "parents": ["5acc728ebd8740e1746524459afed0e3f5e9ebfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "spa5k \u003c79936503+spa5k@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078679 - Release the completed OfflineAudioContext rendering promise. r=media-playback-reviewers,karlt\n\nA completed OfflineAudioContext retains a discarded AudioBuffer through mOfflineRenderingPromise. Move the member into a local RefPtr before resolution. The context releases its internal reference when the method returns. Caller-held promises and output buffers remain valid owners.\n\nThe mochitest fails the output-release assertion before the correction and passes all nine assertions after it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331166\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webaudio/test/test_offlineRendering_promise_release.html"], "git_node": "648c89220dfca90a6b6664bf0af867741a1e8ace", "git_parents": ["6ee1c7753ad2ae62b19d0b663cebd0663d60f530"], "node": "956626e1adf6089f8288e8c748042743cc5870e6", "parents": ["2268cf302c5e0f46adb4db6fa982c90221c03fd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081184 - Make `BrowserParent` verify `WidgetKeyboardEvent::mAlternativeCharCodes` r=smaug\n\nTo avoid performing unintended shortcuts or access keys due to bogus\nreply event, let's check whether the reply event's\n`mAlternativeCharCodes` matches with the original data.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333978\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "67271fe6f72ebf90e4999c378ad286b093d20918", "git_parents": ["648c89220dfca90a6b6664bf0af867741a1e8ace"], "node": "fb0561f4833ead0f520e25bbebe31e25303333ce", "parents": ["956626e1adf6089f8288e8c748042743cc5870e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "def00111 \u003ckernp@gmx.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077700 - Use the browser from the active tab for commands.onCommand. r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330563\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-commands.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_commands_requestPermission.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-permissions.js"], "git_node": "ebb2fd2f328255896549a530e53a94b23076b40d", "git_parents": ["67271fe6f72ebf90e4999c378ad286b093d20918"], "node": "ae50842196fd9a2162f3700efe821eb035573b37", "parents": ["fb0561f4833ead0f520e25bbebe31e25303333ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abel Kalu \u003c59095867+BlessedOneKobo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053552 - Remove unused preferences for extensions.webcompat-report.*. r=mconley,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,twisniewski\n\nUnused preferences removed:\n- extensions.webcompat-reporter.newIssueEndpoint\n- extensions.webcompat-reporter.enabled\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324645\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/installer/allowed-dupes.mn", "browser/modules/test/browser/head.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "b008c6230edf0394e057a2d09341b0d36767aee3", "git_parents": ["ebb2fd2f328255896549a530e53a94b23076b40d"], "node": "0e5ea72b26cca11817ed8870ba793b8a0c5213a5", "parents": ["ae50842196fd9a2162f3700efe821eb035573b37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025851 - Show result to search for a url the user typed. r=dao,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332025\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderHeuristicFallback.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_providerHeuristicFallback.js"], "git_node": "c08bf14244158621691e6e0ac9842a3a6b7bdf03", "git_parents": ["b008c6230edf0394e057a2d09341b0d36767aee3"], "node": "3f66e473e1cedc6a76620542939ae3b8433478b2", "parents": ["0e5ea72b26cca11817ed8870ba793b8a0c5213a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082265 - Reject pending codec support waits when a remote media manager actor is destroyed. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334348\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteMediaManagerChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteMediaManagerChild.h"], "git_node": "e2cdb982c7e17e4f79c12349055a88077f6e58de", "git_parents": ["c08bf14244158621691e6e0ac9842a3a6b7bdf03"], "node": "d9fa6ba7a006e2595a586d512139799fd7faa538", "parents": ["3f66e473e1cedc6a76620542939ae3b8433478b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079160: Compute the name of XUL buttons and toolbarbuttons from the subtree unless the label is invisible. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nPreviously, we used the label attribute directly even if the label was visible, excluding the label element and its text leaf from the accessibility tree.\nThis meant that if there was a label as well as pseudo-elements like ::after, the accessible name would not include the pseudo-element text.\nPractically, this meant that visible keyboard shortcut text was not exposed to accessibility in the Firefox hamburger menu.\n\nTo fix this, we now expose the label and its text leaf in the accessibility tree if it is visible, and the name is then computed from the subtree.\nName subtree computation includes pseudo-element content.\n\nThere are still many cases where the XUL label attribute is used to provide a textual label, but the label is invisible.\nIn these cases, we fall back to using the label attribute as we did previously.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332334\n", "files": ["accessible/base/nsTextEquivUtils.cpp", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_namechange.xhtml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/tree/test_button.xhtml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/tree/test_formctrl.xhtml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_deck.xhtml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_menubutton.xhtml", "accessible/xul/XULFormControlAccessible.cpp", "accessible/xul/XULFormControlAccessible.h"], "git_node": "39232fec6be6805e58be0919a121c90dc6f4cec8", "git_parents": ["e2cdb982c7e17e4f79c12349055a88077f6e58de"], "node": "d2c5caf7ab4ca694989410dffefc681e24be86df", "parents": ["d9fa6ba7a006e2595a586d512139799fd7faa538"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1862805: Remove MozMouseExploreByTouch event. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nThis was previously used for hit testing on Android.\nHowever, as of bug 1822004, Android uses the RemoteAccessible cache for hit testing like every other platform, so this event is now dead code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333986\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/events/EventNameList.inc", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "widget/EventMessageList.inc", "widget/InputData.cpp", "widget/InputData.h", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "5283d666531218ed5eba375fad5daf4fcb5411e0", "git_parents": ["39232fec6be6805e58be0919a121c90dc6f4cec8"], "node": "6228d7e8448cbd4466cfcd3479c8f3ce0ca36b6d", "parents": ["d2c5caf7ab4ca694989410dffefc681e24be86df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081271: Convert the main thread diagnostic assertion in LazyInstantiator::Release to a warning assertion. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nAs I understand it, according to fundamental COM rules, when an object is created in an STA thread (such as our main thread), the COM marshaler should always release it on that same thread, not some other thread.\nHowever, it seems that this does occasionally happen in the wild and I cannot fathom why.\nBug 2002899 speculatively added a lock to protect against this.\nThe diagnostic assertion was added to see whether this was really happening, since the lock is not 0 cost.\nClearly, it *is* really happening.\nTherefore, convert this to a warning assertion, since we'd still like to know when this occurs when debugging in case we can track it down one day.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333983\n", "files": ["accessible/windows/msaa/LazyInstantiator.cpp"], "git_node": "77ad437e173862a37b2a7fb441b0d330e938c3e7", "git_parents": ["5283d666531218ed5eba375fad5daf4fcb5411e0"], "node": "fcf720e1dfe3219819aae6b10d51c31f6675b7cd", "parents": ["6228d7e8448cbd4466cfcd3479c8f3ce0ca36b6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082349 - Ensure attributes for canvas.getContext() are evaluated before context creation. r=gfx-reviewers,ahale\n\nThe problem stems from getContext() triggering CanvasRenderingContextHelper::UpdateContext which evaluates\nJS getters which may recursively call getContext(). All this is done after the context is speculatively\ncreated, leading to a number of inconsistencies with the spec and bugs.\n\nTo resolve this, CanvasRenderingContextOptions is initialized first with the attributes from getContext().\nOnly after this is CanvasRenderingContextHelper::GetOrCreateContext called to create the context, properly\nadjusted to any context that may by now have been created. This ensures, in the case of recursive contexts,\nthat inner calls to getContext() are properly evaluted first, and that outer calls can then return the same\nresult as the inner call.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334048\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContextHelper.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContextHelper.h", "dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.h", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvas.cpp", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvas.h", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvasDisplayHelper.cpp", "dom/canvas/nsICanvasRenderingContextInternal.h", "dom/canvas/test/reftest/2082349-1-ref.html", "dom/canvas/test/reftest/2082349-1.html", "dom/canvas/test/reftest/reftest.list", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-canvas-element/2d-getcontext-options.html.ini"], "git_node": "bcd3856fe0295ec7742421cc07ff5b662eab5a8e", "git_parents": ["77ad437e173862a37b2a7fb441b0d330e938c3e7"], "node": "04f00e475a8753b239e5fd3497da2d44033c3bb8", "parents": ["fcf720e1dfe3219819aae6b10d51c31f6675b7cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082711 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 24417f0c7e8b79bc31234c4819cb26cbf7070bac r=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334357\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "f48f42f9514d3f272d93bae8889b98cb72b7f993", "git_parents": ["bcd3856fe0295ec7742421cc07ff5b662eab5a8e"], "node": "0a53be6e31e951300430067a8d4ae0b1900aae01", "parents": ["04f00e475a8753b239e5fd3497da2d44033c3bb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709494 - Make SourceVideoTrackListener use MediaEventProducer for events to match audio. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nClosing DecodedStreamGraphListener disconnects the audio track's output and\nends notifications, but the video track listener dispatched its notifications\ndirectly, and stays attached until it is forgotten on the main thread. If\nthe audio track ends in between, which happens when the stream is stopped\nafter the audio track has sent all its data, the video track listener sees\nthe ended audio track and starts reporting output to drive the clock, which\nthe closed listener asserts is only possible after it was notified that\naudio ended.\n\nNotify the video track's output and end through events, like the audio\ntrack's, so that closing the listener disconnects them too, including any\nnotification already dispatched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331394\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasink/DecodedStream.cpp"], "git_node": "d913aeb1010472a7ff46c3a6346ef4eaa5571fc4", "git_parents": ["f48f42f9514d3f272d93bae8889b98cb72b7f993"], "node": "3376c6ec94323ecc17439f8f53e435dcf4faba80", "parents": ["0a53be6e31e951300430067a8d4ae0b1900aae01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053552 - Remove unused preferences for extensions.webcompat-report.*. r=mconley,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,twisniewski\" for causing ES lint failures at browser/head.js\n\nThis reverts commit b008c6230edf0394e057a2d09341b0d36767aee3.\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/installer/allowed-dupes.mn", "browser/modules/test/browser/head.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "27754857e0cf558444adc19769233d5a6943048c", "git_parents": ["d913aeb1010472a7ff46c3a6346ef4eaa5571fc4"], "node": "f5a15abea57fda2944f67bca050c8567f8b99535", "parents": ["3376c6ec94323ecc17439f8f53e435dcf4faba80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2079432 - Disable the Widevine/PlayReady EME WPTs in test-verify. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\" for causing eme web platform failures at setMediaKeys\n\nThis reverts commit 6ee1c7753ad2ae62b19d0b663cebd0663d60f530.\n", "files": ["testing/we