nvert StartupPerformance to a class. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sclements\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334455\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/StartupPerformance.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "521b97c1f7ec22bf4200cfbb5f1be9a882e1abea", "git_parents": ["732e95f0a3902737d230ea983abfac58f89b43ff"], "node": "a4b818de138470fc6c8e72cd559902dca9fd1431", "parents": ["2e4c9a18d1ac964494f7f846810ea1c1ea12e8c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077921 - Fix --disable-webspeech. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333692\n", "files": ["config/external/mozinference/mozinference.symbols", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "toolkit/components/ml/backends/llama/LlamaRuntimeLinker.h", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/HWInferenceChild.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/HWInferenceChild.h", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/HWInferenceParent.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/HWInferenceParent.h", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/PHWInference.ipdl", "toolkit/components/ml/ipc/moz.build"], "git_node": "ab50eff0791147e5d65fe30c5ebe734feab0a1c8", "git_parents": ["521b97c1f7ec22bf4200cfbb5f1be9a882e1abea"], "node": "4672a29541b4ca0a5827dc4c4b6931c5d35ab609", "parents": ["a4b818de138470fc6c8e72cd559902dca9fd1431"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076695 - Make nsTimer support thread-safe weak pointers and hold it weakly from nsTimerImpl. r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331822\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsTimerImpl.h"], "git_node": "dbb5bdc9f1751f0271ec809f80465f7f00337ded", "git_parents": ["ab50eff0791147e5d65fe30c5ebe734feab0a1c8"], "node": "23a190f8e323af3ea737c3c74464b5f54f27024b", "parents": ["4672a29541b4ca0a5827dc4c4b6931c5d35ab609"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joe Bowser \u003cjbowser@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063326 - Part 1: Add end-to-end performance coverage for the Smart Window intent classifier. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,jlewis,kshampur\n\nTypes a chat prompt into the Smart Window smartbar, so the intent engine\nis created and run by the production urlbar provider, and reports the\ntime until the smartbar query finishes with the detected intent, peak\nmemory, and the engine series. Both intent models are measured, the\ndefault and the en-fr one served to users whose home region is FR, on\nthe native and wasm backends.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333629\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser_perf/browser_smartwindow_intent_perf.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser_perf/perftest.toml", "python/mozperftest/perfdocs/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/macosx-aarch64.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.md"], "git_node": "4e1652c23b24f9329905515fd367ffb208deac40", "git_parents": ["dbb5bdc9f1751f0271ec809f80465f7f00337ded"], "node": "87f45bee972e212c49c700d43855b3c5f3b0d595", "parents": ["23a190f8e323af3ea737c3c74464b5f54f27024b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joe Bowser \u003cjbowser@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063326 - Part 2: Add end-to-end performance coverage for PDF.js alt-text generation. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nAdds an image through the PDF.js stamp editor, so the alt-text engine is\ncreated by the viewer when the PDF opens and run by the alt-text dialog,\nand reports the time from the Add image click until the guessed alt text\nis shown, inference memory, and the engine series. The backend is not\npinned, so the job measures the one best-onnx resolves to.\n\nPdfJsParent returns a canned alt text in automation. The new\npdfjs.altText.inferenceInAutomation pref lets the test run the real\nmodel, leaving the existing alt-text tests on the canned response.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333630\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/perfdocs/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/macosx-aarch64.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.md", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.build", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_alttext_perf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perftest.toml"], "git_node": "f32e49e57b06fded72a029ba71c5cede1305cc02", "git_parents": ["4e1652c23b24f9329905515fd367ffb208deac40"], "node": "8f577f8fc00622b696a566a8604649cf36b2b9af", "parents": ["87f45bee972e212c49c700d43855b3c5f3b0d595"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081689 - Share numeric type computation across CSS Typed OM math operations; r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nExtract the common numeric type computation logic into AddTypes() and\nMultiplyTypes(), using a shared helper to collect operand types and invoke the\ncorresponding Servo operation.\n\nUpdate the CSSMathSum, CSSMathProduct, CSSMathMin, CSSMathMax, and CSSMathClamp\nconstructors to use these methods, eliminating duplicated code and preparing\nfor their reuse by the CSSNumericValue arithmetic methods.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333683\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/CSSMathClamp.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSMathMax.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSMathMin.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSMathProduct.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSMathSum.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.h"], "git_node": "5d960cda6ce7f1df5aa64255ac1d8117f65207bf", "git_parents": ["f32e49e57b06fded72a029ba71c5cede1305cc02"], "node": "dc797de87a8b58abbe1d5a34bf5614909aaac98e", "parents": ["8f577f8fc00622b696a566a8604649cf36b2b9af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1951304 - Use only CaretImage as the touch area for touch events. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nBug 1809060 comment 4 has an image of the touch area: CaretImage (red box) and\nTextOverlay (blue box). Full is CaretImage + TextOverlay.\n\nThis patch changes the touch area for touch events to use CaretImage, making it\nbehave the same as mouse events. As a result, any touch interaction near the\ncursor on the TextOverlay now works. For example:\n\n- double-tap to select a word\n- long-tap to select a word\n- single-tap to move the cursor\n\nHowever, the trade-off is that dragging the caret by pressing the cursor or the\nedge of the selection highlight stops working. Bug 2082580 tracks the work to\nre-introduce it. This patch keeps the unused TouchArea::Full for the future\nwork.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334237\n", "files": ["layout/base/AccessibleCaret.h", "layout/base/AccessibleCaretManager.cpp", "layout/base/tests/marionette/test_accessiblecaret_selection_mode.py"], "git_node": "e1ccea7082085ec9cf84c05a384a3e8acf141813", "git_parents": ["5d960cda6ce7f1df5aa64255ac1d8117f65207bf"], "node": "bc7a97109ee556d9a08fabb92d02c4b3ae85d0c9", "parents": ["dc797de87a8b58abbe1d5a34bf5614909aaac98e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082597 - Add an is_shallow property to mozversioncontrol repositories, r=ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334293\n", "files": ["python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/base.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/git.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/jj.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/mercurial.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/source.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/test/python.toml", "python/mozversioncontrol/test/test_is_shallow.py"], "git_node": "2571a458a68112def89eceb33266f247a8c87350", "git_parents": ["e1ccea7082085ec9cf84c05a384a3e8acf141813"], "node": "516f7452af352bd1d720b88ed3dafbe2bf54f586", "parents": ["bc7a97109ee556d9a08fabb92d02c4b3ae85d0c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082597 - Support shallow clones with artifact builds, r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334294\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_artifacts.py"], "git_node": "2fa75d4b6f698576c1f92752b823b0a43f6fdfb6", "git_parents": ["2571a458a68112def89eceb33266f247a8c87350"], "node": "e6ff94376c63e7484ad8c49867a3efd6a98fecaa", "parents": ["516f7452af352bd1d720b88ed3dafbe2bf54f586"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081108 - Run the repackage kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nEleven repackage, repackage-l10n and repackage-signing kinds carry\n`run-on-repo-type: [hg]`, so no installer, deb, rpm, msi or msix package is\nproduced on a git-backed push. Removing it only changes scheduling: the\nrepackage transform still pins the clone to Mercurial, and the signing\ntasks have no checkout.\n\nVerified on staging-firefox (git-backed) on Oct 12: every repackage,\nrepackage-l10n (ach) and repackage-signing task on linux64, linux64-aarch64,\nmacosx64 and win64 shippable builds completed, rpm signing included.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333135\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/repackage-deb-l10n/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-l10n/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-msi/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-msix/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-rpm-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-shippable-l10n-msix/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-signing-l10n/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-signing-msi/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-signing-msix/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage/kind.yml"], "git_node": "bc3b1606c3343ce11303e94e72b80d5e158dfedd", "git_parents": ["2fa75d4b6f698576c1f92752b823b0a43f6fdfb6"], "node": "18c7f01de60c19140744641241c327b0809ab0c6", "parents": ["e6ff94376c63e7484ad8c49867a3efd6a98fecaa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042165 - Break down StateInfo into independent updates r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\n... to improve the stale cache problem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324204\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/ipprotection/GeckoIPProtectionDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/ipprotection/GeckoIPProtectionDelegateTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/ipprotection/IPProtectionDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/ipprotection/IPProtectionHandler.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/IPProtectionFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/Actions.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionLocationMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/Reducers.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/FakeEligibilityStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/IPProtectionFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionReducerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/IPProtectionScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/IPProtectionMenuBindingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "e8a5d6162cb271db51a2637146961754fa3c24d2", "git_parents": ["bc3b1606c3343ce11303e94e72b80d5e158dfedd"], "node": "ca097cd74aecc3ff0e76e2920842624c3dc7cb67", "parents": ["18c7f01de60c19140744641241c327b0809ab0c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082660 - Land strings for holiday promo CFRs - r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334311\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/ipProtection.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2082660_ipprotection_holiday_promo_buttons.py"], "git_node": "d8c8f5ed3a0cc852f1f1b6c12ec382a3836da9bc", "git_parents": ["e8a5d6162cb271db51a2637146961754fa3c24d2"], "node": "a1730a3ea67c90dbb9f301cb1e33ce099aabd589", "parents": ["ca097cd74aecc3ff0e76e2920842624c3dc7cb67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067873 - Telemetry for PUWYLO resume cards - r=ngrato,pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332941\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-resume-card/smartwindow-resume-card.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-resume-section/smartwindow-resume-section.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_resume_card.js"], "git_node": "9a47855852b0c393f0d1df18b3810c31f3be2511", "git_parents": ["d8c8f5ed3a0cc852f1f1b6c12ec382a3836da9bc"], "node": "e47901201ddaab222457d503a28b69bf1da89be9", "parents": ["a1730a3ea67c90dbb9f301cb1e33ce099aabd589"], "tags": []}, {"author": "owlishDeveloper \u003cbugzeeeeee@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053909 - [Part 1] Add scroll position to the content metrics r=geckoview-reviewers,emilio,calu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334361\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.h", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java", "widget/android/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "f9d81d379f0afe075f001d5665761ceb91160c99", "git_parents": ["9a47855852b0c393f0d1df18b3810c31f3be2511"], "node": "a157df5f468f01da34ae5ded2c94a4ad5d32baa7", "parents": ["e47901201ddaab222457d503a28b69bf1da89be9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079432 - Disable the Widevine/PlayReady EME WPTs in test-verify. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nThe test-verify jobs run without the network access or CDM configuration\nthe Widevine/PlayReady tests depend on, so they cannot pass there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331874\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-encryption-scheme.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-initdata-type.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-check-status-for-hdcp.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-events-session-closed-event.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-events.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-expiration.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-generate-request-disallowed-input.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-invalid-license.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses-multiple-sessions.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-clear-encrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-encrypted-clear-sources.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-encrypted-clear.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-events.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-expired.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey-sequential-readyState.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey-sequential.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multisession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration-keystatus.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-after-src.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-after-update.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-immediately.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-setMediaKeys-onencrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-two-videos.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-waitingforkey.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-requestmediakeysystemaccess.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-reset-src-after-setmediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-again-after-playback.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-again-after-resetting-src.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-at-same-time.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-multiple-times-with-different-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-multiple-times-with-the-same-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys-to-multiple-video-elements.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-setmediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeys.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeysession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-syntax-mediakeysystemaccess.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-unique-origin.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-waiting-for-a-key.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-not-callable-after-createsession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/encrypted-media/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "7cc7780f0729d1629911e80df5baca3482dbff7a", "git_parents": ["f9d81d379f0afe075f001d5665761ceb91160c99"], "node": "8f5fb19dc297539a6a286612d698e2df32336405", "parents": ["a157df5f468f01da34ae5ded2c94a4ad5d32baa7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082876 - Update PDF.js to dda8b72806ea97d1fd4ed121b081311a34898110 r=pdfjs-reviewers,calixte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334520\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.renderer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.css", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.css", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "5fc8ecd8d97411e90423b48026c558e964ceae53", "git_parents": ["7cc7780f0729d1629911e80df5baca3482dbff7a"], "node": "c00397958e8fec6d8c1fbd4c83a3a0d5d1625231", "parents": ["8f5fb19dc297539a6a286612d698e2df32336405"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073063 - Let raptor support classes run local servers the device can reach r=perftest-reviewers,necko-reviewers,kshampur\n\nSupport classes can list ports for adb to reverse-forward, and profiles of\ncold tests are labelled cold when the manifest rather than the command line\nsays so.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326955\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browsertime/android.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perftest.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/raptor_profiling.py", "testing/raptor/test/test_raptor.py"], "git_node": "9927f9b1d9e5e05467d1fa5696324c3e5a97f4b0", "git_parents": ["5fc8ecd8d97411e90423b48026c558e964ceae53"], "node": "fcdd058bc3ba17adc75272ae84617b60aaea123e", "parents": ["c00397958e8fec6d8c1fbd4c83a3a0d5d1625231"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073063 - Add a browsertime test that replays recorded news-site request timelines against a local DoH server r=perftest-reviewers,necko-reviewers,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,Standard8,valentin,kshampur\n\nThe existing DoH tests do not capture slow lookups on busy pages reliably:\ntrr-multi depends on a live resolver and a live page, and test_trr_bench.js\nis desktop only and never loads a page.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326956\n", "files": [".prettierignore", "taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/mobile.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-platforms.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/browsertime/doh_busy_site.js", "testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/doh_busy_site.py", "testing/raptor/browsertime/utils/doh_busy_site_server.js", "testing/raptor/browsertime/utils/doh_busy_sites.json", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/config.yml", "testing/raptor/raptor/raptor.toml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/custom/browsertime-doh-busy-site.toml", "tools/rewriting/Generated.txt"], "git_node": "7672b2113c99e965ea050e1efa41658864dd2f4e", "git_parents": ["9927f9b1d9e5e05467d1fa5696324c3e5a97f4b0"], "node": "618ef46530f66ead27cf2a3e77c2c5ea1f26a62f", "parents": ["fcdd058bc3ba17adc75272ae84617b60aaea123e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073015 - Read macOS preference sources separately. r=spohl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.ser