c948622ee139c3bd\nzam -\u003e f4c3229afb6af5cc3604f529c948622ee139c3bd\nzh-CN -\u003e f4c3229afb6af5cc3604f529c948622ee139c3bd\nzh-TW -\u003e f4c3229afb6af5cc3604f529c948622ee139c3bd\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "ad7db3d6e34978434ed51b89f02a5a2566a1dafd", "git_parents": ["9b13cdaee9546db1d06a2f8041a4e40feeac904c"], "node": "d1c6cbf20eebd72905a6883724a01481df605683", "parents": ["311e0f858754eeaeee9ed905b87270e0a74cb6fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079139 - Delete the SVG glyphs in gfxFontEntry::DisconnectSVG. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDisconnectSVG is called at xpcom-shutdown to release the SVG glyphs\ndocuments of cached user fonts before the final cycle collection. Since\nmSVGGlyphs became a raw pointer, clearing it no longer deletes the\ngfxSVGGlyphs object, so the documents leak together with everything they\nhold.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331915\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxUserFontSet.cpp"], "git_node": "a5590c1a8002b2c344e4a9895201d8d489d686c6", "git_parents": ["ad7db3d6e34978434ed51b89f02a5a2566a1dafd"], "node": "49a69c87ad48e71038d52a4d77e6764a4544ff1e", "parents": ["d1c6cbf20eebd72905a6883724a01481df605683"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079139 - Make gfxFontEntry::mSVGGlyphs a main-thread-only UniquePtr. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nSVG glyphs are only supported on the main thread, so the atomic pointer\nsuggests a thread safety that does not exist, and as a raw pointer it made\nit easy to drop the object without deleting it. Own it with a UniquePtr and\nguard it with the main thread capability, so the thread safety analysis\nchecks that it is only accessed on the main thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331916\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h"], "git_node": "c902e251797dbe57645242631242688874e5cc0d", "git_parents": ["a5590c1a8002b2c344e4a9895201d8d489d686c6"], "node": "c575f15818d8f1ba59483de61db61cd9de50c161", "parents": ["49a69c87ad48e71038d52a4d77e6764a4544ff1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074209 - Attach color-font palette cache to the individual gfxFontEntry for color fonts. r=gfx-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio,lsalzman\n\nThis is instead of having a shared cache attached to the presContext, and means the\nlifetime of the cache is directly tied to the font entry that owns it.\n\nCache lookups and modifications are guarded by the gfxFontEntry's RWLock.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334249\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "gfx/src/nsFontMetrics.cpp", "gfx/thebes/FontPaletteCache.cpp", "gfx/thebes/FontPaletteCache.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFontEntry.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.h", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.h", "layout/generic/TextOverflow.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.cpp"], "git_node": "b193e850fbf39925b5dfa8c0f8a741371458ee12", "git_parents": ["c902e251797dbe57645242631242688874e5cc0d"], "node": "3cf315ed0a1da043b87f08a1e465dcb01bab6677", "parents": ["c575f15818d8f1ba59483de61db61cd9de50c161"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1917474 - Add a monochrome launcher icon to Focus. r=jonalmeida,android-reviewers\n\nFocus shares Firefox's logo silhouette, so its themed icon is Fenix's monochrome logo cut out of a disk to\nkeep the two apps distinguishable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334770\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/debug/res/mipmap-anydpi/ic_launcher.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/focusBeta/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/focusBeta/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_round.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi/ic_launcher.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/nightly/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml"], "git_node": "4d07cd443a65460e948f40d77da677f271790bf5", "git_parents": ["b193e850fbf39925b5dfa8c0f8a741371458ee12"], "node": "cc742a38ab681ecad311e5ce72c3e6d5e6605417", "parents": ["3cf315ed0a1da043b87f08a1e465dcb01bab6677"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081270 - Update menu layout when the screen size changes r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nStop using the LocalWindowInfo.current.containerSize cached window size.\nTake the menu height cap from the constraints the popup is measured with,\nwhich reflect the visible frame of the app window on every measure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334213\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/menu/MenuButton.kt"], "git_node": "cc0de95409257f6db37575055894a08c2b9a3389", "git_parents": ["4d07cd443a65460e948f40d77da677f271790bf5"], "node": "d3f835bf9bd1157bda6e32c2333172163aa40799", "parents": ["cc742a38ab681ecad311e5ce72c3e6d5e6605417"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071079 - Tie awesomebar suggestion fetches to the caller's coroutine scope r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nSuggestionFetcher.fetch launched each provider into CoroutineScope(dispatcher),\na scope with a fresh root Job and no parent. The provider coroutines were\ntherefore invisible to the LaunchedEffect that called fetch, so neither a new\nquery nor the awesomebar leaving composition could cancel them. Teardown only\nclosed the dispatcher, which takes the threads away without telling any\ncoroutine to stop.\n\nLaunching the providers inside a supervisorScope makes them children of the\ncaller, so Compose cancels them when the effect restarts or the composition is\ndisposed, and fetchJob is no longer needed. supervisorScope rather than\ncoroutineScope keeps a failing provider from propagating into the composition.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326589\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcher.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcherTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties"], "git_node": "7a72918c725a39e6a3dbcc6089fa7a61b03e77f6", "git_parents": ["cc0de95409257f6db37575055894a08c2b9a3389"], "node": "0901d7a4b7b27d7ff853a084e79001db14aaf4ba", "parents": ["d3f835bf9bd1157bda6e32c2333172163aa40799"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075344 - Add a secret setting and nimbus flag to select the search-config-v3 collection r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334264\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml"], "git_node": "d901f199401a15b3e64131d8692136ceaa4aa628", "git_parents": ["7a72918c725a39e6a3dbcc6089fa7a61b03e77f6"], "node": "e6d978946b078b2c9e181f0eff52dfcfec8636eb", "parents": ["0901d7a4b7b27d7ff853a084e79001db14aaf4ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2071079 - Tie awesomebar suggestion fetches to the caller's coroutine scope r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\" for causing lint failures @SuggestionFetcher.kt.\n\nThis reverts commit 7a72918c725a39e6a3dbcc6089fa7a61b03e77f6.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcher.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcherTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties"], "git_node": "5dbf01e0bb333a59d1963b12c5124e10be1bd3f1", "git_parents": ["d901f199401a15b3e64131d8692136ceaa4aa628"], "node": "714022611c2d9a9d9ce8ccd80077b69d9b0e8af1", "parents": ["e6d978946b078b2c9e181f0eff52dfcfec8636eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072506 - Support CSS random() in InspectorUtils.getComputationSteps. r=devtools-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334899\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css_explainers.js", "layout/inspector/InspectorUtils.cpp", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "9193490cf278d03006a34014860bf8de59bc11b7", "git_parents": ["5dbf01e0bb333a59d1963b12c5124e10be1bd3f1"], "node": "efbda672beed07205260913856e1d64c1342b34f", "parents": ["714022611c2d9a9d9ce8ccd80077b69d9b0e8af1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "R