0e65bef0e67b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025197 - Move AddSecurityState to PWindowGlobal. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331666\n", "files": ["docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp", "docshell/base/WindowContext.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "7454acea5a801eca87a57a2161a09e497c300d9c", "git_parents": ["5291a8142423f4c3db9cf2dc7642b9f0590219c0"], "node": "94e57080c78eaa8fabaa6746b270d3c03a864bf1", "parents": ["1473a1c971062be3f63b9c93d836192d696ab7ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083587 - Bug 2083372 - Reuse NamedNodeMap absence checks for attribute insertion. r=dom-core-reviewers,hsivonen\n\nReuse the absence check made after Trusted Types processing and adoption.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334879\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMAttributeMap.cpp"], "git_node": "e92263e94000d0d226178f0bf35fb068ccbe4d95", "git_parents": ["7454acea5a801eca87a57a2161a09e497c300d9c"], "node": "3501765fa1eb1deb2d399c9383394ca22813a8e7", "parents": ["94e57080c78eaa8fabaa6746b270d3c03a864bf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082047 - Set outermost frame formals after fallible bailout operations. r=iain\n\nThis fixes the issue from bug 2082045.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334459\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2082045.js", "js/src/jit/BaselineBailouts.cpp"], "git_node": "f942d6e6910e20a66e910d2687353163f2eb234a", "git_parents": ["e92263e94000d0d226178f0bf35fb068ccbe4d95"], "node": "855847500e32b7d63aef43a3bd5e80eb3f0d3a66", "parents": ["3501765fa1eb1deb2d399c9383394ca22813a8e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082047 - Move Ion recover instruction cleanup to bailout callers. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334460\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2082047-1.js", "js/src/jit/Bailouts.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineBailouts.cpp", "js/src/vm/JitActivation.cpp"], "git_node": "c5a22b75d6d49c79d75b602fb6c4fe2be9518377", "git_parents": ["f942d6e6910e20a66e910d2687353163f2eb234a"], "node": "36260f171efc4fabb5bbc4d1dc47a183db463b15", "parents": ["855847500e32b7d63aef43a3bd5e80eb3f0d3a66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082047 - Preserve exception state when recover instruction execution fails. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334461\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2082047-2.js", "js/src/jit/JSJitFrameIter.h", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/moz.build", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testJitRInstructionResults.cpp", "js/src/jsapi.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.h"], "git_node": "d1a020277b648296fc64ad9fc44bebd0d2276983", "git_parents": ["c5a22b75d6d49c79d75b602fb6c4fe2be9518377"], "node": "edb73aab18d8b0ae890ea532b2645d6e6cff4eb8", "parents": ["36260f171efc4fabb5bbc4d1dc47a183db463b15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068544 - Parse referrerpolicy on supported elements only. r=emilio,smaug\n\nReferrerpolicy attribute is supported in a (HTML, SVG and MathML), area, img, iframe, script, and link element.\n\nSince we only parse it on suuported elements, we can safely remove\nthe gurad `ReferrerPolicyFromAttribute` in ReferrerInfo.cpp.\n\nA new test verify that referrerpolicy on unsupported elements\nis ignored when passing `document.referrer` and the HTTP header.\n\nA new test verify the ancestorOrigins are not masked when a referrerpolicy\nattribute specified on unsupported elements.\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#referrer-policy-delivery\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328089\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLAnchorElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLAnchorElement.h", "dom/html/HTMLAreaElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLAreaElement.h", "dom/html/HTMLIFrameElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLImageElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLLinkElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLScriptElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/security/ReferrerInfo.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-ancestor-origins-referrerpolicy-unsupported-elements.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-ancestor-origins-referrerpolicy-unsupported-elements.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/referrer-policy/generic/unsupported-elements.html"], "git_node": "ae0838823d2ce08dc14c0fe6c6db4c2c57b6cf78", "git_parents": ["d1a020277b648296fc64ad9fc44bebd0d2276983"], "node": "606f59c100b760fa29af6cefd6524a28a6dcba72", "parents": ["edb73aab18d8b0ae890ea532b2645d6e6cff4eb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083415 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Wait for the frame timeline before the export layout transition. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nPort FFmpeg dc54ec7a0d: switch_layout() must wait the frame dep at\nVK_PIPELINE_STAGE_2_ALL_COMMANDS_BIT so the layout barrier runs after\nthe decode signal instead of racing it (SYNC-HAZARD-WRITE-AFTER-WRITE).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334921\n", "files": ["media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/libavutil/hwcontext_vulkan.c", "media/ffvpx/vulkan-export-layout-wait.patch"], "git_node": "0b7759adab26b16b175e068da93b2c92a453cc76", "git_parents": ["ae0838823d2ce08dc14c0fe6c6db4c2c57b6cf78"], "node": "58fab787f6a041fdf90b831c0528e8b748ba85f3", "parents": ["606f59c100b760fa29af6cefd6524a28a6dcba72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2082400 - Ensure map/set iterator link pointer uses atomic accesses in concurrent marking builds r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\" for causing Bug 2083340\n\nThis reverts commit 7f409ba0a2bd28138eb263c7f7db5cb139fa8e36.\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/OrderedHashTableObject.h", "js/src/vm/NativeObject.h"], "git_node": "c4562fa8b373bb0fbb216f5a315d080e34be49c7", "git_parents": ["0b7759adab26b16b175e068da93b2c92a453cc76"], "node": "9202701ac340f728f815700e5b3f6888d1f0e566", "parents": ["58fab787f6a041fdf90b831c0528e8b748ba85f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079678 - Use inherited CERegistry for parser definition lookup r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334998\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp"], "git_node": "18f2474a41f3e1979d3d1b232bd472817aaf929b", "git_parents": ["c4562fa8b373bb0fbb216f5a315d080e34be49c7"], "node": "fd0e2744d3a882165b5aef112bf79e5ba04d341d", "parents": ["9202701ac340f728f815700e5b3f6888d1f0e566"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071871 - Write summary.jsonl from mozharness's StructuredOutputParser r=ahal\n\nThe harnesses write the task's summary.jsonl themselves, through\n--log-testsummary: each run truncates the file it is given, so mozharness\nhands out one part per run and concatenates them afterwards. That leaves no\nway for mozharness to add records of its own in order, which the next patch\nneeds for the lines of Treeherder's failure summary.\n\nmozharness already receives every raw mozlog record on the harness's stdout.\nApply TestSummaryFormatter to them in StructuredOutputParser and append the\nresult to the task's summary.jsonl, which becomes the file's only writer:\nthe per-run parts and append_test_summary() go away.\n\nThe scripts call parser.finish() instead, whichever parser the suite\ngets, so OutputParser gains a no-op finish(): jittest, which is\nunstructured, gets a DesktopUnittestOutputParser.\n\nSuites opt in with \"test_summary\": True in their definition instead of\npassing --log-testsummary to the harness, and web-platform-tests in the\nscript's default config; mochitest flavors, xpcshell and web-platform-tests\nkeep producing the artifact, with the same records as before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325870\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/android/android_common.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/linux_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/mac_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/win_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/log.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/per_test_base.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_emulator_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_hardware_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_base_log.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_per_test_base.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_structured.py"], "git_node": "e35d82b9cc65a8ba7c58ea74946fdd11921da968", "git_parents": ["18f2474a41f3e1979d3d1b232bd472817aaf929b"], "node": "44aba967e07bc646e0e35859f4c5c58ee23eb5d1", "parents": ["fd0e2744d3a882165b5aef112bf79e5ba04d341d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071871 - Keep Treeherder's failure summary lines in summary.jsonl r=ahal\n\nTreeherder builds a job's Failure Summary by running every task log line\nthrough the ErrorParser heuristics of its log parser. A consumer of\nsummary.jsonl that wants the same lines had to fetch and reparse the whole\nlog.\n\nPort those heuristics into mozharness (TreeherderErrorParser, to be kept\nin sync with treeherder/log_parser/parsers.py). While a\nStructuredOutputParser writes a summary.jsonl, it attaches a logging\nhandler of its own to the mozharness logger, from the first line it\nparses, or from evaluate_parser(), until finish(), and appends an\n\"error_line\" record for every line Treeherder would select, judged from\nthe record's level and message, with the mozharness level and message and\nthe time. mozharness/base/log.py is left alone. Every selected line gets a\nrecord, including lines whose structured record is already in the file, so\nthe error_line records alone reproduce the failure summary. A line logged\nwhile a structured record is being parsed is written after that record;\nany other line is written at once, so a FATAL line, which raises\nSystemExit as soon as it is logged, is kept.\n\nThe records carry no position in the task log: that file belongs to the\nworker, which adds lines of its own, so nothing inside the task can number\nits lines reliably. A consumer holding the log finds a record from its\ntext and its time, which run-task stamps on every line.\n\nCall parser.finish() once the run has been evaluated rather than right\nafter the harness exits, so the ERROR lines evaluate_parser logs (\"No\nchecks run.\", ...) are captured too, and from a finally block, so the\nhandler is removed even when the run raises.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325871\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/structuredlog.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/errors.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_emulator_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/android_hardware_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/web_platform_tests.py", "testing/mozharness/test/python.toml", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_structured.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_testing_errors.py"], "git_node": "ef18b429236691020482dde74a75be5a415e635a", "git_parents": ["e35d82b9cc65a8ba7c58ea74946fdd11921da968"], "node": "e51bb8c0a27be8d416bfc1f480e5fc242373d7ce", "parents": ["44aba967e07bc646e0e35859f4c5c58ee23eb5d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079685 - Keep the stack of every record in TestSummaryFormatter output r=jgraham\n\nThe TBPL formatter prints a log record's stack under its message, and\nmozharness logs each of its lines at the record's level, so the failure\nsummary shows every frame of e.g. an xpcshell unexpected exception, while\nsummary.jsonl only kept the message. The stacks of the other records are\nkept too, so that Treeherder can show them on demand.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331978\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozlog/mozlog/formatters/testsummary.py", "testing/mozbase/mozlog/tests/test_testsummary.py"], "git_node": "7ad43ed6f9e969cb6570c6e554bdd231d94d6c47", "git_parents": ["ef18b429236691020482dde74a75be5a415e635a"], "node": "b3b1cf731d9387e8deb1ba296c72740b6df35c77", "parents": ["e51bb8c0a27be8d416bfc1f480e5fc242373d7ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2025197 - Move AddSecurityState to PWindowGlobal. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\" for causing bc failures @ browser_mixedContentFramesOnHttp.js\n\nThis reverts commit 7454acea5a801eca87a57a2161a09e497c300d9c.\n", "files": ["docshell/base/WindowContext.cpp", "docshell/base/WindowContext.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "6bb463334bda323c61a9985fe2ce12468a6b0a14", "git_parents": ["7ad43ed6f9e969cb6570c6e554bdd231d94d6c47"], "node": "960bcd5be763e5410e8597fb3f039ffd7debd755", "parents": ["b3b1cf731d9387e8deb1ba296c72740b6df35c77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071303 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Skip NVIDIA when nvidia_drm is not loaded. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nBug 2067923 only skipped NVIDIA when modeset was explicitly off. If the\nnvidia_drm module is absent, fopen failed and NVIDIA stayed selectable,\nso multi-GPU setups picked it and failed DMA-BUF export. Treat a missing\nmodeset sysfs node like modeset disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334992\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "f9eeb26e898d4299dd1a669e6adfa80dc5761d2b", "git_parents": ["6bb463334bda323c61a9985fe2ce12468a6b0a14"], "node": "d60af3eb0dea973da7c747d758f8c38c0ac6ee6d", "parents": ["960bcd5be763e5410e8597fb3f039ffd7debd755"], "tags": []}, {"author": "spa5k \u003c79936503+spa5k@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078719 - Clear pending PerformanceObserver entries on disconnect. r=canova\n\nPerformanceObserver::Disconnect() leaves pending entries in mQueuedEntries. A disconnected observer can return those entries through takeRecords() or deliver them after observing again. Clear the queue at the start of Disconnect().\n\nAdd web-platform tests for both cases to po-disconnect.any.js.\n\nPrepared with AI assistance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331189\n", "files": ["dom/performance/PerformanceObserver.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/po-disconnect.any.js"], "git_node": "01a92f94e33db18f5c70be1344c562bfc6564f47", "git_parents": ["f9eeb26e898d4299dd1a669e6adfa80dc5761d2b"], "node": "057574168415abaea46104f4ea7dcd251b0a74bd", "parents": ["d60af3eb0dea973da7c747d758f8c38c0ac6ee6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082365 - Don't panic when a quad segment's device size does not fit in i32. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe nine-patch and tile paths panicked in Size2D::to_i32 when a segment's\ndevice size was NaN or out of i32 range. Skip such segments instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334471\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "5c59f60a9f402a9c9fec075fa1022a4008788128", "git_parents": ["01a92f94e33db18f5c70be1344c562bfc6564f47"], "node": "344e6db99ae818b368d919dbc1f3014b89d84ff0", "parents": ["057574168415abaea46104f4ea7dcd251b0a74bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083613 - Add smoke test annotation to verifyGoogleLensFunctionalityTest UI test r=mbarone\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335064\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/GoogleLensSearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "bb596201cf42cd3287cd0490cabd2783d2f61603", "git_parents": ["5c59f60a9f402a9c9fec075fa1022a4008788128"], "node": "cf4b082227e9c2b3669306c7775504b9de66f17f", "parents": ["344e6db99ae818b368d919dbc1f3014b89d84ff0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080609 - Clean up nsWindow::ConstrainPosition. r=gtk-reviewers,stransky\n\nThis is drive-by but I was looking at this code and it can be simpler.\n\nNo behavior change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334976\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "6195dc321cf717ce7d24f2761b421a59b5d12827", "git_parents": ["bb596201cf42cd3287cd0490cabd2783d2f61603"], "node": "3b0008a481a034964f4850b7e8cc106e484cb50d", "parents": ["cf4b082227e9c2b3669306c7775504b9de66f17f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \