nch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080829 - avoid shutdown hang even if GetWindowDesktopId() hangs r=win-reviewers,handyman\n\nCall GetWindowDesktopId() on a named thread and don't want for it at\nshutdown if a request is still pending.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334323\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/ThreadAllows.txt", "widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.h", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWorkspaceID.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "64eaf3f73eaec3434571568862870d81bab10ffd", "git_parents": ["33baf660c52948e6255ebb6bc71f6067ed95ad93"], "node": "4d41ae7bbcb4ebd5852e9246371c8cfa1498db5a", "parents": ["65b729021c644b1e2c50f3b18e88ab4be0cdbd3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Franchuk \u003cafranchuk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082537 - Derive the crashreporter Glean app id in a more general way r=crashreporting-reviewers,gsvelto\n\nThis looks for \"firefox\" and \"thunderbird\" prefixes and shortens the app\nname to those. For good measure, we compare with the lowercase version\nof the string.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334257\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/client/app/src/glean.rs"], "git_node": "8b2a91065298838914470c6382f8b621b54a96d4", "git_parents": ["64eaf3f73eaec3434571568862870d81bab10ffd"], "node": "959fc30a44a6fa13f141de3f05249704b3b69f87", "parents": ["4d41ae7bbcb4ebd5852e9246371c8cfa1498db5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083831 - Remove the version 160 guard on New Tab topsites.click and pocket.click extra keys. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335290\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_context_menu_link_open.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "81d10bcd8ec58cced8e1bab6b877527277054a62", "git_parents": ["8b2a91065298838914470c6382f8b621b54a96d4"], "node": "5b0bba2e7ff08246db17f5af2f4e1c866d0789a0", "parents": ["959fc30a44a6fa13f141de3f05249704b3b69f87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080200 [Wayland] Split nsWindowWayland to nsWindowWaylandToplevel / nsWindowWaylandPopup r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nSeparated nsWindowWaylandPopup class allows us to implement xdg-popup based wayland popups and use xdg-positioner directly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332419\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindow.h", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "a3e3a16db84f52d967d1b8e9913bd32dda992f7a", "git_parents": ["81d10bcd8ec58cced8e1bab6b877527277054a62"], "node": "85288d0f3114b5e4962a1d3fd5a0e32467195ae5", "parents": ["5b0bba2e7ff08246db17f5af2f4e1c866d0789a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings ct-logs r=release-managers,dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335308\n", "files": ["security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-telemetry-v2.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "a5da7048d731b91f031fae2aa87e8ca25940303b", "git_parents": ["a3e3a16db84f52d967d1b8e9913bd32dda992f7a"], "node": "0d914fbf3ffd92194d2deda64996dd8b0dd3e166", "parents": ["85288d0f3114b5e4962a1d3fd5a0e32467195ae5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081319 - Update search engine tests. r=jteow,remote-settings-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333400\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/searchconfigs/test_searchconfig.js"], "git_node": "da38e7b9104ff28310bba23966707bde1aa69686", "git_parents": ["a5da7048d731b91f031fae2aa87e8ca25940303b"], "node": "387a528ffd2e4cf1ef3fb82511ac8331b15d814c", "parents": ["0d914fbf3ffd92194d2deda64996dd8b0dd3e166"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083134 - Allow callers that pass EXPIRE_POLICY to remove EXPIRE_POLICY permissions. r=emz,permissions-reviewers\n\nThe enterprise policy engine needs to remove the permissions it sets while\nthe browser is running. Other callers stay blocked.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334704\n", "files": ["extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp", "extensions/permissions/test/unit/test_permmanager_policy.js", "extensions/permissions/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "netwerk/base/nsIPermissionManager.idl"], "git_node": "424b60ca8e30ca6fd0d3dcf2572eb9ffaa7a4a85", "git_parents": ["da38e7b9104ff28310bba23966707bde1aa69686"], "node": "488af7b4984e071d99c2ce37b04793752bd9a3c7", "parents": ["387a528ffd2e4cf1ef3fb82511ac8331b15d814c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2076441 - Treat a deferred session with no windows or saved groups as nothing to restore. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sthompson\" for causing marionette test failure.\n\nThis reverts commit ff3589c8ab05cce511c4fa8482293202c53cb040.\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/manifest.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/marionette/test_deferred_nothing_to_restore.py"], "git_node": "c46f4716258a38ebfdb336ab89ab9194aee8dc47", "git_parents": ["424b60ca8e30ca6fd0d3dcf2572eb9ffaa7a4a85"], "node": "05e2fbbcb93231a9503cff31fc39b23d3ff4fa70", "parents": ["488af7b4984e071d99c2ce37b04793752bd9a3c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082327 - Annotate a crashtest as an expected timeout.\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/selectors/crashtests/chrome-bug-565742178.html.ini"], "git_node": "722d356d8a72eb37a8f6d02da001e61a76a15ab9", "git_parents": ["c46f4716258a38ebfdb336ab89ab9194aee8dc47"], "node": "90dab5aba36a031341741695f3880be09044584b", "parents": ["05e2fbbcb93231a9503cff31fc39b23d3ff4fa70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082327 - Enable inline use event handlers on a mochitest.\n", "files": ["js/xpconnect/tests/mochitest/test_bug993423.html"], "git_node": "436d7014805933eecd50f0fd6b9b6e7cc63fffbb", "git_parents": ["722d356d8a72eb37a8f6d02da001e61a76a15ab9"], "node": "09002fcc8447fa72ac68b98a1b080e3da1239028", "parents": ["90dab5aba36a031341741695f3880be09044584b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083284 - Report the missing id in the remaining WebRender scene-builder map lookup panics. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nFollow-up to bug 1782001, covering define_clip_chain, push_clip_chain,\npush_clip_id, build_for_tile_cache and get_spatial_node_index, so these\ncrashes report the id and the defined count instead of\n\"no entry found for key\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335002\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs"], "git_node": "30e66c60d822e1a8d5c7a8eda2c1b354dbd0ea49", "git_parents": ["436d7014805933eecd50f0fd6b9b6e7cc63fffbb"], "node": "4d61675d7d7d9795e72aaf656820e7edb2a275d7", "parents": ["09002fcc8447fa72ac68b98a1b080e3da1239028"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lola_t \u003cltokhtamuradova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067135 - Support adaptive screens. Correct/add error state colours. r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333675\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/slider/Slider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/AudioProgressBar.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/ListenSheet.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayPauseButton.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlaybackControls.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayerCompact.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/PlayerExpanded.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/AudioProgressBarTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/ListenSheetTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/icons/src/main/res/drawable/mozac_ic_pause_fill_24.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/icons/src/main/res/drawable/mozac_ic_playback_rewind_24.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/listentopage/ListenSheetIntegration.kt"], "git_node": "a662c866ea52d9f10677c00e4e5cf21dd83005a2", "git_parents": ["30e66c60d822e1a8d5c7a8eda2c1b354dbd0ea49"], "node": "cabca09ced51ee1264368552fb9930bcd2669ad4", "parents": ["4d61675d7d7d9795e72aaf656820e7edb2a275d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081865 - Allow disabling widgets during activation window r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334586\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/docs/v2-system-addon/activation-window.md", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_activation_window.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js"], "git_node": "06eb195ae1728013418ec3ce2e233014a497ed22", "git_parents": ["a662c866ea52d9f10677c00e4e5cf21dd83005a2"], "node": "c6922662998c968b9bb32aa4f8a1318c17c8790d", "parents": ["cabca09ced51ee1264368552fb9930bcd2669ad4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082170 - response card style updates r=gcardieri\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334376\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-tool-ui/aitab-tool-ui.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-tool-ui/aitab-tool-ui.mjs"], "git_node": "eae4e321c1b394e605f4fb4d5e27a68b619bd3a4", "git_parents": ["06eb195ae1728013418ec3ce2e233014a497ed22"], "node": "bd1ee47210ac1fa99de8b2f8e1963db13a290ae5", "parents": ["c6922662998c968b9bb32aa4f8a1318c17c8790d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Rae Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@berkeley.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1778220 - Recompute the hittesting point from scratch when zooming instead of relying on getContentBoundsForDOMElm r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie\n\nWhen running these tests in an iframe, both the iframe (document and\nframe) as well as the iframe's content will be affected by zoom. Our\ntraditional `hitTest(...)` method relies on getContentBoundsForDOMElm\nwhich recomputes the position of content within its document, as well as\nthe iframe document's own screen position. This computation is done\nentirely within the iframe's content process, using `mozInnerScreen[X|Y]`\nvars to get the iframe document's screen position. This happens once at\nthe top of the function, outside any `untilCache` check.\n\nThis function is intermittently wrong about the iframe's own position,\nsometimes it reports the iframe's old (non-zoomed) location, and\nsometimes it reports the iframe's true zoomed position. These\n`mozInnerScreen*` values seem to come from\n`BrowserChild::GetChildToParentConversionMatrix`, and\nI don't see a clean way to await their update in JS.\n\nInstead, this patch creates a new getScreenPos function which manually\nwalks the content \u003e iframe \u003e top level doc chain and computes position.\nWe still compute the content node's position inside the iframe in the\niframe's content process, but we no longer fetch screen coordinates for the iframe's\ndocument there\nInstead, in the top-level doc's content process where the iframe is\nembedded, we compute its position in the top-level doc and add this\nvalue (along with the doc's screen position) to the content node's\nposition.\n\nI've made this change in a test-local method instead of in the general\n`hitTest` function because I think this should only be relevant when\nzooming, and I don't want to cause more disruption.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333025\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/hittest/browser_test_zoom.js"], "git_node": "01401cf9c888fcd0d78f59338ee0e5fab70238e3", "git_parents": ["eae4e321c1b394e605f4fb4d5e27a68b619bd3a4"], "node": "156d0cdccdc1b7c4a1f8aed854a7302e32bade23", "parents": ["bd1ee47210ac1fa99de8b2f8e1963db13a290ae5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Rae Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@berkeley.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082695: Update phabricator review guidance in accessibility review docs r=Jamie\n\nThis patch also adds information about our platform review group, so folks searching don't confuse it for the now-defunct frontend review group.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334774\n", "files": ["docs/bug-mgmt/processes/accessibility-review.md"], "git_node": "13240fa7a48ea80a45051a2ae63084979942ee10", "git_parents": ["01401cf9c888fcd0d78f59338ee0e5fab70238e3"], "node": "dd0ea9f3272953913e1060b1f7efc425950ac5a5", "parents": ["156d0cdccdc1b7c4a1f8aed854a7302e32bade23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082468: Change the source repo for evolve r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nthe other domain is regurally overloaded, the same\nchange was made in\nhttps://hg-edge.mozilla.org/hgcustom/version-control-tools/rev/11de14db3752d0dfbcd7315e5d60051dfd477c99\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334317\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/updatebot/setup.sh"], "git_node": "ff5943c44e6869902a192f07f2275a98b7fef5c4", "git_parents": ["13240fa7a48ea80a45051a2ae63084979942ee10"], "node": "3d112fa619c0c336e966b4b60719a136bc1039ce", "parents": ["dd0ea9f3272953913e1060b1f7efc425950ac5a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082468: Bump updatebot to get new python deps and a bug title fix r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334318\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/updatebot/updatebot-version.sh"], "git_node": "50599c342bec04a90966cd6bea9a75356b8154c0", "git_parents": ["ff5943c44e6869902a192f07f2275a98b7fef5c4"], "node": "e347ec420e6665965e04a397ca1f5df64e7ee803", "parents": ["3d112fa619c0c336e966b4b60719a136bc1039ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082648: Fix libjpeg's update script r=tnikkel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334319\n", "files": ["media/libjpeg/update.py"], "git_node": "5efe4a316ac2ee6c170da34f30628268738fd310", "git_parents": ["50599c342bec04a90966cd6bea9a75356b8154c0"], "node": "40fe8e3c5d667e1768493c227a41a930019cc173", "parents": ["e347ec420e6665965e04a397ca1f5df64e7ee803"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082588 - Bubble up AITab content errors to chat with per-error guidance. r=omarg,tliu,mzhang\n\nWhen the generation model cannot or should not build a page (no usable\ncontent, an impossible edit, a request it refuses), it now returns\n{\"error\": \"...\"} instead of a surface. That message is sanitized with\nsanitizeUntrustedContent, reported to telemetry as content_related, and passed\non to the chat model to surface to the user.\n\nEach AITab error code now carries guidance telling the chat model what to do\nnext (retry with different input, ask the user, offer a new page, or stop).\nCodes without guidance fall back to a generic internal error message, so codes\nadded later default to safe text.\n\nThe tool result now reports the page as `page: {slug}`, dropping the unused\nversion uuid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334252\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_tool_ui.js"], "git_node": "37d6f88a1c67c5e3e415fc3bbd7fc5e40daf33c1", "git_parents": ["5efe4a316ac2ee6c170da34f30628268738fd310"], "node": "6a18cf3adcc92963e1754c43de99789d9bdc9343", "parents": ["40fe8e3c5d667e1768493c227a41a930019cc173"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083226 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Split video-caps query out of VulkanCanDecodeFormat. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nRefactor so CheckDecodeCapabilities runs the video-caps query. Use VulkanProbeFormat instead of H264VulkanProbeFormat, preserving previous behavior (bug 2063809: VulkanCanDecodeFormat only applies the FFmpeg \u003c n7.1 COINCIDE-without-SEPARATE_REFERENCE_IMAGES skip). This allows other functions to use the decode caps.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334917\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "e54432c538930ece0c5e93462fae3747868c97cd", "git_parents": ["37d6f88a1c67c5e3e415fc3bbd7fc5e40daf33c1"], "node": "e9aaabf9364ae277566aeb2e368d2b06329edfb4", "parents": ["6a18cf3adcc92963e1754c43de99789d9bdc9343"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083226 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Strip output DPB usage on pre-63.8.101 libavcodec when the driver reports DISTINCT. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nlibavcodec before 63.8.101 uses dedicated_dpb = !COINCIDE, so VIDEO_DECODE_DPB is on the output whenever COINCIDE is advertised, including when DISTINCT is also set. From 63.8.101 libavcodec uses dedicated_dpb = DISTINCT. Copy hwfc-\u003eusage on new lavc; on older lavc set DPB only if the driver does not report DISTINCT.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334918\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "7f998472474b0f3ea7388398e20f04a1049b5880", "git_parents": ["e54432c538930ece0c5e93462fae3747868c97cd"], "node": "e3569715c1608f342ce9c85af6c10b538bd3b558", "parents": ["e9aaabf9364ae277566aeb2e368d2b06329edfb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083737 - Add a per-tab IPP site rule provider r=ip-protection-reviewers,rking\n\nIPPTabRuleProvider holds a rule for every site in one tab, set with\nsetTabRule(rule, browserId), until the tab closes. Tab rules take precedence\nover the global ones.\n\nThe channel filter passes the channel's browserId to getRule().\n\nWe can use this i.e in Error Pages to let the Tab continue without VPN\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335195\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPChannelFilter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPSiteRuleManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPSiteRuleProviders.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/docs/Components.md", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/head.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPChannelFilter.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPSiteRuleManager.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPTabRuleProvider.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "4921623200d12c8409fb2282b43ed619488f995a", "git_parents": ["7f998472474b0f3ea7388398e20f04a1049b5880"], "node": "d883ad42f1013fa317467c8f5dbcdc4f0aa53912", "parents": ["e3569715c1608f342ce9c85af6c10b538bd3b558"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078462 - Intern rectangles in the display list builder r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe first interned type, plus the machinery every primitive type shares.\nPrimitive keys hold the prim rect, local clip rect and flags, so an item is\nonly its spatial id, clip chain and handle, and the scene builder places the\ninstance from a PrimPlacement store (add_dl_prim). The two ids stay on the\nitem because content numbers them per build.\n\nSince an item no longer carries what its shadow copy needs, primitives pushed\nin a shadow scope record a CapturedKey that the desugar interns copies from.\nA handle-less rectangle in a finished list is a transparent checkerboard,\nkept only for its tile cache barrier.\n\nA fresh builder re-mints every uid, so an identical list from a new builder\nrepaints; test_invalidation covers it. wrshell's capture writer now emits\nplaceholder bounds and colour.\n\nA removed pipeline's namespace is released by the scene build of the\ndocument that removed it, or by any build once that document is deleted.\nThe render backend holds a document's ops while it has no scene to swap, so\na release from another document's build could overtake the namespace's open.\n\nNamespaces are keyed by document and pipeline. Windows can share a render\nbackend, and so a scene builder, and a tab moved to another window sends\ndisplay lists to the new window's document before the old one's low priority\nRemovePipeline arrives. Keyed by pipeline alone, that removal released the\nnamespace the new document was using, and its close could overtake the open\nthe render backend was still holding for the new document.\n\nContent's builder survives its pipeline moving to another window, which\nreleases the pipeline in the old document, so WrUpdated replaces the builder\nand the next display list starts a fresh delta stream in a fresh namespace.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330955\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/test_invalidation.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "b90be128e56ff8222711adf9b00a80c0b8cfe039", "git_parents": ["4921623200d12c8409fb2282b43ed619488f995a"], "node": "2a53f18f1858af74baea0b5e6edf9fd5b8bbab40", "parents": ["d883ad42f1013fa317467c8f5dbcdc4f0aa53912"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David \u003ctamasdavidlaszlo@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1583480 - Only use GetMessageExtraInfo() bits as a pointerId when the tablet signature is present. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nWinUtils::GetMousePointerID() returned GetMessageExtraInfo() & 0x7F for every\nmouse message. That value is only a tablet cursor id when the extra info\ncarries the Windows tablet signature (0xFF515700).\n\nWith Windows Ink disabled, some tablet drivers (observed with Wacom) send the\npen as plain mouse messages. Their extra info has no tablet signature, and\nthe low bits change on nearly every message, resembling a counter. With no\nWM_POINTER* info available, nsWindow::DispatchMouseEvent fell back to that\nvalue, so PointerEvent.pointerId changed on almost every pointermove and\ndiffered between pointerdown and pointerup.\n\nReturn 0 (the mouse id) when the signature is absent, so only messages that\nactually carry a tablet cursor id use those bits.\n\nWith Ink disabled, such a pen is still reported as pointerType \"mouse\", since\nthe driver does not mark its messages as pen. This patch does not change that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334900\n", "files": ["widget/windows/WinUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "de3ab6f09b13748aafda58261864f66a1bd82d2d", "git_parents": ["b90be128e56ff8222711adf9b00a80c0b8cfe039"], "node": "b255c399775490e8e2dd00abf52e187c16184762", "parents": ["2a53f18f1858af74baea0b5e6edf9fd5b8bbab40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge Mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": [], "git_node": "ead265890d9c618cfe989328b6f4108f3e029ae1", "git_parents": ["de3ab6f09b13748aafda58261864f66a1bd82d2d", "fc216bdbdf04fca964b8f241844b0e6d048cc245"], "node": "c923cab08882358f16b0e7330e7fc8c5bc93a50c", "parents": ["b255c399775490e8e2dd00abf52e187c16184762", "3d4ee3ed50eec93899d6c763154bb3c25457a439"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036626 - Only mark private temporary downloads read-only when they are kept in the temp directory, r=mak\n\nWe missed this when we defaulted to starting downloads in the downloads directory.\n\nPrevious context includes bug 1009465 where we started marking files read-only,\nand bug 1790641 which stopped deleting these files for everyone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323214\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/downloads/DownloadIntegration.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/downloads/test/unit/common_test_Download.js"], "git_node": "08a2e2dfba5e0e7a88177e177bd532ba4052ce70", "git_parents": ["ead265890d9c618cfe989328b6f4108f3e029ae1"], "node": "6df3fdd2ff620404656ec5bedda42207b87542d1", "parents": ["c923cab08882358f16b0e7330e7fc8c5bc93a50c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083315 - Improvements for sidebar expand on hover view transitions r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335340\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "dce045bde97c47921eb04e7fbdbad0f14120967e", "git_parents": ["08a2e2dfba5e0e7a88177e177bd532ba4052ce70"], "node": "b6a85d7783193ed8f25c63986971287cf3efee66", "parents": ["6df3fdd2ff620404656ec5bedda42207b87542d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083824 - Fix IntersectionObserver bucketting. r=perftest-reviewers,aglavic DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335287\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browser_function_labels.toml"], "git_node": "64173a675594c52b40c0df4341ae3c65452dd5a1", "git_parents": ["dce045bde97c47921eb04e7fbdbad0f14120967e"], "node": "352d78e33959a7a99212aaf2b86b387fd8cc2180", "parents": ["b6a85d7783193ed8f25c63986971287cf3efee66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083401 - Update profile label matcher for CSS2Properties -\u003e CSSStyleProperties rename. r=canova,perftest-reviewers,aglavic DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334910\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browser_function_labels.toml"], "git_node": "cf03f06e330a331944ea3ac1cf4f4d0c7d9b594a", "git_parents": ["64173a675594c52b40c0df4341ae3c65452dd5a1"], "node": "cf5b4973f759ead30086514b6271ebb7afd6b870", "parents": ["352d78e33959a7a99212aaf2b86b387fd8cc2180"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081108 - Run the repackage-signing-shippable-l10n-msix kind on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDrop `run-on-repo-type: [hg]` so the kind schedules on git-backed pushes\nlike the other repackage-signing kinds that landed under this bug. The task\nis a scriptworker signing task, nothing to clone.\n\nVerified on an hg try staging release build phase with the release kind\nguards removed (push 2067983, 116 tasks all green), which ran\nrepackage-signing-shippable-l10n-msix on win64 next to the other\nrepackage-signing kinds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335077\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/repackage-signing-shippable-l10n-msix/kind.yml"], "git_node": "f268ef565341d8eab7a62171e977523e76f48c51", "git_parents": ["cf03f06e330a331944ea3ac1cf4f4d0c7d9b594a"], "node": "566222744e99d744e541093fa8a4a07099f1085e", "parents": ["cf5b4973f759ead30086514b6271ebb7afd6b870"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083657 - Run the release source, checksums, update-verify-config, bouncer-check and Linux repackage kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDrop `run-on-repo-type: [hg]` and `clone-with: hg` from release-source,\nrelease-generate-checksums, release-update-verify-config(-next),\nrelease-bouncer-check, repackage-deb, repackage-flatpak and repackage-rpm,\nso these promotion tasks schedule on git-backed pushes.\n\nrelease-source and release-generate-checksums now clone the GitHub mirror.\nThe update-verify-config, bouncer-check and repackage transforms still set\n`clone-with: hg` themselves, so for those kinds this change is about\nscheduling only; their checkout switches when the transforms drop the pin,\nas for the repackage kinds that landed under bug 2081108.\n\nTested on try:\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=305a0baea676b1779307fd73801957a786a89443\nrelease-source-firefox-source built its tarball from the Git checkout, and\nrepackage-deb, repackage-flatpak and repackage-rpm on linux64-shippable are\ngreen. release-update-verify-config fails on every platform while still\ncloning with hg: it compares the try nightly version with the last\nwatershed and hits a TypeError, a try environment problem unrelated to\nthis change. release-bouncer-check and release-generate-checksums depend on\nrelease tasks that cannot run at level 1, so they stayed unscheduled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335139\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-bouncer-check/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-generate-checksums/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-source/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-verify-config-next/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-update-verify-config/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-deb/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-flatpak/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/repackage-rpm/kind.yml"], "git_node": "eddcf3a514e5f25df7155d860a948fff52dfccf8", "git_parents": ["f268ef565341d8eab7a62171e977523e76f48c51"], "node": "46c0232f3bd41e7fa0be4e8fdd242403d329065f", "parents": ["566222744e99d744e541093fa8a4a07099f1085e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083169 - update chatbot scout url r=omarg\n\nuse the url from yahoo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334735\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "07529c9b8cf5e47bec89bee5c783e3dcfa80fc5b", "git_parents": ["eddcf3a514e5f25df7155d860a948fff52dfccf8"], "node": "ea08a2f0f85e50ab59911ee693e7595f31ef6b04", "parents": ["46c0232f3bd41e7fa0be4e8fdd242403d329065f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083781: schedule release graphs at high priority regardless of branch r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335193\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/release_promotion.py"], "git_node": "fdb59ddd8c5ec7b9ce993e11bc314f448cf96a02", "git_parents": ["07529c9b8cf5e47bec89bee5c783e3dcfa80fc5b"], "node": "16cc851e2c82ce65fdf8f571aa6bec94c6aa8ac9", "parents": ["ea08a2f0f85e50ab59911ee693e7595f31ef6b04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082887 - Remove non-Nova UI Widgets tests r=hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335264\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome-nova.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/moz.build", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/chrome-nova.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/chrome.toml"], "git_node": "cf70795e1abb0b3eb7520b137d79648b833865c5", "git_parents": ["fdb59ddd8c5ec7b9ce993e11bc314f448cf96a02"], "node": "39b0141d943ba1df01ea04bfe02560b2145bea45", "parents": ["16cc851e2c82ce65fdf8f571aa6bec94c6aa8ac9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083450 - Use IsKnownNewAttr explicitly in SetAttr(). r=webidl,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin,smaug\n\nIn particular the parsers know that these are fresh, and some internal\ncallers do as well like anonymous content and so on.\n\nShould also make the fresh ID setter a bit faster for example, since we\ntrack its presence via flags.\n\nI checked the content sinks and expat does reject dupe attributes, and\nHTML parser does too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334922\n", "files": ["accessible/html/HTMLSelectAccessible.cpp", "dom/base/AnonymousContent.cpp", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Element.h", "dom/base/Link.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMTokenList.cpp", "dom/base/nsTreeSanitizer.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLDetailsElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLOptionElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "dom/html/ImageDocument.cpp", "dom/html/MediaDocument.cpp", "dom/html/TextControlElement.cpp", "dom/html/VideoDocument.cpp", "dom/html/nsDOMStringMap.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.h", "dom/l10n/DOMLocalization.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLElement.cpp", "dom/prototype/PrototypeDocumentContentSink.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGAnimatedClass.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGElement.cpp", "dom/svg/SVGScriptElement.cpp", "dom/xml/nsXMLContentSink.cpp", "dom/xslt/xslt/txMozillaTextOutput.cpp", "dom/xslt/xslt/txMozillaXMLOutput.cpp", "dom/xul/XULBroadcastManager.cpp", "dom/xul/XULButtonElement.cpp", "dom/xul/XULMenuParentElement.cpp", "dom/xul/XULPersist.cpp", "dom/xul/XULPopupElement.cpp", "dom/xul/XULTextElement.h", "dom/xul/XULTooltipElement.cpp", "dom/xul/nsXULSortService.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorDOMAPIWrapper.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLAnonymousNodeEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorObjectResizer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLTableEditor.cpp", "layout/base/AccessibleCaret.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/forms/nsColorControlFrame.cpp", "layout/forms/nsFileControlFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsCanvasFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsFrameSetFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsVideoFrame.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/StylePropertyMap.cpp", "layout/xul/nsMenuPopupFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsScrollbarFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsSplitterFrame.cpp", "layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp", "layout/xul/nsXULTooltipListener.cpp", "layout/xul/tree/nsTreeContentView.cpp", "layout/xul/tree/nsTreeUtils.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/duplicate-attr-constructor-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/duplicate-attr-constructor-crash.xhtml", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuX.mm", "widget/gtk/NativeMenuGtk.cpp"], "git_node": "8651fef044a8e719332eee62d4e5bfc3a30d8ea4", "git_parents": ["cf70795e1abb0b3eb7520b137d79648b833865c5"], "node": "b7222302be08655c56678d3c121ef99959c240c7", "parents": ["39b0141d943ba1df01ea04bfe02560b2145bea45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tin La \u003ctinsila1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071323 Dedupe cancel.py between gecko_taskgraph and taskgraph r=ahal,taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335045\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/cancel.py"], "git_node": "352c9fa24bc5c871d84c49f90576cb2950c57d8f", "git_parents": ["8651fef044a8e719332eee62d4e5bfc3a30d8ea4"], "node": "cf668d5cfbde6c7d2523064ae11d01e9b9554534", "parents": ["b7222302be08655c56678d3c121ef99959c240c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Finn Terdal \u003cfterdal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074918 - Give the card stack a single solid border in high contrast modes r=omc-reviewers,emcminn\n\nIn high contrast modes, the generic multistage `.main-content` border was\ndrawn inside the card stack, as a divider between the illustration and the\ntext and as an inner box in the stacked layout. This patch removes that\nborder for the card stack, and under prefers-contrast gives the front and\nback cards a solid text-color border instead of the default low-contrast one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334263\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "6f3f9df8ec95a754f5fe4ea3716fbd95a98d22b5", "git_parents": ["352c9fa24bc5c871d84c49f90576cb2950c57d8f"], "node": "dead2e5cd2c5d621e4e1b7cbf7e4767bc9b2a22c", "parents": ["cf668d5cfbde6c7d2523064ae11d01e9b9554534"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075294 - [HNT] Load synced tabs in the current homepage tab instead of a new tab. r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- When homepage as a new tab is enabled, loading a synced tab from the tab manager will load in the selected about:home tab.\n- Open a new tab when any other tab is selected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335198\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/TabManagerController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/DefaultTabManagerControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "fa84b5d6c4ece842583a483e9ff1b20ddc1ba80d", "git_parents": ["6f3f9df8ec95a754f5fe4ea3716fbd95a98d22b5"], "node": "3c1ebc123872fb8113420a46211f46d044866406", "parents": ["dead2e5cd2c5d621e4e1b7cbf7e4767bc9b2a22c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048794: Create browser.toolbars.tab-groups.enabled to gate Tab Groups toolbar button r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310861\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableWidgets.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml"], "git_node": "095d5c587459a30b2966ba4a853f01e8c2b32760", "git_parents": ["fa84b5d6c4ece842583a483e9ff1b20ddc1ba80d"], "node": "db9bcfe4e06b71c5f77873326681d437c2e4a919", "parents": ["3c1ebc123872fb8113420a46211f46d044866406"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeremy Swinarton \u003cjswinarton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048790: Turn on browser.tabs.groups.alternateMenu by default in Nightly r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310862\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_group_menu.js"], "git_node": "6ca86fb8bf076987da008dbba75835d16e111fcb", "git_parents": ["095d5c587459a30b2966ba4a853f01e8c2b32760"], "node": "3db73ebd4f3c0c54516d5a3340ba56092e0af205", "parents": ["db9bcfe4e06b71c5f77873326681d437c2e4a919"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083084 - Make the Google Lens setting discoverable in settings search. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334710\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/SettingsSearchProviders.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/search/GoogleLensSettingsSearchProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/search/GoogleLensSettingsSearchProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "72ade1ddee9ec67ce7d75963e6ce70a87399d1b1", "git_parents": ["6ca86fb8bf076987da008dbba75835d16e111fcb"], "node": "98a735c19ff02fc132ecf3bd082abe9b1ec2f19a", "parents": ["3db73ebd4f3c0c54516d5a3340ba56092e0af205"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083805 - Scroll to and highlight settings search results in SearchEngineFragment. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335291\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/search/SearchEngineFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml"], "git_node": "242748166de028a0b532f67e69f7dc7460cb94f6", "git_parents": ["72ade1ddee9ec67ce7d75963e6ce70a87399d1b1"], "node": "f4cf900e7f315c83c6a0264a038ece29335c1407", "parents": ["98a735c19ff02fc132ecf3bd082abe9b1ec2f19a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083254 - Drop redundant Focus resource qualifiers and dead resources. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nminSdkVersion is 26, so the -v24, -v25 and -v26 qualifiers always match and the unqualified\nic_splash_screen.webp files they shadowed never load. For the same reason the adaptive ic_launcher always wins\nover the density-bucket PNGs beside it, and the focusBeta copy of it is identical to main's. The klarNightly\nfolders outside res/ were never part of that source set, the manifest has no roundIcon, and nothing references\nicon_foreground or background_gradient_dark.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334856\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/beta/res/drawable-v24/ic_splash_screen.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/beta/res/drawable/ic_splash_screen.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/beta/res/drawable/ic_splash_screen.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/fo