k\n- One startup per file since SessionStartup and CrashMonitor can only initialize once\n- Add asserts for all_files_corrupt in the existing session file read tests\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334754\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/head.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_glean_backup_can_be_loaded.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_shutdown_success_final_write_incomplete.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_shutdown_success_no_checkpoints.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_shutdown_success_stopped_state.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_startup_nosession_async.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/test_startup_session_async.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "57139a0f2d089a41c2065622f462b37817cdf51c", "git_parents": ["18dd1a81f1de8e749600f9a5a1be34a038da7f46"], "node": "b45f4820cce357ff6055f89cb12c350fff3c44d6", "parents": ["5c277d54065b05f6ae7058f77623befcd7878c72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078028 - Fix browser.sidebarAction.setTitle() leaves the open sidebar header stale r=sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nEnsure that when an extension sets the panel header, the new title is reflected in the revamped sidebar view.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335205\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_extensions_sidebar.js", "testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "046071ee958028a3d39aa29b59574099c2698365", "git_parents": ["57139a0f2d089a41c2065622f462b37817cdf51c"], "node": "1a493daed6c9b983cf57479b7ec9c5738aab5f74", "parents": ["b45f4820cce357ff6055f89cb12c350fff3c44d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059197 - Add Glean telemetry for the Smart Window sidebar.openByDefault pref. r=settings-reviewers,flozia,mconley\n\nThe change event is recorded from a pref observer in SmartWindowTelemetry, so it covers every way the pref can change (the settings checkbox, the sidebar auto-open callout and about:config) without touching those surfaces.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334670\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartWindowTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_sidebar_auto_open_pref_prompt.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_smart_window_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "7336268804b04c192ddc3ec062be081b101abee1", "git_parents": ["046071ee958028a3d39aa29b59574099c2698365"], "node": "7fa220eb8a8e303034eb0ba6977f31200518df13", "parents": ["1a493daed6c9b983cf57479b7ec9c5738aab5f74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082859 - Split test_extensionsettings.js so each file fits the 30s xpcshell timeout, r=mkaply.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335332\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensionsettings.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensionsettings_private_browsing.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensionsettings_runtime_blocked_hosts.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensionsettings_update_url.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "63040b69c728137b7effd7355445f784743876e4", "git_parents": ["7336268804b04c192ddc3ec062be081b101abee1"], "node": "d425082c48b14dc9fdf48bc4364600436789e526", "parents": ["7fa220eb8a8e303034eb0ba6977f31200518df13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083843 - Wait for async policy callbacks before notifying EnterprisePolicies:AllPoliciesApplied on restart, r=mkaply.\n\nThis changes when setupPolicyEngineWithJson resolves for every test that calls it. Real startup is unaffected because only test helpers observe AllPoliciesApplied.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335334\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f8fdd23a632bab01498315427ec43d5ee31c7fc1", "git_parents": ["63040b69c728137b7effd7355445f784743876e4"], "node": "04f4aab6f92bb601597232f40cd0715f219c45b8", "parents": ["d425082c48b14dc9fdf48bc4364600436789e526"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080958 - Show the text selection menu only for a selection the user made. r=ngrato\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo test manually, set `browser.highlightToSearch.featureGate` to true,\nclick a page element that selects its text for you, such as a\nclick-to-select code block, and confirm the menu does not appear. Then\ndrag across some text, or double-click a word, and confirm it does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333036\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAIChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_paste_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "84378bf46c7c802f3baf6b9ebd2dddfb9221d3cf", "git_parents": ["f8fdd23a632bab01498315427ec43d5ee31c7fc1"], "node": "330cf5e60eb71a4f4f8f897bb501ac5acf9d0e5f", "parents": ["04f4aab6f92bb601597232f40cd0715f219c45b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082943 - Don't let queued per-window idle tasks keep closed browser windows alive. r=Gijs,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers\n\nBug 2052772 moved the per-window idle tasks from the window's requestIdleCallback to ChromeUtils.idleDispatch, whose pending runnables keep the window alive until they run. Go back to the window's idle queue, which is dropped when the window closes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334827\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "toolkit/modules/BrowserUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_BrowserUtils_idle_window_leak.js"], "git_node": "1b4dbd497aa62ed9c7766bef94f7039fccbf2e98", "git_parents": ["84378bf46c7c802f3baf6b9ebd2dddfb9221d3cf"], "node": "09f1c94df79c89f7ba0e53a3884e3e4a79365487", "parents": ["330cf5e60eb71a4f4f8f897bb501ac5acf9d0e5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082211 - Patch ICU windows zone data for updated time zones r=platform-i18n-reviewers,dminor\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334748\n", "files": ["config/external/icu/data/icudt78l.dat", "intl/icu-patches/bug-2082211-CLDR-19827-windows-zones.diff", "intl/icu/source/data/misc/windowsZones.txt", "intl/tzdata/source/be/windowsZones.res", "intl/tzdata/source/le/windowsZones.res", "intl/update-icu.sh"], "git_node": "0699e190f3a7b40858880c78e2dcdad0b5f0a2c8", "git_parents": ["1b4dbd497aa62ed9c7766bef94f7039fccbf2e98"], "node": "f82a58bb9c7c0f144438cce2896da0750a9d7007", "parents": ["09f1c94df79c89f7ba0e53a3884e3e4a79365487"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078841 - Remove extraneous metrics.yaml line from metrics_index.py. r=bustage\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "a5b51