l Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335324\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.renderer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer-geckoview.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/viewer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "599897e6fa16566312fcfbfa62942f752723fb2c", "git_parents": ["c1d8c9e155dfbc55b1bb4cf227bd2164cfbaea9d"], "node": "2f60d566b4bcbd0cf9ca225df2f6a77e682cb23b", "parents": ["ecf1c02cf71c6d8b4f88d6096d822ae403251d7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083594 - Don't enter the bound function's realm when calling a bound function. r=iain\n\nBound functions don't have an associated Realm in the spec, so we shouldn't\nswitch realms when calling through them. This is observable when the target is a\nproxy.\n\nIon's generic call trampoline already behaved like this, so this just fixes a\nsmall inconsistency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335058\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/realms/bound-function-realm.js", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIRWriter.h", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp", "js/src/vm/Interpreter.cpp"], "git_node": "3b7830b878203f5119150119644947b7fd860a7d", "git_parents": ["599897e6fa16566312fcfbfa62942f752723fb2c"], "node": "332a5b913ad0af06cc32671a86997e03651f9600", "parents": ["2f60d566b4bcbd0cf9ca225df2f6a77e682cb23b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mirko Brodesser \u003cmbrodesser@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074844 - Part 1) Rename \u003cjavascript-url-navigation-evaluated-to-string-inherits-csp.html\u003e to \u003cjavascript-url-navigation-to-s