entation (#63634)\n\nSee https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12812\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a73e14cfbaeba97744ff40cbc34d1ca96e5a92c7\nwpt-pr: 63634\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-fragmentation-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-fragmentation-001-ref.html"], "git_node": "accf370268d64548b83c4eae55401653d5aa61c0", "git_parents": ["2d6c375181d4691e835cb4d2eb4bb5ce8e7f35ae"], "node": "c70e1c760ae7d72fca0c781ff8a860267199cf12", "parents": ["c31fcbee4ac77797ee410d767beee641294d0eb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081715 [wpt PR 63634] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63634\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-fragmentation-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "f89205004073603b4e2240c901b9972545fec0ef", "git_parents": ["accf370268d64548b83c4eae55401653d5aa61c0"], "node": "3388418ff3562e0fc5aa001107e38015002b4574", "parents": ["c70e1c760ae7d72fca0c781ff8a860267199cf12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "J\u00falio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081731 [wpt PR 63629] - Correct Classic WebDriver pointer dimension WPT expectations, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCorrect Classic WebDriver pointer dimension WPT expectations\n\nWebDriver accepts nonnegative Numbers for pointer width and height.\nMove 0.1 and 2**53 from the invalid-input matrices to acceptance\ncoverage, alongside zero and omitted dimensions. Preserve genuine\ninvalid inputs and balance pointer button state between accepted values.\n\nRemove the obsolete dimension-failure baselines and the invalid-input\nfile's failure expectation. Keep the separate wheel-ordering expectation.\n\nBug: 540482873\nChange-Id: Ifddc71cb77ecaaf65ccd8110fe5460cbde5fb8bc\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-blink-rel,android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8550115\nReviewed-by: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718172}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7c475441e0e09c0b0d3a428ff9540b02bf57e349\nwpt-pr: 63629\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/invalid.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/perform.py"], "git_node": "a0d1dccb55d4c553bc082af64d56bc9b318ec0c1", "git_parents": ["f89205004073603b4e2240c901b9972545fec0ef"], "node": "a8f9c32346a016238a881d4f8b2a23e1902f9766", "parents": ["3388418ff3562e0fc5aa001107e38015002b4574"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081731 [wpt PR 63629] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63629\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/duration.py.ini"], "git_node": "efc31e721f834bc052628278e7d543215d4da833", "git_parents": ["a0d1dccb55d4c553bc082af64d56bc9b318ec0c1"], "node": "014609f232c289449fa578f27703b1f299b7d61b", "parents": ["a8f9c32346a016238a881d4f8b2a23e1902f9766"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Claire Chambers \u003cclchambers@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081773 [wpt PR 63635] - Fix commitStyles crash on replaced+canceled animation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix commitStyles crash on replaced+canceled animation\n\nRunning commitStyles on a canceled animation has no effect as the\nanimation has no effect values. However, a code path for committing\nstyles on a replaced animation assumed that the animation wasn't\ncanceled, as KeyframeEffect::ApplyEffects assumes a valid progress.\n\nThis CL simply skips the calculation in the case where there is no\nprogress, making commitStyles effectively a NOP, as it ought to be in\nthis case.\n\nBug: 571006760, 572653832\n\nChange-Id: I47275237017a484e49675ab1ad334217714c22b2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8564720\nCommit-Queue: Claire Chambers \u003cclchambers@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718190}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 656453151c7d2468bba283abb16e8001aa66419f\nwpt-pr: 63635\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/interfaces/Animation/commitStyles.html"], "git_node": "5f08b6d6dcb3d27b172f1df9aba095e84ab0e37c", "git_parents": ["efc31e721f834bc052628278e7d543215d4da833"], "node": "c4f31d2b2149d17d1b3d27fee45e73640407228b", "parents": ["014609f232c289449fa578f27703b1f299b7d61b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081779 [wpt PR 63636] - Allow anti-aliasing fuzz in svg/coordinate-systems/viewBox-fractional-valid.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAllow anti-aliasing fuzz in svg/coordinate-systems/viewBox-fractional-valid.html (#63636)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a4ef09b59e488667e1e1c63aae83fc77f29f3ed3\nwpt-pr: 63636\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/coordinate-systems/viewBox-fractional-valid.html"], "git_node": "4efbae9fb32bd5bcfcb259a420bc43eae06b97d8", "git_parents": ["5f08b6d6dcb3d27b172f1df9aba095e84ab0e37c"], "node": "00ef615cbe6dee721213b73ffd6a3fcc7e20c106", "parents": ["c4f31d2b2149d17d1b3d27fee45e73640407228b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081725 [wpt PR 63628] - [Media] Disallow mixing opaque and non-opaque responses in MultiBuffer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Media] Disallow mixing opaque and non-opaque responses in MultiBuffer\n\nFail the load in ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::DidReceiveResponse()\nif a resource that has already received a response receives a subsequent\nresponse whose CORS cross-origin taint state differs from the earlier\nresponse. This is guarded by a new kDisallowMixedOpaqueMediaResponses\nkill switch (enabled by default).\n\nThe behavior of mixing multiple range responses via a Service Worker is\nnot defined by the HTML or Service Worker specifications\n(https://github.com/w3c/ServiceWorker/issues/703), and both Firefox and\nSafari already reject mixing opaque and non-opaque range responses with\na load error. Update the existing web test and WPT expectations to match\nthis behavior across all browsers.\n\nFixed: 572307225\nChange-Id: Ie48e2d85b3450d14d40208cf89dd767081a7ffa7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8564157\nReviewed-by: Tsuyoshi Horo \u003choro@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Tsuyoshi Horo \u003choro@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718211}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 80d213ac479dcf94dcfe21b75cf279633e89a7ac\nwpt-pr: 63628\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/service-workers/service-worker/fetch-canvas-tainting-video-with-range-request.https.html"], "git_node": "0073ec7911e1d46cc3e11c874c1aac796397922a", "git_parents": ["4efbae9fb32bd5bcfcb259a420bc43eae06b97d8"], "node": "ad6780646341312a1f7f181ea9e767cbcaad29eb", "parents": ["00ef615cbe6dee721213b73ffd6a3fcc7e20c106"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081725 [wpt PR 63628] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63628\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/fetch-canvas-tainting-video-with-range-request.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "e019aa3c7c89209ed65397917bf092ba493cf180", "git_parents": ["0073ec7911e1d46cc3e11c874c1aac796397922a"], "node": "b868946cdcace8ae7bb7ce455c87839264df6a6e", "parents": ["ad6780646341312a1f7f181ea9e767cbcaad29eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Rivoal \u003cgit@florian.rivoal.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081790 [wpt PR 63637] - test interaction between line clamp and text overflow, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ntest interaction between line clamp and text overflow (#63637)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ac7ff49df82aaf9630eeabb1f0f562279527cf10\nwpt-pr: 63637\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-text-overflow-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-text-overflow-001-ref.html"], "git_node": "f31f5647dd8329083111050af0c3e0b4a99c1694", "git_parents": ["e019aa3c7c89209ed65397917bf092ba493cf180"], "node": "159daa9b1cb857d78fd8d84f69919c2e3175d7fa", "parents": ["b868946cdcace8ae7bb7ce455c87839264df6a6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081790 [wpt PR 63637] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63637\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-text-overflow-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "acc8406d70b8645a23011dcdf056f31df2734527", "git_parents": ["f31f5647dd8329083111050af0c3e0b4a99c1694"], "node": "56c6808ac99810cd6a0fa005573f8c28986aeee4", "parents": ["159daa9b1cb857d78fd8d84f69919c2e3175d7fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081938 [wpt PR 63643] - Ensure we start dbus for Firefox desktop, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure we start dbus for Firefox desktop\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6499c28fbc680e601acecdf700532d30da3789cd\nwpt-pr: 63643\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/run_tc.py"], "git_node": "2af61ad218d7a0b1b973c11d3d9118faf5268a99", "git_parents": ["acc8406d70b8645a23011dcdf056f31df2734527"], "node": "804f5757659b0bbcc9c41b5033123dd53132b3b4", "parents": ["56c6808ac99810cd6a0fa005573f8c28986aeee4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Martinez \u003c157772165+AndrewJMart@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081653 [wpt PR 63414] - ElementInternals-role.html: add items to empty menu / list such that all browsers ingest them equivalent, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nElementInternals-role.html: add items to empty menu / list  such that all browsers ingest them equivalent (#63414)\n\n* ElementInternals-role.html: add children from child_test_roles\n\nBrowsers differ on empty lists and menus, so update this test to include children on all lists / menus: https://github.com/w3c/aria/issues/2930\n\n* Add tentative test for empty list and menu roles: https://github.com/w3c/aria/issues/2930\n\n---------\nAuthored-by: Andrew Martinez \u003camartinez55@apple.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8454617c829fbaf5bc26ebaaea641dfe29ee073d\nwpt-pr: 63414\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/ElementInternals-role.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/wai-aria/role/empty-container-roles.tentative.html"], "git_node": "8fefe204c8b7da98a9c09afb3e4ada496f96da67", "git_parents": ["2af61ad218d7a0b1b973c11d3d9118faf5268a99"], "node": "872319fd572e46c38db39e9f3227abf815a55007", "parents": ["804f5757659b0bbcc9c41b5033123dd53132b3b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yanling Wang \u003cyanlingwang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075094 [wpt PR 62925] - [Masonry] Fix intrinsic inline size of row grid-lanes subgrids, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Fix intrinsic inline size of row grid-lanes subgrids\n\nThis CL fixes intrinsic inline sizing of row grid-lanes subgrids using\ninherited layout data when no sizing tree is available. This prevents\nunderestimating their min-content and max-content widths.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ie2b362d9dd19b4048f6ec8eea38fc3fab8d757c9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8411998\nReviewed-by: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yanling Wang \u003cyanlingwang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718391}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f544753ff68020c44f440f8b6dc3f1ef1c411014\nwpt-pr: 62925\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-lanes-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/row/grid-lanes-subgrid-005a-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-lanes-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/row/grid-lanes-subgrid-005a.html"], "git_node": "e95ce2271dbd0e8c71bc3761df9fbf7351baf58f", "git_parents": ["8fefe204c8b7da98a9c09afb3e4ada496f96da67"], "node": "6cd6650025f75a631955e548bd7f56c45db16367", "parents": ["872319fd572e46c38db39e9f3227abf815a55007"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075094 [wpt PR 62925] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 62925\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-lanes-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/row/grid-lanes-subgrid-005a.html.ini"], "git_node": "24e52ccc18d81064a56a05b194cfddbec8a1267e", "git_parents": ["e95ce2271dbd0e8c71bc3761df9fbf7351baf58f"], "node": "5fb85cdc6313d3310b0f2a5c0200971aa3bfa45b", "parents": ["6cd6650025f75a631955e548bd7f56c45db16367"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081996 [wpt PR 63642] - Remove incorrect moveBefore() CHECK, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove incorrect moveBefore() CHECK\n\nComputedStyle may exist _after_ moveBefore() before the next lifecycle\nupdate, not just while marking during the moveBefore().\n\nBug: 573058979\nChange-Id: I604d56820ef19637aab60194f600779d1b069ebd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8578259\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718402}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c180d702af37264e515dc7cfec32481f9d175ec3\nwpt-pr: 63642\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/moveBefore/chrome-573058979-crash.html"], "git_node": "55c0f428248588ccbd3daa03c174de04b9c4d0fa", "git_parents": ["24e52ccc18d81064a56a05b194cfddbec8a1267e"], "node": "59005215ccb2805ba58f16f0612b38c1589acf96", "parents": ["5fb85cdc6313d3310b0f2a5c0200971aa3bfa45b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082010 [wpt PR 63648] - [wdspec] Fix racy event assertions in BiDi WebDriver WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] Fix racy event assertions in BiDi WebDriver WPTs\n\n- Make five BiDi WebDriver WPTs stop flaking by asserting only event\n  orders and counts that the specs guarantee, and by registering event\n  waiters before triggering the action.\n- HTML emits browsingContext.historyUpdated from the session history\n  traversal queue, unordered with the navigation fetch. Fetch can\n  emit a CORS preflight's responseCompleted after the actual request\n  starts. A popup's initial about:blank can get its own realm.\n  dragleave depends on implementation-defined pointer move\n  interpolation. userPromptOpened could fire before its waiter was\n  added.\n\nBug: 565712857\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-blink-rel,android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I633dc4b1d72bc6f0da3acebdd829c47ff5aa96ba\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8578100\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718526}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a23b7456c5a9be0b7f79e5720036f4991ad8259a\nwpt-pr: 63648\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/user_prompt_opened/user_prompt_opened.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/pointer_mouse_drag.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/integration/navigation.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/combined/network_events.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/realm_created/window_open.py"], "git_node": "514c56e9912786762076ae9196ef0c1dd4cd7ca5", "git_parents": ["55c0f428248588ccbd3daa03c174de04b9c4d0fa"], "node": "4002d17f882c8fc0656f831748cb51e9995c7ae1", "parents": ["59005215ccb2805ba58f16f0612b38c1589acf96"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082010 [wpt PR 63648] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63648\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/user_prompt_opened/beforeunload.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/user_prompt_opened/handler.py.ini"], "git_node": "4d26e9b383b710670f021f5d0fb5fa76692cc422", "git_parents": ["514c56e9912786762076ae9196ef0c1dd4cd7ca5"], "node": "6c5bfe785190a4356b1209fa69f91a089d3aa7d0", "parents": ["4002d17f882c8fc0656f831748cb51e9995c7ae1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081580 [wpt PR 63615] - Make checkable menuitems be separate \u003cmenuitemcheckbox\u003e and \u003cmenuitemradio\u003e elements., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake checkable menuitems be separate \u003cmenuitemcheckbox\u003e and \u003cmenuitemradio\u003e elements.\n\nThe old approach to checkable menuitems was to have a \u003cfieldset\ncheckable=single\u003e (radio-like) or \u003cfieldset checkable=multiple\u003e\n(checkbox-like) be a grouping container for \u003cmenuitem\u003e elements that\nwould become checkable.\n\nInstead, we've decided to create new elements, \u003cmenuitemcheckbox\u003e and\n\u003cmenuitemradio\u003e.  The grouping of \u003cmenuitemradio\u003e elements is by their\nnearest ancestor \u003cmenulist\u003e, \u003cfieldset\u003e, or \u003cmenubar\u003e; there is no\nexplicit grouping mechanism.\n\nThis means the menu elements proposal no longer adds attributes or IDL\nproperties to the \u003cfieldset\u003e element.  Much of the old \u003cmenuitem\u003e\nbehavior now lives on two common base classes: HTMLMenuItemElementBase\nwhich is common to all three of \u003cmenuitem\u003e, \u003cmenuitemcheckbox\u003e, and\n\u003cmenuitemradio\u003e, and HTMLMenuItemCheckableElementBase which is common to\nonly the latter two (and contains common behavior for checkable menu\nitems).   Submenu-related behavior all stays on \u003cmenuitem\u003e.\n\nThis is per the latest discussion in\nhttps://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1189\n\nBug: 406566432\nAX-Relnotes: n/a.\nChange-Id: Ie8eeb2cf8ddf40ae2652adeb770ed1c3739546da\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561601\nCommit-Queue: Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718653}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7e5676e611228380a4c36382f5fc3fdc800803c6\nwpt-pr: 63615\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/idlharness.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menu-content-model-violation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menubar-invoke-menulist.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menuitem-implicit-interest-invoker.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/uncheck-menuitem-dismiss-popover.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/html-menu-elements.tentative.idl"], "git_node": "dd06aeec1330be1170519106297070c0623644c7", "git_parents": ["4d26e9b383b710670f021f5d0fb5fa76692cc422"], "node": "a8f6cfa57585f226fd2a6e6629ab22cc2bd1defe", "parents": ["6c5bfe785190a4356b1209fa69f91a089d3aa7d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081580 [wpt PR 63615] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63615\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/idlharness.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/menubar-invoke-menulist.html.ini"], "git_node": "66793b1e24b43cb8f588d16e9d2d4a90bd9b0754", "git_parents": ["dd06aeec1330be1170519106297070c0623644c7"], "node": "7952eebd2f13c6e514fcf5dba20c3698c9e85205", "parents": ["a8f6cfa57585f226fd2a6e6629ab22cc2bd1defe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082048 [wpt PR 63649] - [wdspec] Fix broken BiDi subscribe and network_conditions WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] Fix broken BiDi subscribe and network_conditions WPTs\n\n- Make session/subscribe/contexts.py run as an async test and pass,\n  and replace the three unimplemented @pytest.mark.skip stub tests in\n  network_conditions_offline.py with TODO comments so the WPT runner\n  no longer fails on disallowed in-test skip decorators.\n- contexts.py was missing pytestmark = pytest.mark.asyncio and reused\n  an already-resolved wait_for_event future across later log.entryAdded\n  checks.\n\nBug: 565712857\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-blink-rel,android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I9fa733a8b3ca93b8782091511802f78b5631e08d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8577160\nCommit-Queue: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Rudenko \u003calexrudenko@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718656}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b995b20d572ac310545539b0b491be0a53974f6f\nwpt-pr: 63649\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_network_conditions/network_conditions_offline.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/session/subscribe/contexts.py"], "git_node": "8c4e9c4b8e1f2a9c600b7b2bb1ea1c2614ce8ca3", "git_parents": ["66793b1e24b43cb8f588d16e9d2d4a90bd9b0754"], "node": "b4c3032ec09f2e631dab58d239451b3502a05dab", "parents": ["7952eebd2f13c6e514fcf5dba20c3698c9e85205"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082062 [wpt PR 63653] - [chromium-bidi] Fix global network interception for popup requests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Fix global network interception for popup requests\n\n- Ensure global network intercepts (`network.addIntercept` with no\n  `contexts` specified) intercept the initial navigation request of\n  newly opened popups.\n- Previously, `CdpTarget` chained `toggleNetworkIfNeeded()` after the\n  `Network.enable` response, allowing `Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger`\n  to unpause the popup before `Fetch.enable` was sent.\n- Schedule `toggleNetworkIfNeeded()` synchronously after\n  `Network.enable` so `Fetch.enable` is dispatched before unpausing the\n  target.\n\nBug: 571161447\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel,mac-webdriver-bidi-rel,win-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I761f1ccff80c9505fc0fa3cc39b6842a91e805da\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8577839\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718660}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d1c5cb6aacd9238e1cd6b999a8507a198c7d32fb\nwpt-pr: 63653\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/add_intercept/contexts.py"], "git_node": "710fadb086ded8ee501ca59725d4b5b608ab0874", "git_parents": ["8c4e9c4b8e1f2a9c600b7b2bb1ea1c2614ce8ca3"], "node": "1d4c93c5e6a4f5af2fa1a6b37fe0d1887f5af97b", "parents": ["b4c3032ec09f2e631dab58d239451b3502a05dab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082062 [wpt PR 63653] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63653\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/add_intercept/add_intercept.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/add_intercept/contexts.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/add_intercept/invalid.py.ini"], "git_node": "01a61bf712de891c2c838367f9a226b3df00ae86", "git_parents": ["710fadb086ded8ee501ca59725d4b5b608ab0874"], "node": "548c49fd28b3757038ffa55da581e5b7be7e32e1", "parents": ["1d4c93c5e6a4f5af2fa1a6b37fe0d1887f5af97b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080502 [wpt PR 63491] - Use a PAC file for FedCM tests instead of disabling well-known checks, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUse a PAC file for FedCM tests instead of disabling well-known checks (#63491)\n\nNow that the HTTP test server can proxy HTTPS requests, route all\nrequests from FedCM tests through it with a PAC file. This makes\nrequests to the default HTTPS port, like the well-known file at\nhttps://\u003csite\u003e/.well-known/web-identity, reach the test server, so\nChrome no longer needs FedCmWithoutWellKnownEnforcement.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15be672cc975f99f5650ce104c95b6e68d6df671\nwpt-pr: 63491\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/alternative-identifiers/fedcm-single-identifier.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-abort-silent-mediation-not-permitted.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-abort.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-endpoint-rejects-redirects.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/fedcm-accounts-push-basic.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/fedcm-accounts-push-caches-pictures.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/fedcm-identity-create-store-collect.tentative.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/fedcm-identity-discovery.tentative.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/store-account-list.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-after-abort.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-continue-on-disallowed.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-continue-on-with-account.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-continue-on.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-disclosure-text-shown.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-params.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-resolve-side-effects.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/fedcm-userinfo-after-resolve.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-authz/resolve-after-preventsilentaccess.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-auto-reauthn-without-approved-clients.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-auto-selected-flag.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-basic.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-active-cannot-replace-active.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-active-replaces-passive.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-button-mode-auto-selected-flag.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-button-mode-basics.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-passive-after-active.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-passive-cannot-replace-active.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-use-other-account-button-flow.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-button-and-other-account/fedcm-use-other-account.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-client-metadata-not-cached.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-context.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-cross-origin-policy.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-csp.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-delegation/evt-basic.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-disconnect-errors.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-disconnect-iframe.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-disconnect.sub.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-domainhint-any.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-domainhint-matches-account.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-domainhint-matches-from-two-accounts.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-error-attribute/fedcm-error-attribute.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-error-basic.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-flexible-token/basic.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-flexible-token/complex.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-flexible-token/resolve-flexible-tokens.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-identity-assertion-nocors.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-iframe.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-login-status/confirm-idp-login.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-login-status/cross-origin-status.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-login-status/idp-login-with-failed-accounts-fetch.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-login-status/logged-out.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-login-status/login-page-broken.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-loginhint.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-manifest-not-in-list.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-multi-idp-abort.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-multi-idp-basic.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-multi-idp-context.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-multi-idp-mediation-optional.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-multi-idp-mediation-silent.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-multi-idp/fedcm-too-many-idps.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-navigation-interception/continue-on-redirect-POST.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-no-domainhint-matches-account.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-no-login-url.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-nonce-is-optional.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-not-observed-by-service-worker.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-opaque-rp-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-pending-call-rejected.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-pending-disconnect.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-pending-userinfo.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-register/fedcm-no-registered-idps.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-reject-invalid-responses.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-returning-account-auto-reauthn.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-same-site-none.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-storage-access-api-autogrant.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-store.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-token-endpoint-rejects-redirects.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-token-returned-with-http-error.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-too-many-disconnect-calls.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-userinfo.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/fedcm-well-known-validation/well-known-client-metadata-validation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/support/proxy.sub.pac", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/third-party-iframe/fedcm-third-party-iframe-active-mode.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fedcm/third-party-iframe/fedcm-third-party-iframe.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/browsers/chrome.py"], "git_node": "c9400b8ab685a0a092fdc777f560abc035b33268", "git_parents": ["01a61bf712de891c2c838367f9a226b3df00ae86"], "node": "79dc36e33c2761899f45de6fd4c5499d8819aa28", "parents": ["548c49fd28b3757038ffa55da581e5b7be7e32e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080502 [wpt PR 63491] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63491\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fedcm/fedcm-accounts-push/fedcm-accounts-push-caches-pictures.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "db3afe2014a8b57f9889a93d930cd8bd2044473c", "git_parents": ["c9400b8ab685a0a092fdc777f560abc035b33268"], "node": "005cc72d62129d95798988f13c362eee60957232", "parents": ["79dc36e33c2761899f45de6fd4c5499d8819aa28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082249 [wpt PR 63655] - [HiC] Disallow SVG masks on SVG content in readback-allowed mode, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Disallow SVG masks on SVG content in readback-allowed mode\n\nWe were missing a check for readback-allowed in SVGMaskPainter,\nused to paint masks on SVG content.\n\nFixed: 572695599\n\nCHECK on privacy\n\nChange-Id: I1a2d07b756f5c6a5d9fe1fb5f2997fa7bf512e6d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8580323\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718722}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0f068db84a14f00daf0f881b8597ea037a271dcf\nwpt-pr: 63655\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-mask-on-svg-content-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html"], "git_node": "c481c68a3f121b2f464051f4a26ce6b4dcfb9649", "git_parents": ["db3afe2014a8b57f9889a93d930cd8bd2044473c"], "node": "f53c61f52e75fb0d4ffb36b73e3fc80ac6fbe268", "parents": ["005cc72d62129d95798988f13c362eee60957232"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082249 [wpt PR 63655] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63655\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/svg/svg-mask-on-svg-content-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "723e50b9b2dfc9fb74597a0163a66b71d28c3247", "git_parents": ["c481c68a3f121b2f464051f4a26ce6b4dcfb9649"], "node": "76687ede0a28a19e9a41707111e7af724179a14f", "parents": ["f53c61f52e75fb0d4ffb36b73e3fc80ac6fbe268"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Fern\u00e1ndez Garc\u00eda-Boente \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082251 [wpt PR 63654] - Fetch: fix the stale bodyUsed assertion in request-disturbed.any.js, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFetch: fix the stale bodyUsed assertion in request-disturbed.any.js\n\nThe test case \"Input request used for creating new request became\ndisturbed even if body is not used\" asserts that new Request(input, {\nbody }) marks the input's body as used. The Request constructor has not\ndone that since whatwg/fetch#675 (2018). It creates a proxy for\ninputBody, which is what disturbs it, only when init supplies no body:\n\n    If initBody is null and inputBody is non-null, then:\n      If inputBody is unusable, then throw a TypeError.\n      Set finalBody to the result of creating a proxy for inputBody.\n\nThe assertion matches the steps as whatwg/fetch@55141d7 left them in\n2017, which disturbed inputBody whenever it was non-null. `#675` limited\nthat to the case where inputBody is the body the new request uses, and\nits tests in #9931 edited this subtest without updating the assertion.\n\nNo engine passes the mentioned subtest [1]. Chromium (since\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8451204), Gecko and WebKit all fail it on this\nassertion, with \"bodyUsed is true when request is disturbed expected\ntrue got false\".\n\n[1] https://wpt.fyi/results/fetch/api/request/request-disturbed.any.html\n\nChange-Id: Ie4ccd82faf4bad53537a095a33f6711ef3c197c4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8562797\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Fernandez \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718728}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 18904ce92770fcbc776f2c112f01c976833653ea\nwpt-pr: 63654\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/api/request/request-disturbed.any.js"], "git_node": "8d1e4a0e6fbc40e85d06c2db35c267d22205ee94", "git_parents": ["723e50b9b2dfc9fb74597a0163a66b71d28c3247"], "node": "3feb12494188f366eba76e61869ee0b55a8c0499", "parents": ["76687ede0a28a19e9a41707111e7af724179a14f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082253 [wpt PR 63658] - [chromium-bidi] Fix network.getData with disown on intercepted requests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Fix network.getData with disown on intercepted requests\n\n- Keep in-flight and intercepted network requests alive when\n  `network.getData` is called with `disown: true` (or when\n  `network.disownData` is called).\n- Previously, disowning the last collector unconditionally deleted the\n  request from `NetworkStorage`, causing subsequent\n  `network.provideResponse` or `network.continueRequest` calls on a\n  blocked request to fail with `no such request`.\n- Track request completion via `NetworkRequest.isFinished` and only\n  evict uncollected requests once they have finished or failed loading.\n\nBug: 571267468\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I504ef540dd6c6e2d636e4a7768237de2c885b7f7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8575161\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718768}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b876b9f39a0e7ee65762918cae96b081d14ceb5\nwpt-pr: 63658\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/disown_data/collector.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/get_data/disown.py"], "git_node": "588d57649e8bb7d48f14e86beefb6456f45363ce", "git_parents": ["8d1e4a0e6fbc40e85d06c2db35c267d22205ee94"], "node": "9c4db15c497049a908a14923e31706ca68cd15c3", "parents": ["3feb12494188f366eba76e61869ee0b55a8c0499"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082253 [wpt PR 63658] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63658\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/disown_data/collector.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/network/disown_data/data_type.py.ini"], "git_node": "1a29491b0106cde84408e04bc4272643fed1a853", "git_parents": ["588d57649e8bb7d48f14e86beefb6456f45363ce"], "node": "5a5a7616d7c12ee5d8f20e556a39ce946a11bb22", "parents": ["9c4db15c497049a908a14923e31706ca68cd15c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082254 [wpt PR 63664] - WebMCP: Don't notify the browser when unregistering in an inactive doc, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Don't notify the browser when unregistering in an inactive doc\n\n`ModelContext::UnregisterTool()` always sends `UnregisterScriptTool()`\nto the browser. But once a document is inactive, e.g., after its iframe\nis removed, its `model_context_host_remote_` (a `HeapMojoRemote`) has\nbeen reset as part of its execution context being destroyed, and calling\na method on an unbound remote crashes the renderer.\n\nThis is reachable from script, by aborting an imperative tool's\n`AbortSignal` after the registering document has become inactive, e.g.,\nafter its iframe is removed:\n\nconst controller = new AbortController();\n  await iframe.contentDocument.modelContext.registerTool(\n      {...}, {signal: controller.signal});\n  iframe.remove();\n  controller.abort();  // Crash.\n\nThis CL still removes the tool from `ModelContext`'s own state, but only\nnotifies the browser when the document is active. An inactive document\nhas no browser host to notify: frameless documents never bind one, and\nthe document of a removed frame becomes inactive before its execution\ncontext is destroyed. This matches the `IsActive()` checks that\n`registerTool()` and `executeTool()` already perform.\n\nSee https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/345.\n\nR=beaufort.francois@gmail.com\n\nBug: 573454028\nChange-Id: If36db9f87aaa750561c1368b9b20e0a5a974b423\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8578418\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718966}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 97180c2fcdef637542dc183d7b328a30eddfbe1f\nwpt-pr: 63664\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/abort-signal-after-iframe-removal-crash.https.html"], "git_node": "9b4788b742644d375f9b870c38f39135916ea6fd", "git_parents": ["1a29491b0106cde84408e04bc4272643fed1a853"], "node": "23885dbe1d93039dd24558c61902bef3f4ed6bbe", "parents": ["5a5a7616d7c12ee5d8f20e556a39ce946a11bb22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082254 [wpt PR 63664] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63664\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/abort-signal-after-iframe-removal-crash.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "c7e3990db600ae251e4425b85f2334da54be2f43", "git_parents": ["9b4788b742644d375f9b870c38f39135916ea6fd"], "node": "e87808aa3614373e9a599ee7880a6347a226b753", "parents": ["23885dbe1d93039dd24558c61902bef3f4ed6bbe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082255 [wpt PR 63666] - [line-clamp] Make webkit-line-clamp-035 match the spec's ellipsis placement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] Make webkit-line-clamp-035 match the spec's ellipsis placement\n\nThe third line of webkit-line-clamp-035 is a single unbreakable word\nthat does not fit in the line-clamp container. The reference expected\nit to be truncated to \"CCC\" followed by the ellipsis, as the old\n-webkit-line-clamp implementations do. css-overflow-4 says that the\nblock overflow ellipsis displaces content from the end of the line\n\"until the last soft wrap opportunity [...] that would still allow the\nentire block overflow ellipsis to fit on the line\", and that if this\ndisplaces the entire contents of the line box, the line box contains a\nstrut:\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#block-ellipsis\n\nSince the word has no soft wrap opportunity, the whole word is\ndisplaced and the third line only contains the (hidden) ellipsis. This\nupdates the reference accordingly. Chromium with line-breaking ellipsis\n(and WebKit with -webkit-line-clamp laid out as line-clamp) render it\nthis way already, while the legacy implementations now fail it.\n\nBug: 40336192\nChange-Id: Ie730121f63330a20806c4ca53ff46544ee3d4c4e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8574804\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719040}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 353ccef3dbad2851c56dcd084eff3f8259604091\nwpt-pr: 63666\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/webkit-line-clamp-035-ref.html"], "git_node": "e0fce639c9c61aea6077bffa38d25df84732ad10", "git_parents": ["c7e3990db600ae251e4425b85f2334da54be2f43"], "node": "584343572f5eddb8eeddffa4d890044a134c277b", "parents": ["e87808aa3614373e9a599ee7880a6347a226b753"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082255 [wpt PR 63666] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63666\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-035.html.ini"], "git_node": "c2ad41682b730368337851d38c35e765f02fb405", "git_parents": ["e0fce639c9c61aea6077bffa38d25df84732ad10"], "node": "4256c0e60ae3823565324029eba07ba880ee4b51", "parents": ["584343572f5eddb8eeddffa4d890044a134c277b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kristin Lee \u003ckristinlee@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082257 [wpt PR 63667] - [\u003cinstall\u003e Element] Remove unused InPagePermissionMixin members, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[\u003cinstall\u003e Element] Remove unused InPagePermissionMixin members\n\nHTMLInstallElement currently includes InPagePermissionMixin, which exposes\npermission status and prompt event members that do not apply to \u003cinstall\u003e.\n\nDeclare only the validation members used by \u003cinstall\u003e. This removes\ninitialPermissionStatus, permissionStatus, onpromptaction, and\nonpromptdismiss while preserving validation behavior.\n\nAdd feature-detection coverage and update web-exposure expectations.\n\nBug: 533049447, 454827186\nChange-Id: I735dd15af02cf04d7af644a96e18bdb2dffa8ac7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8543172\nReviewed-by: Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kristin Lee \u003ckristinlee@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719114}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 929285422eb40f1b91bec40e70670eb27ffe8595\nwpt-pr: 63667\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-feature-detect.tentative.html"], "git_node": "e43166f25305c20c69083bf5d7122109e98ecfb4", "git_parents": ["c2ad41682b730368337851d38c35e765f02fb405"], "node": "d56fe95a83c0fe3e3aecac8475ab5ec7cf3e2046", "parents": ["4256c0e60ae3823565324029eba07ba880ee4b51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082257 [wpt PR 63667] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63667\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/install/install-element-feature-detect.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "c25101107247d20c62fbda490c935fe787308772", "git_parents": ["e43166f25305c20c69083bf5d7122109e98ecfb4"], "node": "6b1d4d443a2bcc26abcb9257d8023aea49063cb1", "parents": ["d56fe95a83c0fe3e3aecac8475ab5ec7cf3e2046"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082264 [wpt PR 63668] - [WebInstallAPI] Restrict navigator.install to secure contexts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebInstallAPI] Restrict navigator.install to secure contexts\n\nApply SecureContext to both navigator.install overloads so the API is\nabsent from insecure contexts, including HTTPS frames with an insecure\nancestor. Preserve exposure on HTTPS and trustworthy HTTP localhost.\n\nDefine is_in_secure_context in the binding generator's callback scope.\nSecure-gated overload dispatch references this symbol, but the missing\nbinding previously caused generation to fail.\n\nBug: 333795265\nChange-Id: I05ab5417fe55e554918f69c0963861e275756c76\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.mac:mac26-arm64-rel-tests|browser_tests\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8544380\nReviewed-by: Robert Paveza \u003cRob.Paveza@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719173}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fdcd7e6936d73e6ad438c0e024a831e9b59aea0b\nwpt-pr: 63668\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/navigator-install-defined.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/navigator-install-not-defined.tentative.http.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/resources/navigator-install-exposure-helper.html"], "git_node": "da83c719a6a9d438aeb8caddc45b219f3acb78c7", "git_parents": ["c25101107247d20c62fbda490c935fe787308772"], "node": "ea476a73b1d4bca323b999f87f1ff585eeab5b51", "parents": ["6b1d4d443a2bcc26abcb9257d8023aea49063cb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082312 [wpt PR 63671] - [Masonry] Stretch fragmented grid-lanes items, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Stretch fragmented grid-lanes items\n\nGrid-lanes items with stacking-axis stretch alignment need their total\nstretched size resolved before fragmentation so that each fragment uses\na consistent size.\n\nRetain the original border-box stacking size on alignment candidates and\nadd the available alignment space once the final candidates are known.\n\nPersist the resulting size on the break token for fragmented layout and\napply it through the existing fixed-size constraints.\n\nThis stretch size may expand due to fragmentation break rules in later\nchanges.\n\nStretch alignment in the grid axis is already well tested and working as\nexpected.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ia604372da162cc2540b939683405737367dae83d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8574018\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719197}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f695672d2c3be4261059172afebc0fa733af68f3\nwpt-pr: 63671\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-021.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-022.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-024-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-single-lane-fragmentation-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-022.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-023.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-024.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-025-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-025.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-026.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-006.html"], "git_node": "91fb0877fe9c3fe28c634c9285db52cc986e8d62", "git_parents": ["da83c719a6a9d438aeb8caddc45b219f3acb78c7"], "node": "f3cd51ea2a54c71f6ee6d90bc4a9ff2b1e83a172", "parents": ["ea476a73b1d4bca323b999f87f1ff585eeab5b51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082312 [wpt PR 63671] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63671\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-021.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-022.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-023.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-multi-lane-fragmentation-025.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/column-single-lane-fragmentation-006.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-022.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-023.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-025.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-multi-lane-fragmentation-026.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/grid/grid-lanes/row-single-lane-fragmentation-006.html.ini"], "git_node": "58787b3c43055551ca4c62c11e1df9a28eadb342", "git_parents": ["91fb0877fe9c3fe28c634c9285db52cc986e8d62"], "node": "92a60ac186fed2affd642f74ae5743a41d3b6c93", "parents": ["f3cd51ea2a54c71f6ee6d90bc4a9ff2b1e83a172"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082321 [wpt PR 63669] - WebMCP: Re-check document activity after serializing `inputSchema`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Re-check document activity after serializing `inputSchema`\n\n`ModelContext::registerTool()` checks that its document is active up\nfront, but then serializes `inputSchema`, which can run script via a\n`toJSON()` method. If that script makes the document inactive, e.g., by\nremoving its iframe, `registerTool()` carries on and dereferences the\ndocument's now-null frame (and would then call into its reset\n`ModelContextHost` remote), crashing the renderer:\n\n  iframe.contentDocument.modelContext.registerTool({\n    name: 'tool',\n    description: 'desc',\n    inputSchema: {toJSON() { iframe.remove(); return {}; }},\n    execute: () =\u003e {},\n  });  // Crash.\n\nThis CL checks again after serialization, and rejects with the same\n`InvalidStateError` as the up-front check. This matches the re-check\nadded to the spec in\nhttps://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/345.\n\nR=khushalsagar\n\nBug: 573671121\nChange-Id: I9afb20dfa0d23d6aa54d34b568e17461b88d39db\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8582224\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719223}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ee021e0ffdd4b9c17d38c764d614227909cf64b6\nwpt-pr: 63669\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/register-tool-input-schema-removes-iframe-crash.https.html"], "git_node": "dddc4f3f2e8f1217bd1a5176bfeee45cca26f878", "git_parents": ["58787b3c43055551ca4c62c11e1df9a28eadb342"], "node": "e0a0061b0fdbc1e14252cc30d09536270bfed71b", "parents": ["92a60ac186fed2affd642f74ae5743a41d3b6c93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082321 [wpt PR 63669] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63669\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/register-tool-input-schema-removes-iframe-crash.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "1bbbd806901e35852cde103f7f4674a7fe591c8e", "git_parents": ["dddc4f3f2e8f1217bd1a5176bfeee45cca26f878"], "node": "a4392e9df9b8b6b363d49cad320d95b6378facea", "parents": ["e0a0061b0fdbc1e14252cc30d09536270bfed71b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082324 [wpt PR 63678] - WebMCP: Re-check for a duplicate tool name after serializing inputSchema, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebMCP: Re-check for a duplicate tool name after serializing inputSchema\n\n`registerTool()` rejects a duplicate tool name up front, but then\nserializes `inputSchema`, which can run script (via `toJSON()`) that\nregisters another tool with the same name. `registerTool()` then still\nsends the duplicate to the browser, which kills the renderer.\n\nCheck for a duplicate name again after serialization, next to the\nexisting document-activity re-check, and reject with the same\n`InvalidStateError` as the up-front check.\n\nSee https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/347 for the spec\nfix.\n\nR=khushalsagar\n\nBug: 573722078\nChange-Id: I044e3ad96fb00c624829eb182047aa30575f81a6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8583183\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719227}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 91d7226786906fc1c9cb08ab5d5984ceaeef6416\nwpt-pr: 63678\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/register-tool-input-schema-registers-same-name.https.html"], "git_node": "76b0620591dbb7627a569f55f922f0547e3c87c1", "git_parents": ["1bbbd806901e35852cde103f7f4674a7fe591c8e"], "node": "68b38bd4b2d103d17827d5dbb2670234f1bf5ce0", "parents": ["a4392e9df9b8b6b363d49cad320d95b6378facea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082324 [wpt PR 63678] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63678\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/register-tool-input-schema-registers-same-name.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "02841d90531562f1d78bded39806d3fc563512ce", "git_parents": ["76b0620591dbb7627a569f55f922f0547e3c87c1"], "node": "42be6812fed71a757410c558e791f5835b9ae6c4", "parents": ["68b38bd4b2d103d17827d5dbb2670234f1bf5ce0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082330 [wpt PR 63672] - [3/N] WebMCP: Introduce the `Tool` interface object, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[3/N] WebMCP: Introduce the `Tool` interface object\n\nThis CL replaces the `RegisteredTool` dictionary returned by\n`getTools()` and accepted by `executeTool()` with a `Tool` interface\nobject. Each `Tool` carries the non-web-exposed `tool_id` of the tool it\nrepresents. `executeTool()`, including cross-document execution through\nthe browser, now targets tools by that ID rather than by name.\n\nThis fixes the execution-time race described in the parent CL. If a\npage unregisters a tool and registers a new one under the same name,\nexecuting the stale `Tool` used to run the new tool. Now it rejects.\nThe new WPT\nexternal/wpt/webmcp/imperative/tool-re-registration-race.https.html\nexercises this.\n\nWhen the ID isn't found, the rejection message is deliberately generic\nso the ID is not leaked to web content. DevTools still receives the ID\nvia the probe.\n\nEmbedders (the actor) and DevTools still identify tools by name, via\n`ModelContext::ExecuteToolByName()`, so they remain subject to the race.\nMoving them to IDs is follow-up work.\n\nSee\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1psoB7k71-Dgkxg2tTG62DYJDTg02x8zOS3jCEd0QlbM/edit?tab=t.0.\n\nR=mfoltz\n\nBug: 536063275\nChange-Id: I18a8277bbf73208b9f55f9404ae9aca4e79847ed\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8510757\nCommit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Moshchuk \u003calexmos@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mark Foltz \u003cmfoltz@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719188}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15e7837b850f4fef5b3106e97de484bfdfa460f5\nwpt-pr: 63672\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-invalid-dictionary.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unauthorized-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/exposedTo-defaults-same-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/getTools-imperative-annotations.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/opaque-origin-tools.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/permissions-policy.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/resources/iframe-register-tool.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/tool-re-registration-race.https.html"], "git_node": "8dae5d6fed2ad8f91c7409e7fcec673ede4fe73e", "git_parents": ["02841d90531562f1d78bded39806d3fc563512ce"], "node": "60f1649be2e37941ffdbae6e5f0b903ebc9ae6b4", "parents": ["42be6812fed71a757410c558e791f5835b9ae6c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082330 [wpt PR 63672] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63672\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-invalid-dictionary.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/executeTool-unauthorized-origin.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/getTools-imperative-annotations.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/imperative/tool-re-registration-race.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "1ac0650ee6979fe5bd70b0f11ea49c93c3c17332", "git_parents": ["8dae5d6fed2ad8f91c7409e7fcec673ede4fe73e"], "node": "ce9597bfcb7b700a62271aceb3b31734c10a9df8", "parents": ["60f1649be2e37941ffdbae6e5f0b903ebc9ae6b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082332 [wpt PR 63675] - Pass block-size to fieldset content in min/max sizing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPass block-size to fieldset content in min/max sizing\n\nMin/max sizing ignored the fieldset's height, so images with percentage\nheights used their natural widths.\n\nPass the block-size when there is no rendered legend, and resolve\npercentage padding as in layout.\n\nBug: 368131302\nChange-Id: Ia441304b4778818adcf1c02651e4623099d9863e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8522097\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719234}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b1cc64dcc0919d76bd1c1ba3038f2901fec565bc\nwpt-pr: 63675\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/fieldset-intrinsic-size-percent.html"], "git_node": "d6d762c7067f8fe9f2652b5fb2f4b886d0495c00", "git_parents": ["1ac0650ee6979fe5bd70b0f11ea49c93c3c17332"], "node": "2c2fe61857866f07f1bb6d466ce1f8551570f9c9", "parents": ["ce9597bfcb7b700a62271aceb3b31734c10a9df8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076317 [wpt PR 63027] - Improve edge cases with \u003cselectedcontent\u003e updating, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImprove edge cases with \u003cselectedcontent\u003e updating\n\nThis patch implements feedback in the HTML PR for \u003cselectedcontent\u003e\nelement updates: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12263\n\n- Decouples \u003cselectedcontent\u003e updates from ResetToDefaultSelection() and\n  adds ResetSelectedness() to only update \u003cselectedcontent\u003e when an\n  option's selectedness actually changes (including when select.size,\n  select.multiple, option.disabled, or optgroup.disabled changes, or\n  when an option is removed).\n- Updates \u003cselectedcontent\u003e on form.reset(), when option.selected is\n  set to false, and when re-assigning option.selected = true on an\n  already-selected option.\n- Avoids redundant \u003cselectedcontent\u003e updates during atomic moves within\n  the same \u003cselect\u003e or when setting option.selected = false on an\n  already-unselected option in a single-select listbox.\n\nThis patch is mostly tested by this upstream WPT PR:\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62242\n\nBug: 40078978\nChange-Id: I932e39618aa0adee43ea34172c7732428833796d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8300572\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719267}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c9731ae2ec9f5fc16c0de13d73f81ca82ac5385e\nwpt-pr: 63027\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent.html"], "git_node": "6b301a30f36772b232c20aaf60d34403f37868c2", "git_parents": ["d6d762c7067f8fe9f2652b5fb2f4b886d0495c00"], "node": "ccddb02dfe310a6f0ad854f98225e2ea2bd49dd6", "parents": ["2c2fe61857866f07f1bb6d466ce1f8551570f9c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076317 [wpt PR 63027] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63027\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-optgroup-legend.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent.html.ini"], "git_node": "808184108f14ece8809a91b3982ff59674732799", "git_parents": ["6b301a30f36772b232c20aaf60d34403f37868c2"], "node": "6155f7c875e083c2c856316f8093779a73db20c8", "parents": ["ccddb02dfe310a6f0ad854f98225e2ea2bd49dd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082362 [wpt PR 63683] - Revert \"WebMCP: Re-check for a duplicate tool name after serializing inputSchema\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"WebMCP: Re-check for a duplicate tool name after serializing inputSchema\"\n\nThis reverts commit bbf032940645a5dcea55e6dc1bdb34b8c989650f.\n\nReason for revert:\nLUCI Bisection has identified this change as the culprit of a build failure. See the analysis: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/bisection/compile-analysis/b/8667914546796401745\n\nSample failed build: https://ci.chromium.org/b/8667914546796401745\n\nIf this is a false positive, please report it at http://b.corp.google.com/createIssue?component=1199205&description=Analysis%3A+https%3A%2F%2Fchromium-review.googlesource.com%2Fc%2Fchromium%2Fsrc%2F%2B%2F8583183&format=PLAIN&priority=P3&title=Wrongly+blamed+https%3A%2F%2Fci.chromium.org%2Fui%2Fp%2Fchromium%2Fbisection%2Fcompile-analysis%2Fb%2F8667914546796401745&type=BUG\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e WebMCP: Re-check for a duplicate tool name after serializing inputSchema\n\u003e\n\u003e `registerTool()` rejects a duplicate tool name up front, but then\n\u003e serializes `inputSchema`, which can run script (via `toJSON()`) that\n\u003e registers another tool with the same name. `registerTool()` then still\n\u003e sends the duplicate to the browser, which kills the renderer.\n\u003e\n\u003e Check for a duplicate name again after serialization, next to the\n\u003e existing document-activity re-check, and reject with the same\n\u003e `InvalidStateError` as the up-front check.\n\u003e\n\u003e See https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/347 for the spec\n\u003e fix.\n\u003e\n\u003e R=khushalsagar\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 573722078\n\u003e Change-Id: I044e3ad96fb00c624829eb182047aa30575f81a6\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8583183\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719227}\n\u003e\n\nBug: 573722078\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: I76d0fe146b570f7b8590eaadea632794afe24ea3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8575491\nCommit-Queue: luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nBot-Commit: luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nOwners-Override: luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719232}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a3a0228dfac64d20cdd5a4c9189ff810c153dad\nwpt-pr: 63683\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/imperative/register-tool-input-schema-registers-same-name.https.html"], "git_node": "89903ea780454d59688612be14b56a4e6b3bc00e", "git_parents": ["808184108f14ece8809a91b3982ff59674732799"], "node": "983fb2595bf6f586061ef7308578392f626494d8", "parents": ["6155f7c875e083c2c856316f8093779a73db20c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081801 [wpt PR 63638] - layout: Accumulate ancestors's opacity for `paintable`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd WPT for iframe\n\nSigned-off-by: Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4f650b84483741dd8cde4c6c1c690dffc04e3dac\nwpt-pr: 63638\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/paint-timing/first-paint-only/iframe-in-invisible-ancestor.html"], "git_node": "e396cb0d637721c9ca5636808cd27366390026be", "git_parents": ["89903ea780454d59688612be14b56a4e6b3bc00e"], "node": "fa658b163f91b49616153424cf3292eaa26c9192", "parents": ["983fb2595bf6f586061ef7308578392f626494d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082488 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to 4f650b84483741dd8cde4c6c1c690dffc04e3dac, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: 4f650b8448