Rs to correct wording issue - r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335636\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/ipProtection.ftl"], "git_node": "a47d579ee130e13cbfdc20e69aeeb1954f2953b7", "git_parents": ["b3e806e7265ac80479b9e998fc31d230f77dcc04"], "node": "066385aa03afc07f5a95796a1516425355f54ef2", "parents": ["d9cd977c986efecb04951bbc674ba8ae77d421e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082386 - Speed up BigInt division on AArch64 devices r=mgaudet\n\nAArch64 lacks a two-word division instruction, so it's much faster there\nto multiply by an inverse than to divide.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334073\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/BigIntType.cpp", "js/src/vm/BigIntType.h"], "git_node": "c1afc7e5dd666ffc7c58ea5c18801ed286d5db06", "git_parents": ["a47d579ee130e13cbfdc20e69aeeb1954f2953b7"], "node": "3830ad935b505dbc40ca9b95eda57eff2d166f16", "parents": ["066385aa03afc07f5a95796a1516425355f54ef2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083740 - Snap all axis-aligned widget transforms. r=mac-reviewers,mstange\n\nAccount for scale as well as translation. In bug 2083140, Nikki is\nadding a scale() transform, and that is losing the snapping, causing it\nto be jumpy.\n\nI checked and the window server is snapping on desktop pixels. Do the\nsame so that the animation looks good.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334919\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "e77e5f5b459f54782d1ac113fe9f92fe60d4c63f", "git_parents": ["c1afc7e5dd666ffc7c58ea5c18801ed286d5db06"], "node": "ba7bdd26a25be06d01d1ebc0dbf4236737a294dd", "parents": ["3830ad935b505dbc40ca9b95eda57eff2d166f16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Mendez \u003cjmendez@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081908 - Release failGuard on the encrypted open path in Connection::initialize. r=mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333819\n", "files": ["storage/mozStorageConnection.cpp", "storage/test/gtest/moz.build", "storage/test/gtest/test_encrypted_open.cpp"], "git_node": "193ca7a3c3a77802fa4ba324eed66fe75f05a4f0", "git_parents": ["e77e5f5b459f54782d1ac113fe9f92fe60d4c63f"], "node": "e856140e681c4cbac0b1093907bc43aed06f489e", "parents": ["ba7bdd26a25be06d01d1ebc0dbf4236737a294dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082804 - Remove UrlbarProviderQuickSuggestContextualOptIn. r=adw,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335168\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderQuickSuggestContextualOptIn.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProvidersManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/enUS-searchFeatures.ftl", "browser/components/urlbar/moz.build", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_contextual_optin.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/dynamic-results.css", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml", "tools/@types/subs/FeatureManifest.sys.d.mts", "tools/@types/subs/RFPTargetConstants.sys.d.mts"], "git_node": "a9522ff31ef542d292d158828b24d1bde8e8174a", "git_parents": ["193ca7a3c3a77802fa4ba324eed66fe75f05a4f0"], "node": "c622fc230f55a7c2c1abac1626dae4405c0baec9", "parents": ["e856140e681c4cbac0b1093907bc43aed06f489e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052166 - Drop the element parameter from onBeforeSelection. r=urlbar-reviewers,adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335169\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/docs/process-boundary.md"], "git_node": "55cf2a6ddfc24fbe12e696ba5e65b4567c2bd49e", "git_parents": ["a9522ff31ef542d292d158828b24d1bde8e8174a"], "node": "eea6e16c05c1c8f1ee66cd82a7184a82a0725760", "parents": ["c622fc230f55a7c2c1abac1626dae4405c0baec9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SaaSha Pina \u003csaasha@heysparkbox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066751 - Prevent Nova infobar warning icon border from clipping in forced-colors. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,mstriemer\n\nDraw the Nova message bar icon divider with border-inline-end only, remove\nthe padding-offset token, and drop the infobar icon ring so forced-colors\ndoes not clip the warning icon.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327844\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/infobar.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-message-bar/moz-message-bar.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs"], "git_node": "90fafe0c672c695ea960319a3c08f06df57bf78e", "git_parents": ["55cf2a6ddfc24fbe12e696ba5e65b4567c2bd49e"], "node": "1dd72cd9fe9f6cef1c6c5b0cef0014c9d754fd90", "parents": ["eea6e16c05c1c8f1ee66cd82a7184a82a0725760"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081216 - Save the prefs file of test_libPrefs.js in the temp dir, r=gstoll.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333300\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/test/unit/test_libPrefs.js"], "git_node": "cf5f19ecfa4a3db66a8f0e4438b2123dd0a9a123", "git_parents": ["90fafe0c672c695ea960319a3c08f06df57bf78e"], "node": "cb32b3483f1e5cb407a6dd0e76e7c1f391e69673", "parents": ["1dd72cd9fe9f6cef1c6c5b0cef0014c9d754fd90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081216 - Don't write into the test directory in storage xpcshell tests, r=mak.\n\ntest_storage_connection.js created storage_attach.sqlite in the test directory, and test_storage_service.js opened the checked-in goodDB.sqlite read-write from two connections. Create the attached database in the profile, and use a copy of goodDB.sqlite there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333301\n", "files": ["storage/test/unit/test_storage_connection.js", "storage/test/unit/test_storage_service.js"], "git_node": "ec1b73b78896f6d5ebde81f2e7fad92461e2ba22", "git_parents": ["cf5f19ecfa4a3db66a8f0e4438b2123dd0a9a123"], "node": "7561b0720d3af857bc4beb2d977f3b71db065666", "parents": ["cb32b3483f1e5cb407a6dd0e76e7c1f391e69673"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julie De Lorenzo \u003cjdelorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066533 - Upstream drag and drop into a module in A-C r=petru,android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers\n\n- Moves the grid and list logic that supports reordering as well as drag and drop functionality\n  into an A-C module so that it can be re-used by other features outside the TabsTray.\n- Includes a README that explains usage.\n- keys are now Any\n- the dragged item's size is captured at drag start to support multi-height lists\n- factory arguments stay current through SideEffect\n- ignored items can't start a drag\n- reduced the size of the public API\n