anch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083877 - Use the default installed Chrome or Safari binary path when running Raptor locally without --binary. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nLocal runs only forward a binary for Firefox, so Chrome and Safari runs\nfailed with \"--binary is required!\", and mach looked up a Firefox build\nthose runs never use.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335313\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/browsertime.md", "testing/perfdocs/generated/debugging.md", "testing/perfdocs/generated/webextension.md", "testing/raptor/mach_commands.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/cmdline.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/browsertime.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/debugging.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/webextension.md", "testing/raptor/test/test_cmdline.py"], "git_node": "d5f4186058c0b8abb78a44f4ccb1fa7c2e958b26", "git_parents": ["13a4da0f93dda833e54a882a1980b9d26a270195"], "node": "d2f136e93239b3fe53d8b39cb2ab9c8f7c093160", "parents": ["bb9913ac761397b4320710bf50e0facea17e036b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043009: Fix text-wrap balance for `line-clamp` containers, particularly with `auto`. r=layout-reviewers,dshin,jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332184\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-balance-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-balance-005.html.ini"], "git_node": "cf431015fa2f23bc01c7dec5c2b1efca41c5c15b", "git_parents": ["d5f4186058c0b8abb78a44f4ccb1fa7c2e958b26"], "node": "74a1e68b52e85e8ef475dcc66153a305e0a9e807", "parents": ["d2f136e93239b3fe53d8b39cb2ab9c8f7c093160"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex G \u003cagain@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082500 - [Monitor Agent][Models] Preserve the MLPA 429 error code so monitors can tell an exhausted budget from rate limiting r=fluent-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,yjamora,bolsson,npodgurski\n\nMLPA returns HTTP 429 for both the daily budget being exhausted and short-lived per-second throttling, but only the budget case carries the \"daily budget exhausted\" error subcode. The Smart Window Assistant already reads that subcode to tell the two apart; the monitor run path in Monitor.sys.mjs collapses the error to a generic rate-limit failure, so the subcode is gone by the time the check result reaches the UI. That is why a transient 429 currently shows \"The Smart Window had reached its check limit for today\" .\n\nPath:\nbudget exceeded from mlpa --\u003e openai api client is a 429 too many requests status but does include error subcode of \"daily budget exhausted\" for that case.\nThis phab just stops us from dropping that so that we can surface it on the frontend as needed.\n\nextends the documented value set of the agentic_action_execute_complete error_code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334171\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/Monitor.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_agent.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_monitor_errors.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/monitor-error-copy.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/AIWindowTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/backends/Pipeline.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/MLTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_openai.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_pipeline.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "6ac6e2b7394e842f8d241bd201d7e553336a7842", "git_parents": ["cf431015fa2f23bc01c7dec5c2b1efca41c5c15b"], "node": "49e6ed44e89af195123d5084c2a2a625a8da87db", "parents": ["74a1e68b52e85e8ef475dcc66153a305e0a9e807"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2083857 - Do not show the text selection menu for text selected in a textarea. r=flozia\" for causing bc failures @ browser_chat_shortcuts.js\n\nThis reverts commit a6127c21fee3ddc8f142a318e78d5c2b9fd7668c.\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "035dfa356048293a1dd2f87ad7a5aa93bba4047e", "git_parents": ["6ac6e2b7394e842f8d241bd201d7e553336a7842"], "node": "bfb2ed95a0d28f0512fef4f01f6276d06f2d13f3", "parents": ["49e6ed44e89af195123d5084c2a2a625a8da87db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2082639 - Modify card transition animation r=emcminn,omc-reviewers\" for causing node & bc failures\n\nThis reverts commit c922d546a0a5774fc074bd3ae84c64003e2cb4ae.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/MultiStageProtonScreen.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_newtab_card_stack.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/MultiStageAWProton.test.jsx"], "git_node": "74506d5fb14e10b61468e99677684e22a1c90f73", "git_parents": ["035dfa356048293a1dd2f87ad7a5aa93bba4047e"], "node": "57f297a895003c5c17a839b941aafc7784aadd29", "parents": ["bfb2ed95a0d28f0512fef4f01f6276d06f2d13f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067782 - Removed focus promo from asrouter. r=omc-reviewers,yazan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335289\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/PanelTestProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e8ead5ec4adf1427117fe34121a4d095a7597b40", "git_parents": ["74506d5fb14e10b61468e99677684e22a1c90f73"], "node": "6de2b55ce2a098871cb40468a48efc018c381801", "parents": ["57f297a895003c5c17a839b941aafc7784aadd29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2076423 - Test worklet module script MIME type checks. r=arai\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit e41ed36043b05a7b86faa779768a322b0914cce4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2076423 - Enforce module script MIME type checks for worklets. r=arai,necko-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes,valentin,padenot\"\n\nThis reverts commit 62d54a6253862362ce6c94f712ab038cf985526f.\n", "files": ["devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/test-worker-promise-error.html", "dom/media/test/crashtests/audioworkletnode-after-unload-1.html", "dom/worklet/WorkletFetchHandler.cpp", "dom/worklet/WorkletFetchHandler.h", "dom/worklet/loader/WorkletModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/worklet/tests/mochitest.toml", "dom/worklet/tests/server_mime_type.sjs", "dom/worklet/tests/test_audioWorklet_mimeType.html", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "78999663e11f618bd1c1ed93cdbabd49e0739a01", "git_parents": ["e8ead5ec4adf1427117fe34121a4d095a7597b40"], "node": "40858e7f3f70e1c2d641485a95c9d84823d4421b", "parents": ["6de2b55ce2a098871cb40468a48efc018c381801"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2081937 - Test importing one URL as two module types in a worklet. r=arai\" for causing wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit d3e5ca7088f1aadd7ebb538f3ed4308403921596.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2081937 - Key worklet fetching requests by module type as well as URI. r=arai\"\n\nThis reverts commit fea583e49f28e1cadaf0bc26372723541584464d.\n", "files": ["dom/worklet/WorkletFetchHandler.cpp", "dom/worklet/WorkletFetchHandler.h", "dom/worklet/loader/WorkletModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/worklet/loader/WorkletModuleLoader.h", "dom/worklet/tests/import_same_url_twice_target.mjs", "dom/worklet/tests/mochitest.toml", "dom/worklet/tests/test_import_same_url_twice.html"], "git_node": "561b21401249f1b7609763960764e0a38e5844b8", "git_parents": ["78999663e11f618bd1c1ed93cdbabd49e0739a01"], "node": "60b05c626397151f1da7d95536e38ce1a283d6ee", "parents": ["40858e7f3f70e1c2d641485a95c9d84823d4421b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "sarah541 \u003csarahkhan1107@hotmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071079 - Tie awesomebar suggestion fetches to the caller's coroutine scope r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nSuggestionFetcher.fetch launched each provider into CoroutineScope(dispatcher),\na scope with a fresh root Job and no parent. The provider coroutines were\ntherefore invisible to the LaunchedEffect that called fetch, so neither a new\nquery nor the awesomebar leaving composition could cancel them. Teardown only\nclosed the dispatcher, which takes the threads away without telling any\ncoroutine to stop.\n\nLaunching the providers inside a supervisorScope makes them children of the\ncaller, so Compose cancels them when the effect restarts or the composition is\ndisposed, and fetchJob is no longer needed. supervisorScope rather than\ncoroutineScope keeps a failing provider from propagating into the composition.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326589\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcher.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/SuggestionFetcherTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties"], "git_node": "2484f54dcc73ed5ed22e6e868301c90345ae29ba", "git_parents": ["561b21401249f1b7609763960764e0a38e5844b8"], "node": "b530a6a9b6790a158e60aa93223bbf24361a9cc7", "parents": ["60b05c626397151f1da7d95536e38ce1a283d6ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082578 - Remove the unreachable IP Protection OptedOut service state. r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,twhite,kaya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334671\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/ipprotection/GeckoIPProtectionDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/ipprotection/IPProtectionHandler.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/Reducers.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionReducerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationTools.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/