ail to start with an error like:\n\n\u003e Info: Could not load the Qt platform plugin \"xcb\" in\n\u003e \"...\" even though it was found. (:0, )\n\u003e\n\u003e Fatal: This application failed to start because no Qt platform plugin\n\u003e could be initialized. Reinstalling the application may fix this\n\u003e problem.\n\u003e\n\u003e Available platform plugins are: linuxfb, minimal, offscreen, vnc, xcb\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332871\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozrunner/mozrunner/devices/android_device.py"], "git_node": "2d7e2d0fe696574ae4f9e27a1c3078386161d0f6", "git_parents": ["623e478cd46969e3e4734a160fdd95290b16e3b2"], "node": "7480bf6306c1737c213775deba2f2076b0572801", "parents": ["ac9e96123366a8132935d46e77fe372212c9a26d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084137 - Support StylePropertyMap.set() with multiple values. r=janv\n\nTrivial-ish now that we support append().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335595\n", "files": ["layout/style/typedom/StylePropertyMap.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/StylePropertyMap.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/declared/set.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/inline/set.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/declared/append.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/inline/append.tentative.html"], "git_node": "5a1c2d214fbe500cf8ca47a6f6c569dfb1d6d8ab", "git_parents": ["2d7e2d0fe696574ae4f9e27a1c3078386161d0f6"], "node": "d7118266afd47e8a4f6a39326053353fc96e718c", "parents": ["7480bf6306c1737c213775deba2f2076b0572801"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084311 - ensure OneCRL bundle is loaded at init r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335790\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/RemoteSecuritySettings.sys.mjs", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_onecrl_loads_bundle.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "2e02d8d098d040f6b2f26e308fe8c6dc11db2b02", "git_parents": ["5a1c2d214fbe500cf8ca47a6f6c569dfb1d6d8ab"], "node": "9315ef5d8106553aebbfa6957f252d008427519d", "parents": ["d7118266afd47e8a4f6a39326053353fc96e718c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083212 - Recognize mini window in session store. r=sessionstore-reviewers,sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335128\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_pop_tab.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_sessionstore.js", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_sessionstore_taskbartabs.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "430b48d8f61d089a632756bfbb31a039bba8f73f", "git_parents": ["2e02d8d098d040f6b2f26e308fe8c6dc11db2b02"], "node": "1fd9933fd8bf89010eb3db5a8b1ac5a205378be9", "parents": ["9315ef5d8106553aebbfa6957f252d008427519d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080652 - Forbid foreignObject in \u003csvg:use\u003e. r=smaug\n\nEven same-origin. This introduces a lot of security edge cases like\nclonable shadow DOM etc. Matches other engines.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334190\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGUseElement.cpp", "layout/reftests/svg/use-restrictions-not-restricted-ref.svg", "layout/reftests/svg/use-restrictions.svg", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/struct/reftests/use-foreignObject.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/scripted/use-script-not-executed.html"], "git_node": "aa6f23e00ed078a13675c06e17bd68577ba8a8b6", "git_parents": ["430b48d8f61d089a632756bfbb31a039bba8f73f"], "node": "3ec560fdc16f36b779fc73b734a481f4bfc4b5bc", "parents": ["1fd9933fd8bf89010eb3db5a8b1ac5a205378be9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083469 - Use SetReferenceDrawTargetTransform for SkGDI fallback. r=lsalzman\n\nInstead of manually passing an offset and downscaling.\n\nWe can do it now that handling of that transform is fixed\nin the recording.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334893\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/HelpersSkia.h", "gfx/skia/gdi/SkGDIDocument.cpp", "gfx/skia/gdi/SkGDIDocument.h", "gfx/thebes/PrintTargetWindows.cpp"], "git_node": "02d6885e47fd0917257914625ae471994657115f", "git_parents": ["aa6f23e00ed078a13675c06e17bd68577ba8a8b6"], "node": "0f16b59ffd9fcc9556c474ac8edbff5c951b4cd6", "parents": ["3ec560fdc16f36b779fc73b734a481f4bfc4b5bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Welpy-cw \u003c58345540+Welpy-cw@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084270 - Stop applying ancestor clips outside popups in intersection observations. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nStop ancestor clipping at the popup frame while preserving clipping inside\nit, so visible popup content can intersect outside subdocument viewports.\n\nCover the regression with a chrome mochitest using a same-origin iframe,\na panel, and a plain observed element outside the embedding viewport.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335689\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMIntersectionObserver.cpp", "dom/base/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/chrome/file_intersectionobserver_popup.xhtml", "dom/base/test/chrome/test_intersectionobserver_popup.xhtml"], "git_node": "50a9f61b8325000abef3561d1072d7c6881b004e", "git_parents": ["02d6885e47fd0917257914625ae471994657115f"], "node": "62f28182f0aa11f2a5662be1afa9419c7ae8f67c", "parents": ["0f16b59ffd9fcc9556c474ac8edbff5c951b4cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079575 - Provide the search widget preview images at every screen density. r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nThe Fenix previews were 3x exports and the Focus previews 4x exports sitting in drawable-hdpi, so they now\nlive in the density folder matching their scale, with the lower densities downscaled from them. All copies are\nencoded with cwebp -near_lossless 60, which keeps every pixel within 4/255 of the source. The Focus snackbar\nbackground is a shape drawable and moves out of drawable-hdpi.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335834\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/beta/res/drawable-hdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/beta/res/drawable-mdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/beta/res/drawable-xhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/beta/res/drawable-xxhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable-hdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable-mdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable-xhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/nightly/res/drawable-hdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/nightly/res/drawable-mdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/nightly/res/drawable-xhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/nightly/res/drawable-xxhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/release/res/drawable-hdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/release/res/drawable-mdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/release/res/drawable-xhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/release/res/drawable-xxhdpi/fenix_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-hdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-hdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-hdpi/focus_snackbar_background.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-mdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-mdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-hdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-hdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-mdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-mdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xxhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xxhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xxxhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night-xxxhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxxhdpi/focus_search_widget.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxxhdpi/focus_search_widget_promote_dialog.webp", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable/focus_snackbar_background.xml"], "git_node": "240835807014f0acd45b6a43ce27adc59d20d22f", "git_parents": ["50a9f61b8325000abef3561d1072d7c6881b004e"], "node": "d6c7cf6bc2289926f46054c6c8f0698e2152317d", "parents": ["62f28182f0aa11f2a5662be1afa9419c7ae8f67c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Meg Viar \u003clmegviar@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080751 - Re-enable the add button on a personalized tile if the user rejects pinning via the OS prompt and allow tile to reappear in subsequent messages r=omc-reviewers,hsohaney,mimi\n\n`PIN_TASKBAR_TAB` used to return before the user answered the Windows OS pin prompt. Declining the prompt had two effects:\n\n- The personalized taskbar tabs tile's Add button stayed disabled if a user declined (bug\u00a02080751).\n- The Taskbar Tab entry and its Start Menu shortcut were left behind. `PinnableSitesProvider` then treated the site as already pinned and left it out of future personalized spotlights (bug\u00a02081217). It also counted toward `installedWebAppsCount` targeting.\n\nChanges in this patch:\n\n- `TaskbarTabsPin.pinTaskbarTab` now takes an optional `onRejected` callback.\n- `TaskbarTabs.findOrCreateTaskbarTab` takes an opt-in `waitForPin` option. When set, it waits for the pin attempt to finish and returns `pinRejected`.\n- `PIN_TASKBAR_TAB` now uses waitForPin. If a user declines, it removes the Taskbar Tab if this action created it, and returns false. That re-enables the Add button and lets the site appear in later spotlights.\n\n//Note - MSIX builds can't report a decline, so they keep the old behavior.//\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333637\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_targeting.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/PinnableSitesList.test.jsx", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_cmd.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_icons.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_manifest.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_pageAction.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_pin.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_telemetry.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_title.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_existingInstalledCountMetric.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_installedCountMetric.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinLinux.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinMsix.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinWindows.js", "browser/modules/test/browser/browser_BrowserDOMWindow_openURI.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_pin_taskbar_tab.js"], "git_node": "36e5885fd2caf50359b7bd5a57c5ac5d337f8705", "git_parents": ["240835807014f0acd45b6a43ce27adc59d20d22f"], "node": "29abbd038c88fc210071c0a2d12d82dc8dd949d5", "parents": ["d6c7cf6bc2289926f46054c6c8f0698e2152317d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082215 - Make the page height in helper_zoomToFocusedInput_dynamic_toolbar_bug1828235.html halfway between 100svh and 100lvh. r=ajakobi\n\n98lvh is only taller than 100svh if the dynamic toolbar is taller than 2% of 100lvh.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333975\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_zoomToFocusedInput_dynamic_toolbar_bug1828235.html"], "git_node": "d86a2bcff70f0d4e3d58f73b9eee6ad8f4c4259f", "git_parents": ["36e5885fd2caf50359b7bd5a57c5ac5d337f8705"], "node": "6c7d8791335e5e40114202883d4e03594c934872", "parents": ["29abbd038c88fc210071c0a2d12d82dc8dd949d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082215 - Compute ZoomToRect's minimum zoom against the composition size without the dynamic toolbar for pages shorter than 100lvh. r=ajakobi\n\nSuch a page only needs to fill the composition size without the dynamic toolbar, a taller page the whole composition bounds. Previously this relied on the scrollable rect being expanded to the composition bounds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333976\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_doubletap_zoom_out_dynamic_toolbar.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_double_tap_zoom.html"], "git_node": "b402ca7911cba615f7291b46fa610ace7b37b1ee", "git_parents": ["d86a2bcff70f0d4e3d58f73b9eee6ad8f4c4259f"], "node": "1fe663db276774dbe38b2461e40440a98162fd44", "parents": ["6c7d8791335e5e40114202883d4e03594c934872"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1981478 - Flip prefs to switch to NDK decoding/encoding on Android on nightly. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D260149\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "ab8bc00bce32e62ccc37ad3f5f787cf3e0ffc1b5", "git_parents": ["b402ca7911cba615f7291b46fa610ace7b37b1ee"], "node": "c1557fb45d8b7e3cdd66cfde39675a150a9993f6", "parents": ["1fe663db276774dbe38b2461e40440a98162fd44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-kmr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml"], "git_node": "1f11b5ad57439af872081d0b9b870de5862fb075", "git_parents": ["ab8bc00bce32e62ccc37ad3f5f787cf3e0ffc1b5"], "node": "d6bddd22ae74768c5c09983b0580507454b12287", "parents": ["c1557fb45d8b7e3cdd66cfde39675a150a9993f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729196 - Disable browser_doorhanger_generated_password.js on macOS 15 aarch64 opt and Windows 11 32-bit debug for frequent failures. r=intermittent-reviewers,aryx DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335793\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "fb78851d4deaafd7eb8037865448b2f0cd8a02e3", "git_parents": ["1f11b5ad57439af872081d0b9b870de5862fb075"], "node": "1ac66a984a04bbdafbc22351fec818c3667979de", "parents": ["d6bddd22ae74768c5c09983b0580507454b12287"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081032 - Disable browser_canonizeURL.js on macOS 15 aarch64 debug for frequent failures. r=intermittent-reviewers,aryx DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335831\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "4e9b08d93aec59e5b9310cb199ddcd4fd6b348ca", "git_parents": ["fb78851d4deaafd7eb8037865448b2f0cd8a02e3"], "node": "6d7425708ea0380afd0be3f131ace36117ba79a0", "parents": ["1ac66a984a04bbdafbc22351fec818c3667979de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081443: Respect background URL opens on macOS. r=mac-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,jhirsch,mstange,bradwerth,Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333481\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/tests/unit/test_command_line_handler.js", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser_background_external_url.js", "browser/modules/BrowserDOMWindow.sys.mjs", "toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.mm"], "git_node": "514a53dcccf617c047434326bc32d0e265c0f34a", "git_parents": ["4e9b08d93aec59e5b9310cb199ddcd4fd6b348ca"], "node": "9de9d58d5c33a7697f12bf6a7b992cb35789d46b", "parents": ["6d7425708ea0380afd0be3f131ace36117ba79a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083323 - [loong64] Part 1: Switch VPR zeroing instruction from VXOR.V vd, vd, vd to VLDI vd, 0 to match GCC output. r=yury\n\nGCC 16.2.1 chooses VLDI vd, 0 for zeroing a vector. This is safer since\nit doesn't rely on microarch's recognition capabilities.\n\nThis part is neutral in terms of performance, with both \"before\" and\n\"after\" versions having ~6 IPC on Loongson 3B6000.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334838\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "ce39c1abe2afb8ccb9f79bd7eea4e3f22d338ce0", "git_parents": ["514a53dcccf617c047434326bc32d0e265c0f34a"], "node": "955af462fdeb7e4cad7abdb94b5e2a09ea8b0be3", "parents": ["9de9d58d5c33a7697f12bf6a7b992cb35789d46b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083323 - [loong64] Part 2: Match disassembly of V{LDREPL,STELM}.[BHWD] to {,llvm-}objdump's output. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334839\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/disasm/Disasm-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "4ed18743c8e2f163ae8f78f291492be4bce54079", "git_parents": ["ce39c1abe2afb8ccb9f79bd7eea4e3f22d338ce0"], "node": "20da4b776690a4a27943682915526ccd77425489", "parents": ["955af462fdeb7e4cad7abdb94b5e2a09ea8b0be3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083323 - [loong64] Part 3: Optimize widening Float64 Simd128 loads. r=yury\n\nThis helps reducing one scratch register use, and avoiding a\ncross-domain register move which generally has bad throughput and\nlatency.\n\nMicrobench results of the generated sequence (BATCH=2048,\nN_BATCHES=50000, N_WARMUP=5000, FREQ=2.2GHz):\n\n                Type            IPC     Latency (ns)\n        Before  Indexed         2.96    5.895\n                Base+offset     2.99    5.896\n        After   Indexed         3.98    5.443\n                Base+offset     3.98    5.442\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334840\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "7d0898fc4ba69cb2edd97f3cc7546cc69be8e5a2", "git_parents": ["4ed18743c8e2f163ae8f78f291492be4bce54079"], "node": "33b5e6ae5435dcbac2e1d78735076c993fc10efe", "parents": ["20da4b776690a4a27943682915526ccd77425489"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083323 - [loong64] Part 4: Implement splat Simd128 loads without GPR data trips using VLDREPL.[BHWD]. r=yury\n\nThis also helps avoiding a cross-domain register move.\n\nMicrobench results of the generated sequence:\n\n* Indexed:\n\n                Width   IPC     Latency (ns)\n        Before  B       2.00    5.435\n                H       1.99    5.436\n                W       3.99    4.979\n                D       1.99    4.983\n        After   B       3.99    4.981\n                H       3.99    4.982\n                W       3.99    4.981\n                D       3.99    4.982\n\n* Base+offset:\n\n                Width   IPC     Latency (ns)\n        Before  B       2.00    5.435\n                D       1.99    4.982\n        After   B       2.00    4.512\n                D       1.99    4.512\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334841\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/load-splat-widen-loong64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp"], "git_node": "e75dc88a2456733b114a14eb2c1475dfa080b0dc", "git_parents": ["7d0898fc4ba69cb2edd97f3cc7546cc69be8e5a2"], "node": "166fcd2fc26009414ebab63b42ad340a93aa071a", "parents": ["33b5e6ae5435dcbac2e1d78735076c993fc10efe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083323 - [loong64] Part 5: Implement Simd128 lane stores without GPR data trips using VSTELM.[BHWD]. r=yury\n\nThis also helps avoiding a cross-domain register move.\n\nMicrobench results of the generated sequence:\n\n                Width   IPC\n        Before  B       2.00\n                D       2.00\n        After   B       3.97\n                D       3.97\n\nNote that latency cannot be measured for store instructions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334842\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/simd/store-lane-loong64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp"], "git_node": "c19545e637ca286c1552a540461d79c5447a08bd", "git_parents": ["e75dc88a2456733b114a14eb2c1475dfa080b0dc"], "node": "9fd6a9b7ac7ecd5c21be5b4620946a37a0512b17", "parents": ["166fcd2fc26009414ebab63b42ad340a93aa071a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080572 - Add Feature::WEBRENDER_ANGLE_GL and its handling to gfxConfigManager r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nAdd Feature::WEBRENDER_ANGLE_GL like Feature::WEBRENDER_ANGLE_METAL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332726\n", "files": ["gfx/config/gfxConfigManager.cpp", "gfx/config/gfxConfigManager.h", "gfx/config/gfxFeature.h", "gfx/tests/gtest/TestConfigManager.cpp", "widget/GfxInfoFeatureDefs.inc"], "git_node": "384cce07b219ae8d9bb10e8d92e9d83c4f39f506", "git_parents": ["c19545e637ca286c1552a540461d79c5447a08bd"], "node": "5ff8628d1caaa1c93e21192beb620ae037561ef9", "parents": ["9fd6a9b7ac7ecd5c21be5b4620946a37a0512b17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079100: Queue Cocoa file pickers and refresh download directories. r=mac-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs,bradwerth\n\nResolve each download's starting directory after the preceding picker has finished, so queued downloads see the user's new location. Closing the parent window cancels active and waiting download prompts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333966\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/downloads/HelperAppDlg.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/downloads/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/downloads/tests/browser/browser_download_save_directory.js", "widget/cocoa/nsFilePicker.h", "widget/cocoa/nsFilePicker.mm", "widget/tests/gtest/TestCocoaFilePickerQueue.mm", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "6b4da118c43dc5ced66dbe1adc530b6de87b794d", "git_parents": ["384cce07b219ae8d9bb10e8d92e9d83c4f39f506"], "node": "5b8e1a8a848a9146a69fbe9a04e079295515fd06", "parents": ["5ff8628d1caaa1c93e21192beb620ae037561ef9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084311 - ensure OneCRL bundle is loaded at init r=jschanck\" for causing bc failures @ browser_receive_push_messages.js\n\nThis reverts commit 2e02d8d098d040f6b2f26e308fe8c6dc11db2b02.\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/RemoteSecuritySettings.sys.mjs", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_onecrl_loads_bundle.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "ac36601846d345477391e1e406b4c86933a084f6", "git_parents": ["6b4da118c43dc5ced66dbe1adc530b6de87b794d"], "node": "ea805bd8b7e573113072df58f5fe3d704e1f50ab", "parents": ["5b8e1a8a848a9146a69fbe9a04e079295515fd06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080652 - Forbid foreignObject in \u003csvg:use\u003e. r=smaug\" for causing wpt failures @ /svg/struct/scripted/use-inline-event-handlers.html\n\nThis reverts commit aa6f23e00ed078a13675c06e17bd68577ba8a8b6.\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGUseElement.cpp", "layout/reftests/svg/use-restrictions-not-restricted-ref.svg", "layout/reftests/svg/use-restrictions.svg", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/struct/reftests/use-foreignObject.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/scripted/use-script-not-executed.html"], "git_node": "16a89ce9ee5eaf23d5ebfea1c0a44fe19ecd0e0a", "git_parents": ["ac36601846d345477391e1e406b4c86933a084f6"], "node": "331d31a92bb45dd6f31bdef5c34f497761ba826f", "parents": ["ea805bd8b7e573113072df58f5fe3d704e1f50ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055099 - Disable browser_aiwindow_smartbar_telemetry.js on Windows 11 asan for frequent failures. r=intermittent-reviewers,aryx DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335787\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "050cb92ee6be534dc6edc8a9a639706e0363fc2e", "git_parents": ["16a89ce9ee5eaf23d5ebfea1c0a44fe19ecd0e0a"], "node": "59082306c2e989347030ab47a7b2f0e5e41bd8ac", "parents": ["331d31a92bb45dd6f31bdef5c34f497761ba826f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077922 - Cancel pending libsecret calls at xpcom-will-shutdown. r=keeler\n\nLibSecret passes no GCancellable to secret_password_{store,lookup,clear}_sync.\nOSKeyStore runs these on BgIOThreadPool, and BackgroundEventTarget::Shutdown()\njoins that pool with nsThreadPool::Shutdown(), which waits with no timeout. If\nthe keyring daemon shows a prompt that never completes (for example,\ngnome-keyring asking to create or unlock the default keyring with no prompter\non screen), the call never returns and shutdown hangs at\nxpcom-shutdown-threads until the terminator crashes the process.\n\nLibSecret now owns a GCancellable, passes it to all three calls, and cancels it\nat xpcom-will-shutdown. For a pending prompt, libsecret dismisses it and the\ncall fails as soon as the daemon confirms.\n\nOnce shutdown has reached xpcom-will-shutdown, OSKeyStore's background\noperations also reject with NS_ERROR_ILLEGAL_DURING_SHUTDOWN without calling\nthe key store, so a job that runs late cannot start a new call on any backend.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333373\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/LibSecret.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/LibSecret.h", "security/manager/ssl/OSKeyStore.cpp"], "git_node": "67ec6e39232b11140d545ef29da799755f27a5c3", "git_parents": ["050cb92ee6be534dc6edc8a9a639706e0363fc2e"], "node": "30f8ae02615bb76a1ab204ac9c7fa831081cedd5", "parents": ["59082306c2e989347030ab47a7b2f0e5e41bd8ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022097 - Disable browser_smartwindow_prompts.js on Linux 24.04 x64 opt and Windows 11 x64 asan and ccov for frequent failures. r=intermittent-reviewers,aryx DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335807\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow.toml"], "git_node": "fa1415303a3991047df7eaa0bafddbc8f38db1f3", "git_parents": ["67ec6e39232b11140d545ef29da799755f27a5c3"], "node": "edb791b2c82b7dd390c486201ccc84da6267c5cb", "parents": ["30f8ae02615bb76a1ab204ac9c7fa831081cedd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068172 - Connect the tab groups strip to its store so it shows while in a tab group r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333716\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupsStrip.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupsStripTest.kt"], "git_node": "457ce2cf5a7264f87b36ba6667d09f4db8343ac9", "git_parents": ["fa1415303a3991047df7eaa0bafddbc8f38db1f3"], "node": "996d27cf64b5242b4db45089376f25cc112f87ff", "parents": ["edb791b2c82b7dd390c486201ccc84da6267c5cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084397: Reject `types` with \"-ua-\" prefix in `@view-transition` rule. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335836\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/view_transition_descriptors.toml", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/view_transition_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/animation.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/navigation/with-types/at-rule-with-types-parsing.html.ini"], "git_node": "39be7f42e21f7ae4ecc433889639e1662707b4e0", "git_parents": ["457ce2cf5a7264f87b36ba6667d09f4db8343ac9"], "node": "92fa34ee03dd5dff48ddae4f1ecf900dcba3cc6d", "parents": ["996d27cf64b5242b4db45089376f25cc112f87ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069157 - Record impressions of the text selection menu's search action. r=jteow,search-reviewers,echa\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo manually experiment with this feature, here is [[ https://searchux.netlify.app/highlight-to-search/ | the UX prototype ]].\n\nRecords a `sap.impression_counts` entry for `text_selection` each time the menu is shown with the Search action visible, labelled with the engine it would search with.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334793\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/components/search/BrowserSearchTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/search/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "a2561d64d27cd5841523cad7fbdeb21cc9f0479c", "git_parents": ["39be7f42e21f7ae4ecc433889639e1662707b4e0"], "node": "696e2ca32cc4cabde3af47430ed3ad53386dac42", "parents": ["92fa34ee03dd5dff48ddae4f1ecf900dcba3cc6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "owlishDeveloper \u003cbugzeeeeee@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053909 - [Part 3] Add ScrollCaptureCallback implementation r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334363\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoView.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoViewScrollCaptureCallback.java"], "git_node": "2d2fcfd4d95edc13b0b5d125a63bb34ab5aa8f68", "git_parents": ["a2561d64d27cd5841523cad7fbdeb21cc9f0479c"], "node": "dbea8c53cc617d12f779f1c91e98387cdc45fbbf", "parents": ["696e2ca32cc4cabde3af47430ed3ad53386dac42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069157 - Record impressions of the text selection menu's search action. r=jteow,search-reviewers,echa\" for causing bc failures @ browser_chat_shortcuts.js\n\nThis reverts commit a2561d64d27cd5841523cad7fbdeb21cc9f0479c.\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/components/search/BrowserSearchTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/search/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "d9ee22d0cc687471272ce6ba7fe3b36b4954d26b", "git_parents": ["2d2fcfd4d95edc13b0b5d125a63bb34ab5aa8f68"], "node": "1d8290c33a9408fcd2a327a776e3ab3844c89c90", "parents": ["dbea8c53cc617d12f779f1c91e98387cdc45fbbf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084270 - Stop applying ancestor clips outside popups in intersection observations. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\" for causing mochitest failures @ test_intersectionobserver_popup\n\nThis reverts commit 50a9f61b8325000abef3561d1072d7c6881b004e.\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMIntersectionObserver.cpp", "dom/base/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/chrome/file_intersectionobserver_popup.xhtml", "dom/base/test/chrome/test_intersectionobserver_popup.xhtml"], "git_node": "27948cb96b5e4ab3d9a22f20dbec9571a60b6d55", "git_parents": ["d9ee22d0cc687471272ce6ba7fe3b36b4954d26b"], "node": "f022ed180f319fd15def9f51ab5879609f8cbc88", "parents": ["1d8290c33a9408fcd2a327a776e3ab3844c89c90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mirko Kerezovic \u003cmirko@kerezovic.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1297305 - Move document timeline tests to WPT. r=birtles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332703\n", "files": ["dom/animation/test/document-timeline/test_document-timeline.html", "dom/animation/test/document-timeline/test_request_animation_frame.html", "dom/animation/test/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/timing-model/timelines/document-timelines.html"], "git_node": "b904e1573ba6c082748009a18322b6dbd47c2134", "git_parents": ["27948cb96b5e4ab3d9a22f20dbec9571a60b6d55"], "node": "40198dd041214a193e027a428d7003bbbb687143", "parents": ["f022ed180f319fd15def9f51ab5879609f8cbc88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083857 - Do not show the text selection menu for text selected in a textarea. r=flozia\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo manually experiment with this feature, here is [[ https://searchux.netlify.app/highlight-to-search/ | the UX prototype ]].\n\nIgnores `textarea` while `browser.highlightToSearch.featureGate` is on, so users who already have a chatbot configured keep the menu there until the feature ships.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335297\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "5b8ccec8050cd383e7f8696e10cf60c148f00333", "git_parents": ["b904e1573ba6c082748009a18322b6dbd47c2134"], "node": "613238ae31af888b21b17191ffa6e673bb5050fb", "parents": ["40198dd041214a193e027a428d7003bbbb687143"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1981478 - Flip prefs to switch to NDK decoding/encoding on Android on nightly. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\" for causing mda failures in test_hevc_playback.html.\n\nThis reverts commit ab8bc00bce32e62ccc37ad3f5f787cf3e0ffc1b5.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "e23be3677d589e4e3bf8a3f2bf7f533256cf1311", "git_parents": ["5b8ccec8050cd383e7f8696e10cf60c148f00333"], "node": "e672705e945bffd6f8a7f145570017b8758f99a8", "parents": ["613238ae31af888b21b17191ffa6e673bb5050fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084464 - Determine the filename of a SharedFTFace used in an UnscaledFontFreeType. r=gfx-reviewers,ahale\n\nCurrently, when Thebes creates an UnscaledFontFreeType/Fontconfig with only a SharedFTFace, it does not\nknow the filename of the font from which the data is loaded. Subsequent attempts to call GetFontFileData\non it will not see any filename and thus instead of creating a descriptor for the font, it will attempt\nto transfer the entire data contents of the font instead.\n\nThe SharedFTFace actually already knows the filename of its included data, we just didn't query it yet.\nThe fix is simply to query the filename from it when creating the UnscaledFontFreeType. This should allow\nmore descriptors based on filenames to be sent over the process gap instead of data blobs, which should\nspeed up font transmission.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335861\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/UnscaledFontFreeType.h"], "git_node": "318107af6976780a78e45207eb0185718461a9b4", "git_parents": ["e23be3677d589e4e3bf8a3f2bf7f533256cf1311"], "node": "005f38007ef92951e4cf0e9d855e76668b90f374", "parents": ["e672705e945bffd6f8a7f145570017b8758f99a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082978 - make \"Open in new tab\" open next to current tab r=ngrato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335839\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ToolUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_tool_ui.js"], "git_node": "d818168e04fdaf9314dddb3faa9b73053c15e338", "git_parents": ["318107af6976780a78e45207eb0185718461a9b4"], "node": "522971ca49a4c0cf1a9d6e1ea965b497cf2dfe5d", "parents": ["005f38007ef92951e4cf0e9d855e76668b90f374"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081105 - Handle SplitAndAllocRun failure properly r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333946\n", "files": ["memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "f10ec88da089ea8f071353db7f10e0a4739641af", "git_parents": ["d818168e04fdaf9314dddb3faa9b73053c15e338"], "node": "9c0333c3cf4b5acf40f85a05f7dfc22ba4e17a0d", "parents": ["522971ca49a4c0cf1a9d6e1ea965b497cf2dfe5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082087. Use the hardware f16 to f32 conversion in qcms on aarch64. r=jrmuizel,gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nIn a profile of decoding an HDR JXL image f16_to_f32 was 7.3% of the time inside qcms, and miniscule after this patch.\n\nx86 has a f16 to f32 instruction also, but integrating it is a little more involved.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333892\n", "files": ["gfx/qcms/src/transform.rs"], "git_node": "ee6dffdce98143e49a1a426fd3759274921dbf59", "git_parents": ["f10ec88da089ea8f071353db7f10e0a4739641af"], "node": "b5f6b84fe025bac60bcfb07ccd308368bb32f0e4", "parents": ["9c0333c3cf4b5acf40f85a05f7dfc22ba4e17a0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Louis-Philippe \u003clpmanette@omnicesoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079213 - Make sure we release wl_buffer created over dmabuf surface. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335712\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.cpp", "widget/gtk/W