475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\ntl -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\ntr -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\ntrs -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nuk -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nur -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nuz -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nvi -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nwo -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nxh -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nzam -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nzh-CN -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\nzh-TW -\u003e 475670d0a2a66c85159ea0a0a974427135d10076\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "b56fee81d473fd115d5cead0c9ecff661c2cd8a7", "git_parents": ["81cc538a26fb6fd426b09253ffad42379d03fe24"], "node": "1ab461fbae6024255a718bc87d36364ee043cd1d", "parents": ["0ca3437df824aa88d5471f6ba2c699bd0f0e9739"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Koehler \u003cchkoehler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071101 - Clear the cookies of Cookies.Block hosts every time the policy is applied. r=mkaply\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331655\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_clear_blocked_cookies.js"], "git_node": "aa51ceb6d41dd60363073f912a9d1a0522dc462e", "git_parents": ["b56fee81d473fd115d5cead0c9ecff661c2cd8a7"], "node": "c68efddc68900849dcae662bcad53f892810858f", "parents": ["1ab461fbae6024255a718bc87d36364ee043cd1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2078254 [Linux] Respect nsWindow::MakeFullScreen() return state and disable fullscreen for xx-pip r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\" for causing bustage @ nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit bc576c01b19d81e850da5daca68b8fb438060ce0.\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.h", "widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindow.h", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.h"], "git_node": "a89bac696251aacc663c70eb750baa3e3dcb522b", "git_parents": ["aa51ceb6d41dd60363073f912a9d1a0522dc462e"], "node": "6fc3aa129408c56160dd7b1233fa232a9ce72361", "parents": ["c68efddc68900849dcae662bcad53f892810858f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084187. Stamp vendored Rust files with the current time so jj and hg see same-size changes. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\ncargo vendor extracts every crate with the fixed mtime stored in its\n.crate archive (2006-07-23), and it rewrites all of third_party/rust on\neach run. jj's working copy snapshot treats a file as unchanged when its\nsize and mtime match the recorded state, so after any earlier\n./mach vendor rust in the same checkout, a vendored file whose size does\nnot change is invisible to jj status, jj diff and jj commit. A version\nbump is exactly that case: in a test vendoring jxl 0.8.0 over 0.7.4, jj\nmissed 13 files (the crates' Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml.orig, Cargo.lock and\n.cargo_vcs_info.json), leaving a commit whose vendored sources do not\nmatch Cargo.lock. hg's dirstate has the same blind spot. git is not\naffected because it also compares ctime.\n\nSetting each vendored file's mtime to the current time after cargo vendor\nruns makes jj and hg hash the files on the next status. Checksums are\nunaffected, and this costs a one-time rehash of third_party/rust.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335618\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/vendor_rust.py"], "git_node": "4bbac9ad04925bcc117b943ed1e1aeef33475294", "git_parents": ["a89bac696251aacc663c70eb750baa3e3dcb522b"], "node": "a85adbffd5ad132bc1a06eff2c4aab86dccda220", "parents": ["6fc3aa129408c56160dd7b1233fa232a9ce72361"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083544. Back out the local jxl_simd workaround so the 0.8.0 vendor bump is a pure upstream delta. r=saschanaz,supply-chain-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThis backs out the bug 2043090 macOS x86_64 workaround.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335586\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "third_party/rust/jxl_simd/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/jxl_simd/src/x86_64/avx.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl_simd/src/x86_64/avx512.rs"], "git_node": "fcf6b147c29168d43121714207d87821abaed4c8", "git_parents": ["4bbac9ad04925bcc117b943ed1e1aeef33475294"], "node": "9a426fcd7fcdff259eff05dff7ab20867c98ab74", "parents": ["a85adbffd5ad132bc1a06eff2c4aab86dccda220"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083544. Upgrade jxl-rs to 0.8.0. r=saschanaz,supply-chain-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nPlain ./mach vendor rust.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335587\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "image/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/jxl/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/jxl/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/jxl/README.md", "third_party/rust/jxl/benches/blending.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/box_parser.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/codestream_parser/frame_info.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/codestream_parser/frame_scan_info.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/codestream_parser/image_info.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/codestream_parser/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/color.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/data_types.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/decoder.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/