": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081115 - Remove the unreachable tail of APZBridge::ReceiveInputEvent (Coverity CID 1702966) r=hiro\n\nEvery case of the switch on the event class returns, including the\ndefault one, so the code after it can never run.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333145\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/APZBridge.cpp"], "git_node": "e1ac6e4d7aa652fd246f70f2badfb944d086257f", "git_parents": ["9c8dc9b2fc24962bf733d46717b2eba566984f13"], "node": "df8348f93c57402dab6f3cbebd8b3f8abc3f1918", "parents": ["4bdda83c924ce44094f84c5546769a71d616a629"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081116 - Explicitly ignore the posix_fadvise result in ReadAhead (Coverity CID 1702967) r=xpcom-reviewers,nika\n\nThe read-ahead is only a hint, so a failure needs no handling.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333146\n", "files": ["xpcom/glue/FileUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "4fbf9b7f98427b85edf8830e4c158cbc0f971e22", "git_parents": ["e1ac6e4d7aa652fd246f70f2badfb944d086257f"], "node": "41ce66c76f973ea9e566bf88d59ea8e0ca607f18", "parents": ["df8348f93c57402dab6f3cbebd8b3f8abc3f1918"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081117 - Read the mutable flag before moving the declarative push data (Coverity CID 1702918) r=saschanaz\n\nRecordTelemetry was given declarativePush after it had been moved into\nGetNotificationOptionsForDeclarativePush. It only reads the mutable_\nflag, which the move leaves alone, but any field it might read later\nwould already be gone. Capture the flag before the move.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333147\n", "files": ["dom/push/Declarative.cpp"], "git_node": "406d8fbf1a4597d8bdf196e02222c81087d30de7", "git_parents": ["4fbf9b7f984